VALUES (
    '22502935', '10159832', 'Acute cholecystitis  Myelodysplastic syndrome  Anxiety', 'CHOLECYSTITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via observation admit for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute gallbladder disease.', 'HPI: Ms. ___ is a ___ yr old F with MDS, diagnosed on BM bx  showing excess blasts, and cytogenetic findings of translocation  3;5 and +WT-1 mutation with high risk of transformation to AML,  currently on C215 Decitabine who presents from clinic with  significant jaundice and direct bilirubinemia.   The patient reports developing nausea and vomiting last week  after eating large meal at ___ the nausea and vomiting  has persisted since. She was also noted to have yellow skin tone  in the clinic today but did not note this at home. She had no  emesis yesterday but 2 episodes on ___ and emesis again this  morning. No hematemesis, vomit is non-bilious, most c/w gastric  contents. Since yesterday taking mostly liquids as solids cause  abdominal discomfort. The pain is intermittent and epigastric.  Denies RUQ pain. She reports baseline constipation but has had  at least small BM most days and denies melena, hematochezia, or  mucoid stool. Reports fatigue of several weeks duration. Denies  Tylenol use or any recent changes to medications. She reports  approximately 2 episodes per month of over-eating followed by  abdominal pain and vomiting. She experiencing frequent  generalized abdominal pain which she attributes to long-standing  constipation, but the current episode is the worst she has  experienced.   Denies mouth sores, skin blisters, dermatomal pain. Also denies  fever/chills/sweats, cough, SOB, itchy skin or new rashes, or  dysuria.    ROS: A 10-point ROS was performed with pertinent findings noted  in HPI.  PAST ONCOLOGIC HISTORY: Dx ___. Patient had presented with  progressive fatigue and was found to have pancytopenia and  particularly significant anemia. A bone marrow was performed,  which showed multilineage dysplasia and a 3;5 translocation.   This was consistent with a myelodysplastic syndrome that may be  associated with more rapid progression towards AML.  The patient  was also on rapid heme panel found to have evidence of WT1  amplification. On C2 of Decitabine without major complications.', 'MDS ___ - she was hospitalized for this at age ___ and ___, sees  counselor ___ in ___ Hx herniated disc   Social History: ___ Family History: She is adopted, she is not aware of any siblings and is not  aware of her biological parents health.', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 122/80 HR: NA O2Sat: 98 Weight: NA  [EXAM] ADMISSION EXAM:  VS: 98.5 122/80 90 18 96 RA  GEN: Generally well appearing, in no acute distress. markedly  jaundiced.  HEENT: PERRLA. Oropharynx clear with moist mucous membranes. No  gum hypertrophy. +scleral icterus LYMPH: No palpable cervical or supraclavicular lymphadenopathy. CV: Regular rate and rhythm, S1, S2, ___ systolic murmur at ___ RESP: CTAB, no crackles, wheeze, rhonchi ABD:  Soft, ND, +BS. Diffusely tender to palpation most  prominent in epigastic region. Neg ___, no rebound or  guarding.  EXT: Warm, without edema. NEURO: Alert and oriented. Grossly normal strength,  coordination, and gait. SKIN: No rashes or bruising. LINES: Left PIV without erythema or tenderness',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


