VALUES (
    '25275098', '10176741', 'Gangrenous cholecystitis  Secondary: Coronary artery disease s/p CABG HLD T2DM', 'CHOLECYSTITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via observation admit for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute gallbladder disease.', 'HPI(4): Mr. ___ is a ___ male with history of T2DM, HTN, HLD, colon cancer s/p hemicolectomy w/ adjuvant chemotherapy in ___, CAD with RCA and LAD stents placed in ___, and s/p coronary artery bypass grafting x 4 here on ___ presents with abdominal pain and feeling unwell.   ___ speaking History obtained via phone interpreter.  Patient w/ PMH of Per son, abdominal pain began 3 days ago and is mostly in the upper abdomen/epigastric area. Denies any chest pain,  SOB, N/V/D, leg swelling or cough. Had a fever of 100.5 today. Last  BM ___, but he reports he has been passing gas since. Patient''s son called his cardiac surgery doctor who recommended he present to the ED.   In the ED:  >VS: Tmax 100.1, BP 97-109/47, P 95, 97% on RA >ECG: TWI II, aVL, V3-V6  >Exam: appears unwell; pale; diaphoretic; no ___ edema;  epigastric tenderness; sternal incision c/d/I, non tender; RRR, no murmurs  >Labs: LFTs, AST: ___ ALT: 800 AP: 494 Tbili: 2.4 Alb: 3.3; trops: neg  >Imaging: CXR: no acute process; RUQUS  >Interventions: morphine 4mg IV, cipro 400mg IV, flagyll 500mg  IV  >Impression: new transaminitis. some EKG changes but flat trop and no chest pain.  Dispo: admitting to medicine. ERCP will follow, trend LFTs, plan for ERCP vs MRCP tomorrow. NPO at midnight, IVF >Consults:  1.Cardiac Surgery: Completed ___ 18:03  No surgical issues, so no indication for csurg admission. If studies return normal he may return home with aggressive bowel regimen. Encouraged to take pain medication for chest pain only, not for abdominal pain. Simethicone for gas pain.  Ensure/glucerna for poor appetite. If abnormal studies, admit to medicine for work-up. Note to follow in OMR. Dr. ___.   2.GI - ERCP/Biliary: Requested ___ 20:34   3.Surgery: Acknowledged ___ 19:55 ___ ___   On arrival to the floor patient reported recent flatulence with diffuse abdominal discomfort and bloating. He notes significant unintentional weight loss over the past year with ongoing loss  of appetite. The abdominal pain and flatulence is new and he also notes recent change in skin color. Today he has felt unsteady on his feet with dizziness on standing. At baseline he is able to ambulate independently without issue. He endorses fevers and chills today but denies nausea or vomiting, dysuria, or  diarrhea. He hasn''t had a bowel movement in 4 days and feels constipated but n notes he was told he''s not supposed to strain since the CABG.   ROS: Pertinent positives and negatives as noted in the HPI.  All other systems were reviewed and are negative', 'CAD s/p RCA and LAD stents ___ ___ and 4vCABG ___ Colon cancer s/p hemicolectomy w/adjuvant chemo ___ Hypertension Dyslipidemia Diabetes Mellitus Peripheral arterial disease Bilateral carotid artery stenosis  TIA ___ yr ago)  Malignant neoplasm of colon s/p chemo  BPH     Social History: ___ Family History: Reviewed and found to be not relevant to this illness/reason for hospitalization.', '[VITALS] Temp: 100.5 BP: 144/67 HR: 91 O2Sat: 100 Weight: NA  [EXAM] ADMISSION: -------------- VITALS: Temp: 100.5 (Tm 100.5), BP: 144/67, HR: 91, RR: 18, O2 sat: 93%, O2 delivery: Ra ___: Weight: 153 (With Clothes; With Shoes) ___: BMI: 24.5 GENERAL: Alert , tired appearing, diaphoretic, sl jaundiced, dry mucous membranes EYES: Anicteric, pupils equally round CV: Heart regular, no murmur, no S3, no S4.  No JVD. RESP: Lungs clear to auscultation with good air movement bilaterally. Breathing is non-labored GI: Abdomen soft, nontender, nondistended.  Percutaneous chole  drain placed with minimal bloody drainage.  GU: No suprapubic fullness or tenderness to palpation SKIN: No obvious rashes or ulcerations noted on cursory skin  exam NEURO: Alert, oriented, face symmetric, speech fluent, moves all limbs PSYCH: pleasant, appropriate affect',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
