    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute pancreatitis.', '___ w/breast CA, polycytemia ___ presents with vomiting.  Pt had had 1 month of nausea, nonradiating epigastric abd pain,  anorexia and 10 lb weight loss. Was seen in ___ GI clinic for  evaluation of this and found to have elevated LFTs, elevated T.  bili; RUQ u/s confirmed biliary dilatation with ?mass v. biliary  sludge. Pt scheduled for an outpatient ERCP w/ Dr. ___  ___. However, yesterday AM patient had worsening nausea,  intractable emesis and loose stools so presented to the ED. In ED ERCP contacted. Pt given 1.5Lns and zofran.  ROS: +as above, otherwise reviewed and negative', 'Mitral valve prolapse  Hypertension, essential  Osteopenia  Breast CANCER, left ___  SPINAL STENOSIS - LUMBAR L4-5  Degeneration of lumbar or lumbosacral intervertebral disc  SPONDYLOLISTHESIS - L4-5 grade 1  Stroke, small vessel  Hyperlipemia with goal LDL<100  Polycythemia ___  ___ of shoulder  HOH (hard of hearing)  Chronic renal insufficiency, stage III (moderate)  Gait instability     Social History: ___ Family History: sister CVA', '[VITALS] Temp: 98.1 BP: 134/69 HR: NA O2Sat: 98 Weight: NA  [EXAM] Vitals: T:98.1 BP:134/69 P:85 R:16 O2:96%ra   PAIN: 0 General: nad EYES: anicteric Lungs: clear CV: rrr no m/r/g Abdomen: bowel sounds present, soft, nt/nd Ext: no e/c/c Skin: no rash Neuro: alert, follows commands',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


