VALUES (
    '26013833', '10189947', 'Acute cholecystitis', 'CHOLECYSTITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute gallbladder disease.', 'Ms. ___ is a ___ yo woman followed by GI (Dr. ___ Dr.  ___ for recurrent RUQ pain, abdominal distention, and  excessive soiling after bowel movements who presented 1 day  before admission with RUQ pain and nausea. She developed  symptoms after attending a cookie tasting event. Previously HIDA  scan on ___ showed an ejection fraction of 23% suggesting  biliary dyskinesia. Ultrasound at OSH on ___ showed  gallstonse with pericholecystic fluid suggestive of acute  cholecystits. She was then transferred to ___ for further  care.   Upon arrival at the ED, she was in no acute distress. Her BMs  are loose at baseline and the patient denies any recent changes  in bowel habits or change in urine or stool color. Denies pain,  fevers chills, night sweats, unexplained weight loss,  fatigue/malaise/lethargy, changes in appetite, trouble with  sleep, pruritis, jaundice, rashes, bleeding, easy bruising,  headache, dizziness, vertigo, syncope, weakness, paresthesias, hematemesis, melena, BRBPR, dysphagia, chest pain, shortness of  breath, cough, edema, urinary frequency, urgency', 'IBS recently diagnosed fructose intolerance pelvic floor dysfunction eating disorder anxiety    Social History: ___ Family History: Breast CA in mother', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: NA HR: 80 O2Sat: NA Weight: NA  [EXAM] Upon presentation to ___: GEN: A&O, NAD HEENT: No scleral icterus, mucus membranes moist CV: RRR, No M/G/R PULM: Clear to auscultation b/l, No W/R/R ABD: Soft, nondistended, nontender, Wound dressings at trocar  sites CDI, No erythema/swelling Ext: No ___ edema, ___ warm and well perfused',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


