VALUES (
    '28446121', '10234917', 'Primary: Acute Cholecystitis Secondary: Acute Myelofibrosis', 'CHOLECYSTITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute gallbladder disease.', 'HPI: ___ yo F with acute myelofibrosis on decitabine recently  discharged from ___ on ___ with a coagulase negative staph  bacteremia treated with daptomycin who presents to the ED with  acute onset abdominal pain and vomiting x1 day. The patient was  doing well at home until this morning, when she developed sudden  onset epigastric abdominal pain radiating to her back after  eating a sandwich this afternoon. Pain was ___ and colicky,  dull in nature. She took tylenol without good effect. Associated  with bilious vomiting. No diarrhea. Fever to 102.2 at home.  Patient has been receiving her daptomycin at home and was being  treated for a 7 day course on discharge.   .   In ED VS were 99.8 167/70 93 18 96% on RA. Patient''s labs  significant for WBC of 1.5, lactate of 2.2, and elevated LFTs  with a tbili of 4.9. Received a dose of IV Cefepime, Tylenol 1  gram x1, and Zofran 4 mg IV x1, and 1 L normal saline IVFs. RUQ  U/S showed evidence of sludge, stones, and gallbladder wall  edema c/f acute CCY, no common bile duct dilation. Surgery was  consulted and deemed the patient not a candidate for  cholecystectomy and recommended a ___ guided PTC. Patient was  admitted to the ___ service. On the floor, she denied any pain.    .   Review of systems:   (+) Per HPI   (-) Denies headache, sinus tenderness, rhinorrhea or congestion.  Denied cough, shortness of breath. No diarrhea. Denied chest  pain or tightness, palpitations. No dysuria. Denied arthralgias  or myalgias.', 'Acute myelofibrosis with panmyelosis   - ___: presented with pancytopenia. Bone marrow biopsy at ___    showed >40% blasts. Subsequent bone marrow biopsy done at ___    showed acute myelofibrosis with panmyelosis, a rare form of  acute   leukemia, versus acute megakaryoblastic leukemia with acute   myelofibrosis. The patholgy report favors the former given CD34    positive expression on blast cells.   - ___: started on decitabine   - ___: repeat bone marrow biopsy showed ~50% cellularity   (previously 20%), 5% blasts by CD4 staining, grade ___ fibrosis    (fibrosis essentially unchanged from previous), with   normal-appearing megakaryocytes. Her chemo cycle duration was   increased from every 28 days to 42 days.      Social History: ___ Family History: Daughter is s/p lumpectomy (?breast cancer) ___ years ago. Father died at ___ & brother died at ___ both from bone cancer.', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 136/72 HR: NA O2Sat: 99 Weight: NA  [EXAM] VS: 99.2 136/72 86 20 95% on RA   GA: elderly F lying in bed, AOx3, NAD   HEENT: PERRLA. MMM. no LAD. no JVD. neck supple.   Cards: PMI palpable at ___ IC space. No RVH. RRR S1/S2 heard.  no murmurs/gallops/rubs.   Pulm: CTAB no crackles or wheezes   Abd: soft, TTP in epigastrium, +BS. no g/rt. neg HSM. positive  ___ sign.   Extremities: wwp, no edema. DPs, PTs 2+.   Skin: no rashes.',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


