VALUES (
    '28242311', '10260237', 'Gallstone pancreatitis Choledocolithiasis (gallstone in duct)', 'OTHER_ABDOMINAL',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with abdominal pathology.', 'Patient is a ___ with h/o gallstones, transferred from ___ ED where she presented with two days of N/V and ___ epigastric pain. She had heartburn during her ___ month of pregnancy but she has never had this epigastric pain before. Prior to this she was in ___ She said that this all started on ___ night, first with the pain which she describes as a "tightening" in her abdomen. Pain worse at night. She had some difficulty breathing because the pain but denies SOB. She had some ? L sided chest pain but this has since resolved. She could not walk given her degree of discomfort. On ___ she began vomiting everything she ate. She notes last emesis was 2am day  of presentation. At ___, abdominal U/S concerning for likely acute cholecystitis. She is ___ weeks post c/s at ___ for first child. Her epigastric pain radiates downwards to her stomach. Pain worse with turning to the side and sitting up.  In ED BG = 66 thus given 1 am D50.  . ultrasound from ___: perisplenic ___ pouch, pericholecystic fluid. Gallstones, gallbladder wall thickening. Not definitely tender although patient reports having been medicated. Findings suggest acute cholecystitis. . ___: notable for lipase >1000, Alk phos 227, ALT 670,  AST 545, Amylase 1753 . In ER: (Triage Vitals:98.8, 113/70, 76, 18, 99% on RA )  Meds Given: Pantoprazole as pt with radiating chest pain  thought to be reflux.  Unasyn 3 g IV once Fluids given: 1L NS  Radiology Studies: none consults called. . PAIN SCALE: ___ - epigastrum  ROS: 12 point ROS reviewed and otherwise negative', 'S/p Csection 6 weeks ago for birth of her first child at ___  H/o gallstones    Social History: ___ Family History: Mother with asthma', '[VITALS] Temp: 98.0 BP: 118/72 HR: NA O2Sat: 98 Weight: NA  [EXAM] 1. VS: T = 98.0 P = 72 BP = 118/72 RR = 16 O2Sat on  100% on RA  GENERAL:  Young female laying in bed. Husband and baby at her side.  Nourishment:OK Grooming:  2. Eyes: [] WNL  EOMI without nystagmus, Conjunctiva: clear 3. ENT [] WNL [X] Moist  [] Endentulous  [] Ulcers  [] Erythema  [] JVD ____  cm [] Dry  [] Poor dentition  [] Thrush  [] Swelling  [] Exudate 4. Cardiovascular [X] WNL [X] Regular  [] Tachy  [X] S1 [X] S2 [-] Systolic Murmur     /6, Location: [] Irregular  []Brady []S3  [] S4  [] Diastolic Murmur    /6, Location: [X] Edema RLE  None  [X] Edema LLE None  2+ DPP b/l [] Vascular access  [X] Peripheral [] Central site: 5. Respiratory [ X]WNL [X] CTA bilaterally  [ ] Rales  [ ] Diminshed  [] Comfortable     [ ] Rhonchi   [ ] Dullness  [ ] Percussion WNL  [ ] Wheeze   [] Egophony  6. Gastrointestinal [ ] WNL Diminished BS throughout. Soft. No RUQ tenderness. + mid LLQ  and, superior supra-pubic and RLQ tenderness. 7. Musculoskeletal-Extremities [] WNL [ ] Tone WNL  [ X]Upper extremity strength ___ and symmetrical   [ ]Other: [ ] Bulk WNL    [X] Lower extremity strength ___ and symmetrica  [ ] Other: [] Normal gait  []No cyanosis  [ ] No clubbing  [] No joint swelling 8. Neurological [X] WNL [X ] Alert and Oriented x 3 [ ] Romberg: Positive/Negative  [ ] CN II-XII intact  [ ] Normal attention  [ ] FNF/HTS WNL [] Sensation WNL  [ ] Delirious/confused  [ ] Asterixis Present/Absent  [ ] Position sense WNL [ ] Demented  [ ] No pronator drift  [] Fluent speech 9. Integument  [X] WNL [X] Warm  [X] Dry  [] Cyanotic [] Rash: none/diffuse/face/trunk/back/limbs   10. Psychiatric [X] WNL [X] Appropriate [] Flat affect [] Anxious [] Manic []  Intoxicated [] Pleasant [] Depressed [] Agitated [] Psychotic   Exam',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


