    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute appendicitis.', '___ with chronic abdominal pain, presented to ED with episode of mid-abdominal pain since 3pm.  Describes pain as dull and points to a band across her mid/upper abdomen.  Does endorse nause but no vomiting or diarrhea.  Has had 3 episodes since ___, seen at OSH ED once without source identified.  Also had many similar episodes when in college.  She last ate at 11am yesterday.  No sick contacts', 'Past Medical History: depression  Past Surgical History: none    Social History: ___ Family History: non contributory', '[VITALS] Temp: 98.7 BP: 142/100 HR: 92 O2Sat: 98 Weight: NA  [EXAM] Temp 98.7   HR 92   BP 142/100   RR 16   Os sat 100%  GEN: A&O, NAD HEENT: No scleral icterus, mucus membranes moist CV: RRR, No M/G/R PULM: Clear to auscultation b/l, No W/R/R ABD: Mild/moderate ttp LLQ; non-tender RLQ; soft, nondistended, no rebound or guarding, normoactive bowel sounds, no palpable masses Ext: No ___ edema, ___ warm and well perfused',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


