    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute pancreatitis.', '___ M s/p duodenal tumor enucleation in ___ now with abdominal  pain. He has had acute abdominal pain for approximately 2 hours,  prior to which he had no symptoms. He has had nausea associated  with pain; no vomiting. He has had no fevers or chills. He has  been diaphoretic since the start of his symptoms and has had no  hematochezia/melena, no hematemesis. He has had no diarrhea.  He  was last in the hospital in ___ for syncope from  hypovolemia ___ infectious colitis for which he was treated with  2 weeks of cipro/flagyl.', 'GIST, HTN, GERD, mitral valve prolapse, DU (prior to GIST resection), HL, Colitis   Social History: ___ Family History: Father with aortic aneurysm, HTN, CAD. Mother ___ ALS.   Negative for GI cancer or recurrent ulcer disease.', '[VITALS] Temp: 96.8 BP: 133/97 HR: NA O2Sat: 96 Weight: NA  [EXAM] Admission Exam: T 96.8   P 68  BP 133/97  RR 18  O2 99RA NAD/A&O CTAB RRR Abd soft, tender at midepigastrium, minimally tender in RUQ/LUQ, no guarding/rebound, no peritoneal signs DRE: No palpable masses, stool in vault, guaiac negative No ___ edema.',
