    'A patient was admitted via eu observation for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute gallbladder disease.', 'Mrs. ___ is a ___ year old female with acute onset abdominal  pain since ___. The patient states that she had pain starting  on ___ that and was given a diagnosis of gallbladder disease  at ___ and sent home with percocet & instruction to  follow up with a surgeon there. She was unable to make that  appointment. Since that time, her pain had initially resolved,  but has now returned, worse since the evening prior to  admission. She has had some nausea, has not had any diarrhea.  She did have a black bowel movement, but has tried pepto-bismol  for her symptoms. She has not had any true fevers or chills.', 'Past Medical History: HTN, Gerd  Past Surgical History: None    Social History: ___ Family History: Non-contributory', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 137/75 HR: NA O2Sat: 98 Weight: NA  [EXAM] On admission:  Vitals: 98.7 91 137/75 18 100RA GEN: A&O, NAD HEENT: No scleral icterus, mucus membranes moist CV: RRR, No M/G/R PULM: Clear to auscultation b/l, No W/R/R ABD: Soft, nondistended, Tender RUQ no rebound or guarding, no ___ Ext: No ___ edema, ___ warm and well perfused',
