VALUES (
    '22612249', '10335293', '1. Diverticulitis 2. Atrial Fibrillation', 'DIVERTICULITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with diverticular disease.', 'Per Surgical Consult Note in Emergency Department: ___ with known diverticulosis in usual state of health until 1PM today when she had acute onset of sharp, severe ___ abdominal pain in both lower quadrants without radiation. She  had cereal a little earlier and was standing in her kitchen when the pain started. Pain has been constant intensity, unremitting, and is worsened by movement. She has never had something like this before.  Pt denies flatus at baseline. Her last bowel movement was this morning, without melena/hematochezia, and pt has ___ BMs/day at baseline. She endorses subjective fever, chills, malaise. Denies nausea/vomiting, constipation/diarrhea, chest pain, dyspnea, dysuria, hematuria.', 'PMH: Scoliosis, back pain managed by facet injections, nephrolithiasis, HTN, small R occipital hemorrhagic CVA ___,  no residual deficits), IBS. Last colonoscopy in ___ was positive for internal hemorrhoids and diverticulosis. PSH: R knee replacement (___), bladder suspension, TAH.    Social History: Lives in ___, involved daughter', '[VITALS] Temp: 99.0 BP: 128/52 HR: 77 O2Sat: 99 Weight: NA  [EXAM] At admission Per Surgical Consult Note: Vitals: Temp 99.0, HR 77, BP 128/52, RR 16, SaO2 97% on RA  Gen: Thin woman appearing stated age, uncomfortable, AOx3. CV: RRR, nl S1/S2, ___ systolic murmur at RUSB, no R/G. Pulm: CTAB, no W/R/R. Abd: Soft, non-distended, with moderate TTP in the lower quadrants bilaterally, most severe at the midline, with  voluntary guarding. No rebound. Extrem: WWP, no C/C/E. Neuro: Grossly intact.',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


