VALUES (
    '24862340', '10373195', 'Acute Appendicitis', 'APPENDICITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute appendicitis.', 'The pt is a ___ F who was in her usual state of health and on vacation from ___ when on ___ she began to experience  diffuse dull periumbilical discomfort and bloating. She reports "not feeling right" and experiencing constipation, which she  attempted to alleviate with a suppository and laxative, producing a small amount of watery stool she considered abnormal. She denies any dietary changes, chills, diarrhea, hematochezia, urinary symptoms, or vaginal discharge. She reports her menses to be normal experiencing her last menstrual period on ___.  This diffuse dull pain gradually worsened until the afternoon of ___, when it converted to a sharp focal pain in her RLQ characterized as an ___ on a 10 point scale. She denies experiencing this type of pain previously and describes it as "unbearable" and causing her to "double over." She experienced nausea and has been unable to eat since breakfast on ___. She vomited 2x during the afternoon of ___ and was brought to the ED by her parents and husband. Upon presentation she reports a low-grade fever and nausea but denies chills,  vomiting, or diarrhea. She currently reports RLQ discomfort but denies pain, which she attributes to analgesics adminstered in the ED.', 'Seasonal Allergies', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 128/86 HR: NA O2Sat: 99 Weight: NA  [EXAM] PE on presentation:  99.4  114  128/86  16  100 on RA GEN: NAD, A&Ox3, well-appearing HEENT: NCAT, PERRLA, sclera anicteric Cardiac: RRR, no m/r/g Pulm: CTA b/l Abdominal: Abdomen soft, non-distended. No hepatosplenomegaly. RLQ tenderness upon light palpation. Maximal tenderness approx. ___ from ASIS to umbilicus. Diffuse rebound tenderness is noted. No guarding. Obturator sign is negative. Rovsing''s sign and  Psoas sign both positive. Extremities: distal pulses palpable',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
