VALUES (
    '20852444', '10429123', 'Acute appendicitis', 'APPENDICITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute appendicitis.', 'Mr. ___ is a ___ year old man with no significant past medical history who was previously healthy until 2 months ago, when he developed sharp, RLQ abdominal pain. The pain began in the RLQ and sometimes radiated to the LLQ. The pain was intermittent in nature, coming in waves lasting ___ hours and then abating for ___ hours. The pain occurred for about a week  at a time, and then did not occur for ___ days. His most recent episode of pain started 5 days ago and was similar to his previous episodes. It was ___ in intensity. He also reports nausea and one episode of NBNB emesis 2 days prior to presentation. He has been able to eat and drink. He has been passing flatus and having normal bowel movements. He denies fevers, chills, and changes in bowel or bladder habits.', 'PMH: GERD in ___, treated with omeprazole BRBPR-- colonoscopy at OS___ revealed anal fissure  PSH: ankle repair    Social History: ___ Family History: Father with CAD Mother living and healthy Maternal aunt with breast cancer No fam hx of colon cancer, Crohn''s, or UC', '[VITALS] Temp: 97.0 BP: 122/67 HR: 63 O2Sat: 97 Weight: NA  [EXAM] Temp 97.0   HR 63   BP 122/67   RR 16   O2 sat 100%/RA Gen: young man, NAD, sitting comfortably Pulm: CTAB Cor: RRR, nl S1 S2, no m/g Abd: soft, tender to palpation in RLQ. No rebound/guarding. Neg Rovsings, Psoas, and obturator signs.',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


