VALUES (
    '20073240', '10441211', 'Acute cholecystitis', 'CHOLECYSTITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via eu observation for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute gallbladder disease.', 'Mr. ___ is a ___ year old male with a history of LFT  abnormalitis, gallstones, HTN, and H. pylori (treated twice) who  presents with 1 day of epigastric pain, nausea, and vomiting.   He has had about ___ of these episodes over the past 6 months  that normally last about an hour.  Three 3 days ago, he ate  lobster and pie, had an attach he attributes to the gallbladder,  and the pain subsided.  Last night around 9 pm after eating rice  cake pudding, he got another attack and the symptoms did not  subside as usual but persisted and continue now. His pain is  epigastric with radiation to the LUQ that he describes as about  ___.  He has had 2 episodes of vomiting, non-bloody but  bilious. He endorses fevers/chills at home.  No diarrhea.  Last  bowel movement around noon was well-formed.  He has been seen by Dr. ___ in hepatology and Dr. ___ in  surgery.  His periodic elevations in LFTs have been attributed  to transient obstruction from passing gallstones, given a  negative viral workup with negative autoimmune and genetic  workup.  Dr. ___ has also recommended a laparoscopic  cholecystectomy with intraop cholangiography and liver biopsy.', 'PMH: 1. LFT abnormalities 2. Cholethiasis 3. HTN 4. Persistent hypokalemia 5. H. pyloria (treated x2)  PSH: None    Social History: ___ Family History: Father has renal failure, IgA nephropathy, HTN, colon cancer, thyroid cancer, CAD.  Mother has HTN.', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 136/87 HR: NA O2Sat: 97 Weight: NA  [EXAM] 97.9F 86 136/87 18 100%RA Gen - NAD, resting comfortably in bed HEENT - MMM, PERRL CV - RRR, nml S1/S2, no M/R/G Resp - CTAB, no W/R/R Abd - S, mild approp TTP over incisions, ND, +BS, no  rebound/guarding Wound - abdominal laparoscopic incisions C/D/I Ext - WWP, no C/C/E Neuro - AAOx3, CN2-12 grossly intact',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
    clinicalcaseid, patientid, title, type,
    description, symptom, medicalhistory, pe,
    status, createdBy
)
VALUES (
    '23248166', '10441330', 'Acute pancreatitis  Nausea/vomiting  Diarrhea  Anemia, iron deficiency  Vitamin B12 deficiency  Crohn''s  Celiac disease', 'PANCREATITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via direct emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute pancreatitis.', '___ year old woman with a h/o ulcerative colitis status post  colectomy ___, prior DVT/PE, celiac sprue, pancreas divisum  admitted with 2 weeks of epigastric pain, nausea and nonbloody,  nonbilious vomiting after p.o., nonbloody diarrhea. She reports  that she had been feeling well after her long admission last  ___ until about ___ weeks ago. She noticed an increase in  her diarrhea and nausea. Then over the past 10 days, she has had  worsening abdominal pain as well as intermittent nausea and  vomiting. She describes the pain as dull but intense and  constant, midepigastric, occasionally radiates to the back.  Sometimes better with sitting forward. Notes that nausea and vomiting progressively worse over the past  ___ weeks. Sometimes as delayed as an hour after eating, but  that is more common when has taken an antiemetic before hand.  poor appetite. Had gained some weight since her last admit  130-->147, but weight up and down recently given decreased po  intake. As for diarrhea, her baseline since her colectomy is ___ bms/d,  incl 3 at nighttime. More recently, having diarrhea q 1 hour.  non bloody. worse after eating, sometimes stools float.  Eating ice chips "all the time". Has also had shortness of breath, mostly with exertion. Feels  palpitations if goes up the stairs. Similar sensation to prior  anemia. Has not noticed leg swelling. No fevers or chills,no cough, no dysuria. No sick contacts.  pt here with abd pain x 2 weeks with n/v/d and dec appetite. no  f/c/sick contacts. also has had some intermittent DOE the past  two weeks, speaking full sentences now. no calf pain/swelling.  otherwise well.  Vitals in ED: 98.0 73 128/58 98% Given zofran, morphine, IV fluids in ED.', '- Ulcerative colitis dx''d ___ status post colectomy ___ with  reattachment with J-pouch ileostomy (all occurred at ___ - has  chronic diarrhea - Celiac sprue - dx''d ___ in setting of chronic worsening  diarrhea - H/o C diff picked up in ___ over the ___, no exposure to  healthcare settings - H/o elevated lipase and amylase in assoc with abd pain  (hospitalized in ___ - Bilateral AVN of hips on CT not on XR ___, denies h/o  osteoporosis - History of DVT and pulmonary embolism in ___, s/p ___ year  anticoagulation, seen by hematologist who did not feel that she  needed lifelong anticoagulation - Pancreatic divisum seen on ___ MR enterography and MRCP ___   Social History: ___ Family History: Malignant melanoma both parents. No family history of GI  illnesses.', '[VITALS] Temp: 98.5 BP: 105/61 HR: NA O2Sat: 98 Weight: NA  [EXAM] T 98.5 p 70 r 18 bp 105/61 99% on RA Gen in NAD, pleasant, somewhat pale appearing HEENT o/p clear, mm somewhat dry Neck supple, no ___ CTA bilaterally, end expiratory wheeze in left base CV RRR no murmurs/rubs/gallops Abd soft not distended, + significant pain to palpation in  epigastric area, no rebound, no HSM. active bowel sounds Ext no edema 2+ pulses Neuro alert and oriented, grossly non-focal',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
    clinicalcaseid, patientid, title, type,
    description, symptom, medicalhistory, pe,
    status, createdBy
)
VALUES (
    '22470405', '10448910', 'PRIMARY: ============== Pancreatitis, gallstone Acute blood stream infection  SECONDARY: ============= Non-ST-Segment Elevation Myocardial Infarction Transaminitis Hypokalemia Acute kidney injury Anemia Hypertension Hyperlipidemia', 'OTHER_ABDOMINAL',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with abdominal pathology.', '___ ___ man with HTN and HLD who presents  with nausea and vomiting x 2 days. He reports that 2 days ago he  and his family ate at a restaurant, and that evening he  developed lower abdominal cramping accompanied by severe chills.  Patient reports that he soaked through multiple sheets that  evening. The following morning he begun to have nausea and  vomiting, with persistent rigors. He therefore came to the ED,  and in triage had an episode of bilious emesis. No CP or SOB. No  orthopnea or PND. He has no subjective fevers, no urinary  symptoms. No cough or hemoptysis. No recent sick contacts though  he lives at a senior home.   In the ED, initial vital signs were: T 98, HR 109, BP 160/81, RR  18, SaO2 95% RA. Rectal temp 101. Tmax 101.8, HR 93, BP 108/57  RR 20 SaO2 95% on RA. - Exam notable for:  dry lips, lightheadness when sitting up.  - Labs were notable for WBC 11.9, H/H 15.2/44.1, ALT/AST 55/54,  Amylase 424, Lipase 487, Tbili 1.1. Lactate 3.4 10:40 AM > 2.8  11:32 AM. Potassium 2.8. BUN/Cr ___. blood cx pending. - Studies performed include CXR c/f LLL pneumonia.  CT abdomen  w/contrast showed no acute intra-abdominal process. The pancreas  is normal in attenuation and there is no peripancreatic fat  stranding or pancreatic ductal dilatation. - Patient was given CTX 1gm IV Q24H x1/azithromycin 500mg x1, 3L  NS IVF, K repletion with KCl 60mEq, MgSO4 2gm IV x 1, Tylenol  ___ mg PR x1. - Vitals on transfer: T 98, HR 82, BP 106/60, RR 16, SaO2 95% on  RA  Upon arrival to the floor, the patient hemodynamically stable,  reports ___ headache.    ROS: 10-point ROS NEGATIVE except as noted above in HPI', 'Hypertension Hyperlipidemia    Social History: ___ Family History: Denies any significant FH.', '[VITALS] Temp: 97.8 BP: 106/57 HR: 77 O2Sat: 97 Weight: NA  [EXAM] ON ADMISSION: ====================== Vitals: T 97.8, BP 106/57, HR 77, RR 16, SaO2 96% on RA GENERAL: Resting comfortably, in no acute distress. HEENT: NC/AT. Neck supple, JVD flat. No carotid bruits. PULM: CTAB, no wheezes. CARDIAC: RRR, normal S1/S2, III/VI SEM @ LUSB radiating to the  carotids.  ABD: Soft, nontender, nondistended, bowel sounds hypoactive. No  rebound or guarding. EXT: WWP, no c/c/e. NEUROLOGIC: A&Ox3. CNII-XII grossly intact. ___ strength  througout.  Normal sensation.',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


