VALUES (
    '23352202', '10456934', 'Acute appendicitis', 'APPENDICITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute appendicitis.', '___ yo M presenting to the ED from his PCP''s office for acute  onset RLQ pain and fevers.  Pt reports feeling ''gassy'' the day  prior to admission with RLQ pain starting around 10:30AM.  He describes the pain as sharp, focal  and non-radiating.  The pain is constant and prevents him from  sleeping. He has also been experiencing mild nausea,  constipation, distension, and fevers to 104 (at home. He denies  any similar prior episodes, sick contacts, dysuria, diarrhea or  emesis.', 'GERD, gout (podagra), L knee arthroscopy & partial medial meniscectomy   Social History: ___ Family History: noncontributory', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: NA HR: NA O2Sat: NA Weight: NA  [EXAM] Physical exam on admission.  Vital Signs:  Afebrile. General:  Not in acute distress. Extremities:  No edema. Skin:  The skin over the first MTP joint is dark colored.there  is eczematous rash over hte L elbow.  Musculoskeletal:  There is no more synovitis with no more increased warmth or tenderness.  NO more bursitis  Movement of the first MTP joint does cause no more pain Neurologic:  Nonfocal.  Physical exam at the time of dicharge NAD, AOx3, comfortable RRR, chest CTAB Abd soft, minimally distended, no rebound or guarding.  Appropriately tender at portsites otherwise nonfocal and  minimally tender. Wounds are clean, dry and intact.',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


