VALUES (
    '28721835', '10469621', '1. Acute cholecystitis with possible Mirizzi syndrome, with  gangrenous cholecystitis 2. Acute kidney injury 3. Post op ileus', 'CHOLECYSTITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute gallbladder disease.', '___ with severe Pulm HTN, Dm, PVD,  on Coumadin for CVA with INR 5 presents with diffuse abdominal pain most prominent in RUQ since ___.  Patient states that pain has been severe and abruptly began ___ day, not precipitated by any event.  Pain at worst in ___ now ___ accompanied with nausea, intromittant nausea, and inability to take PO.  She has had low grade fever  99 but no chills.  + diarrhea per baseline, + flatus, No jaundice, lite colored stools or dark urine noted.  On presentation to the ED she was hypotensive in the ___ systolic with improvement to 110s with 2 L of fluid.  She has never had similar pain in the past.', '-HTN   -Hyperlipidemia (HDL ___ and LDL ___ on simvastatin 40) -Heavy chronic smoking history -Type II Diabetes (recent A1cs are in good range 6-7% on home  metformin monotherapy after weight loss of 40lbs last year) -Chronic left great toenail fungus/removal nail bed ___  -s/p toe amputation ___ (necrotic), c/b popliteal DVT (was Tx  with Warfarin A/C until suffering a LGIB (Hgb 5) in ___, polyps  removed, Hgb stable at ___ since ___ -Appendectomy   -Tonsillectomy    Social History: ___ Family History: One sister, age ___, with diabetes. One brother with diabetes.', '[VITALS] Temp: 99.5 BP: 87/38 HR: 78 O2Sat: 99 Weight: NA  [EXAM] Temp 99.5   HR 78   BP 87/38   RR 16   O2 sat 98% RA GEN: NAD, A&Ox3, no jaundice or scleral icterus ___: RRR no m/r/g Pulm: clear but decreased throughout precordium Abd: Firmness to RUQ with diffusely tender abdomen, no rebound but mild voluntary guarding. Ext: WWP, No cyanosis or edema.',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


