VALUES (
    '29565262', '10522176', 'Acute cholecystitis', 'CHOLECYSTITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute gallbladder disease.', 'Mrs. ___ is a ___ year old female with history of obesity  who presents with RUQ and epigastric pain starting at 3am on the  morning of admission.  She reports that she went out to dinner the previous evening and  went to bed at 11pm. She then woke up around 3am on day of  admission with ___ cramping pain located in the RUQ and  epigastric region. She reports NBNB emesis x 10 and multiple BM  with normal consistency of stool. The pain improved at 7am after  multiple episodes of emesis and she went back to sleep. She woke  up at 11 am and after talking to her sister decided to come in  to the ED for evaluation. She denies fever, anorexia, jaundice, flank pain,  and dysuria.  She reports having a similar episode 3 weeks ago with RUQ and  epigastric pain but no vomiting that self-resolved.', 'PMH:  Obesity HTN GERD Depression Hypothyroidism Headaches Vertigo  PSH: Back surgery in ___ Denies any previous abdominal surgeries.    Social History: ___ Family History: Non-contributory', '[VITALS] Temp: 98.3 BP: 138/80 HR: 84 O2Sat: 98 Weight: NA  [EXAM] On admission:  Vitals: temp 98.3  BP 138/80  HR 84  RR 18  SaO2 100%RA General: Obese female in NAD. A&O x3 HEENT: MMM. Anicteric sclera. Heart: RRR. Normal S1 and S2. Lungs: CTAB Abdomen: Soft, non distended with minimum RUQ and epigastrium tenderness. +BS. NO guarding or rebound. Back: No CVA tenderness.',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


