VALUES (
    '20009581', '10681550', 'Acute Diverticulitis', 'DIVERTICULITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with diverticular disease.', 'Ms. ___ is a ___ woman with a history of asymptomatic MS  who presents with 3 days of worsening lower abdominal pain. The  pain began without any precipitating events 3 days ago and was  an achy ___ pain in her lower abdomen bilaterally. Two days ago  the pain was intermittently worse with spikes to ___ pain that  occured about every ___ minutes. The pain became more constant, and localized to her left lower abdomen. The pain is  alleviated when she bends her legs and is worse with walking and  sudden movements. She denies nausea/vomiting amd tolerates soups  and liquids. She does acknowledge decrease in her apetite. She  denies diarrrhea, hematochezia, or melena. Her last bowel movement was 2 days ago, though she has continued to pass  gas even today. She did take her temperature at home and has had  intermittent fevers to 100.6 with associated headaches.  Last colonoscopy ___ years ago, and it was negative for  pre-malignant polyps or divurticulosis.  She went to see her PCP the morning prior to admission because  the pain was so severe, and her PCP recommended she come to the  ED.', '-MS: Diagnosed by MRI ___ after some neurologic symptoms; asymptomatic since then with no current medications. -Hospitalized for meningitis ___ years ago -Chronic iron deficiency anemia  PSH:  -Cholecystectomy, ___ -Cesaerian section x1, ___ -Tonsillectomy, age ___    Social History: ___ Family History: -Brother with pancreatic cancer at age ___ -Daughter with diverticular disease', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: NA HR: NA O2Sat: NA Weight: NA  [EXAM] VS: AVSS GEN: AA&O x 3, NAD, calm, cooperative. HEENT: (-)LAD, mucous membranes moist, trachea midline, EOMI,  PERRL. CHEST: Clear to auscultation bilaterally, (-) cyanosis. ABDOMEN: (+/-) BS x 4 quadrants, soft, Non tender to palpation,  non-distended. EXTREMITIES: Warm, well perfused, pulses  palpable, (+/-) edema.',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


