VALUES (
    '24493759', '10689830', 'gallstone pancreatitis, cholangitis', 'OTHER_ABDOMINAL',
    'A patient was admitted via observation admit for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with abdominal pathology.', 'Mr. ___ is a ___ year old gentleman with history of recurrent  DVT due to FVL on Coumadin, PUD s/p partial gastrectomy 1960s,  prior c diff colitis, cholecystitis s/p PTC on ___ (removed  ___, alpha thalassemia, MGUS and possible ITP, congenital  blindness who presented to ___ ED for nausea and vomiting.  This started abruptly without prodrome at 2PM on ___. He also  had accompanying abdominal pain in RUQ, RLQ, and radiating to  right flank distribution, somewhat dull alternating with sharp  pain. It is more intense but similar characteristics to pain he  had with cholecystitis in ___ last month. He is blind and  cannot see if there was blood in the vomit or bile. He vomited  10 times. He does feel some alleviation in nausea and pain since  arrival to ED. He has no associated fever, SOB, dysuria.   In ___ he had cholecystitis with pneumobilia; he had  studies performed including MRCP and cholangiogram that  confirmed the dx but did not have any fistulas found. He had PTC  placed ___, removed as outpt on ___. He said he wasn''t sure  but there wasn''t a plan for cholecystectomy as outpt since  discharge.  In the ED: lipase 2676, ALT 276, AST 435, TBili 2.2 (which was  1.0 on discharge last month). Lactate 1.0.   Had 100.3F but no subjective fever.  Abdominal US showed steatosis with "distended gallbladder  containing multiple small gallstones. The distal CBD is not  visualized but not dilated." ERCP team was contacted and there  is plan for ERCP.', 'recurrent DVT due to FVL on Coumadin prior c diff colitis  cholecystitis s/p PTC on ___ (removed ___ alpha thalassemia,  MGUS possible ITP BPH s/p TURP congenital blindness HTN HLD  PAST SURGICAL HISTORY: Bilateral carpal tunnel syndrome s/p CTR ___ Long history of venostasis ulcers since early ___ with history of skin grafting. Peptic ulcer disease status post partial gastrectomy in ___. History of appendectomy. Eye surgeries as a newborn.    Social History: ___ Family History: Mother had diabetes, obesity', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: NA HR: 120 O2Sat: NA Weight: NA  [EXAM] Vitals: AVSS, see flowsheets  GEN: A&O, NAD, pleasant, conversant  HEENT: No scleral icterus, mucus membranes moist    CV: RRR   PULM: Clear to auscultation b/l, no increased work of breathing  ABD: Obese, abdomen soft, minimally tender near incision with  staples, c/d with 4 cm area open and packed with wet-to-dry  gauze    Ext: No ___ edema, ___ warm and well perfused',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


