    status, createdBy
)
VALUES (
    '25053495', '10707726', 'Acute appendicitis', 'APPENDICITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via observation admit for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute appendicitis.', 'Patient is a ___ y/o M  with a history of SBO, bowel resection in ___ in childhood and ileostomy reversal in the  ___ in ___ presenting with right lower quadrant abdominal pain. He reports the pain started 4 days ago. He states the pain started as cramping pain diffusely through his abdomen. He denies  fevers, chills, nausea, vomiting, diarrhea. He reports he last passed flatus in the ED but his last bowel movement was 3 days ago. Because of the aforementioned symptoms, the patient presented to the emergency department.', 'Past Medical History: SBO, hospitalized in ___ in ___  ________________________________________________________________ Past Surgical History: Bowel Surgery - unknown, done in ___ in Childhood  Colostomy reversal in ___    Social History: ___ Family History: noncontributory', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 122/88 HR: 88 O2Sat: NA Weight: NA  [EXAM] Admission  Vitals: T 28.3,  HR 88, BP 122/88, RR 19, SaO2 100% RA  GEN: Alert and oriented, no acute distress, conversant and interactive. HEENT: Sclerae anicteric, mucous membranes moist, oropharynx is clear. CV: Regular rate and rhythm, no audible murmurs. PULM/CHEST: Clear to auscultation bilaterally, respirations are unlabored on room air. ABD: Soft, distended, tender in the R mid abdominal and RLQ region, no rebound or guarding.  Ext: No lower extremity edema, distal extremities warm and well-perfused.',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


