    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute pancreatitis.', 'Pt is a ___ y.o male with h.o OSA, ETOH abuse, HTN, HL, obesity,  RLS, UGIB who presented to the ED with abdominal pain. Pt  reports onset of pain after eating dinner ~5pm last night.  Reports pain is dull with sharp components starts RUQ and  radiates all over the abdomen. He never had this before. He  reports n/v non bloody. He reports last BM yesterday, denies  melena, brbpr, dysuria, CP, sob, fever, chills.  Drinks 1 bottle  of wine + daily. Last drink ___ evening. +h.o withdrawal. . ___ the ED, pt was noted to be hypertensive. He was given PO  labetalol, Zofran, IVF, and pain medications. He was given PO  labetalol.  . 10 pt ROS reviewed and otherwise negative for headache,  dizziness, CP, sob, cough, dysuria, paresthesias, weakness. He  reports chronic paresthesias, and chronic LBP', '- Obstructive sleep apnea on CPAP - Alcohol abuse - Hypertension - Hyperlipidemia - Obesity - Gout  - Restless leg syndrome   - Diverticulitis - UGIB secondary to NSAIDs ___  - RLE foot drop secondary lumbar radiculopathy - S/P right carotid endarterectomy for amaurosis fugax OD ___ - S/P L3-4/L4-5 lumbar laminectomy/discectomy ___  - S/P right hallux fracture, osteomyelitis, amputation ___. -ETOH abuse hip replacement R. CEA after TIA   Social History: ___ Family History: Suspected MI ___ dad ___ his ___, prostate ca   mom with thyroid problems brother with DM', '[VITALS] Temp: 97.8 BP: 203/127 HR: 93 O2Sat: 97 Weight: NA  [EXAM] ADMISSION PHYSICAL EXAM GEN: sleepy appearing, NAD vitals:T 97.8 BP 203/127 HR 93 RR 20 sat 94% on RA HEENT: ncat eomi anicteric MMM neck: supple chest: b/l ae no w/c/r heart: s1s2 rr no m/r/g abd: +bs, +TTP diffusely worse RUQ/epigastric area, no guarding  or rebound ext: no c/c chronic venous stasis changes, chronic ___ edema 2+  b/l, R.greater toe s/p amputation  neuro: face symmetric, speech fluent psych: calm, cooperative',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


