VALUES (
    '21061497', '10822797', 'Acute pancreatitis Duodenal diverticulum Abdominal pain', 'PANCREATITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute pancreatitis.', '___ with obesity and htn presents to ED for evaluation of 1 hour  epigastric pain with radiation to the back associated with  diaphoresis, nausea,dry heaves. Described the pain as initially  sharp, but now has residual dull sensation in epigastrium and  over xiphoid process. She reports similar symptoms 1 week ago  that resolved spontaneously. No recent illness, no fever. Pain  seemed to be triggered by eating. ___ pain which took her  breath away. + diaphoresis. She tried to make herself throw up  without success. She had some constipation earlier during the  week of admission which resolved with OTC stool softners.    In ER: (Triage Vitals: ___, 77, /146/67, 22 ,97% RA )  Meds Given: None Fluids given: 1 L NS Radiology Studies:RUQ US consults called: none  REVIEW OF SYSTEMS:  CONSTITUTIONAL:  No fevers/chills/weight loss  HEENT:  [X] All normal  RESPIRATORY:  [X] All normal except for sob when pain was  intense  CARDIAC:  [X] All normal  GI:  As per HPI  GU:  [X] All normal  SKIN:  [X] All normal  MUSCULOSKELETAL:  [+] chronic arthritis but no new msk sx  NEURO:  [X] All normal  ENDOCRINE:  [X] All normal  HEME/LYMPH:  [X]  All normal  PSYCH:  [X] All normal All other systems negative except as noted above', 'PAST MEDICAL HISTORY:   Minor thalassemia, arthritis, obesity, and depression.  PAST SURGICAL HISTORY:   Gastric bypass surgery, abdominoplasty, left total knee  replacement, knee arthroscopy, and bladder mesh.    Social History: ___ Family History: Father with brain cancer and he died in his ___,  thalassemia, and arthritis.', '[VITALS] Temp: 99.1 BP: 123/60 HR: NA O2Sat: 99 Weight: NA  [EXAM] Admission exam:  Vitals:  T 99.1  P 85  BP 123/60  RR 18  SaO2 97% on RA   GEN: Obese, very pleasant female NAD, comfortable appearing    HEENT: ncat anicteric MMM    NECK:  supple  CV: s1s2 rr early peaking SEM at LUSB   RESP: b/l ae no w/c/r    ABD: +bs, soft, mild epigastric tendernesss, ND, no guarding or  rebound    EXTR:no c/c/e 2+pulses    DERM: no rash    NEURO: face symmetric speech fluent    PSYCH: calm, cooperative',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


