    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with diverticular disease.', 'Ms. ___ is a ___ year old ___ woman with a  history of infectious colitis and diverticulosis who presents  with severe, left-sided abdominal pain. The patient reports that  she began experiencing the abdominal pain 2 months ago, but that  the pain has become acutely worse in the past two days. Two  months ago, she saw her doctor and was given antibiotics for for  infection in her colon which helped the pain to resolve. The  pain returned yesterday in the same location and feels the same  as her most recent episode.  She rates the pain a ___ in  severity. ___ denies nausea or vomiting, fevers, sweats.  Patient reports having chills last night. She reports having ___  nonbloody stools yesterday with her last being bowel movement  being today. Ms. ___ has had a good appetite and last ate  yesterday in the mid-afternoon.  Her last colonoscopy on ___  showed severe diverticulosis, and she was scheduled for a one  year follow-up colonoscopy this ___ (due to poor bowel prep).   Patient reports increased urinary frequency but denies dysuria,  hematuria. She denies chest pain, SOB, lightheadedness.', 'Chronic low back pain- degenerative lumbar spondylosis Thyroid nodule Depression    Social History: ___ Family History: No family history of GI problems. Sister has a thyroid condition  but she is not certain of the details.  Sister had lung cancer.   Mother with cardiovascular disease.  Diabetes mellitus in 3  sisters and mother.', '[VITALS] Temp: 98.0 BP: 120/56 HR: 57 O2Sat: 98 Weight: NA  [EXAM] Vital Signs: T 98 BP 100-120/56-70 HR 57-63 RR 20 SaO2 96% RA General: Pleasant, middle-aged lady.  Alert, oriented, no acute  distress   HEENT: Sclera anicteric, MMM, oropharynx clear   Neck: supple, JVP not elevated, no LAD   Lungs: Clear to auscultation bilaterally, no wheezes, rales,  ronchi   CV: Regular rate and rhythm, normal S1 + S2, no murmurs, rubs,  gallops   Abdomen: soft, non-distended, tender to palpation in LLQ and  LUQ, bowel sounds present, no rebound tenderness or guarding, no  organomegaly   Ext: Warm, well perfused, 2+ pulses, no clubbing, cyanosis or  edema',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


