VALUES (
    '24318512', '10905906', 'PRIMARY: Acute pancreatitis SECONDARY: Chronic kidney disease, gout, hypertension, GERD,  hyperlipidemia', 'PANCREATITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via observation admit for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute pancreatitis.', 'Per admitting hospitalist:    Mr. ___ is a ___ ___ speaking male with PMH of gastric ulcer presents today for abdominal pain. He began having epigastric abdominal pain this AM while watching TV. Pain is epigastric, non radiating, and dull achy in nature with pain level ___. Eating worsens the pain but no alleviating factor. These symptoms are similar to his previous when he had his gastric ulcer. He denies any diarrhea or constipation, chest  pain or SOB. No sick contact. He did start amoxicillin x 4 days previously. Otherwise, no changes in diet or alcohol or raw food consumption.   ROS: Pertinent positives and negatives as noted in the HPI.  All other systems were reviewed and are negative.   The day following admission, the patient added additional  history that he was told he had a gastric ulcer in the past  after presenting with bleeding, not abdominal pain.  He tells me  he has never been diagnosed with H pylori.  He has never had any  symptoms like this before.  He has not recently started any  medications.  He does not recall being told about ever having  had a low blood count, CKD or diagnosis of CHF before.', '- CKD (baseline Cr 1.5) - Gout - BPH - HTN - Gastric Ulcer - HLD - Anemia (baseline hgb ___   Social History: ___ Family History: No family history of pancreatic disease', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: NA HR: NA O2Sat: NA Weight: NA  [EXAM] ADMISSION: ==========  VITALS: Afebrile and vital signs stable (see eFlowsheet) GENERAL: Alert and in mild discomfort EYES: Anicteric, pupils equally round ENT: Ears and nose without visible erythema, masses, or trauma.  Oropharynx without visible lesion, erythema or exudate CV: Heart regular, no murmur, no S3, no S4.  No JVD. RESP: Lungs clear to auscultation with good air movement bilaterally.  Breathing is non-labored GI: Abdomen soft, non-distended, epigastric tender to palpation with some guarding.  Bowel sounds present. No rebound rigidity. GU: No suprapubic fullness or tenderness to palpation MSK: Neck supple, moves all extremities, strength grossly full and symmetric bilaterally in all limbs SKIN: No rashes or ulcerations noted NEURO: Alert, oriented, face symmetric, gaze conjugate with  EOMI, speech fluent, moves all limbs, sensation to light touch grossly intact throughout PSYCH: pleasant, appropriate affect',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


