    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute gallbladder disease.', 'This is a ___ y/o female with a history notable for recurrent  cholelithiasis who now presents with RUQ abd pain x ___ days.   Pain is described as sharp, worse with food, and constant.  No  f/c/s.  +nausea, vomiting, decreased po intake. She notes that  she experiences these symptoms every few years, so it is not  frequent, and is typically exacerbated by ___ food or clam  chowder.  Symptoms typically last for ___ days.  She has been  told to see surgery previously for consideration of a CCY but  has not done so yet.  This time, the episode lasted much longer  and was more intense, with severe pain occuring everytime she  ate and with dull pain in the RUQ -> right shoulder blade during  times of rest.  No urinary symptoms, no changes in her bowels,  no bleeding.  Of note, has lost 50-lbs in the last 6 months  intentionally.   . In the ED, initial VS 99.0, rest stable.  Labs notable for  marked transaminitis with normal tbili and slightly elevated Alk  Phos.  She was sent directly to ERCP from the ED.  She underwent  a sphincterotomy with extraction of slight sludge.  Stones were  noted in the GB, but no evidence of obstruction.  Received  ___ ciprofloxacin and dilaudid x 1. She is now being  admitted to Medicine. . Currently, the patient c/o ___ RUQ pain.  No nausea at this  time.  12-pt ROS otherwise negative in detail except for as  noted above.', 'Cholelithiasis s/p knee surgery   Social History: ___ Family History: Mother - HTN ___ - CAD', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 141/81 HR: 52 O2Sat: 98 Weight: NA  [EXAM] VS: Tc 98.1, BP 141/81, HR 52, RR 16, SaO2 98/RA General: Well-appearing female in NAD, but somewhat  uncomfortable, AO x 3 HEENT: NC/AT, PERRL, EOMI. Anicteric sclerae, MM dry, OP clear Neck: supple, no LAD Chest: CTA-B, no w/r/r CV: RRR s1 s2 normal, no m/g/r Abd: soft, ND, minimal TTP in the RUQ, negative ___ sign,  NABS Ext: no c/c/e',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


