    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute pancreatitis.', '___ yo woman h/o highly functioning autism, anxiety, obesity s/p  gastric bypass ___, seizure admitted with severe abd pain.   Patient at baseline is functional, living at home with son  (autism/aspergers).  Has had lost ~100 lbs since the gastric  bypass and nearly 50 lbs reportedly over the past 2 months.   Describes having significant reduction in PO appetite.    Last night at 2 AM, awoke with severe abd pain - epigastric  region.  Initially located in the back and then went forward to  the front.  Denies significant nausea, significant loss of  appetite, fever, jaundice, chills. Called EMS to be brought in the hospital for further mgmt.     In the ER, VS stable, lipase elevated to 1600.  Given 50 mcg  fentanyl and zofran with significant relief.  Abd CT prelim read  showed mildly distended GB, otherwise no other abnl.  Pain at  ___ presently.', '- ADHD, Asperger - Anxiety disorder -psoraic arthritis - PCO -seasonal allergies -asthma -epilepsy, starting at age ___ (petit mal), had temporal seizures,  last seizure was at age ___, no longer on AED''s - obesity s/p gastric bypass surgery in ___ - breast reduction ___ c/b blood loss anemia   Social History: ___ Family History: son has ADHD, ?PDD. brother who has bipolar and history of substance abuse.', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 120/70 HR: NA O2Sat: 97 Weight: NA  [EXAM] VS 97.5  120/70  75  20  100% RA Gen: pleasant lying in bed NAD, responsive and appropriate HEENT: PERRLA, EOMI, OP dry/clear, neck supple, sclera anicteric Heart: RRR, no m/r/g Lung: CTA, no r/r/w Abd: soft, mod tender in the epigastric, LUQ area, + BS, skin  stretch marks Ext: occ ecchymoses, no c/c/e Neuro: non focal Psychiatric: appropriate.',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


