    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute appendicitis.', '___ moderately obese female, presents for diffuse abdominal pain  since late yesterday evening. By this morning her pain had  migrated to her RLQ. She denied any nausea/ emesis/ subjective  fevers or urinary sxs. This the first time she has experienced  these sxs, her pain has been continuous since this am. Positive anorexia, last meal 18 hrs ago. LMP 1 week ago. Of note she c/o  constipation x ___ days.', 'PMH: None  PSH: None   Social History: ___ Family History: Non-contributory', '[VITALS] Temp: 99.4 BP: 134/84 HR: 93 O2Sat: 99 Weight: NA  [EXAM] On admission: Vitals:  temp 99.4 Hr: 93 BP:134/84 18  sat:100%RA GEN: A&O, NAD HEENT: No scleral icterus, mucus membranes moist CV: RRR, No M/G/R PULM: Clear to auscultation b/l, No W/R/R ABD: Soft, nondistended, + Mc ___, neg Rovsing sign. Ext: No ___ edema, ___ warm and well perfused',
