VALUES (
    '25633498', '10965294', 'Acute cholecystitis', 'CHOLECYSTITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute gallbladder disease.', 'This is a ___ gentlemanwith a known history of  gallstones who presented to the emergency room with right upper  quadrant pain since about 2 o''clock in the morning.  He says he has had intermittent  abdominal pain for the last several months, and had been in the  emergency room twice with it.  He was trying outpatient pain  medications and diet modifications, and was taking both Dilaudid  and Tramadol.  He did have a plan to have an internal or  outpatient cholecystectomy, but came to the emergency room today  with worsening right upper quadrant pain, diarrhea.  No nausea  or vomiting.  No fevers or chills.  He was seen emergency department.  A right upper quadrant ultrasound demonstrated a 6-mm cystic duct stone, and a normal-caliber common bile duct; but given the patient''s severe pain and persistent nature of symptoms, he was planned for the operating room for laparoscopic cholecystectomy.', 'Symptomatic cholelithiasis   Social History: ___ Family History: Non-contributory.', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: NA HR: 26 O2Sat: NA Weight: NA  [EXAM] On admission:  Resp: 26   Constitutional: Uncomfortable HEENT: Normocephalic, atraumatic Chest: Clear to auscultation Cardiovascular: Regular Rate and Rhythm, Normal first and second heart sounds Abdominal: Very tender in the RUQ with a positive ___ sign Neuro: Speech fluent Psych: Normal mood, Normal mentation',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


