VALUES (
    '26609729', '11012637', 'Primary diagnosis   - Pancreatitis   - ingestion of foreign objects Secondary diagnosis   - smoking   - depression', 'PANCREATITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via eu observation for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute pancreatitis.', '___ hx of COPD, depression with recent eval for SI presents to  ED following swallowing his tooth from his prosthesis and new  onset lower umbilical pain. Pt states he was in his usual state  of health until this morning when, while eating an apple, he  felt the tooth and a supporting piece of metal come off from his  prosthetic and go down his throat. Pt noted he felt some minor  scratching on the way down his esophagus but his pain quickly  subsided. Denies sensation of aspiration/choking, cough,  hemoptysis, or nausea/vomiting. States that several hours went  by during which time he had 4 bouts of loose, watery bowel  movements, the last time during which he noted some blood on his  tissue. Otherwise denies gross BRBPR, melena, or hematochezia.  Of note: pt completed 7 day course of antibiotics one week prior  to evaluation for antecubital abscess developed from IVDA.  States he also developed severe, intermittent, ___ stabbing  hypogastric and umbilical pain not improved with repositioning  or PO intake. This constellation of symptoms made him concerned  and he presented to the ED for evaluation. In ED: VSS - 97.3 90 135/87 18 97% ra. Physical exam by resident  was benign, including abdominal exam, which was not tender to  palpation even with deep palpation while being examined during  auscultation and while talking. Oropharynx was clear, no visible  mucosal damage or blood. Pt was mildly tachycardic but normal  heart sounds otherwise. But by ED attending, patient On the Floor, he continues to complain of RLQ pain that radiates  to RUQ. Reports a few episodes of non-blood watery diarrhea.  Denies recent abx use. REVIEW OF SYSTEMS: Denies fever, chills, night sweats, headache, vision changes,  rhinorrhea, congestion, sore throat, cough, shortness of breath,  chest pain, abdominal pain, nausea, vomiting, diarrhea,  constipation, BRBPR, melena, hematochezia, dysuria, hematuria. All other 10-system review negative in detail.', 'Chronic low back pain recent eval for SI LFT abnormalities   Social History: ___ Family History: Notable for grandfather w/ liver cancer, no hx of alcoholism. Father had DM', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 130/80 HR: NA O2Sat: 98 Weight: NA  [EXAM] ADMISSION LABS VS 98.3 130/80''s 64 16 97% on RA GEN Alert, oriented, no acute distress, lying comfortable in  bed. HEENT NCAT MMM EOMI sclera anicteric, OP clear NECK supple, no JVD, no LAD PULM Good aeration, CTAB no wheezes, rales, ronchi CV RRR normal S1/S2, no mrg ABD soft ND normoactive bowel sounds, no r/g, TTP in RLQ. EXT WWP 2+ pulses palpable bilaterally, no c/c/e NEURO CNs2-12 intact, motor function grossly normal SKIN no ulcers or lesions',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


