VALUES (
    '25348101', '11039753', 'Acuter appendicitis', 'APPENDICITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via eu observation for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute appendicitis.', '___ w hx HTN, anxiety p/w abdominal pain x 2 days. In usual  state of health until day prior to presentation when she  developed epigastric abdominal discomfort. Over the next ___  pain migrated to RLQ. Described as ___ severity, constant,  non-radiating. Worse w movement. No alleviating factors. No  prior episodes of similar pain. Endorses associated chills, anorexia,  nausea and non-bloody emesis. Came to ED for evaluation. Surgery  consult obtained.   On surgery eval, patient relays hx as above. Minimal po intake  since onset of pain. No po intake for greater than 6 hours.  +Flatus/BM. Denies fever, chest pain, shortness of breath,  constipation, diarrhea, blood per rectum, dysuria.', 'PMH: HTN, anxiety/depression, insomnia  PSH: Inguinal hernia repair, exploratory laparoscopy for fertility workup   Social History: ___ Family History: No fam hx GI malignancy of IBD', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 119/72 HR: NA O2Sat: 98 Weight: NA  [EXAM] P/E: VS:  98.9 75  119/72  16  100% RA   GEN: WD, WN in NAD HEENT: NCAT, anicteric CV: RRR PULM: non-labored, no respiratory distress ABD: soft, +tender to palpation in RLQ, negative Rovsings, ND,  no mass PELVIS: deferred EXT: WWP, no CCE NEURO: A&Ox3, no focal neurologic deficits',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
    clinicalcaseid, patientid, title, type,
    description, symptom, medicalhistory, pe,
    status, createdBy
)
VALUES (
    '26157459', '11041085', 'acute cholecystitis', 'CHOLECYSTITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via eu observation for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute gallbladder disease.', 'Mr. ___ is a ___ ___ speaking male with a PMHx significant GERD and H. Pylori and PSHx significant for open appendectomy who presented to the emergency department with burning epigastric pain. He said the pain radiated to his chest. He also endorses emesis, but no nausea. He reports prior episode 2 days ago as well as many episodes in the past, including last episode 2 days ago. Normally he finds relief from omeprazole,  but he did not endorse relief in this circumstance.   He presented to the ED with a similar episode in ___ and at the time as believed to have an exacerbation of GERD.  He endorses that sometimes associated with nausea after eating, but that  this episode was independent of PO.  He also endorses about 10lbs weight loss related to discomfort swallowing.  He denies fever, chills, back pain, diarrhea, constipation, bloody stools or  black stools.  He has a history of H. Pylori, he is unclear if it was treated. He also had an EGD ___ with Dr. ___ at ___ which had a squamous epithelium within normal limits at the GE junction. Gastric mucosa with mild acute and chronic  inflammation and regenerative changes. As well as, antral mucosa with mild chronic inflammation. No bacteria and no ___.  Of note,  his last colonoscopy ___ with a transverse colon and rectal adenoma polyp.', 'Past Medical History: HTN HLD Esophageal Reflux, no ___ in ___ on EGD, medically managed  Past Surgical History: appendectomy     Social History: ___ Family History: Family History: noncontributory', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 128/79 HR: NA O2Sat: 98 Weight: NA  [EXAM] Admission Physical Exam Vitals: 98.6, 79, 128/79, 16, 98% RA GEN: A&O, NAD HEAD: NC/AT EYES: No scleral icterus, mucus membranes moist CV: RRR  PULM: breathing comfortably on room air ABD: Soft, nondistended, tender to palpation in RUQ, + ___, nontender to percussion, no rebound, voluntary guarding RUQ, distractable. well healed scare RLQ Ext: No ___ edema, ___ warm and well perfused Neuro: no gross deficits Psych: appropriate affect',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
    clinicalcaseid, patientid, title, type,
    description, symptom, medicalhistory, pe,
    status, createdBy
)
VALUES (
    '21265715', '11044320', 'Pancreatitis Gallstones Febrile neutropenia Gastroenteritis T cell leukemia with pancytopenia', 'OTHER_ABDOMINAL',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with abdominal pathology.', '___ yo man with history of T cell large grancular lymphcytic  leukemia, here with nausea, vomiting and diarrhea.  He has been  feeling generally well for the past few weeks, after a prolonged  hospitalization in ___ for pseudomonas pneumonia.   . Yesterday, he developed acute onset of nausea, vomiting,  diarrea, multiple episodes. The emesis and diarrhea were non  bloody. He had no associated abdominal pain.  His wife had a  similar syndrome several days prior.  He felt incredibly weak,  and called Dr. ___ then presented to ___ for  evaluation.  There he was found to have a lipase of over 4000,  and bilirubin of 2.6, and was transferred to the ___.  An  ultrasound showed cholelithiasis.  He received cefepime/flagyl  given neutropenia due to his t cell disease.  He had a low grade  fever of 100.1 at ___ and 99.6 in the ED at ___.  His  vital signs on transfer:  afebrile 100/54  18  99% RA. . At the present time, he has had several other episodes of  diarrhea, and has mild RUQ pain as well as diffuse abdominal  tenderness. He has no cough or chest pain, no palpitations, no  recent jaundice or skin changes.  He was recently bitten by his  dog on his left cheek. . ROS was as above, otherwise positive for recent ARF due to  cyclosporine, causing severe leg pain, now resolved.  Insomnia  since starting steroids.  Good appetite and some weight gain  since starting prednisone. Otherwise, 8 other systems reviewed  and negative.', '-T cell large granular lymphocytic leukemia, with neutropenia -Severe pneumonia ___ -BPH -IBS -lactose intolerance - anxiety - chronic neck pain - tonsillectomy, vocal cord polypectomy, pilonidal sinus  excision   Social History: ___ Family History: Unclear on family history as currently estranged from his  family.  Possible history of blood disease.  From OMR:  Father  died of cardiac disease, mother of old age.  No cancer or  respiratory disorders.', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 123/70 HR: 60 O2Sat: 100 Weight: NA  [EXAM] Exam  VS  T max 100.1  T current 97.1   BP  123/70   HR 60 RR  18   97%RA    O2sat   Gen:  In NAD.  Thin man, appears his stated age. HEENT:  PERRL, EOMI.  Slight scleral icterus.  No conjunctival  injection.   Mucous membranes moist.  No oral ulcers. Neck:  Supple, no LAD, no JVP elevation. Lungs: CTA bilaterally, no wheezes, rales, rhonchi.  Normal  respiratory effort. CV:  RRR, soft systolic murmur at USB, rubs, gallops. Abdomen:  soft, no HSM.  Slight tenderness in RUQ to deep  palpation.  Positive bowel sounds throughout.  No rebound or  guarding. Extremities:  warm and well perfused, no cyanosis, clubbing,  edema.  Slight hyperpigmenetation of lower legs. Neurological:  alert and oriented X 3, CN II-XII intact.  Skin:  No rashes or ulcers.  Left cheek at mandible, below left  eye with small excoriation without significant surrounding  erythema. Psychiatric:  Appropriate. GU:  deferred.',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
    clinicalcaseid, patientid, title, type,
    description, symptom, medicalhistory, pe,
    status, createdBy
)
VALUES (
    '21510024', '11052273', 'Diverticulitis', 'DIVERTICULITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with diverticular disease.', '___ year old female with a history of diabetes and hypertension  who presents to the ED with abdominal pain. She started having  pain gradually three days ago. She did not notice a relationship  with food or bowel movements but described the pain as a  persistent ache. She noticed some blood on the toilet paper  after a bowel movement one day prior to admission. Of note she  had a recent admission to BID for lower GI bleed. A colonoscopy  revealed a polyp and severe diverticulosis. The polyp was not  biopsied as the patient was admitted for bleeding. The bleeding  was likely from diverticula that resolved on its own. She has  had no other bleeding since being dischaged aside from blood  noted on toilet paper as above. She reports having chills, but  no recorded fevers. She reports decreaesd appetite. She has not  had any nausea or vomiting. She denies chest pain and shortness  of breath. No edema.   .   In the ED, vitals were stable. She had a guiac positive brown  stool. She was noted to be in sinus tach which resolved with 2L  NS. A CT was consistent with diverticulosis.   .   ROS: Denies fever, cough, shortness of breath, chest  pain,nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, constipation, BRBPR, melena,  hematochezia, dysuria, hematuria.', 'Diabetes Mellitus type II Hypertension   Diverticulosis with recent LGIB Internal hemorrhoids   Social History: ___ Family History: Father died of stroke at ___ years of age.   Mother died of diabetes complications in her ___.', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: normotensive HR: NA O2Sat: NA Weight: NA  [EXAM] Vitals - afebrile, satting well on room air, normotensive  GENERAL: NAD   HEENT: MMM, OP clear   CARDIAC: S1+, S2+, Tachy, No M/R/G   LUNG: CTA b/l   ABDOMEN: Obese, soft, ND, +TTP worse in LLQ, +BS   EXT: No edema   NEURO: AAOx3, CNII-CXII, ___ and motor intact upper and lower  ex. grossly.',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


