VALUES (
    '20743201', '11065944', 'Acute appendicitis', 'APPENDICITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute appendicitis.', 'Mr. ___ is a ___ old man with a history of HLD who presents to the ED with abdominal pain since 10pm the evening prior to presentation. He had his last normal meal at 4PM and developed pain at 10PM, initially in the LUQ, sharp, and eventually migrating to the periumbilical area and  infraumbilical quadrants. Currently his pain in localized mainly in the right lower quadrant. He did endorse nausea and vomiting at home, and has not been able to keep anything down since the pain started. He also took his temperature at home with a high of 100.3, and chills. His last normal bowel movement was yesterday with a glycerin suppository (to which he responded marginally, and he still does feel somewhat backed up), and he continues to pass flatus.   ROS: (+) per HPI (-) Does not endorse night sweats, unexplained weight loss, fatigue/malaise/lethargy, changes in appetite, trouble with sleep, pruritis, jaundice, rashes, bleeding, easy bruising, headache, dizziness, vertigo, syncope, weakness, paresthesias, hematemesis, melena, BRBPR, dysphagia, chest pain, shortness of breath, cough, edema, urinary frequency, urgency', 'HLD    Social History: ___ Family History: HTN, DM, father maybe has heart disease, no cancers', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: NA HR: 103 O2Sat: 55 Weight: NA  [EXAM] Physical Exam on Admission: V/S: Tmax102.7, Tnow98.3, HR103, BP100/55, RR18, Sat95%RA GEN: A&O, NAD HEENT: No scleral icterus, mucus membranes moist CV: RRR, No M/G/R PULM: Clear to auscultation b/l, No W/R/R ABD: Soft, moderately distended, tender to palpation especially  in RLQ with voluntary guarding, no rebound  Ext: No ___ edema, ___ warm and well perfused  Physical Exam',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


