History: Reports all of his family members have died of "old age" around  the age of ___', '[VITALS] Temp: 98.6 BP: 152/90 HR: 99 O2Sat: 98 Weight: NA  [EXAM] ADMISSION  Vitals - T: 98.6 BP: 152/90 HR: 99 RR: 16 02 sat: 97%RA GENERAL: NAD, laying in bed comfortably, speaking full sentences  in ___ HEENT: AT/NC, EOMI, PERRL, anicteric sclera, pink conjunctiva,  MM dry NECK: nontender supple neck, no LAD, no JVD CARDIAC: mild tachycardia, S1/S2, no murmurs, gallops, or rubs LUNG: CTAB, no wheezes, rales, rhonchi, breathing comfortably  without use of accessory muscles ABDOMEN: distended, +BS, nontender in all quadrants, no  rebound/guarding EXTREMITIES: 2+ edema above the ankles, no cyanosis, clubbing,  MAE PULSES: 2+ ___ pulses bilaterally NEURO: CN II-XII intact SKIN: warm and well perfused, no excoriations or lesions, no  rashes',
