VALUES (
    '27108318', '11185210', 'Primary: Acute perforated calculous cholecystitis Klebsiella bacteremia Atrial fibrillation  Secondary:  Glaucoma', 'CHOLECYSTITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute gallbladder disease.', 'HPI: ___ came in today following a fall due to a syncopal  episode. She reports that she felt dizzy, but is unsure if she  lost any conciousness. She has a history of HTN, and had a  medication changed from diltiazem to metoprolol today by her  PCC. She was unable to get up after her fall, and called  lifeline. She currently has no dizziness or any other symptoms.  In her ED work up, an abdominal CT found a distended and  perforated gallbladder. She denies any abdominal pain.', 'Past Medical History: - Glaucoma, predominantly left - Hypertension, noted blood pressure reduced with development of the above complaint and antihypertensives were stopped   Social History: ___ Family History: Family Hx: Mother with lymphoma.  No neurological complaints in family.', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 114/69 HR: NA O2Sat: 98 Weight: NA  [EXAM] ADMISSION EXAM Vitals: 98.2 110 114/69 13 98% RA GEN: A&O, NAD HEENT: No scleral icterus, mucus membranes moist. CV: RRR, No M/G/R PULM: Clear to auscultation b/l, No W/R/R ABD: Tenderness to palpation in RLQ, soft, nondistended, no rebound or guarding, normoactive bowel sounds, no palpable  masses',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
    clinicalcaseid, patientid, title, type,
    description, symptom, medicalhistory, pe,
    status, createdBy
)
VALUES (
    '20357427', '11185241', 'Primary Diagnoses: Acute pancreatitis Pulmonary effusion Aspiration Pneumonia   Secondary Diagnosis: Hypothyroidism', 'PANCREATITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via urgent for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute pancreatitis.', 'The patient is a ___ year-old female with a history of  hypothyroidism, who presents with severe epigastric pain.  The  patient was in her usual state of good health until 3pm on the  day of admission (___), when she developed rapid-onset sweating  and ___ constant (non-fluctuating) epigastric pain that  radiated to her back.  Coincident with the onset of pain, she  reports new-onset nausea, with 1 episode of non-bloody vomiting.   The patient reports a chronic alcohol intake of ___ drinks per  day.  She denies previous episodes of abdominal pain, history of  hyperlipidemia, history of discolored urine, recent flu-like  illness, or abdominal trauma.  Due to the severity of the pain,  the patient was immediately driven by her husband to ___  ___.    At ___ (___), the patient had Hb 16, lipase >3000, K  2.8, undetectable EtOH.  CIWA score was less than 4.  ___  score was 0 on admission.  She received IV fluids, folate,  multivitamin injection, and thiamine.  A CT of the  abdomen/pelvis revealed a ___ fluid collection, with  fat stranding and a 4 cm calcified focus near the ampula of  vater.  MRCP was obtained, showing no ductal dilation and no  gallstones.  On ___, a CXR showed a LLL opacity, and the  patient was started on levo/ceftriaxone.  The patient developed  fever, change in mental status, hypoxia, and tachypnea leading  to intubation, which was complicated by aspiration during the  intubation procedure (ABG post-intubation on ___ was  7.39/34/102). Aspiration from OG tube revealed coffee-ground  emesis after intubation.  She was transfered to ___ on ___ for  further care and evaluation.       ROS: 1 month prior to presentation, patient reports diffuse rash  on the torso (sparing arms/legs) composed of 1 mm red, intensely  itchy papules.  Patient reports new bluriness of vision within  the past 2 weeks, which is partially corrected by corrective  lenses.  Review of systems was otherwise negative except as  specified in the HPI (patient denies recent constipation,  changes in hearing, tingling/ numbness/weakness, coughing of  blood, hematuria, dysuria, blood in the stool, or easy  bleeding).', 'Hypothyroidism    Social History: ___ Family History: Patient''s mother: CVA Patient''s father: DM, HTN, alcoholism (pt.''s father "died of  alcoholism") Patient''s 2 brothers: alcoholism', '[VITALS] Temp: 100.7 BP: 120/70 HR: 80 O2Sat: 100 Weight: NA  [EXAM] VITALS: T 100.7, BP 120/70, HR 80, RR 16, Sat 93% (RA)   General: Patient is comfortable and conversational, nontoxic, in  no apparent distress.  Mild confusion in fact finding/verbal  response.  Skin: Warm and well perfused. Few ___ small skin-colored 1mm  papules on left side of abdomen.  No petechiae/ecchymoses. No  jaundice. HEENT: Sclera anicteric. Oral mucosa pink. Dentition intact.   Trachea midline. Neck supple. Thyroid non-enlarged.  Pulmonary: Breath sounds diminished bilaterally at bases,  extending up 20-30 cm from base on left, and 10 cm from base on  right.  Positive egophony noted bilaterally, with transition at  the levels of diminished breath sounds (described above).   Slight dullness to percussion, with transition at same levels.   No rales/wheezes/rhonchi.  Cardiac: Regular rate and rhythm. No m/r/g.  PMI was firmly  tapping, quarter-sized, located btwn ___ intercostal space  along midclavicular line.   Lymphatic: No cervical or supraclavicular lymphadenopathy.  GI: +Bowel sounds, abdomen soft.  Moderate distention. Moderate  tenderness to palpation in mid-epigastrum.  No organomegaly.  Neuro: AAOx3.  PEERLA, EOMI, tongue midline, face symmetric.  Moving  ___.  Extremities: WWP.  Radial and DP pulses 2+ bilaterally.  No  edema. ROM intact.',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
    clinicalcaseid, patientid, title, type,
    description, symptom, medicalhistory, pe,
    status, createdBy
)
VALUES (
    '23430198', '11190494', 'Pancreatitis', 'PANCREATITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute pancreatitis.', '___ with h/o alcohol abuse, HTN, GERD presented with ___  epigastric pain radiating to his back. Pain started 1 week ago  and has progressively worsened. He has had nausea with no  vomiting over this time. Denies any changes in bowel habits and  no yellow or black stools. No fever, chills, or recent  headaches. He says he only drinks 24oz of alocohol per day and  denies recent hard alcohol consumption. He continues to have an  appetite despite his abdominal pain.  In the ED vitals on arrival were 97.3 80 147/83 16 99% RA. EKG  was sinus at 87, NA, LVH with nonspecific ST changes,with no  available comparison. Labs were notable for a lipase of 674 and  K of 3.2. He was made NPO and started on IVF with 40meq of K+.  Pain was controlled with morphine. RUQ US showed no gallstones.   Admission vitals: HR 87 BP 155/80 RR 17 O2 100%', 'Metoprolol succinate 400 BID Omeprazole 40mg daily Clonazepam 2mg TID loratidine 10mg prn allergies      Social History: ___ Family History: No family hx of pancreatic problems or malignancy. Mother and  father believed to be healthy.', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 155/80 HR: 87 O2Sat: 87 Weight: NA  [EXAM] Admission: Vitals: HR 87 BP 155/80 RR 17 O2 100%  General: Alert, oriented, no acute distress   HEENT: Sclera anicteric, MMM, swollen left tonsil, no LNA.   Neck: supple, JVP not elevated, no LAD   Lungs: Clear to auscultation bilaterally, poor air entry, no  wheezes, rales, ronchi   CV: Regular rate and rhythm, normal S1 + S2, no murmurs, rubs,  gallops   Abdomen: soft, non-tender, non-distended, bowel sounds present,  no rebound tenderness or guarding, no organomegaly   Ext: Warm, well perfused, 2+ pulses, no clubbing, cyanosis or  edema   Skin:No rashes   Neuro:CN ___ grossly intact, ___ strength in all extremities,  alert and oriented x3, gait deferred.',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
    clinicalcaseid, patientid, title, type,
    description, symptom, medicalhistory, pe,
    status, createdBy
)
VALUES (
    '21310093', '11190737', 'Pancreatitis  Septic shock  Alcoholic hepatitis  Cirrhosis  ___', 'OTHER_ABDOMINAL',
    'A patient was admitted via urgent for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with abdominal pathology.', '___ yo F with hx of HTN, GERD, chronic EtOH abuse who presents  with jaundice and fatigue from ___. Ms. ___ drinks ___  bottles of wine per day over the past ___ years; her last  drink may have been ___ days ago, but she is a poor historian.  She notes ~1 week of worsening jaundice associated with fatigue,  some epigastric cramping. Also endorses nausea and nonbloody  vomiting during this time. Denies melena, hematemesis, BRBPR,  dysuria, chest pain, cough.   Went to ___ and ___ to have Hb 8 and received 2L before  being transferred to ___. In ED initial VS: Tm 98.6, HR  109-122, BP 86/55-109/78, found to have Na 132, AST/ALT 335/83,  AP 180, T. bili 9.4, H/H 6.6/20.0, INR 1.8 lactate 2.9 -> 3.1.   Bedside ultrasound without much ascites. Grossly melanotic stool  on rectal exam. Per patient, she had EGD ___ years ago in which  she was told she had mild gastritis and GERD. A colonoscopy at  ___ ___ months ago was reportedly normal. She received 2U RBC, 1  g ceftriaxone, octreotide (100 mcg IV Q8H), diazepam (10 mg IV,  20 mg PO per CIWA).   On arrival to the MICU, patient was noted to be seeing animals  in the room and confabulating. She did recall possibly being  treated for alcohol withdrawal and seizures at ___ in ___.', 'HTN  GERD  Alcohol abuse     Social History: ___ Family History: Noncontributory', '[VITALS] Temp: 98.5 BP: 97/57 HR: 114 O2Sat: 98 Weight: NA  [EXAM] ============================ MICU ADMISSION PHYSICAL EXAM ============================ VITALS:  T 98.5, HR 114, BP 97/57, 99% RA  GENERAL: Alert, oriented to person and year only (not to place),  no acute distress   HEENT: scleral icterus, dry mucous membranes   NECK: supple, JVP not elevated, no LAD   LUNGS: Decreased breath sound in RLL, no wheezes, rales, rhonchi    CV: tachycardic, regular, no murmurs, rubs, gallops   ABD: soft, non-tender, non-distended, bowel sounds present,  hepatomegaly  EXT: Warm, well perfused, 2+ pulses, 1+ edema at ankles. No  asterixis  =======================',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
    clinicalcaseid, patientid, title, type,
    description, symptom, medicalhistory, pe,
    status, createdBy
)
VALUES (
    '26193253', '11197798', 'Pancreatitis Duodenitis  secondary Atrial fibrillation COPD', 'PANCREATITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute pancreatitis.', 'Ms. ___ is a ___ with history of atrial fibrillation on  warfarin, cerebrovascular accident, gastrointestinal bleed, and  cholecystectomy who initially presented to ___  with abdominal and back pain, now transferred for further  evaluation in the setting of elevated lipase and liver function  tests. She was in her usual state of health until 3 to 4 days  prior to admission, when she developed sudden onset "burning"  back pain with associated epigastric pain, nonpostprandial and  exacerbated by lying in bed. She endorses poor oral intake over  the same period, but denies fever, chills, sweats, or  nausea/vomiting. She also reports reports small volume epistaxis  on the day of admission that resolved spontaneously.    On the day of admission, she was seen by her primary care  provider, who noted that she was jaundiced and referred her to  the ___ ED. At ___, labs  were significant for ALT of 157, AST of 213, AlkP of 398, lipase  of 551, TBili of 6.1 (4.2 direct), INR of 11.3, Wbc of 11.3, Hct  of 41.7, and platelets of 222. Right upper quadrant ultrasound  revealed intra- and extrahepatic biliary dilatation with common  bile duct of 19.8mm from 15mm in ___. She was given  piperacillin/tazobactam 3.375g IV and vitamin K 5mg PO.     In the ___ ED, initial vital signs were as follows: 98.3 82  149/73 20 95% 4L. Labs significant for Ca of 10.6, ALT of 186,  AST of 277, TBili of 8.5, lipase of 831, albumin of 3.8, Wbc of  9.7, INR of 12, and UA with gross/microscopic hematuria. CXR  demonstrated questionable RLL infiltrate. CT abdomen/pelvis  revealed biliary dilatation without clear focus of obstruction,  as well as simple free fluid in the stomach and along the liver.  The ERCP service was consulted and advised 2 units FFP and  vitamin K 5mg IV in anticipation of ERCP the following day if  coagulopathy effectively reversed.    On the floor, she is comfortable without chills, sweats, nausea,  or vomiting.', 'Atrial fibrillation on warfarin   Cerebrovascular accident  Gastrointestinal bleed Status post cholecystectomy   Peripheral neuropathy   Hypertension   Hyperlipidemia Coronary artery disease (occluded RCA with left to right  collaterals)   Nonocclusive carotid stenosis   Chronic venous insufficiency   Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease Obstructive sleep apnea   Status post hysterectomy   Diverticulitis status post partial bowel resection   Social History: ___ Family History: Cerebrovascular accidents in multiple family members.', '[VITALS] Temp: 98.1 BP: 143/94 HR: 87 O2Sat: 98 Weight: NA  [EXAM] On admission: Vitals - T: 98.1 BP: 143/94 HR: 87 RR: 20 02 sat: 99% RA   GENERAL: NAD, Obese   HEENT: AT/NC   CARDIAC: RRR, S1/S2, no murmurs, gallops, or rubs   LUNG: CTAB, no wheezes, rales, rhonchi, breathing comfortably  without use of accessory muscles   ABDOMEN: nondistended, +BS, nontender in all quadrants, no  rebound/guarding, no hepatosplenomegaly   EXTREMITIES: moving all extremities well, no cyanosis, clubbing  or edema   PULSES: 2+ DP pulses bilaterally   SKIN: Slightly jaundiced, warm and well perfused, no  excoriations or lesions, no rashes',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
    clinicalcaseid, patientid, title, type,
    description, symptom, medicalhistory, pe,
    status, createdBy
)
VALUES (
    '28337776', '11199428', 'Acute gangrenous cholecystitis', 'CHOLECYSTITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via observation admit for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute gallbladder disease.', '___ with a history of DMII presents with abdominal pain and  intractable nausea and vomiting. The patient was in her usual  stage of health until last ___, when she  developed acute onset nausea and vomiting, followed by abdominal  pain. She cannot recall an inciting event. She reports that the  emesis has been non-bloody, non-billious, "clear" by her  description, and she continues to vomit multiple times per day.  She reports cramping/burning abdominal pain in the RUQ and epigastrium that  worsens with retching. She has had minimal PO intake since  ___. She was evaluated at urgent care today, noted to be  tachycardic to the 140s with a leukocytosis of 24.5 and was  transferred to ___ for further evaluation. She endorses  fevers and chills at home. Now transferred to ___ for  management.  She denies diarrhea or constipation, melena or BRBPR, urinary  frequency/urgency, dysuria, unexplained weight loss, chest  pain/shortness of breath, dizziness/lightheadedness, vertigo,  syncope, weakness.   Of note, Her last upper and lower endoscopies were in ___. EGD  showed a hiatal hernia, mild esophagitis and multiple gastric  polyps. Colonsocopy was notable for colonic polyps (biopsied,  adenomas), scattered diverticulosis, and internal hemorrhoids.', 'DMII, GERD, morbid obesity, depression, LBP, lumbar disk displacement    Social History: ___ Family History: NC', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: NA HR: 120 O2Sat: NA Weight: NA  [EXAM] Vitals: AVSS, see flowsheets GEN: No distress, pleasant, conversant HEENT:  Sclera non-icteric, neck is supple without  lymphadenopathy, thyromegaly or JVD HEART:  RRR with no murmurs CHEST:  No increased work of breathing, clear to auscultation  bilaterally, no crackles or wheezes ABDOMEN: Soft, non-tender, no rebound or guarding INCISIONS: Incisions are clean and intact with minimal drainage  and erythema EXTREMITIES: Warm, well perfused, no edema',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
    clinicalcaseid, patientid, title, type,
    description, symptom, medicalhistory, pe,
    status, createdBy
)
VALUES (
    '23917302', '11204526', 'Primary diagnosis:  Acute pancreatitis Gastroparesis  Headache  Secondary diagnosis: Polycystic kidney disease Hypertension', 'PANCREATITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute pancreatitis.', 'Ms. ___ is a ___ year-old woman with polycystic kidney  disease here after 5 days of N/V and PO intolerance.    She has a history of n/v and occasional diarrhea since ___  that was diagnosed as gastroparesis and resulted in 25lb weight  loss during ___. These symptoms culminated in a hospitalization  in ___ and responded to surgical decortication of several R  renal cysts, which were thought to be obstructing the gastric  outlet (emptying studies normalized). She experienced a  recurrence of nausea/vomiting in early ___, which coincided  with a new UTI (diagnosed by her nephrologist, Dr. ___ and  transiently responded to a 10-day course of ciprofloxacin.   There is a longstanding history of recurrent nausea and vomiting  with many possible precipitating factors including renal cyst  enlargement, UTI, cipro course.  The greatest relief came, when  the right upper pole kidney cyst was unroofed. Now, she is  getting recurrent symptoms, but never to the extent noted  previously.  Today, she is unable to tolerate PO; is passing flatus but no  stools for ___ days. She rates abdominal pain ___, crampy, no  alleviating/exacerbating factors. She notes that the abdominal  pain and n/v have a similar quality as the episode she  experienced back in ___ before she underwent surgical  decortication of several R renal cysts, which seemed to relieved  her symptoms.   She describes a dystonic reaction to all anti-emetics and thus  must take benzos for chronic nausea. No fevers, no black/bloody  stools. Abdominal pain is pan-abdominal.  In the ED, initial vital signs were: 98.7 95 149/99 22 100% RA.  Exam in the ED notable for diffuse abdominal tenderness.     Upon arrival to the floor, the patient endorsed abdominal pain  bilaterally at the flanks. Also has nausea.     Review of systems:   (+) Per HPI   (-) Denies headache, fever, constipation, diarrhea, dysuria,  hematuria.', '-Hysterectomy at age ___ complicated by small bowel and bladder  injury, sepsis requiring resection and peritonitis requiring  multiple operations. - Ventral hernia mesh repair at age ___  - ADPKD c/b hemorrhagic cyst rupture ___ yr - Osteoporosis - Osteoarthritis - HTN secondary to PCKD - Gastroparesis- Diaganosed by ___   Social History: ___ Family History: Patient adopted, so previous generation family history  is  unknown.  She has 4 daughters, 2 of whom have been diagnosed  with ADPKD, 1 who has been screened and is negative and one who has not been screened.', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 149/99 HR: NA O2Sat: 98 Weight: NA  [EXAM] Admission exam: VS: 98.7 95 149/99 22 100% RA  Gen: reclining in bed in NAD,  HEENT: NC/AT, moist mucous membranes   CV: regular rate and rhythm, normal S1 & S2 w/o M/R/G   Pulm: clear to auscultation bilaterally with no W/C/R   Abd: Obese, non-distended abdomen with midline laparotomy scar.  Normoactive BS present; soft and largely tender to palpation  throughout (especially on sides) GU: no foley   Ext: WWP with no edema or cyanosis. Pedal pules palpable. Skin: no rashes   Neuro: A&Ox3 and conversing appropriately. CN II-XII grossly  intact',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
    clinicalcaseid, patientid, title, type,
    description, symptom, medicalhistory, pe,
    status, createdBy
)
VALUES (
    '21865534', '11213607', 'Cholecystitis', 'CHOLECYSTITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute gallbladder disease.', '___ yo M with CAD and HTN who noted severe RUQ pain 2 days ago  which resolved after vomiting. He then noted itching yesterday  and presented to the ED. His abd pain has since resolved and he  is without complaints.', '- Chronic AF   - CAD, s/p septal MI ___   - Mitral regurgitation   - Aortic regurgitation   - HTN   - Dyslipidemia   - LBBB   - CKD   - Gouty arthritis   - Hypothyroidism   - fatty mass in the left mid abdomen (possible liposarcoma but  declined further w/u)      Social History: ___ Family History: Mother - unknown   Father - unknown   Siblings - decesased sister, old age   Children - my patient, ___, HTN, lipids', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 140/86 HR: NA O2Sat: 97 Weight: NA  [EXAM] VS - 97.3 140/86 86 22 92% GENERAL - mild jaundiced but otherwise well-appearing male in  NAD, comfortable, appropriate HEENT - NC/AT, PERRLA, EOMI, sclerae icteric, MMM, OP clear   LUNGS - diffuses wheezes, using accessory muscles for  inspiration   HEART - RRR, no MRG, nl S1-S2   ABDOMEN - obese, NABS, soft/NT/ND, no masses or HSM, no  rebound/guarding   EXTREMITIES - trace pedal edema, 2+ peripheral pulses (radials,  DPs)',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
    clinicalcaseid, patientid, title, type,
    description, symptom, medicalhistory, pe,
    status, createdBy
)
VALUES (
    '26213063', '11214417', 'Primary Diagnosis:  1. Acute pancreatitis (post-ERCP)     Secondary Diagnosis:   1. Primary sclerosing cholangitis   2. Crohn''s Disease   3. likely thromboplebitis', 'OTHER_ABDOMINAL',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with abdominal pathology.', '___ y/o M  with h/o crohn''s, and LFT abnormalities, s/p ERCP  today, with evidence of PSC, who presents with one day of  abdominal pain. Pain started after ERCP today, associated with  nausea/vomiting. Initially went home, but returned to hospital  due to severe ___ mid-abdominal pain. No radiation to back.   Not relieved with home pain meds. no associated yellowing of his  skin or eyes. no pruritis.   In ER, lipase 11,495. Afebrile, VSS. Given 2 L NS IVF, demerol  50mg IV for pain and zofran for nausea. Admit to medicine.   ROS: as per hpi. also no brbpr or melanotic stools, no fever,  chills. no headache, vision changes. + thirsty. ROS otherwise  negative', '-crohns disease  -mild exertional asthma  -___    Social History: ___ Family History: Father suffers from multiple sclerosis.  There is no history of  liver disease, hematologic abnormalities, or anemia.  He is of  ___ descent.  His paternal grandfather suffers from  pancreatic cancer, maternal grandmother lung cancer.', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 150/70 HR: 67 O2Sat: 96 Weight: NA  [EXAM] vitals- 96.3, BP 150/70, HR 67, RR 20, 99% RA, Pain ___ mid  abdominal  heent- EOMI. no scleral icterus. MM dry neck -supple. no jvd pulm- CTA b/l. no r/r/w cv- RRR. no m/r/g. normal s1/s2 abd- soft, NT/ND, mild mid-epigastric ttp w/o rebound or  guarding. NABS. multiple subcutaneous nodules (lipomas)  Ext- no clubbing, cyanosis, edema neuro- alert and oriented x 3. motor strength full affect- normal',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
    clinicalcaseid, patientid, title, type,
    description, symptom, medicalhistory, pe,
    status, createdBy
)
VALUES (
    '24649986', '11215260', 'Diverticulitis', 'DIVERTICULITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with diverticular disease.', 'HPI: This patient is a ___ who presents with a 2 day h/o abdominal pain. The patient reports gradual onset of lower abdominal pain since ___. The pain is sharp, worse with movement, ___ in intensity. He reports nausea here in ED  without emesis. He also reports loose bowel movement here. The patient states that he has experienced this pain twice before, once one month ago and once two weeks ago. Both times, the pain was self-limited and not as severe.', 'none   Social History: ___ Family History: Non-applicable', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: NA HR: 120 O2Sat: NA Weight: NA  [EXAM] General: awake and alert CV: RRR Lungs: CTA bilaterally Abdomen: soft, (+) diffuse tenderness greatest in LLQ>suprapubic region, (+) rebound without guarding, non-distended with some tympany in RUQ>LUQ, hypoactive BS Rectal: vault empty, heme (-) Ext: warm, no edema',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
    clinicalcaseid, patientid, title, type,
    description, symptom, medicalhistory, pe,
    status, createdBy
)
VALUES (
    '24140304', '11227282', 'acute appendicitis', 'APPENDICITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute appendicitis.', 'HISTORY OF PRESENTING ILLNESS   Patient is a ___ female with chief complaint of right-sided abdominal pain. Patient states her symptoms started approximately 48 hours ago. She describes some abrupt onset of a sharp focal right-sided pain. She was evaluated in the emergency department yesterday, CT imaging was negative at that time. Since discharge, the patient states her pain has worsened. She states that she does also have pain with urination. And mild right back pain. She notes chills but no fever. Mild nausea and anorexia.', 'none   Social History: ___ Family History:  Grandparents with heart disease.', '[VITALS] Temp: 97.6 BP: 124/69 HR: 106 O2Sat: 97 Weight: NA  [EXAM] upon admission ___   Temp: 97.6 HR: 106 BP: 124/69 Resp: 18 O(2)Sat: 100   Constitutional: uncomfortable HEENT: anicteric mucosa moist Chest: CTA B Cardiovascular: Regular Rate and Rhythm Abdominal: focal right lower quadrant tenderness with guarding. No rebound. Nondistended. Pelvic: no CMT, mild right adnexal discomfort with pelvic exam per resident GU/Flank: mild right costovertebral angle tenderness Extr/Back: Normal Skin: Normal Neuro: Normal Psych: Normal  Physical examination',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
    clinicalcaseid, patientid, title, type,
    description, symptom, medicalhistory, pe,
    status, createdBy
)
VALUES (
    '23341169', '11230823', 'Gallstone pancreatitis', 'PANCREATITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute pancreatitis.', 'Ms. ___ is a ___ F with a medical history notable for  dementia. Due to this, she is not able to remember all of the  details of her symptoms today. However, her 24-hour care  assistant is with her and is able to provide additional details.  At approximately 2pm on ___ Ms. ___ awoke from sleep with  RUQ and chest pain. She noted no associated symptoms including  fevers, chills, nausea, vomitting, or change in bowel habits.  She does not remember having similar pains in the past.  Vitals on arrival to ___  ED: T 98.7, P 80, BP 154/72, 99% on  RA. Her evaluation was notable for a RUQ US that revealed a  mildly distended gallbladder with mild wall thickening, trace  pericholecystic fluid, and a 5mm stone in the CBD. In the ED she  received Unasyn and 2.5mg of Haldol for agitation.  ROS: no recent illnesses. No fevers, chills, weight loss. Ms.  ___ is quite clear that she does not like taking medications  and takes none at home.', 'PAST MEDICAL HISTORY: 1.  Dementia 2.  Osteoporosis 3.  Hypothyroidism 4.  History of bladder cancer 5.  Hypertension 6.  Hypercholesterolemia 7.  Gait disorder with falls     -see surgical hx below 8.  Depressed mood PAST SURGICAL HISTORY: 1.  Right thyroid lobectomy  ___ 2.  Transurethral resection of small carcinoma of bladder  ___ 3.  Left cemented hemiarthroplasty, status post ___ 4.  ORIF right hip  ___ 5.  Cataract surgery right eye   Social History: ___ Family History: non-contributory.', '[VITALS] Temp: 96.5 BP: 155/85 HR: NA O2Sat: 96 Weight: NA  [EXAM] Vital Signs: T 96.5, P 72, BP 155/85, 97% on RA.    - Gen: Elderly female sitting upright in NAD. - HEENT: Sclera anicteric. - Chest: Normal respirations and breathing comfortably on room  air. Lungs clear to auscultation bilaterally. - CV: Regular rhythm. Normal S1, S2. No murmurs or gallops. JVP  <5 cm.  - Abdomen: Normal bowel sounds. She has tenderness to deep  palpation of the RUQ. Equivocal ___ sign. - Extremities: No ankle edema. - Neuro: Alert, oriented x1-2. Limited fund of knowledge about  today''s events but remembers her son and health aid well. She is  calm and pleasant. CN ___ intact. Speech and language are  normal.',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
    clinicalcaseid, patientid, title, type,
    description, symptom, medicalhistory, pe,
    status, createdBy
)
VALUES (
    '29723478', '11231379', 'Acute cholecystitis', 'CHOLECYSTITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute gallbladder disease.', '___ yo M h/o HTN, HLD, CAD, hypothyroidism, prostate CA (s/p  resection ___ p/w epigastric and RUQ pain sine yesterday  night. Pain began suddenly yesterday, initially ___ but has  since been improving, currently ___.  Movement makes the pain  worse, pain medication and rest make it better. Reports nausea  but no vomiting. No fever or chills.', 'PMH: HTN, HLD, CAD, hypothyroidism, prostate cancer, anxiety,  gout  PSH: Prostatectomy ___    Social History: ___ Family History: ___', '[VITALS] Temp: 97.9 BP: 164/84 HR: 86 O2Sat: 97 Weight: NA  [EXAM] T 97.9  HR 86  BP 164/84  RR 18  SaO2 94%RA NAD, A&O, comfortable, ambulating independently RRR CTAB, no resp distress Abd soft, appropriately tender, slight distention, dressings  c/d/i Ext wwpx4, no c/c/e, palp DPs b/l',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
    clinicalcaseid, patientid, title, type,
    description, symptom, medicalhistory, pe,
    status, createdBy
)
VALUES (
    '26138916', '11235666', 'Primary diagnosis: 1. Pancreatitis 2. Atypical chest pain', 'PANCREATITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute pancreatitis.', '___ yoM w/ a h/o HOCM initially diagnosed in ___ s/p septal  ablations x 2 and myomectomy on ___, chronic chest pain,  presents with worsening of chest pain.   .   At baseline the patient states that he gets roughly 4 episodes  of chest pain per day, lasting about ___ minutes. The day of  admission he had 5 episodes and his ___ episode brought him to  the ER as it did not resolve and he was told to come to the ER  if he has CP lasting more than 90 minutes. His chest pain is a  substernal chest pressure with L arm numbness and associated  with some shortness of breath and today was associated with  nausea / vomiting x 1. He occasionally feels lightheaded with  his pain and did today, in addition he occasionally feels  palpitations with his pain which he did today as well. Pain is  not pleuritic or positional. No heart failure symptoms  (orthonpea, PND, ___ edema) and no claudication symptoms.   .   His baseline functional capacity is walking up 2 flights of  stairs which predictably reproduces his symptoms.   .   Intermittent diarrhea over the past few days, otherwise rest of  ROS is negative.   .   In the ED, initial vitals: T 98.6, HR 96, BP 130/70 RR 16, O2  98% RA. He rec''d IV morphine for his chest pain.   .  ___ yoM w/ a h/o HOCM initially diagnosed in ___ s/p septal  ablations x 2 and myomectomy on ___, chronic chest pain,  presents with worsening of chest pain.   .   At baseline the patient states that he gets roughly 4 episodes  of chest pain per day, lasting about ___ minutes. The day of  admission he had 5 episodes and his ___ episode brought him to  the ER as it did not resolve and he was told to come to the ER  if he has CP lasting more than 90 minutes. His chest pain is a  substernal chest pressure with L arm numbness and associated  with some shortness of breath and today was associated with  nausea / vomiting x 1. He occasionally feels lightheaded with  his pain and did today, in addition he occasionally feels  palpitations with his pain which he did today as well. Pain is  not pleuritic or positional. No heart failure symptoms  (orthonpea, PND, ___ edema) and no claudication symptoms.   .   His baseline functional capacity is walking up 2 flights of  stairs which predictably reproduces his symptoms.   .   Intermittent diarrhea over the past few days, otherwise rest of  ROS is negative.   .   In the ED, initial vitals: T 98.6, HR 96, BP 130/70 RR 16, O2  98% RA. He rec''d IV morphine for his chest pain.   .', '- Hypertrophic Obstructive Cardiomyopathy: echo ___ w/  resting LVOT Gradient 65, inducible LVOT Gradient 73, + h/o NSVT    - septal myomectomy on ___   - S/P EtOH septal ablation ___   - S/P AICD placement for prevention of sudden death ___,  replaced ___   - Hyperlipidemia   - Secundum ASD   - Chronic chest pain: no CAD by cath ___   - Chronic Low Back Pain with RLE Radiculopathy: MRI ___ L5-S1  Rt paracentral disc herniation, displacing S1 nerve root.   - GERD   - Spontaneous Pneumothorax S/P Rt lobectomy   - Left testicular seminoma S/P bilateral orchiectomy   - Hemorrhoids s/p hemorrhoidectomy   - s/p Appendectomy   - s/p Tonsillectomy      Social History: ___ Family History: Notable for a number of family members with MI and sudden  cardiac death. Uncle sudden death. Brother and sister with HCM.', '[VITALS] Temp: 96.5 BP: 120/85 HR: 80 O2Sat: 96 Weight: NA  [EXAM] VS - T 96.5 HR 80 BP 120/85 RR 18 O2 96% RA   Gen: NAD. Oriented x3. Mood, affect appropriate.   HEENT: NCAT. Sclera anicteric. PERRL, EOMI. Conjunctiva were  pink, no pallor or cyanosis of the oral mucosa. No xanthalesma.    Neck: Supple with JVP of 11cm.   CV: PMI located in ___ intercostal space, midclavicular line.  RR, normal S1, S2. ___ SEM at the USB, increases to a ___ with  valsalva maneuver. No thrills, lifts. No S3 or S4.   Chest: No chest wall deformities, scoliosis or kyphosis. Resp  were unlabored, no accessory muscle use. CTAB, no crackles,  wheezes or rhonchi.   Abd: Soft, LLQ and LUQ tenderness- no pain at rest, no rebound  or guarding. No HSM or tenderness. Abd aorta not enlarged by  palpation. No abdominial bruits.   Ext: No c/c/e. No femoral bruits.   Skin: No stasis dermatitis, ulcers, scars, or xanthomas.',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
    clinicalcaseid, patientid, title, type,
    description, symptom, medicalhistory, pe,
    status, createdBy
)
VALUES (
    '24706695', '11241609', 'PRIMARY DIAGNOSIS 1. Pancreatitis  SECONDARY DIAGNOSIS 1. Cirrhosis 2. Hepatitis C', 'PANCREATITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via eu observation for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute pancreatitis.', '___ w/ ___ Class A HepC/Alcoholic cirrhosis  (decompensated by: ascites, hepatic encephalopathy) s/p TIPS  ___ who complains of epigastric pain. He has had on and off  epigastric pain x 3 weeks which became constant on ___ and  went to ___. He was there for x3 days from which  he left (?AMA) to seek care here. The pain started in his LUQ  but has radiated to a band around his abdomen. He reports  vomitting this AM, and maybe there was blood in it. He had  subjective fever/chills this AM prior to coming to ___, but  nothing at OSH. No chest pain, SOB, constipation/diarrhea. He  hasn''t eaten since ___ so is unsure if food makes it worse.  No back pain. He has started to have increased pain with  urination as well.   .   Per verbal report with ___: initial lipase 728  ~1100 (ref 73-393), increased bili, SGOT 63. WBC 3.67 H/H  12.___. Lipase trended up to 2902. RUQ US cirrhotic liver,  benign hepatic cyst, no hepatic solid lesions, cholelithiasis  without evidence of biliary obstruction. Admitted to hospital  x3d at which point he left AMA to see care here.   In the ED, the initial vitals were: 99.1 83 140/71 16 97%. Labs  significant for ALT 61, AST 81, T bili 1.2, Alb 3.9, lipase 68.  Lactate 1.5. UA was negative. He received 1L NS, 0.5mg dilaudid  IV x2, zofran 4mg IV. On the floor, patient reports ___ pain  but is walking around the room. Has not taken any NSAIDs or new  medications.   Of note, patient had a similar presentation in ___ from which  he left AMA.     ROS: per HPI, denies increased cough, shortness of breath, chest  pain, abdominal pain, diarrhea, constipation, BRBPR, melena,  hematochezia.', '- HCV genotype 3/ETOH cirrhosis dx ___ c/b portal HTN with   refractory ascites requiring weekly paracenteses s/p TIPS ___,  h/o hepatic encephalopathy   - Last EGD ___ with 1 cord of grade I varices in the lower    third of the esophagus and portal hypertensive gastropathy.   - s/p TIPS ___   - HCV: genotype 3 went through treatment with pegylated  interferon and ribavirin for genotype 3 hepatitis C in ___,  completed 12 weeks of therapy; however, due to side effects,  treatment had to be   withdrawn and the virus relapsed following withdrawal.   - MCV due to DUI in ___ with head trauma   - asthma/COPD   - sciatica   - arthritis   - gout   - h/o gall stones, none recently      Social History: ___ Family History: Father - EtOH abuse   Mother (age ___ - M.S., HTN, h/o EtOH abuse   No family history of liver disease', '[VITALS] Temp: 100.0 BP: 127/71 HR: 127 O2Sat: 71 Weight: NA  [EXAM] ADMISSION  VS: 127/71, 68, 18, 100RA   General: Pleasant male, NAD   HEENT: Dry mucous membranes, sclera anicteric   Neck: Supple, no LAD   CV: RRR, no m/r/g   Lungs: Prolonged expiratory phase, no wheezes/rales/rhonchi   Abdomen: +BS. Diffusely tender without rebound/guarding   Ext: 2+ peripheral pulses, no edema',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


