VALUES (
    '22841113', '11275704', 'CHOLECYSTITIS Elevated T bilirubin ASTHMA', 'CHOLECYSTITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute gallbladder disease.', '___ year old woman with severe asthma, transferred from ___  ___ after five days of nausea and abdominal pain. Patient  reports developing diffuse myalgias starting 6 days PTA, which  were accompanied by "dry heaves". Patient was only able to  tolerate "crackers and water" due to pain, which developed over  the right upper quadrant. Patient began vomiting 4 days PTA,  which she describes as gastric contents, non bilious or bloody.  Denies diarrhea or change in color of stool. Denies any sick  contacts, but does report low grade fevers at home up to 101.  Patient reports she called her PCP who believed this could be  "flu". Pain continued to worsen so Ms ___ decided to go to  the closest hospital.  ROS: Patient denies any chest pain, palpitations, shortness of  breath, dizziness or syncope. She does report heat/cold  intolerance and frequent "hot flashes". ~20lb weight loss over ___  years.  ___ course: Suspicion for cholangitis; CT scan obtained which revealed  percholecystic fluid and gallstones. Patient trasiently placed  on on pressors (lowest documented SBP in ___) and given unasyn,  ceftriaxone and flagyl. Transfered to ___ for further  management.  ED Course: Patient re-dosed with antibiotics, right upper  quadrant ultrasound and MRCP ordered. Admitted to medicine for  further evaluation.', 'Medical History Asthma Diabetes (non insulin dependent) Hypothyroidism Gastroesophageal reflux  Surgical History T&A  s/p appendectomy  s/p ruptured ectopic pregnancy   Social History: ___ Family History: Mother died of old age, father died of "bone cancer". Oldest  sister with ___ dementia', '[VITALS] Temp: 99.4 BP: 104/50 HR: 76 O2Sat: 99 Weight: NA  [EXAM] Temp: 99.4 (oral)   BP 104/50  HR 76  O2 Sat: 96%RA  GEN: Obese, elderly female in no acute distress, appears  comfortable, speaking in full sentences HEENT: EOMI, sclera anicteric, dry mucous membranes CV: Regular rate, no murmurs, rubs or gallops.  Lungs: Very mild crackles at right lower base. Breathing easily Abdomen: Soft, no guarding, no rebound tenderness. Mild  tenderness to palpation over superior quadrants along inferior  costal margin. No epigastric tenderness, no shifting dullness Extremities: No clubbing, cyanosis, edema Skin: intact, no rashes, abrasions or lacerations.',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


