VALUES (
    '22605409', '11303674', '# Acute Pancreatitis  # Eosinophilia # Epilepsy # HTN # Asthma # Depression # GERD # Uterine Prolapse # spina bidida', 'PANCREATITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute pancreatitis.', '___ with spinal bifida, paraplegia, epilepsy who p/w abd pain.  She states that she has had worsened epigastric abdominal pain  over the past couple of days though vague of exact location on  repeat questioning. There has been nausea and ___  vomiting. EMS witnessed GTC seizures - though its reported pt  also has recent neurology evaluations with additional  pseudoseizure activity.  Pt reports having ?generalized ab pain  for few months - but worsening past 3 days with - possible  greatest in epigastrum - but noted pt a vague historian.   no  f/c, no diarrhea, +report of cough, +vague cp complaints with  pain - also with sob - states due to asthma per patient.  No  recall of sick contacts but not clear - no HA, wt changes, no  gen myalgias/arthralgias. <br>  ROS - as above with 10 point ROS, no new rashs, note h/o  paraplegia below waste - no changes, no new numbness/weakness  complaints - noted no new urinary complaints - no blood - has  urostomy.  Sz report per EMS - pt can not recall.', '- spinal bifida - paraplegia - mild mental retardation - psychogenic dysarthria and tremor - urostomy - hypertension - asthma/copd - h/o VRE pyelonephritis - GERD - Depression - genital herpes - atopic dermatitis - back pain - uterine prolapse - twins - reported seizures and/or pseudoseizures, suggestion of  conversion d/o.    Social History: Per report prior - She lives alone in an apartment in ___.  She is mostly wheelchair bound but is able to transfer  independently, she has no assistance at home "I don''t want  strangers in my house." She identifies her boyfriend ___ as  her emergency contact, gives permission for him to be contacted,   saying he lives at ___ Assisted Living. ___ calls her   every morning to encourage her to take her medication and visits  her every afternoon to evening. She misses doses of her  medications due to fatigue and forgetting. ___ states she is  able to do all her ADLs. She has 2 twin ___ year old boys who  live with their aunt, she asks that they not be contacted. Per  the record there is a history of cocaine use. -Tobacco: she smokes quantity unknown  -ETOH: drinks quantity unknown  -Drugs: according to prior notes, there is a question of cocaine   abuse     Family History: Unable to obtain - pt can not recall.', '[VITALS] Temp: 98.6 BP: 120/75 HR: 74 O2Sat: 98 Weight: NA  [EXAM] VS: Temp: 98.6  BP: 120/75  HR: 74  RR: 22  O2sat: 99% 2L   .   Gen: aggitated - during ___ - pt with mild full body shakes -  but able to be ___ and answered questions during brief  episodes  HEENT: PERRL, EOMI. No scleral icterus. No conjunctival  injection. Mucous membranes moist. No oral ulcers.   Neck: Supple, no LAD, no JVP elevation.   Lungs: poor effort but clear - no crackles, mild exp wheezing   CV: RRR, no murmurs, rubs, gallops.   Abdomen: soft/obese, diffuse ttp - possible greatest in  epigastrum, +urostomy intact with clear outpt, ND, NABS   Extremities: warm and well perfused, +trace ___ edema bilat  Neurological: min strength below waste (no change) - given  aggitation - not completely cooperating with full exam but able  to answer brief questions with fluent speech - gen symmetric  exam.    GU: + uterine prolapse seen - no bleeding - ___   Psychiatric: aggitated',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
