)
VALUES (
    '26137090', '11309272', 'Acute pancreatitis', 'PANCREATITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute pancreatitis.', '___ transferred from OSH for severe abdominal pain after injury  operating mechanical tractor on hill.  Patient reports pain  started after vehicle stopped unexpectedly and his abdomen  impacted hard against the armrest. Pain increased ___ severity to  ___ over the day, and he sought attention at ___  ___ at 1am, where cat scan showed inflammation of pancreas  and WBC of 18.5 was noted.  Patient was then transferred to  ___.  Pain is constant and only partially alleviated by lying  on his back. Patient reports nausea/vomiting with no  hematemesis, and diaphoresis.  Patient has been passing gas  today though it is painful.  Last bowel movement was yesterday  at 6pm. Patient denies loss of consciousness, chest pain, or  dizziness.', 'lumbar disc injury, treated with daily methadone   Social History: ___ Family History: - father: diabetes - controlled by diet; prostate cancer  (treated surgically) - mother: alive and health - sister:  gall bladder removal', '[VITALS] Temp: 95.0 BP: 147/95 HR: 116 O2Sat: 95 Weight: NA  [EXAM] ADMISSION  ========================= Vitals- T 95, HR 116, BP, 147/95, RR 20, SPO2 99% RA  General- ___ distress. Diaphoretic and cool. Frequent belching. AOx3. HEENT- Normcephalic/atraumatic. EOMI. PERRL.  Mucus membranes pink and moist.  CV- Elevated rate (110-120). Regular rhythm. No M/R/G. Very  pronounced heart sounds.   Lungs- CTA. Cannot take deep breaths without pain on  inspiration. Abd- Moderately rigid (guarding) and distended, diffuse  tenderness but focused primarily on left side (middle and lower  quadrants). Unable to palpate deeply given pain and resulting  nausea. Audible bowel sounds. Audible pulse ___ abdomen, may  reflect pronounced heart sounds. Extremities- WWP. Normal strength and bulk bilaterally. Neuro- GCS 15. CNII-XII grossly intact.',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


