VALUES (
    '29105302', '11313489', 'Post ERCP pancreatitis Hypertension, benign Acute diastolic congestive heart failure Pulmonary arterial hypertension Mediastinal Lymphadenopathy Pilonidal Cyst w/o abscess', 'OTHER_ABDOMINAL',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with abdominal pathology.', 'PCP:  Name: ___  Location: ___ FAMILY PRACTICE  Address: ___, ___  Phone: ___  Fax: ___   Admission ___ 0200  CC:abd pain  ___ who 2 days PTA had an ERCP which was done for CBD  dilitation. The procedure was done under MAC and there was  unsuccessful canulation of the bile duct. A pancreatic stent was  placed to assist, but was again unsuccessful. The stent was left  in place and plan were made to have the patient return in one  week to have the PD stent removed and a repeat attempt to  canulate the CBD performed. In the interim, the patient  developed acute epigastric abd pain yesterday, with radiation to  the back, and associated nausea. She went to her local ER and  was transferred to ___.    In ER: ERCP team was called. A CT abd showed the stent in place  and no other complications. She was given cipro/flagyl and  admitted. VSS  ROS:   -Constitutional: [x]WNL []Weight loss []Fatigue/Malaise []Fever  []Chills/Rigors []Nightweats []Anorexia   -ENT: [x]WNL []Dry Mouth []Oral ulcers []Bleeding gums/nose  []Tinnitus []Sinus pain []Sore throat   -Cardiac: [x]WNL []Chest pain []Palpitations ___ edema  []Orthopnea/PND []DOE   -Respiratory: [x]WNL []SOB []Pleuritic pain []Hemoptysis []Cough    -Gastrointestinal: see HPI -GU: [x]WNL []Incontinence/Retention []Dysuria []Hematuria  []Discharge []Menorrhagia   -Skin: [x]WNL []Rash []Pruritus   -Musculoskeletal: [x]WNL []Myalgias []Arthralgias []Back pain   -Neurological: [ x]WNL []Numbness of extremities []Weakness of  extremities []Parasthesias []Dizziness/Lightheaded []Vertigo  []Confusion []Headache', 'h/o CCY, hernia, lupus with ___ and arthritis no renal  disease,  exercise induced Asthma,  HTN    Social History: ___ Family History: FHx of MS and scleroderma', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 125/78 HR: NA O2Sat: 97 Weight: NA  [EXAM] VS: 97.0 125/78 78 16 93RA Gen: Well appearing, no acute distress, awake, alert,  appropriate, and oriented x 3. Skin: warm to touch, no apparent rashes.  HEENT: No conjunctival pallor, no scleral jaundice, PERRLA,  OP  clear, no cervical LAD. CV: JVP 6 cmH20, RRR no audible m/r/g, pulses 2+, no ___ edema Lungs: clear to auscultation  Abd: soft, diffusely tender Ext: No C/C/E Neuro: strength and sensation intact bilaterally.',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


