VALUES (
    '29394743', '11341524', 'Pancreatitis Systemic lupus erythematosus Rheumatoid arthritis Left elbow antibiotic spacer placement COPD Atrial fibrillation Gastroesophageal reflux disease Hypothyroidism Chronic anemia', 'OTHER_ABDOMINAL',
    'A patient was admitted via direct emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with abdominal pathology.', '___ F s/p left elbow I&D with antibiotic spacer placement on  ___ admitted from clinic for clogged PICC line, abdominal  pain and dehydration.  Pt is currently on week ___ of vancomycin  administered via right-sided PICC.  She is complaining of dull,  crampy abdominal pain, ___ in severity, and states that it is  similar to previous experience with peptic ulcer disease.  She  states that she has not had an appetite recently due to the pain  and reports four episodes of nausea and vomiting, no  hematemesis, yellowish clear in color.  Pain is constant and  unremitting, and nothing seems to help it.  She states the pain  is mildly better while leaning forward, and worse when leaning  back.  Pt has been somewhat constipated lately, although she had  a BM while at the hospital, which was normal in color and  consistency.  She reports no melena or hematochezia, no dysuria  or hematuria.  She has noticed no discoloration of her skin or  eyes.  .   In the ED, initial VS: 96.5  136/69  68  16  98/2L  .   Currently, pt reports the severity of the pain is similar to  presentation (___), and is complaining of pain, saying that the  Vicodin did not help her.  She is still nauseous and is feeling  very restless.', '-Rheumatoid arthritis: On low dose prednisone and MTX  (etanercept help in context of ORIF) -SLE on prednisone (history of pericarditis, no known renal  involvement) -Raynaud''s syndrome ?   -Osteoporosis with spontaneous rib fractures in ___   -COPD ___ FEV1 1.46 L FEV1/FVC of 61 c/w mod COPD   -GERD  (hx of Schatzki ring) -Hiatal Hernia   -Hypothyroidism -Anxiety   -Oral HSV   -Chronic anemia (on empiric folate and B12)   -History of atypical chest pain with negative stress tests -___ Syndrome due to cefazolin -Paradoxical Afib -___ Left total elbow replacement ___ removal of  hardware due to infection)   Social History: ___ Family History: Her mother died of MI and father of complication of diabetes in  their ___.', '[VITALS] Temp: 97.6 BP: 136/68 HR: 66 O2Sat: 97 Weight: NA  [EXAM] Vitals - T: 97.6 BP: 136/68 HR: 66 RR: 16 02 sat: 98%2L  GENERAL: NAD, AAOx3, looks uncomfortable, is constantly changing  her position HEENT: PERRL, pale conjunctiva, no scleral icterus, MMM, no  pharyngeal exudates  CARDIAC: RRR, S1/S2, no m/r/g audible LUNG: CTAB, no w/c/r ABDOMEN: +BS, normoactive, soft, moderately tender at RUQ and  epigastric area, non-distended, negative ___ sign, no  organomegaly, spleen tip not palpable, no masses palpable, no  guarding or peritoneal signs, negative ___ Turner''s  sign EXT: WWP, no cyanosis or clubbing, changes of venous  insufficiency noted, purplish blue hue to most of leg  NEURO: AAOx3, CN II-XII intact  DERM: no visible rashes',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


