VALUES (
    '24636219', '11365171', 'Acute cholecystitis/choledocholithiasis', 'CHOLECYSTITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via urgent for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute gallbladder disease.', '___ yo 2 months post partum presents as transfer from ___  ___ for ERCP. Pt reports that she has had intermittent RUQ  and epigastric abd pain for about 1 month, worse with food. She  attributed pain to gas. 5 days PTA pain became constant and pt  presented to ___. There she had RUQ US, was told she  had GB disease given tramadol and demerol and discharged with  instructions not to eat rich foods. The following day pt had  PB&J sandwich which she was not aware was considered rich and  pain returned. She tried 800mg IBP and T#3 without relief. She  then went to ___ where she was found to have acute  cholecysitis and obstructing gallstone. She was admitted to  surgical service and had ERCP attempted x2, both attempts failed  to remove stone. She is transferred to BID for repeat  ERCP.Currently pt reports ___ RUQ and epigastric pain as well  as nausea. Last emesis was 3 days ago. No fevers. Patient with  persistent RUQ abdominal pain. Patient taken to the OR for  uncomplicated laproscopic cholecystectomy.  ROS: otherwise negative', 'migraines Uterine fibroids Abnormal papsmear   Social History: ___ Family History: mother with diabetes', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 124/91 HR: NA O2Sat: 98 Weight: NA  [EXAM] VS: 98.7  124/91  75  18  100%ra Gen: nad, sitting up in bed Resp: ctab CV: rrr no m/r/g Abd: bowel sounds present, tender epgastrium and RUQ,  nondistended Ext: wwp, no e/c/c Neuro: alert, answering questions appropriately, follows  commands',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


