    'A patient was admitted via eu observation for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with abdominal pathology.', 'This patient is a ___ year old female with a history of cholecystectomy who presents with one day of constant RUQ/epigatric abdominal pain with associated subjective fevers, chills, bilateral lower flank pain, nausea, and diarrhea. She had subjective fevers earlier this week, and yesterday developed the abdominal pain, which has been constant since. Today she has also had lower flank pain bilaterally with nuasea and diarrhea. She denies any vomiting, cough, dysuria, hematuria, vaginal bleeding or discharge, or any other symptoms. She denies any previous similar episodes.                        Timing: Gradual, Constant                      Severity: Moderate                      Duration: 1 day                      Location: RUQ/ epigastric         Context/Circumstances: History of cholecystectomy                   Mod.Factors: ___. with Time     Associated Signs/Symptoms: subjective fevers, chills,                                bilateral lower flank pain,                                ___, diarrhea', 'PMH: denies  PSH: cesarian delivery     Social History: ___ Family History: Non contributory.', '[VITALS] Temp: 96.8 BP: 108/70 HR: 101 O2Sat: 96 Weight: NA  [EXAM] ___   Temp: 96.8 HR: 101 BP: 108/70 Resp: 16 O(2)Sat: 100 Normal   Constitutional: Comfortable HEENT: Normocephalic, atraumatic, Pupils equal, round and reactive to light, Extraocular muscles intact Oropharynx within normal limits Chest: Clear to auscultation Cardiovascular: Regular Rate and Rhythm, Normal first and second heart sounds Abdominal: Mild RUQ tenderness to palpation GU/Flank: No costovertebral angle tenderness Extr/Back: No cyanosis, clubbing or edema Skin: Warm and dry Neuro: Speech fluent Psych: Normal mentation ___: No petechiae',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


