VALUES (
    '22197376', '11415267', 'Gangrenous cholecystitis and large umbilical hernia.', 'CHOLECYSTITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via eu observation for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute gallbladder disease.', 'Patient is a ___ y/o F with a history of DM2, HTN, HLD presenting  with right upper quadrant abdominal pain. She reports the pain  started yesterday at 6pm, she had eaten 2 hours before this. She  states the pain started in the right upper quadrant. She describes the pain as cramping in nature and radiates to her  back. She reports nausea, vomiting, but denies fevers, chills,  diarrhea. She has had this pain one times before, ___ years  ago related to "gallstones. Her last meal was at 5 pm yesterday.  Because of the aforementioned symptoms, the patient presented to  the emergency department.', 'PMH: DIABETES TYPE II                                                 HYPERCHOLESTEROLEMIA                                             GASTROESOPHAGEAL REFLUX                                          OSTEOARTHRITIS                                                   HYPERTENSION                                                     OBESITY                                                          DEPRESSION                                                       ANXIETY                                                          CHOLELITHIASIS                                                   DERMATITIS UPPER BACK    PSH: WISDOM TEETH EXTRACTION    No other intra-abdominal surgeries         Social History: ___ Family History: Mother    ___  ___  STROKE, DIABETES MELLITUS                         Father    ___  ___  STROKE MGM       Deceased  ___  DIABETES MELLITUS, STROKE Sister    Living    ___  CYST', '[VITALS] Temp: 97.8 BP: 113/73 HR: 91 O2Sat: 97 Weight: NA  [EXAM] Vitals: T 97.8,  HR 91, BP 113/73, RR 16, SaO2 94% RA  GEN: Alert and oriented, no acute distress, conversant and interactive. HEENT: Sclerae anicteric, mucous membranes moist, oropharynx is clear. CV: Regular rate and rhythm, S1 S2. PULM/CHEST: CTAB, respirations are unlabored on room air. ABD: Soft, mildly distended, slightly tender around incision  sites;gauze with tegaderm CD&I Ext: No lower extremity edema, distal extremities warm and  well-perfused.',
