VALUES (
    '25326227', '11418296', 'appendicitis s/p laparoscopic appendectomy ___ acute on chronic abdominal pain with familial visceral myopathy  Hypophosphatemia', 'APPENDICITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via observation admit for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute appendicitis.', '___ of Present Illness: Mr. ___ is a ___ M with familial visceral myopathy  (___) who had 48 hours of acute, severe, and diffuse abdominal  pain, nausea, feculent vomiting, chills, rigors, and bowel habit  changes. He had not had a bowel movement for 2 days, and prior  to this he had mucous diarrhea (compared to his baseline  diarrhea or constipation fluctuations d/t FVM). He had not  passed flatus for 36 hours.  He had leukocytosis( WBC 17.6) and  a lactate of 2.0, and therefore had a CT A/P that demonstrated a  large retrocecal appendix with diffuse wall thickening and three  fecoliths, with concern for cecal bascule.   Due to his FVM, he had surgical evaluation for his impaired  motility on Barium swallow, low volume gastric filling, and ___  and ___ portion duodenal dilatation with distal takeoff  concerning for SMA syndrome.', 'familial visceral myopathy (chronic abdominal pain, alternating  diarrhea and constipation using 40 tablespoons of Milk of  Magnesia daily, difficulty passing flatus requiring physical  manuevers) exercise induced asthma  PSH:  none   Social History: ___ Family History: Familial visceral myopathy with his mother who is TPN dependent  and s/p multiple abdominal procedures, and brother who is less  severely affected', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 117/61 HR: NA O2Sat: 99 Weight: NA  [EXAM] Admission  VS:  99.0  107  117/61  16  100%RA GEN: Demonstrably uncomfortable, thin NEURO: AOx3, CN II-XII grossly intact HEENT: Sclerae anicteric, trachea midline, no JVD CV: RRR, 2+ peripheral pulses bilaterally   RESP: No respiratory distress GI: Abdomen soft, non-distended but diffusely tender. No voluntary or involuntary guarding. Rectal exam deferred EXT: WWP no CCE',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


