    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with diverticular disease.', 'Pt is a ___ with known diverticulosis who presents to the ___ ED with LLQ abdominal pain.  She states that she has been feeling generally, but only slightly, unwell since her colonoscopy 3wks ago.  Over the past five days she has become more fatigued and she began to have bloating and pain in her lower abdomen, L>R.  This has escalated over the past 3 days and is accompanied by nausea but no emesis. She describes the pain  as dull, achy and sore, and constant.  She denies BRBPR or melena.  She states her stools have been normal, slightly lighter in color, without mucous, last yesterday AM.  She is passing  flatus. She denies previous episodes of this pain but does endorse intermittent "pulling" pain at the site of her previous L  femoral hernia repair that has returned with recent feel of bloat.  She denies any bulging from that site.', 'mod-->severe mitral regurgitation, diverticulosis, colon polyp, hx depression, ___ (serology neg), insomnia    Past Surgical History: Repair L femoral hernia ___, Breast augmentation ___, tonsillectomy as a child      Social History: ___ Family History: no family history of GI malignancy or inflammatory bowel disease', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 128/68 HR: NA O2Sat: 98 Weight: NA  [EXAM] 98 60 128/68 16 98%RA Gen - A&O x 3, NAD Pulm - no respiratory distress CV - rrr Abd - +BS, soft, NTND, w/o rebound or guarding Extrem - no c/c/e',
