VALUES (
    '29167571', '11432819', 'PRIMARY DIAGNOSIS/ES: -Acute Pancreatitis -Acute on Chronic Kidney Injury due to pre-renal azotemia  SECONDARY DIAGNOSIS/ES: -Pancreatic Pseudocysts, chronic -Hypoglycemia due to poor intake -Pancytopenia, chronic -History of primary sclerosing cholangitis status post liver  transplant -Hepatitis C, genotype 1a -Chronic Kidney Disease -Hypertension', 'PANCREATITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via observation admit for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute pancreatitis.', 'Ms ___ is a ___ yo F with PMHx of PSC s/p liver tx in ___  c/b acute moderate allograft rejection on triple  immunosuppression, untreated HCV, CKD who was transferred from  ___ to the ED on ___ with abdominal pain  and vomiting.  Patient reports being in usual state of health until ___  ___, when she started to feel a mild but sharp epigastric pain.  She noted a loss of appetite and tried to sleep it off. The next  morning she woke up with pain that was about 10x worse. It would  radiate throughout her torso, especially to her back. She  vomited trying to eat and even drink water.  She was brought to her local hospital where she was told she had  an issue with her pancreas and would be transferred to ___ due  to her history of liver transplant.   With recent admission ___ for E coli UTI and elevated LFTs  and Cr thought to be due to medication non-compliance.  In the ED, initial vitals were:  98.1 70 158/101 18 98% RA  - Exam notable for:  abdominal pain - Labs notable for:  elevated lipase, cr 2.1, wbc 2.9, alb 3.2,  mild transaminitis and low tacro level, both of which improved - Imaging was notable for:  edema and pseudocysts in pancreas,  normal appearing liver transplant - Hepatology was consulted and admission to ___ service  was recommended - Patient was given:  home meds, IV Ativan x 1 IV dilaudid  titrated to pain control, IVF.  - ED course complicated by hypoglycemia ___ AM prompting  addition of D5 to her IVF fluids. She remains NPO on transfer to  the floor.  - Vitals prior to transfer:  85 140/92 20 100% RA    Upon arrival to the floor, patient reports pain controlled with  IV dilaudid but persists between doses. Her pain is overall  better and she feels hungry but would like to wait for the  morning to eat.  She denies f/c/n/v/dysuria/diarrhea/rash. She denies sick  contacts. No recent EtOH.', '- Primary Sclerosing Cholangitis s/p liver transplant - Asthma   Social History: ___ Family History: Per OMR: -Father died from cancer in ___, primary unknown, DM -No FH liver disease', '[VITALS] Temp: 98.3 BP: NA HR: 186 O2Sat: 98 Weight: NA  [EXAM] ADMISSION EXAM: Vital Signs:  98.3 186 / 104 64 18 98 Ra  General: Alert, oriented, no acute distress   HEENT: Sclerae anicteric, MMM, oropharynx clear, EOMI, PERRL.   Neck: Supple CV: Regular rate and rhythm. Normal S1+S2, no murmurs, rubs,  gallops.   Lungs: Clear to auscultation bilaterally Abdomen: Well healed surgical scars. Soft, non-tender, slightly  distended, bowel sounds present, no organomegaly, no rebound or  guarding   GU: No foley   Ext: Warm, well perfused, 2+ pulses, no clubbing, cyanosis or  edema   Neuro: Grossly intact',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
