VALUES (
    '26877856', '11436948', 'Acute appendicitis', 'APPENDICITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via direct observation for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute appendicitis.', 'Ms. ___ ("___") is ___ presenting with acute onset abdominal pain. The patient was in her usual state of health until yesterday evening when she developed acute onset abdominal pain following a meal of ___ food. She had six episodes of non-bloody non-bilious emesis, diarrhea and chills. She  presented to the ED for evaluation. Since last night, the pain has  worsened and localized to the RLQ. She continues to have chills and emesis.  She denies urinary symptoms, vaginal bleeding, constipation. She denies chest pain/shortness of breath.', 'Past Medical History: N/A   Past Surgical History: N/A     Social History: ___ Family History: noncontributory', '[VITALS] Temp: 98.0 BP: NA HR: 94 O2Sat: 70 Weight: NA  [EXAM] Admission  Vitals: T98.0, HR94 BP110/70 RR16 98% RA  GEN: A&O, NAD HEENT: No scleral icterus, mucus membranes moist CV: RRR, No M/G/R PULM: Clear to auscultation b/l, No W/R/R ABD: Soft, distended, tender to palpation in right upper and right lower quadrants with rebound, (-)psoas sign Ext: No ___ edema, ___ warm and well perfused',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
    clinicalcaseid, patientid, title, type,
    description, symptom, medicalhistory, pe,
    status, createdBy
)
VALUES (
    '26837038', '11437257', 'pancreatitis', 'PANCREATITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via observation admit for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute pancreatitis.', '___ female with a history of obesity, sleep apnea,  seizure disorder going to see Neuro today, hypertension, DVT  status post six months of warfarin, chronic renal  failure(baseline Cr 1.9-2.1), incontinence of both urine and  stool who is here for chronic N/V/D.  Reports about a 6 month history of persistent NBNB vomitus with  eating or drinking. Additionally reports concomitant loose  watery brown, non bloody, non-mucous diarrhea. These happen  intermittently. Of note today, she had sharp abdominal pain  intermittently for 2 hours this morning. It has since resolved.  Has endorsed chills/rigors, and tactile fevers only (no measured  temps at home). She has been evaluated as outpatient by PCP but  no formal GI evaluation, endoscopy or colonoscopy per our  records though she thinks she may have had a colonoscopy in the  last year. No CT imaging of abdomen since ___.   She reports no new medications. She does endorse about 30 pounds  of weight loss in two months and stating clothes are looser  fitting, however this is not supported by her OMR record. Her  daughter has noticed this as well. She states her stools are  loose and cannot comment on ___ colored, however she does  endorse "chocolate colored urine." She states this urine does  not dilute with increased oral intake of water. Denies pruritis.  No dysuria, hematuria. Chronic incontinence of urine, not taking  oxybutynin at home.  In the ED, initial vitals were:   98.2 89 172/59 18 99% RA    ED Exam notable for tremulous, but stable. AOx3 anicteric sclera. dry oral MM RRR. Soft SEM I/VI (possibly flow) Neg CVA obese. +bs. non distended. Mid epigastric tenderness w/moderate  palpation.  Labs notable for lipase 231, Alk phos 142 of LDH 451, Na 147, Cl  112, bicarb 21, BUN 39, Cr2.0(at baseline), Ca, lactate wnl AST/ALT, Tbili, albumin, lactate wnl; H/H at baseline, no  leukocytosis  Imaging notable for: CT Abd/pelvis pending  Patient was given: 1L NS, declined zofran   On the floor, the patient has no complaints. She states she has  not had consistent abdominal pain or diarrhea since visiting  emergency department. She is hungry and requests dinner.', 'SEIZURE DISORDER MITRAL REGURGITATION SLEEP APNEA/NARCOLEPSY  LVH URINARY INCONTINENCE DVT ___ s/p 6 mos warfarin CKD, arteriosclerosis on biopsy   Social History: ___ Family History: no family GI cancer', '[VITALS] Temp: 98.1 BP: NA HR: 147 O2Sat: 98 Weight: NA  [EXAM] Admission: VS:  98.1PO 147 / 52 72 18 100 ra  Gen:  obese female, comfortable appearing NAD in bed HEENT:  MMM, no sceral icterus, PERRLA CV:  RRR, nl s1, s2, ___ systolic ejection murmur,  Pulm: limited by habitus, CTAB no wheezes Abd: ttp to epigastric area, soft, NABS, no HSM appreciated, no  rebound or guarding GU: no foley Ext: trace edema to B/L extremities, DP pulses intact b/l  Skin:  chronic appearing skin changes to ___ b/l Neuro:  A&Ox3, impaired attention, cannot spell world backwards Psych:  appropriate, affect cheery',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
    clinicalcaseid, patientid, title, type,
    description, symptom, medicalhistory, pe,
    status, createdBy
)
VALUES (
    '21216421', '11438173', 'PRIMARY ======= Cholecystitis  SECONDARY ========= Ileus', 'CHOLECYSTITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute gallbladder disease.', '___ with significant cardiac history (syncope Mobitz II block ; V paced; last interrogation ___, HTN, PVD, abdominal aortic  aneurysm, and ___ disease who presented for evaluation  of sudden onset epigastric abdominal pain that woke him up from  sleep with associated nausea and vomiting x2.   The pain, described as dull and twisting, did not radiate to the  back or pelvis and was ___ at its worst. It is now described as  a throbbing diffuse pain over the abdomen. The patient''s wife  reports that he had a prior episode of similar pain 2 weeks ago  which subsided spontaneously. Of note, the patient has a known  infrarenal AAA, last imaged via US in ___, measuring 4.2 x 3.8  cm. States that he currently feels comfortable, with dull pain.  Denies chest pain or difficulty breathing, changes in bowel  habits. Denies fevers, chills, or cough. No dysuria or  hematochezia. No lightheadedness, headache or dizziness.  In the ED: initial VS Temp 97.6 HR 66 BP 161/76 RR 22 100% RA  - Exam: comfortable with minor ttp at epigastrum. "On  reevaluation, he was tachypneic, and uncomfortable due to  respiratory status, however was with good O2 sat." - Labs: "elev wbc (16.4), AST 65, ALT WNL, lipase 63, lactate  3.1." - Studies: EKG w vpaced rhythm. CXR w "Multifocal patchy  opacities, most prominent in the lingula.  This may reflect  pneumonia versus sequela of aspiration." - Interventions: Vanc/Zosyn, 1L NS, morphine 2mg, Tylenol - Consults: Vascular Surgery: "paged given known AAA. bedside  ultrasound with ?dissection (although this doesn''t change  management as blood pressure control is care). they agree with  ultrasounds and micu admit."  On arrival to the MICU, he is comfortable and recounts the  history above. He denies fevers, chills, night sweats, weight  loss, chest discomfort, palpitations, current abdominal pain,  current nausea/vomiting, diarrhea/constipation, focal neuro sxs.  No recent abx, hospitalizations, unusual travel, unusual food,  or sick contacts. No one else is unwell. He denies any lower  urinary tract symptoms, hx of urinary stones, or dysuria.   Review of systems:   As above', '- Coronary artery disease status post CABG x 4 in ___ - LIMA to LAD, SVG to D1 (occluded), SVG to OM1/OM4 (jump segment patent), status post DES to the OM vein graft in ___, status post DESx2 to the RCA vein graft in ___ - Hypertension. - Dyslipidemia ___ - TC 14, ___ 113, HD 32, LD 87). - Dilated ascending aorta ___ cm by TTE). - Abdominal aortic aneurysm with a family history of aortic rupture ___ cm). - Peripheral vascular disease (mild bilateral tibial disease). - Recurrent syncope last ___ - Mobitz I second-degree block, prolonged PR interval and left anterior hemiblock. Decision made to proceed with ___ Sensia single-chamber pacemaker with Dr. ___ on ___. - Hypercholesterolemia - Pernicious Anemia  - Tubular adenomas in colon  - BPH - s/p TURP - Testicular nodule - trigeminal neuralgia - Memory loss / Dementia - Hearing loss - Appendectomy - Stroke (MRA neck ___ neg) - Parkinsons - ?pulmonary fibrosis   Social History: ___ Family History: Sister w/ breast CA, no family history of colon/prostate CA. 2  brothers w/ aneurysms. No CAD or known heart disease', '[VITALS] Temp: 95.0 BP: 138/70 HR: 138 O2Sat: 70 Weight: NA  [EXAM] ADMISSION  Vitals: BP: 138/70 P:95 R: 18 O2: 97%   GEN: A&O, moderate distress CV: RRR (paced) PULM: Decreased breath sounds bilaterally with bibasilar fine  crackles ABD: Soft, non distended, TTP epigastrium, lower abdomen  bilaterally and RUQ, no pulsatile mass appreciated. ___  sign',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


