    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with diverticular disease.', '___ with history of breast ca now remission p/w 1 week of  worsening lower abdominal pain. Pain localized to lower abdomen,  L>R and described as colicky and crampy abdominal pain. She  initially attributed pain to excessive gas pains but continued  to feel distended/bloated. Reports poor oral intake during this week. Pain worsened with oral intake and limited to bland diet.   BM initially loose but now hard. Denies fever, chills, dysuria,  diarrhea, n/v.   Last colonoscopy was ___, per reports, sigmoid diverticulosis  was noted. Reports 3 lb weight loss this week due to limited PO  intake. All other ROS negative.', 'PMH: - Right mucinous cystadenoma s/p oophorectomy ___ Retinal detachment - ___ hospitalized with erythema multiforme, unclear trigger - Osteopenia ___ BMD, Ca/D  Oncologic history: ___ left breast cancer s/p lumpectomy/SNB; grade 2 ILC 1.5 cm, ER/PR+, HER2 neg, neg SNB (___). Adjuvant RT, anastrozole ___ - ___ All: sulfa, bactrim    Social History: ___ Family History: mother ___, father prostate ca, no h/o colon ca', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 127/74 HR: NA O2Sat: 99 Weight: NA  [EXAM] On admission -  Vitals: 99.5 72 127/74 16 98% RA  Gen: pleasant, NAD Lungs: unlabored Cardio: RRR Abd: soft with slight distention, ___ incision intact, tender to suprapubic abdomen, L>R, TTP at lower quadrants. No guarding, non-peritoneal rect: no blood, no masses Ext: wnl',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


