    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute appendicitis.', '___ with 12-hour history of abdominal pain.  He had a normal colonoscopy yesterday with removal of two small polyps in the ascending colon.  He felt fine post-procedure, then developed vague abdominal pain this morning.  His pain worsened throughout the day, and he presented to the ED for evaluation.  He denies nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, constipation, fever, chills, chest  pain, dyspnea or syncope.', '- bicuspid AV - AV endocarditis ___ with strep viridans after dental cleaning treated w/ 6 wks pen/gent, endocarditis (no valvular lesion)  with step mutans - Polymyalgia in ___ rheumatic ___ years ago w/ steroids for a  year - HTN - AR and MR - Hypercholesterolemia - R tib-fib fracture repair ___    Social History: ___ Family History: Mother -breast ca early ___ Father -died of cerebral ___ age ___, high bp, obesity, smoking Children: 2. One daughter with ___ syndrome', '[VITALS] Temp: 98.1 BP: 129/45 HR: 68 O2Sat: 98 Weight: NA  [EXAM] On admission:  Vitals: T 98.1, HR 68, BP 129/45, RR 14, O2 100%  Gen: a&o x3, nad CV: rrr, no murmur Resp: cta bilat Abd: soft, minimally ttp, ND, +BS; -obturator, +psoas sign Extr: warm, well-perfused, 2+ pulses DRE: normal tone, no gross or occult blood',
