VALUES (
    '25695876', '11474392', 'Perforated diverticulitis', 'DIVERTICULITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via urgent for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with diverticular disease.', 'Mrs. ___ is a ___ year old female transferred from OSH after  presenting ___ w weakness and diarrhea.  She reports being too  weak to climb out of the tub for approximately 4h until she was found by her son last night.  She  complains of roughly 2 months of diarrhea associated with fecal  incontinence alternating with constipation; she also noticed  occasional bright red blood on the toilet paper.  She was seen  by a gastroenterologist, who felt she had hemorrhoids, and recommended a colonoscopy.  Ms. ___ was taken by her son to ___ where her WBC was 17, and  troponin 0.975 / MB 9.5.  She had a new LBBB on EKG there, which  was new from prior exams at ___.  Shortly after admission, she  complained of new abdominal pain, and a subsequent abdominal CT  revealed "sigmoid perforation with diffuse peritonitis."   When  a surgical consultant recommended colectomy, the patient was  transferred to ___ at the request of her family.  Per OSH  records, she was receiving vancomycin, zosyn, and flagyl.   Tm102.   NPO.  She has never had a colonoscopy.', 'Past Medical History:  CAD s/p MI, DES 04, HTN, DM2, neuropathy, paroxysmal atrial tachycardia, GERD, HLD  Past Surgical History:  back surgery ___    Social History: ___ Family History: Denies.', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 143/57 HR: NA O2Sat: 99 Weight: NA  [EXAM] On admission:  Vitals:  99.1 74 143/57 15 93% 2L NC GEN: A&Ox3, perseverating on antibiotic prescriptions, cooperative, NAD HEENT: No scleral icterus, mucus membranes dry CV: RRR, +systolic murmur PULM: Diminished bilaterally ABD: Softly distended, no peritoneal signs, focal tenderness to deep palpation in the LLQ.  Palpable stool-filled colon. DRE: Normal tone, +external hemorroids; hard stool in the rectal vault.  No gross blood but occult positive. Ext: Trace bilateral ___ edema.  Warm.',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


