    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with diverticular disease.', 'This is a ___ year old previously healthy female who presents  with abdominal pain, and low grade fever of two days duration.   .   Her symptoms started ___ days ago. She initially had abdominal  and pelvic cramping, and then developed diffuse abdominal pain,  which later laterazed to the LLQ. The pain was sharp and severe.  It did not radiate. She also noted elevated temperatures (>100.  + nausea/-vomiting. She has been constipated for the past 4  days. She denied vomiting, diarrhea, hematochezia, dysuria,  recent sexual activity, rash or joint pain. She recently  returned from a cruise to ___, but none of her family members  that traveled with her are experiencing similar symptoms. No  history of similar episodes.  .   She presented to the ED and her initial vitals were: ___ Family History: none', '', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 114/75 HR: NA O2Sat: 97 Weight: NA  [EXAM] Vitals: 97 114/75 87 18 100RA   General: Awake, alert, NAD, pleasant, appropriate, cooperative.    HEENT: NCAT, PERRL, EOMI, no scleral icterus, MMM, no lesions  noted in OP   Neck: supple Pulmonary: Lungs CTA bilaterally, no wheezes, rhonchi or rales   Cardiac: RR, nl S1 S2, no murmurs, rubs or gallops appreciated   Abdomen: soft, ND, normoactive bowel sounds, no masses or  organomegaly noted. TTP at LLQ quadrant, no rebound/guarding Extremities: No edema, 2+ radial, DP pulses b/l   Skin: no rashes or lesions noted.   Neurologic: Alert, oriented x 3. Cranial nerves II-XII grossly  intact.',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


