VALUES (
    '21317138', '11494934', 'PRIMARY DIAGNOSIS: ================== Acute gangrenous cholecystitis  SECONDARY DIAGNOSES: ==================== Tachycardia-bradycardia syndrome Encephalopathy Dementia Hypertension Atrial fibrillation Atrial flutter', 'CHOLECYSTITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via observation admit for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute gallbladder disease.', '___ history of atrial fibrillation on xarelto, L left basal ganglia infarct ___ (presumed cardioembolic ___ poor  adherence to xarelto), with residual R sided hemiparesis and mild  dementia, who presents for altered mental status.   Per patient''s wife, the patient has not been himself since  ___ afternoon. She noticed the patient was fatigued with decreased appetite. She says he has also been weak upon standing and less coordinated, now walking with a shuffling gait. Also reports one episode of urinary incontinence on morning of presentation which is new for him. Given concern for altered mental status, his  wife and granddaughter brought him into the ED.  On arrival in the ED, patient agrees that he has been weaker  than normal at home, and had to have his wife and granddaughter help him out of bed this morning, which is new. He also endorses new  R sided rib and right upper abdominal pain since ___. He says the rib pain is pleuritic, sharp, and intermittent. He is unable to described the abdominal pain, but denies nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, constipation. Otherwise, no shortness of breath, chest pain. Has chronic cough, but that is baseline per wife. No fevers/chills. No changes in bowel movements, urinary symptoms. No recent falls/trauma. No headaches or changes in vision.   In the ED, initial VS were: T: 99.7, HR: 80, BP: 139/63, RR: 16, 98% RA   Exam notable for: AAOx3, EOMI, PERRL, ___ strength right side (chronic), ___ left side, LT sensation grossly intact all 4 extremities  ECG: Sinus rhythm, rate 82bpm, PACs, RBBB morphology, no ST/T wave changes.   TELEMETRY: Intermittent bursts of atrial fibrillation vs. atrial flutter and sinus tach to 130s. Also with episodes of sinus bradycardia to ___ with pauses. Patient asymptomatic both in tachyarrythmias and bradyarrythmias. Most consistent with sick sinus syndrome.  Labs showed: - WBC 31.7 (83.5% PMNs) - HgB 13.9, Hct 41.2, Plt 201   - Lactate: 2.1 - UA: neg leuks, neg nitrites, few bacteria - Trop <0.01 x 2 - BUN 26, Cr 1.3 (baseline 1.0) - ___: 22.7, PTT 33.6, INR 2.1 - Elevated Tbili at 2.4 - ALT 12, AST 20, AP 84  - Lipase PND - TSH: 1.1 - Blood and urine cultures PND  Imaging showed:   CT HEAD: No acute intracranial process. CXR: Bibasilar atelectasis. No large effusion or consolidation worrisome for infection.   Consults: None  Patient received:  ___ 15:42 IVF  NS 1000 mL     ___ 17:05 IV CefePIME 2g  ___ 17:46 IV Vancomycin  ___ 18:13 IVF  NS 1000mL  ___ 18:15 PO Acetaminophen 1000 mg   ___ 18:53 PO Diltiazem 30 mg    Transfer VS were: T: 98.2, BP: 137/92, HR: 120, RR: 20, 92% RA   On arrival to the floor, patient is AAOx3, able to do days of week backwards. Only complaint is R sided rib pain and RUQ abdominal pain. Otherwise, no fevers/chills, shortness of  breath, chest pain. No N/V/D. No urinary symptoms. Unable to reach wife for collateral history.', 'HYPERTENSION                                                     PAROXYSMAL ATRIAL FIBRILLATION                                   CHADS SCORE 2 = HTN and Age                                      DYSPNEA                                                          ASTHMA                                                          COLON ADENOMA                                       H/O BACK PAIN                                                    H/O GOUT                                                         H/O SHOULDER PAIN                                                H/O BILATERAL CATARACTS                                          H/O PROSTATE CANCER                                              ___: s/p brachy- under care of dr ___ annual visits with dr   ___ (implanted device)        Social History: ___ Family History: Mother    ___  ___  HYPERTENSION                             Father    Unknown                                                Uncle     ___  ___  CORONARY ARTERY DISEASE', '[VITALS] Temp: 98.5 BP: 147/99 HR: 155 O2Sat: NA Weight: NA  [EXAM] ADMISSION  ======================== VS: ___ 0235 Temp: 98.5 PO BP: 147/99 R Lying HR: 155 RR:  20 O2 sat: 93% O2 delivery: Ra  GENERAL: NAD, AAOx3, able to ___ backwards  HEENT: AT/NC, anicteric sclera, MMM   NECK: supple, no LAD   CV: Irregular rate, tachycardic, no murmurs, gallops, or rubs   PULM: CTAB, no wheezes, rales, rhonchi, breathing comfortably without use of accessory muscles   GI: abdomen soft, nondistended, tender to palpation in the RUQ,  + ___ sing, no rebound/guarding, no hepatosplenomegaly   EXTREMITIES: no cyanosis, clubbing, or edema   PULSES: 2+ radial pulses bilaterally   NEURO: Alert, moving all 4 extremities with purpose, face symmetric. EOMI, PERRL, ___ strength right side (chronic), ___ left side, sensation grossly intact all 4 extremities.  DERM: warm and well perfused, no excoriations or lesions, no rashes',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


