INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
    clinicalcaseid, patientid, title, type,
    description, symptom, medicalhistory, pe,
    status, createdBy
)
VALUES (
    '20119824', '11526031', 'Primary diagnosis:  -pancreatitis presumed secondary to a spontaneously passed CBD  stone  Secondary diagnosis:  -Hypertension  -History of POTS', 'PANCREATITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via urgent for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute pancreatitis.', 'Ms. ___ is a ___ female with hx of arrhythmia, known heart  murmur, and cholelithiasis s/p cholecystectomy on ___ who  presents as a transfer for epigastric and substernal chest pain  from ___.    The patient recently underwent a laparoscopic cholecystectomy at  ___ for cholelithiasis diagnosed incidentally during evaluation  for nephrolithiasis. Was having intermittent nausea, so  underwent elective cholecystectomy on ___. Tolerated the  procedure well and recovered without difficulty. Since ___  ___, has had intermittent nausea, vomiting and nonbloody  diarrhea. Denies any fevers/chills. Initially without abdominal  pain. On ___ at 10 am developed acute onset ___ epigastric  pain with radiation to her mid chest. Associated with shortness  of breath. Has never had this kind of pain before. Pain started  after she was vomiting. Denies BRBPR or melena. No hematemesis.  Denies fevers. She presented to ___ for further  evaluation.    While at ___, labs were notable for Sodium 137, Cre 0.8,  Tbili 1.5, Dbili 0.5, AST/ALT 270/164, AP 103, Trop I 0.11,  Lipase 345, WBC 8.3, H/H 13.2/39.3. RUQ U/S with borderline  intrahepatic and extrahepatic bile ducts without definite  filling defect. She was given ertapenem 1g IV x 1, morphine IV x  1, and transferred to ___ for evaluation by possible ERCP to  look for retained stone.    In the ED, initial vitals were: 98.1 57 135/72 14 100% RA    - Exam notable for: epigastric tenderness to palpation    - Labs notable for: lactate 0.8, Cre 0.8, K 3.3, trop <0.01,  ALT/AST 221/227, AP 113, Tbili 0.7, WBC 4.5    - Patient was given: 1L NS x 1, started on LR at 100cc/hr, and  given morphine 4mg IV x 1, and ondansetron 4mg IV x 1    - Vitals prior to transfer: 3 97.8 58 124/71 15 98% RA     Upon arrival to the floor, patient reports that overall her pain  has improved. Continues to report ___ epigastric, SSCP.  Associated with nausea. No BRBPR or melena. No shortness of  breath.    REVIEW OF SYSTEMS:    (+) Per HPI    (-) 10 point ROS reviewed and negative unless stated above in  HPI', 'Hypertension    Hyperlipidemia    Hypothyroidism    Palpitations   POTS followed by Dr. ___ at ___ q6 months  Cardiac murmur    Nephrolithiasis    s/p cholecystectomy for gallstones  (performed at ___    Social History: ___ Family History:  Brother with lung cancer    Brother with melanoma of the eye requiring resection    Son died from ?colon/liver cancer in his ___', '[VITALS] Temp: 97.7 BP: NA HR: 151 O2Sat: 97 Weight: NA  [EXAM] =========================== ADMISSION PHYSICAL  ===========================  Vital Signs: 97.7PO 151 / 88 58 16 98 RA    General: Alert, oriented, no acute distress    HEENT: Sclerae anicteric, dry mucous membranes, PERRL    Neck: Supple. JVP not elevated. no LAD    CV: Bradycardic, II/VI systolic murmur heard across precordium     Lungs: Clear to auscultation bilaterally, no wheezes, rales,  rhonchi    Abdomen: Soft, epigastric tenderness and chest wall tenderness  to palpation; no rebound or guarding; well-healed abdominal  incisions.    GU: No foley    Ext: Warm, well perfused, 2+ pulses, no clubbing, cyanosis or  edema    Neuro: CNII-XII grossly intact; moving all four extremities;  sensation intact    ===========================',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


