    'A patient was admitted via observation admit for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute gallbladder disease.', '___ year-old female with past medical history of prosthetic  mitral ___, on warfarin, congestive heart failure,  hypertension, yperlipidemia, diabetes presenting with dyspnea  and abdominal pain. SOB has been ongoing for 2 weeks and has  been getting worse. Notabyl this is associated with orthopnea  requiring 5 pillows from 2 pillows previously. Also reports  weight has increased and reports worsening ___ edema. She does  report compliance with all of her medications but did not take  her home torsemide on the day of admission.    She has also been complaining of RUQ pain that has been also  ongoing for days. She initially associated it with food but is  now constant. Reports early satiety as well. Reports  intermittent constipation and diarrhea. Has been nauseous but no  vomiting.    She went to her PCP (referral on ED dash) for an outpatient  routine follow-up visit. She was found to be dyspneic with  concern for volume overload. Her PCP referred her to the ED for  further evaluation.', '- Severe MR: s/p mechanical MVR in ___.    - Atrial fibrillation s/p DCCV ___    - Hypertension    - Hyperlipidemia    - Diabetes, type 2    - Hyperthyroidism    - Anxiety    - Asthma    - CHF with EF 43%    - GERD      Social History: ___ Family History: Family history is significant for brother with CAD in his ___.  Her grandmother died of coronary artery disease when she was  elderly. Reports family history of hypertension.', '[VITALS] Temp: 97.5 BP: NA HR: 137 O2Sat: 97 Weight: NA  [EXAM] Admission exam: =============== VS: 97.5 137 / 81 48 24 95    Gen: middle aged female, uncomfortable appearing, tachypneic    HEENT: MMM, no scleral icterus, PERRL, EOMI. JVD to jaw    CV: RRR, normal S1, S2. +S3 with mechanical mitral sound.    Pulm: Rales in bases bilaterally; decreased BS bilaterally, no  wheeze or rhonchi    Abd: soft, ND, RUQ TTP +Murphys. No appreciable ascites    GU: no foley    Ext: 2+ pitting edema to knee bilaterally    Skin: no rash    Neuro: CNII-XII intact, ___ strength in UE and ___ bilaterally,  normal sensation to touch in UE and ___. Gait deferred.',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


