VALUES (
    '25121224', '11532808', 'Primary: Pancreatitis Lymphoma  Secondary: Paroxysmal Atrial Fibrillation  Rectal Hemorrhoids Sleep apnea on CPAP', 'PANCREATITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute pancreatitis.', 'Mr ___ is a ___ year old male with a history of recurrent large  cell lymphoma status post nonmyeloblative allogeneic stem cell  transplant from sibling donor (now Day 200+) who is admitted for  workup of FDG-avid pancreas and elevated lipase. The pt states  that over the past few weeks he has had mild abdominal pain, and  over the past few days the pain has intensified in the LLQ with  some nausea. The pt denies vomiting. He is unsure if the pain is  related to eating, but does note that this morning he had to  stop eating breakfast secondary to abdominal pain and nausea.', 'ONC HISTORY: Recurrent large cell lymphoma.   -Found to have mesenteric mass ___ during workup after a fall    from a tree. Biopsy ___ revealed mixed lymphocytes, CD19/20 +,    CD5 -, CD10 weakly positive, BCL-2/BCL-6 positive. PET scan   demonstrated uptake in the abdomen and rectal area.   -Underwent R-CHOP * 6 (___) with complete remission. PET   scan in ___ demonstrated recurrent disease (L retrocrural area    2.5 cm c SCV 8.8 c/w lymphomatous recurrence).   -Treated with R-ICE ___ and then had a second cycle of R-ICE    ___, autologous BMT ___. PET scan ___ showed   resolution of lesion in L retrocrual area, but repeat PET   ___ suggested recurrence.   -received radiation therapy to retrocrural area of disease,   which has been his prior site of involvement   -followup scan, however, showed a new lymph node in periaortic   area that was PET-avid. He underwent a cycle of Navelbine and   Gemzar, complicated by aflutter (s/p cardioversion).   -PET on ___ showed increased avidity in celiac node   concerning for progression of disease   - Received ESHAP on ___   .   PAST MEDICAL HISTORY:   - PE diagnosied in ___, was on coumadin   - Paroxysmal Atrial Fibrillation - was on digoxin. Then on   metoprolol. One episode in the setting of caffeine intake +   adderrall use. Developed again in setting of Gemzar, s/p 2 weeks    of anticoagulation   -Low Testosterone - Presented with muscle weakness, improved   with testosterone injections. Injections discontinued secondary    to elevated LFTs and lymphoma   -GERD   -Rectal Hemorrhoids   -Sleep apnea on CPAP -   -Elevated LFTs, elevated CPK - Had been seen by Dr. ___. He   was concerned that chronically elevated CPK may represent muscle    etiology ___ IM injections of testosterone. However, liver   biopsy ___ showed mild steatosis without balloon degeneration /    intracellular hyalin, and mild portal/lobular mononuclear cell   inflammation. Chronically elevated CPK is not currently   explained as far as we can find.      Social History: ___ Family History: Mother with ovarian cancer. Brother died of esophageal cancer.', '[VITALS] Temp: 98.1 BP: NA HR: NA O2Sat: 98 Weight: NA  [EXAM] VS 98% RA BP158/86 86 P 20 RR T 98.1   GEN: NAD, well appearing, obese male   HEENT: Eyes anicteric, OP clear, moist, without lesions, no   palpable ___, thick neck, JVP flat   CV: RRR, no MRG   PULM: CTAB no w/r/r   ABD:obese, soft, tender diffusely to deep palpation   EXT: 2+ pitting edema bilateral ___   NEURO: AOx3 CNs intact, strength ___ UE and ___, sensation  symmetric, coordination intact, gait normal, mood/affect  appropriate   SKIN: No rash, no lesions. Midline incision scar on abdomen.',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
    clinicalcaseid, patientid, title, type,
    description, symptom, medicalhistory, pe,
    status, createdBy
)
VALUES (
    '20849847', '11533366', 'Acute pancreatitis Acute renal failure Toxic metabolic encephalopathy (confusion) COPD', 'PANCREATITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute pancreatitis.', 'Ms. ___ is a ___ with a past medical history of CHF, Afib,  COPD, CKD III, RA, HTN, HLD, breast ca, lung ca, and tracheal  ca, who who presents w/ nausea, vomiting, chest pain and  lethargy.   Pt was somnolent on arrival and all history was obtained from  her son/HCP. At baseline, pt lives at home, she is able to walk  with a walker. She is A+Ox3. 1d prior pt went to church and ate  at ___. Shortly thereafter, she developed nausea and  vomiting. Per family, breathing was labored. Pt also endorsed  CP, but this is difficult to clarify with family. In addition,  she endorsed feeling warm and having had diarrhea.    In the ED, initial VS: T 97.4 (Tm 99.5) P ___ BP 146/101 R 18  O2 Sat 100% RA. Labs were significant for Cr 2.4, lipase 1250,  UA negative. RUQ US was unremarkable. EKG showed sinus rhythm at  8-bpm, LAD, LBBB, unchanged from prior. CTH showed no acute  anomalies. GI evaluated pt and recommended IVF, NPO, and to hold  off on CT abdomen.   On arrival to the MICU, pt is somnolent and not able to respond  to questions.', '- CHF ___ echo: EF 40-45%, global dyskinesis, LV  hypertrophy, RV dilation, dyssyncrhony) - Afib on coumadin - COPD - CKD (baseline creat 2.0-2.1) - Fibromyalgia/chronic pain syndrome - Osteoarthritis - Rheumatoid arthritis, on narcotics agreement - Asthma  - Bronchomalacia  - Chronic rhinosinusitis  - Hypertension   - Depression   - Hyperlipidemia   - Obesity   - Migraine   - GERD   - Bilateral carpal tunnel syndrome w/ hand weakness   - Spondylolisthesis of L4-5, radiculopathy w/stenosis   - Right total shoulder arthroplasty ___   - Right total knee arthroplasty   - Left shoulder replacement   - Breast cancer stage II (T2N0M0), ___: treated with  lumpectomy, XRT, and CMF. No evidence of recurrent disease.   - Lung SCC stage IA (T1bN0M0), resected on ___    - Tracheal cancer diagnosed in ___ s/p chemo and XRT w/  complete resolution when imaged in ___ and ___ ___ut  residual dysphagia s/p dilatation    Social History: ___ Family History: Mother had breast cancer, died of MI. Father had rectal cancer.', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: NA HR: NA O2Sat: NA Weight: NA  [EXAM] ADMISSION  ========================= General- Somolent; able to answer simple questions with  extensive redirection HEENT- Mild proptosis; pinpoint pupils   Neck- supple, JVP not elevated, no LAD   Lungs- Clear to auscultation bilaterally, no wheezes, rales,  ronchi   CV- Regular rate and rhythm, normal S1 + S2, no murmurs, rubs,  gallops   Abdomen- Obese; voluntary guarding, mild diffuse ttp   GU- +foley Ext- warm, well perfused, 2+ pulses, no clubbing, cyanosis or  edema; s= multiple ___ amputations   Neuro- Moving all extremities spontaneoulsy; CNII-XII grossly  intact',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
    clinicalcaseid, patientid, title, type,
    description, symptom, medicalhistory, pe,
    status, createdBy
)
VALUES (
    '26053830', '11542488', 'Acute uncomplicated diverticulitis', 'DIVERTICULITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with diverticular disease.', 'Ms. ___ is a ___ female with COPD, HTN, recent h/o  NSTEMI, and non-obstructive CAD who presented to the ED with  acute RLQ pain.  At around 16:00 on ___, she developed ___ RLQ pain. Earlier  that day, she was not feeling well - she did not feel like  eating, was slightly nauseated, and felt fatigued. She was  having fevers the day before, as well. No nausea, vomiting, or  changes in bowel movements. No dysuria or hematuria. No chest  pain, shortness of breath, or palpitations. She has been  coughing for months since she was diagnosed with pneumonia in  ___. She gets back pain when she has a coughing spell.  She has never had abdominal pain like this before. No bloody  bowel movements.   On arrival to the floor, she is still having the same RLQ pain  and she is slightly nauseated.', 'COPD Hypertension H/o NSTEMI (___) H/o pneumonia (___) Non-obstructive coronary artery disease (admission for NSTEMI with cath ___   Social History: ___ Family History: No family history of early MI, arrhythmia, cardiomyopathies, or sudden cardiac death.', '[VITALS] Temp: 97.4 BP: 108/70 HR: 62 O2Sat: 62 Weight: NA  [EXAM] ADMISSION EXAM: ==================  VITALS: T97.4, HR 62, BP 108/70, RR 18, SpO2 97% on RA GENERAL: Alert, appears slightly uncomfortable but not in acute  distress EYES: Anicteric, PERRL ENT: mmm, OP clear CV: NR/RR, no m/r/g RESP: Diffuse crackles ABD/GI: Soft, ND, TTP with guarding in the RLQ without rebound  tenderness, normoactive bowel sounds GU: No suprapubic fullness or tenderness to palpation MSK: Neck supple, moves all extremities, strength grossly full  and symmetric bilaterally in all limbs VASC/EXT: No ___ edema, 2+ DP pulses SKIN: No rashes or lesions noted on visible skin NEURO: Alert, oriented, face symmetric, gaze conjugate with  EOMI, moves all limbs  PSYCH: pleasant, appropriate affect',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
    clinicalcaseid, patientid, title, type,
    description, symptom, medicalhistory, pe,
    status, createdBy
)
VALUES (
    '25416816', '11545313', 'Gallstone pancreatitis, status post total gastrectomy Gram negative bacteremia', 'CHOLECYSTITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute gallbladder disease.', '___ yo F with one day of epigastric abdominal pain, nausea, vomiting, and diarrhea. Non-bloody, non-bilious vomitus. Non-bloody, brown, watery diarrhea. A CT scan of the abd/pelvis shows a large, distended gallbladder with a small amount of pericholecystic fluid. US notes the presence of sludge within  the gallbladder, however the patient''s pain is clearly centered over the epigastrium and not in the RUQ.   Her LFTs were elevated as listed below, raising concern for a common duct stone (Tbili 1.6, baseline 0.3-0.5), and transaminitis concerning for perhaps some other primary liver disease. Her lipase is elevated, though, which could account for the n/v/d and abdominal pain.', 'Type ___ DM--diagnosed in ___, diet controlled   HTN   Left breast CA s/p lumpectomy and ___   Gastric cancer--Stage III, s/p gastrectomy ___   GERD   osteoporosis   arthritis   tinnitus   Fe deficient anemia   cataract      Social History: ___ Family History: Her mother died at age ___ from an unspecified cancer. Her father  died at ___ of "natural causes". No family history of CAD, but  sister has Type ___ DM.', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 107/47 HR: NA O2Sat: 99 Weight: NA  [EXAM] 99.6  90  107/47  24  982L NAD, lying comfortably in bed RRR CTA B S/ND/tender in the epigastrium  WWP',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
    clinicalcaseid, patientid, title, type,
