    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with diverticular disease.', 'Pt is an ___ with no significant ___ who presents with acute onset RLQ abdominal pain x12h.  Pt states that yesterday afternoon, after lunch, she developed pain that extended across her lower abdomen. She describes the pain as a "soreness".  The LLQ pain resolves and remained localized to the RLQ.  She states it hurts to move.  She had her last BM the previous day.  SHe  has not passed flatus since yesterday AM.  She denies nausea, change in appetite, diarrhea, constipation, hematochezia or melena, fevers or chills.  She has never had pain like this before.  She has never had a colonoscopy.', 'Past Medical History: HTN, HLD, anxiety, ?COPD, vertigo on lying flat, IBD  Past Surgical History:  L mastectomy for breast ca (___), multiple throat polyps removed    Social History: ___ Family History: Family History:  Denies hx GI malignancy or inflammatory bowel disease', '[VITALS] Temp: 97.6 BP: 177/87 HR: 90 O2Sat: 97 Weight: NA  [EXAM] VS: T 97.6; HR 90; BP 177/87-->140/60; RR 16;  POx 100% RA GEN: A&O, NAD   HEENT: No scleral icterus, mucus membranes moist   CV: RRR, No M/G/R   PULM: Clear to auscultation b/l, No W/R/R, URT coarse   ABD: Soft, normoactive bowel sounds, no palpable masses, RLQ slightly distended and very TTP with focal guarding and minimal rebound.  Palpation of L U/LQ radiated to RLQ tenderness, RUQ  TTP without rebound or guarding DRE: normal tone, no gross or occult blood, no palpable masses, +external hemorrhoids   Ext: No ___ edema, ___ warm and well perfused, pulses palpable b/l .',
