    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute gallbladder disease.', 'Mrs. ___ is a ___ w/h/o gallstone panc and p/w RUQ pain. Pt  started to vomit(nonbilious, no associated nausea) and  experience RUQ pain 5hrs ago. The pain was ___, constant,  lasting 4hrs. It felt similar to the pain she had with  pancreatitis and cholangitis for which she was hospitalized from  ___ to ___. Her temperature taken at home was 99.6. Pt  also reports diaphoresis and that her "chest felt funny" around  the onset of RUQ pain. She denies chest pain and SOB. Throughout  the day, pt felt fatigued. At present, pt reports pain as  improved.', '-legally blind -afib not on anticoag (fall risk w/blindness) -HLD -angina w/multiple negative workups -Lung cancer with right lower lobe nodule Status post  thoracotomy with right lower lobectomy on ___. Stage  IA or IB. -GERD -retinitis pigmentosa -hypothyroidism    Social History: ___ Family History: The patient states that her mother died in her ___ of unknown  causes.  Her father died in his ___ also of unknown causes.  She  denies any history of colon or gastrointestinal cancer.', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 165/74 HR: NA O2Sat: 100 Weight: NA  [EXAM] On Admission:  Vitals: 100.3, 81, 165/74, 16, 97%RA GEN: A&O, NAD HEENT: No scleral icterus, mucus membranes moist CV: RRR, No M/G/R PULM: Clear to auscultation b/l, No W/R/R ABD: Soft, nondistended, slightly tender, no rebound or guarding,normoactive bowel sounds, no palpable masses, negative ___',
