VALUES (
    '27929956', '11589051', 'Pancreatitis, Acute Eosinophilic esophagitis, gastritis, enteritis IgG Deficiency PUD Steroid Psychosis Anemia', 'PANCREATITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute pancreatitis.', '___ y/o F w/ h/o eosinophilic esophagitis/gastritis, PUD presents  with severe nausea, vomiting, abd pain and hematemesis. She has  had multiple admission ofr n/v/abd pain but claims that this  episode is much worse than before. She has not been able to  eat/drink anything. She has had atleast 5 episodes of  hematemesis in the last 3 days along with ___. She also says  that this time around her epigastric pain is radiating to the  back which is unusual for her. She has been feel very weak and  dizzy for the past few days. . ED: Her vitals were stable. Her HCT was stable. She got a CT Abd  which did not show free air; however evaluation of the bowel,  particularly the posterior wall of the duodenum was limited due  to extensive high density barium.', 'eosinophilic esophagitis/gastritis Peripheral eosinophilia PUD with negative H. pylori Anemia NOS   Social History: ___ Family History: Father with ___.  He also has CAD and PVD.  Mother''s side of  family with breast cancer and ovarian cancer (aunt at age ___.   No FH of celiac.  No FH of leukemia, lymphoma, MEN cancers.', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 98/58 HR: NA O2Sat: 97 Weight: NA  [EXAM] ROS: GEN: - fevers, + Chills, - Weight Loss EYES: - Photophobia, - Visual Changes HEENT: - Oral/Gum bleeding CARDIAC: - Chest Pain, - Palpitations, - Edema GI: + Nausea, + Vomitting, + Abdominal Pain, + Hematemesis, +  ___, - Diarhea Constipation, - Hematochezia, Poor Intake x3 days PULM: - Dyspnea, - Cough, - Hemoptysis HEME: - Bleeding, - Lymphadenopathy GU: - Dysuria, - hematuria, - Incontinence SKIN: - Rash ENDO: - Heat/Cold Intolerance MSK: - Myalgia, - Arthralgia, - Back Pain NEURO: - Numbness, - Weakness, + dizziness, - Vertigo, -  Headache .  VS: 97.4, 98/58, 74, 18, 98%/RA, 239 lbs GEN: appears in mild distress ___ abdominal pain Eyes: PERRLA, EOMI, no conjuctival injection, anicteric Neck: supple ENT: no sinus tenderness, dry MM, op without exudate or lesions,  no supraclavicular or cervical lymphadenopathy Respiratory: CTA bilat, no wheeze or crackles Cardiovascular: RRR, nl S1, S2; ___ SEM at LUSB Gastrointestinal: diffuse tenderness throughout abdomen with  maximal tenderness in epigastric and RUQ region. No  guarding/rigidity elicited. NABS. No masses or  hepatosplenomegaly Musculoskeletal/extremities: no cyanosis, clubbing; trace ___  edema Skin/nails: warm, no rashes/no jaundice/no splinters Neurological: AAOx3.  Cn II-XII intact.  ___ strength  throughout.  No focal neurologic deficits Heme/Lymph: no cervical or supraclavicular lymphadenopathy Back: No CVA tenderness',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


