VALUES (
    '27369388', '11593760', 'cholecystitis', 'CHOLECYSTITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute gallbladder disease.', 'HPI: ___ hx of hypothyroidism (s/p thyroidectomy), GERD, remote PUD, p/w one day of pain in chest/epigastrum which woke up her  up early this morning. The pain radiated around to the back as  well. She concomitantly has had diarrhea today with multiple loose stools of light brown then green color. No bright red blood or dark stools noted. The pt took 2 tylenol which have helped the pain although discomfort is still significant. She ate peanut butter with bread and fruit last night. No chicken, beef, or raw fish. She denied having nausea, vomiting.   She denies a hx of colicky pain, post-prandial pain, or similar episodes. Apparently has had PUD decades ago. Per ED note, pt recently had GI distress ___ colestipol which was then d/c about 10 days ago.', 'HTN, High Cholesterol    Social History: ___ Family History: NC', '[VITALS] Temp: 97.3 BP: 147/90 HR: 75 O2Sat: 97 Weight: NA  [EXAM] upon admission:  ___   Temp: 97.3 HR: 75 BP: 147/90 Resp: 16 O(2)Sat: 99 Normal   Constitutional: Comfortable HEENT: Normocephalic, atraumatic Chest: Clear to auscultation Cardiovascular: Regular Rate and Rhythm Abdominal: Soft, Nontender GU/Flank: No costovertebral angle tenderness Extr/Back: No cyanosis, clubbing or edema Skin: No rash Neuro: Speech fluent Psych: Normal mood  Physical examination',
