    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute gallbladder disease.', '___ w/ hx of recurrent symptomatic cholelithiasis with acute  abdominal pain.  Pain began at 0200, was epigastric in location  then moved to the RUQ with radiation to the back.  Pain was  associated with nausea, vomiting x3 of yellow liquid without  blood, and chills. Pt endorses mild chest pain, similar to her heartburn symptoms. Pt denies fevers, sweats, and SOB.  BM x2  this morning, normal, no blood. Denies urinary symptoms.  Last  food intake was last night at 7 pm, last fluid intake was a sip  of water this morning.', 'PMH: ?GERD lower back pain  PSH: b/l tubal ligation C-section x1    Social History: ___ Family History: noncontributory', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 111/63 HR: 76 O2Sat: 97 Weight: NA  [EXAM] vitals: Tmax:97.2 Tc:98.2 HR:76 BP:111/63 RR:16 SaO2:99% Gen: lying in bed, NAD, moving all extremities CV: RRR, no m/r/g Resp: CTAB, no r/r/w Abd: Soft, Diffuse epigastric pain on palpation, most tender in RUQ. ___ elicits pain but not inspiratory arrest. No  rebound or gaurding, +BS Neuro: AOx3, moving all extremities Ext: +DPP, WWP',
