VALUES (
    '21101590', '11617428', 'Acute appendicitis', 'APPENDICITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute appendicitis.', '___ yo otherwise healthy male with 1 day of gradually worsening  lower abdominal pain. At 4 pm yesterday, he developed a sudden  onset ___ sharp pain midline in the epigastric region. By 11  pm, the location of the pain gradually migrated to the  periumbilical region. The pain was constant and exacerbated by movement and allieved by remaining still and sitting with hips  flexed. He was able to sleep through the night but the pain  persisted the following morning while walking to work and he  presented to the ED. He has had minimal nausea, fever of ___ F,  no vomiting, some loose stool. He denies dysuria, increased urinary freq, back/flank pain. He has noticed a darker color to  his urine but no hematuria.', 'none   Social History: ___ Family History: No h/o abdominal disease in the family', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 116/69 HR: NA O2Sat: 100 Weight: NA  [EXAM] PE on admission: Vitals: 100.8   78   116/69   18   100%   GEN: A&O, NAD CV: RRR PULM: CTAB ABD: soft, non distended, tender to palation in LLQ and RLQ, no masses, negative psoas sign, negative obturator sign DRE: deferred Ext: No ___ edema, ___ warm and well perfused',
