    'A patient was admitted via observation admit for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute gallbladder disease.', '___ with h/o biliary colic 1 month ago presents with RUQ abdominal pain radiating to her back x 12 hours. Pain started at noon, and was severe ___. It was associated with dizziness, nausea and vomiting. It is made worse with PO intake. She has experienced pain like this previously, but she did not seek medical attention and she states that this episode is much  worse. She was febrile earlier today subjectively and upon arrival to the ED her temp was 103.1.  Also of note, she has blanching redness on her left lower extremity. No associated fluctuance, evidence of trauma, abscess or laceration. Area was demarcated. She states that this redness started today.', 'Past Medical History:  Aortic Stenosis Complete Heart Block status post ___ pacemaker Duplicated ureter, left Hypertension Lumbago with sciatica Osteoarthritis Osteoporosis Past Surgical History: Carpal Tunnel Release, ___ Exploratory laparotomy, Total abdominal hysterectomy, Bilateral salpingo-oophorectomy, Right pelvic lymph node resection with Omental biopsy and Cystoscopy, ___ Rectocele repair Past Cardiac Procedures:  s/p ___, Adapta Model Number: ___    Social History: ___ Family History: Father throat cancer Mother ___ - Type II; Hyperlipidemia; Hypertension; Stroke Brother ___ - Type II; Hyperlipidemia; Hypertension Sister ___ - Type II; Hyperlipidemia; Hypertension;  Stroke(2) Son ___ infarction age ___ (reportedly clean coronaries at the time)', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: NA HR: NA O2Sat: NA Weight: NA  [EXAM] GENERAL: AAOx3 NAD   HEENT: NCAT, EOMI, PERRLA, No scleral icterus, mucosa moist CARDIOVASCULAR: R/R/R PULSES: 2+ radial pulses b/l  PULMONARY: CTAB, breathing comfortably on room air   GASTROINTESTINAL: soft, appropriately TTP, no distension. No  guarding, rebound, or peritoneal signs   INCISION/WOUNDS: lap port sites C/D/I, bandages appropriate   EXT/MS/SKIN: No C/C/E  NEUROLOGICAL: strength, and sensation grossly intact',
