VALUES (
    '24449784', '11622905', 'Acute Pancreatitis', 'PANCREATITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via observation admit for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute pancreatitis.', 'PCP:   PCP: ___. ___   _ ________________________________________________________________ HPI:  ___ w/o history of diabetes, CKD from glomerulosclerosis, PUD,  HCV on Zepatier, breast cancer ER-/PR-/HER2+NEU+ p/w two weeks  of BLE swelling (per ED- pt does not report this to author)  which is new for her, one week of epigastric non-radiating abd  pain exacerbated by eating/drinking but not by movement (no  excess EtOH/smoking hx), with a few episodes of NBNB vom but no  diarrhea in the past week.  She presented to PCP today got meds  for gastroenteritis, d/c''d home, then they called her in the ___  and recommended she go to the ER for new acute on chronic CKD,  new BUN/Cr 68/3.55 (nl no higher than 2). No  cough/ST/rhinorrhea. No CP or SoB. No fever. Never had this pain  before. Her epigastric pain is worsened by eating. She has lost  ___ lbs over this last week. No sick contacts. No foreign travel  or trauma.  ttp epigastrium only, no RUQ tenderness BLE swelling 1+ to mid-shins     In ER: (Triage Vitals: 0 98.6 | 100 |137/67 |15 | 99% RA  )  Meds Given: None Fluids given: 1 L IVF Radiology Studies: None consults called: None  .  PAIN SCALE:- ___ abdominal pain worse than before since she was  examined by so many doctors who also ___ her abdomen.   REVIEW OF SYSTEMS: CONSTITUTIONAL:  As per HPI HEENT:  [X] All normal RESPIRATORY:  [X] All normal CARDIAC:  [X] All normal GI:  As per HPI GU:  [X] All normal SKIN:  [X] All normal MUSCULOSKELETAL:  [X] All normal NEURO:  [X] All normal ENDOCRINE:  [X] All normal HEME/LYMPH:  [X] + Chronic easy bruising PSYCH:  [X] All normal All other systems negative except as noted above', '- Breast cancer: ___: self palpated a right breast mass ___: mammogram showed dense breast tissue with a 2.8 cm  oval isodense mass in the right breast slightly lower outer  quadrant, middle depth.  ___: Ultrasound-guided biopsy- the lesion at the 8 to 9:00  position of the right breast 7 cm from the nipple showed  invasive ductal carcinoma, poorly differentiated, involving both  cores and measuring at least 1.5 cm. Ductal carcinoma in situ  was also seen. Lymphovascular invasion was suspected. Biopsy of  the right breast lesion at the 8:00 position 2 cm from the  nipple showed similar findings. Ultrasound-guided core needle  biopsy of the right lymph node showed findings consistent with a  benign lymph node. The invasive carcinoma was estrogen and  progesterone receptors negative and HER-2/neu +3. Subsequent  FISH testing was performed and showed that the patient for  HER-2/neu was amplified (ratio of 7.9) ___: PET-CT showed large intensely FDG avid right breast mass  as well as small FDG avid right axillary nodes and a  multinodular thyroid gland with focal areas of high FDG avidity ___: cycle 1 neoadjuvant chemotherapy using  pertuzumab/trastuzumab/docetaxel ___: admitted to ___ with febrile neutropenia,  abdominal pain; ANC 0; all cultures negative; treated with  empiric antibiotics; CT A/P negative; thought to have possible  gastritis- PPI increased ___: cycle 2 neoadjuvant chemotherapy using  pertuzumab/trastuzumab/docetaxel (25% dose reduction of  taxotere); neulasta administered on ___. - Biospy-proven FSGS (at ___ in ___, Stage 3 CKD (basline Cr  of 1.4-1.9)  - Depression - Peptic ulcer disease - GERD - HCV genotype 1b - not treated; awaiting newer agents - OA - chronic pain   Social History: ___ Family History: Father died of lung cancer in ___.  Brother and sister died  cancer of unknown source in ___.  Brother with diabetes.  No  reported CAD in family.', '[VITALS] Temp: 97.6 BP: 159/65 HR: NA O2Sat: 97 Weight: NA  [EXAM] Admission Exam: Vitals:  T 97.6  P 96  BP 159/65  RR 18  SaO2 100% on RA  CONS: uncomfortable appearing  but does not appear toxic HEENT: ncat anicteric MMM     CV: s1s2 rr no m/r/g   RESP: b/l ae no w/c/r   GI: +bs, soft, + epigastric tenderness ND, no guarding or  rebound   MSK:no c/c/e 2+pulses   SKIN: hyperpigmented macular rash on lateral aspect of RLE   NEURO: face symmetric speech fluent   PSYCH: calm, cooperative   LAD: No cervical LAD',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


