VALUES (
    '21948836', '11654859', 'Cholecystitis', 'OTHER_ABDOMINAL',
    'A patient was admitted via urgent for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with abdominal pathology.', '___ G1P0 at ___ presents to labor and delivery as a transfer  from ___ with cholelithiasis and pancreatitis.  Patient reports epigastric and right upper quadrant pain since  ___. Pain radiates to her back. She also complains of  nausea and vomiting. Denies fever or chills. Denies diarrhea.    Patient initially presented to ___ on ___. She was  admitted for observation and treated with IV Cefoxitin and  Demerol. She was seen by GI and general surg at ___,  recommended MRCP.  Patient requested transfer to ___.  She denies complications with this pregnancy. Denies  contractions, vaginal bleeding, loss of fluid. She reports  active fetal movement.', 'PRENATAL COURSE ___: ___ (2)Labs: O+/Ab- (3)U/S: FFS nl, posterior placenta (4)Testing: no genetic testing  PAST OBSTETRIC HISTORY G1P0  PAST GYNECOLOGIC HISTORY denies h/o abnl pap, STIs, fibroids  PAST MEDICAL HISTORY (___) + MRSA wound cx  PAST SURGICAL HISTORY (___) I&D perirectal abscess   Social History: ___ Family History: mother and grandmother with gallstones s/p cholecystectomy', '[VITALS] Temp: 97.6 BP: 116/62 HR: 80 O2Sat: 97 Weight: NA  [EXAM] VITALS: T 97.6  BP 116/62  HR 80  RR 20 GENERAL: NAD, nonicteric HEART: RRR LUNGS: CTAB ABDOMEN: soft, gravid, mild epigastric and RUQ pain,          no rebound or guarding, no CVAT ___: NT/NE SVE: FT ext os, closed int os, long, firm, post U/S: EFW 688g(64%), BPP ___, nl fluid, vtx  Labs: (at ___ (___) 16.2>29.9<378 lytes nl AST 48 ALT 47 T. bili 2.2 D. bili 1.7 Amylase 164 Lipase 488  (___) AST 34 ALT 43 T bili 0.9 D bili 0.6 Amylase 132 Lipase 118  (at ___ RUQ U/S: cholelithiasis, small amount paracholecystic fluid, slightly thickened gallbladder wall, common bile duct dilated measuring 7.6mm. Normal kidneys, no hydro. Normal pancreas.  (___) RIGHT UPPER QUADRANT ULTRASOUND IMPRESSION: Gallbladder wall thickening and edema with common bile duct dilatation and positive sonographic ___ sign. These findings are suggestive of ____, although no cholelithiasis was identified. Patient may have recently passed stone or stone may be within the distal CBD, which was not visualized on this exam. An MRCP can be performed if clinically indicated.  (___) MRCP IMPRESSION:  1. A few areas of narrowing and dilatation of the intra- and extra-hepatic biliary tree. These findings may be the sequela of a passed gallstone with a component of cholangitis. Another possibility includes a congenital variation and autoimmune pancreatitis with involvement of the biliary tree. A ___ month followup MRCP is recommended to evaluate for resolution.  2. No evidence of choledocholithiasis.  3. No MR evidence of pancreatitis.  4. Edematous nondistended gallbladder with small amount of    sludge/tiny stones.',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


