VALUES (
    '21081277', '11667451', 'cholecystitis', 'CHOLECYSTITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute gallbladder disease.', 'CC: ___ pain  HPI: Asked to see this ___ M who was transferred from ___ after presenting with acute onset of abdominal pain starting at  3 pm this afternoon. Pain came on suddenly and located in epigastrium and RUQ. + chills. He denies fevers, nausea, vomiting, shortness of breath, or chest pain. He also denies constipation, diarrhea, or any urinary symptoms. Pain unrelated to eating.', '# Coronary artery disease -- s/p multiple PCI, last in ___ records from ___ -- s/p MI in ___ with stent placement # Dilated Cardiomyopathy -- LVEF of ___ -- s/p PPM/ICD placement # Hypertension # Hyperlipidemia # Hypothyroidism # Depression  # ICH -- while on Coumadin # Benign Prostatic Hypertrophy # Bilateral Hydroceles # Colonic polyps # Hand osteomyelitis history # Babesiosis history # SCC -- left ___ finger and penis # Appendectomy # Gout    Social History: ___ Family History: # Father -- died from throat cancer at age ___, heavy smoker and  alcohol consumption # Mother -- congenital heart problem (unsure what), but lived  into her ___ # Brother -- renal cancer, treated # Sister -- healthy # Children --  all healthy', '[VITALS] Temp: 98.1 BP: 118/72 HR: 87 O2Sat: 98 Weight: NA  [EXAM] PHYSICAL EXAMINATION upon admission   Temp: 98.1 HR: 87 BP: 118/72 Resp: 22 O(2)Sat: 93   Constitutional: Comfortable HEENT: Pupils equal, round and reactive to light, Extraocular muscles intact Chest: Clear to auscultation Cardiovascular: Regular Rate and Rhythm Abdominal: Tender right upper quadrant epigastric area, good bowel sounds, no palpable masses GU/Flank: No costovertebral angle tenderness Extr/Back: No cyanosis, clubbing or edema',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
