    'A patient was admitted via eu observation for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute appendicitis.', '___ with history of chronic vague abdominal pain, with diagnoses of cannabis hyperemesis syndrome (no longer using) and IBS, presenting with acutely worsened abdominal pain in the past day. She normally has epigastric/upper abdominal pain predominantly, but reports this is more generalized. She has had severe nausea with several episodes of emesis (last last night) and has been unable to tolerate PO. She also reports shaking chills, no  fever, chest pain, or dyspnea.', 'Past Medical History: Cannabis Hyperemesis Syndrome IBS "Psych history"  Past Surgical History: none   Social History: ___ Family History: non-contributory. No fam hx of colon or GI cancer.', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 125/69 HR: NA O2Sat: 97 Weight: NA  [EXAM] Admission  Vitals:97.9 94 125/69 18 98% RA GEN: A&Ox3, NAD HEENT: No scleral icterus, mucus membranes moist CV: RRR PULM: Breathing comfortably on room air ABD: Soft, nondistended, diffuse mild tenderness with focal moderate tenderness in the RLQ, with voluntary guarding but no rebound Ext: No ___ edema, ___ warm and well perfused',
