    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with abdominal pathology.', '___ man with history of HTN and HLD, who presents with ~1 month  of vague complaints, worst in the past week, including fatigue,  loss of appetite, and occasional epigastric pain treated with  peptobismol. Two days prior to presentation he developed a fever  to 101.4 at home with shaking chills; he presented to an OSH ER  where he was ruled out for flu and sent home. He was seen by his  PCP the day prior to admission as follow up; his PCP sent ___ full  set of labs and noted WBC 19 and elevated transaminases. He was  sent to ___ ER for further evaluation. He denies current  abdominal pain. He says that he has had little to no appetite in the last week, that he is overall  fatigued and feels unwell. He has had one episode of fever at home prompting the OSH ER visit. He denies changes in bowel or bladder habits, denies CP/SOB/cough, denies N/V. Blood cultures were sent upon presentation to ED and within hours returned positive for GNR''s.', 'HTN, HLD, nephrolithiasis, spinal stenosis  PSH: lithotripsy    Social History: ___ Family History: non-contributory', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 122/58 HR: NA O2Sat: 97 Weight: NA  [EXAM] Physical Exam on Admission: Vitals: 97.4 70 122/58 20 94% ra  GEN: A&O, NAD HEENT: No scleral icterus, mucus membranes moist CV: RRR, No M/G/R PULM: Clear to auscultation b/l, No W/R/R ABD: Soft, obese, gallbladder palpable in RUQ, mild TTP RUQ, no ___ sign, no rebound/gaurding Ext: No ___ edema, ___ warm and well perfused  Phsyical Exam',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
