VALUES (
    '29476577', '11689448', 'Pancreatitis, acute Type 2 diabetes mellitus, uncontrolled Hypertension CAD', 'PANCREATITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute pancreatitis.', '___ MEDICINE ATTENDING ADMISSION NOTE    Date: ___ Time seen: 23:35pm PCP: ___, MD   The patient is a ___ male w/ history of CAD s/p CABG HTN, DM2 on  ___ who presents with acute onset epigastric pain around 12:30pm  today after eating.  He had a normal formed BM at 1300 with no  change in pain.  He feels abdominal distention.  No N/V/D,  fevers, diarrhea.  He denies known gallstones     In ER: developed nausea and vomiting, c/o ___ abdominal pain VS: 98.8, 136/77, 62, 16, 100% Studies: CT abdomen w/ peripancreatic haziness on wet read Fluids given: 2liter IVNS Meds given: 8mg Morphine sulfate, 4mg Zofran VS prior to transfer to the floor: 99.2, 131/68, 72, 18, 95%  Review of Systems:  Otherwise negative in 13pt detail system  review (+) Per HPI   (-) Denies fever, chills, night sweats, recent weight loss or  gain. Denies visual changes, headache, sinus tenderness,  rhinorrhea, congestion or sore throat. Denies chest pain or  tightness, palpitations, orthopnea, dyspnea on exertion. Denies  cough, shortness of breath, wheezes or pleuritic pain. Denies  nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, constipation, BRBPR, melena, or  abdominal pain. No dysuria, urinary frequency. Denies  arthralgias or myalgias. Denies rashes. No numbness/tingling or  muscle weakness in extremities. No feelings of depression or  anxiety. All other review of systems negative.', 'Coronary Artery Disease s/p CABG ___, prev PTCA/stent of LAD  ___ (In ___ ECHO: EF 70%, mild symm LVH, dil RV, ?pulmHTN) Diabetes Mellitus type II c/b polyneuropathy Hypertension, benign Benign Prostatic Hyperplasia - no meds currently, previously on terazosin Hypotestosteronism - s/p testosterone pellet implant Osteopenia Thrombocytopenia - stable ___ (base 120s) Arthritis, mild of hands h/o herpes zoster diastasis recti h/o MRSA on hand ___ ___ s/p appy   Social History: ___ Family History: Mother - died ___ breast cancer Father - died heart disease ___ No GI illnesses.', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 142/76 HR: NA O2Sat: 98 Weight: NA  [EXAM] VS: 98.0, 142/76, 70, 20, 97% RA  Pain ___ GEN: ___, Alert and oriented to person, place and situation;  no apperent distress HEENT: no trauma, pupils round and reactive to light and  accomodation, no LAD, oropharynx clear, no exudates, no icterus,  OP clear and moist CV: regular rate and rhythm, no murmurs/gallops/rubs PULM: clear to auscultation bilaterally, no  rales/crackles/rhonchi GI: soft, mild epigastric tender, mildly distended; no  guarding/rebound, (+) bowel sounds present EXT: no clubbing/cyanosis/; 2+ distal pulses; peripheral IV  present, trace edema bilaterally NEURO: CN II-XII intact, ___ motor function globally DERM: chronic venous stasis changes bilat.',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
    clinicalcaseid, patientid, title, type,
    description, symptom, medicalhistory, pe,
    status, createdBy
)
VALUES (
    '23102684', '11690136', 'Primary diagnosis: - Gallstone pancreatitis (self resolved) - Elevated liver enzymes  Secondary diagnosis: - ITP', 'CHOLECYSTITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute gallbladder disease.', 'Ms. ___ is a ___ woman with history of ITP, CML, HTN, cholelithiasis s/p CCY now presenting with abdominal pain.  The patient reports that she developed severe right upper quadrant pain and was found to have cholelithiasis. She  underwent cholecystectomy at the end of ___. She had been doing well since then, until about 1 week prior to admission. She developed acute onset right upper quadrant pain that radiated throughout her body. The pain was severe and last throughout the night. Associated with nausea and vomiting. No fevers and chills. The next morning, the pain was still present but somewhat improved. The pain waxed and waned in intensity over the following days. The pain felt similar to her pain prior to her gallbladder surgery. She also notes that a few days prior to admission her urine became dark. She also was more constipated.  She presented to ___, where labs were notable for Tb 4.4 and lipase >3000. CT A/P obtained and reportedly showed ostsurgical changes status post cholecystectomy as noted above without evidence of drainable fluid collection. The  patient was transferred to ___ for ERPC evaluation.  In the ED, vitals: 98.1 68 188/72 18 96% RA  Labs notable for: WBC 10, Hb 11, plt 63; BMP wnl; AST 457, ALT 404, Tb 4.7, lipase 2893, triglycerides 76 Imaging notable for: RUQUS with mild intrahepatic biliary dilation in the right hepatic lobe without dilated CBD measuring up to 6 mm. No evidence of obstructive stones. Patient given: 2L LR, Zofran 4 mg IV, morphine 4 mg IV  On arrival to the floor, the patient reports that her pain is improved. She denies any nausea at present. No other complaints.', '- ITP - CML - HTN - Cholelithiasis s/p CCY - Diverticulosis s/p sigmoidectomy    Social History: ___ Family History: Father died of heart failure. Brother died of stomach cancer.', '[VITALS] Temp: 97.9 BP: NA HR: 179 O2Sat: 97 Weight: NA  [EXAM] Admission physical exam ========================= VITALS: 97.9 179 / 77 78 18 94 RA  GENERAL: Alert and in no apparent distress EYES: +Icteric, pupils equally round ENT: Ears and nose without visible erythema, masses, or trauma.  Oropharynx without visible lesion, erythema or exudate CV: Heart regular, no murmur RESP: Lungs clear to auscultation with good air movement bilaterally. Breathing is non-labored GI: Abdomen soft, non-distended, tender to palpation in right upper quadrant and mid-epigastrium. Bowel sounds present. No HSM GU: No suprapubic fullness or tenderness to palpation MSK: Neck supple, moves all extremities, strength grossly full and symmetric bilaterally in all limbs SKIN: No rashes or ulcerations noted NEURO: Alert, oriented, face symmetric, gaze conjugate with  EOMI, speech fluent, moves all limbs, sensation to light touch grossly intact throughout PSYCH: Very pleasant, appropriate affect',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
