VALUES (
    '22553685', '11728692', 'appendicitis', 'APPENDICITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via eu observation for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute appendicitis.', 'This is an otherwise healthy ___ year-old female with a one-day history of abdominal pain. Patient reports having felt mild periumbilical discomfort last night that migrated to the right lower quadrant earlier this morning and became sharp, of  moderate intensity (___), non-radiated, with no known alleviating factors, worsened with movements. Concomitantly, she endorsed intermittent nausea but no emesis, as well as headache. She denies fever, chills.', 'Migraines    Social History: ___ Family History: NC', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 151/82 HR: NA O2Sat: 98 Weight: NA  [EXAM] ___:  upon admission:  Vital signs - 98.8 102 151/82 18 100%RA Constitutional - Well appearing, in no distress Cardiopulmonary - RRR, normal S1 and S2. No murmurs Abdomen - Soft, non-distended, tender to palpation over right lower quadrant. No rebound or guarding. Negative Rovsing''s Extremities - Well perfused. No clubbing, cyanosis or edema Neurologic - Grossly intact. Appears alert and oriented x 3  Physical examination',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
    clinicalcaseid, patientid, title, type,
    description, symptom, medicalhistory, pe,
    status, createdBy
)
VALUES (
    '20326816', '11737161', 'acute diverticulitis colovesicular fistula bladder cancer gastritis anxiety', 'OTHER_ABDOMINAL',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with abdominal pathology.', 'This is a ___ M with hx of bladder ca with recent surgical  intervention who now presents with epigastric pain. Patient was  seen earlier today by Urology for removal of ureteral stent.  Patient then began to experience the epigastric pain shortly  after, which radiates to the back. States it''s constant.  endorses nausea but no vomiting. denies black or bloody stools,  diarrhea. No fever or chills.   .   In ED, initial VS were 99.3 67 142/90 20 99% RA. PE showed ttp  in epigastric region, guiac neg. EKG showed sinus rhythm, no ST  changes. Labs were unremarkable except WBC 16.6 and Cr 1.4  (baseline 1.2). Pt had a renal ultrasound which was neg. UA was  dirty however could be contaminant so treatment was not started.  Urine culture was sent. Pt had a contrast study earlier in day,  thus will need to wait for CT abd/pelvis. Pt was given Zofran,  Ativan and Morphine in ED. Also rec''d 3L NS. Pt was then  admitted for continued abd pain. On transfer, VS were Temp -  98.6 oral, HR - 57, BP - 111/72, RR - 16, O2 Sat - 96% room air.    .   On the floor, pt is sleeping comfortably in bed. Awakes to  voice. When asked about pain, states he has ___ epigastric  pain. States was nauseous and vomiting earlier on the floor, now  better with meds. Emesis was nonbloody.   . Review of Systems:   (+) Per HPI   (-) endorses night sweats, recent weight loss. Denies blurry  vision, diplopia, loss of vision, photophobia. Denies headache,  sinus tenderness, rhinorrhea or congestion. Denies chest pain or  tightness, palpitations, lower extremity edema. Denies cough,  shortness of breath, or wheezes. endorses nausea, vomiting,  denies diarrhea, endorses constipation, denies abdominal pain,  melena, hematemesis, hematochezia. Denies dysuria, hematuria,  stool or urine incontinence. Denies arthralgias or myalgias.  Denies rashes or skin breakdown. No numbness/tingling in  extremities. All other systems negative.', 'PAST ONCOLOGIC HISTORY:   Pt had epigastric discomfort for ___ years. He lost 30 lbs in the  past ___ years and then another 15 lbs in past 2 months. He became  very fatigue at the end of ___. His WBC was 25,000 on  ___. He was sent to ___ and CT A/P on  ___ showed wall thickening of sigmoid colon and wall  thickening/possible nodular mass involving the bladder that is  adjacent to this area of the sigmoid colon. MRI abd/pelvis on  ___ showed marked thickening and soft tissue signal  involving the sigmoid colon, measuring 8.3x5.0cm. A 0.6cm  necrotic LN in the sigmoid mesentery was also noted. The lesion  extends to left side of the bladder which demonstrated lobulated  lesion measuring 6.8x5.4cm. MRI also showed a large 8.2x6.5cm  lesion in the left hepatic lobe, somewhat wedge-shaped. There  appears to be a nonenhancing portal vein branch in this region,  suspicious for thrombosed vessel. Per MRI report, this is most  likely a perfusion abnormality from underlying thrombosed portal  vein branch, but underlying tumor/tumor thrombus can not  entirely be excluded. He had EGD/colonoscopy on ___ which  showed gastritis, duodenitis and 2 colon polyps. It also showed  sigmoid diverticulosis with suspicion for an extrinsic process.  Per PCP''s note, he had cystoscopy per urologist Dr. ___  ___, which showed a 5cm mass in the bladder with surrounding  edema suspicious for transitional cell ca.   .   .   PAST MEDICAL HISTORY:   TOBACCO DEPENDENCE   VOCAL CORD NODULES   COLONIC POLYP   HELICOBACTER PYLORI INFECTION     Social History: ___ Family History: mother with breast cancer at age ___. maternal grandmother had  ovarian cancer at her late ___. 2 Maternal aunts had breast  cancer. Maternal cousin had ovarian cancer.', '[VITALS] Temp: 97.6 BP: 129/68 HR: NA O2Sat: 97 Weight: NA  [EXAM] Vitals - T: 97.6 BP: 129/68 RR: 20 02 sat: 98% RA   GENERAL: well-appearing NAD   SKIN: warm and well perfused, no excoriations or lesions, no  rashes   HEENT: EOMI, PERRLA, anicteric sclera, pink conjunctiva, MMM   NECK: nontender supple neck, no LAD, no JVD   CARDIAC: RRR, S1/S2, no mrg   LUNG: CTAB, no wheezes or crackles   ABDOMEN: nondistended, +BS, +ttp in epigastric area, no  rebound/guarding, no hepatosplenomegaly   M/S: moving all extremities well, no cyanosis, clubbing or edema    NEURO: CN II-XII intact, strength and sensation intact',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
    clinicalcaseid, patientid, title, type,
    description, symptom, medicalhistory, pe,
    status, createdBy
)
VALUES (
    '24214818', '11739512', 'Acute pancreatitis Dementia', 'PANCREATITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute pancreatitis.', '___ ___ speaking male with past medical history of  vascular vs Alzheimer dementia presents with abdominal pain and  weakness. On ___, the patient began having abdominal pain,  with 4 episodes of nonbloody vomiting. On ___, per ED the  patient reported dysuria with possible hematuria. During this  time, the patient''s abdominal pain has persisted, but + fever to  100, headache, body aches, and urinary frequency. The patient  then refused to eat out of fear of emesis. The patient''s last  bowel movement was today, which was normal. The patient''s  symptoms described above were preceded by approximately 2 weeks  of abdominal distention which was new for him. Patient denies  chest pain, shortness of breath, hematemesis, hematochezia. He  then went to see his PCP''s coverage who referred him to the ED.  . REVIEW OF SYSTEMS: CONSTITUTIONAL:  As per HPI HEENT:  [X] All normal RESPIRATORY:  [X] All normal CARDIAC:  [X] All normal GI:  As per HPI GU:  [+] Per HPI SKIN:  [X] All normal MUSCULOSKELETAL:  [X] All normal NEURO:  [+] H/o dementia with worsening short term memory over  the past ___ years ENDOCRINE:  [X] All normal HEME/LYMPH:  [X]  All normal PSYCH:  [X] All normal All other systems negative except as noted above .', 'BENIGN PROSTATIC HYPERTROPHY    -Patient has undergone prostate biopsy which was negative for  malignancy. He was maintained on doxazosin and proscar. ___: Per urology, no need to do annual PSA as they have been  stable at 2.0.  CATARACT -s/p R cataract surgery on ___  REMOTE DYSPHAGIA  - resolved x ___ years GASTRITIS?- per dtr pt never had sx of this and this was found  as part of evaluation for his dysphagia above.    HEADACHE - pt attributed to aricept  MEMORY LOSS - Followed by Dr. ___ Behavioral ___.  Believed to be ___ to microvascular infarcts as seen on MRI. Was  recommended to take ASA and Aricept. patient not taking either  medication --> ASA caused GI upset; Pt with some side effects on Aricept but continued on 10 mg daily  but was switched to namenda OSTEOARTHRITIS    OSTEOPENIA - Magnesium and Vitamin D  POLYURIA     Pt complains of polyuria, but numerous UA negative, lytes WNL.  ___ be ___ to intake vs. cultural- ___: resolved without  intervention. Per pt''s dtr this improved with ___ chi H/O KIDNEY "CRYSTALS" in his ___ for which he was hospitalized  with abdominal pain in ___ and given IVF.    Social History: ___ Family History: His father had dementia and died at ___. His mother died her ___  from natural causes. His brother had diabetes.', '[VITALS] Temp: 97.5 BP: 142/85 HR: NA O2Sat: 97 Weight: NA  [EXAM] Vitals:  T  97.5,  P  98 BP 142/85  RR 16 SaO2 97% on RA  GEN: Pale flushed elderly male, who appears ill HEENT: ncat anicteric MMM   NECK:  supple CV: s1s2, tachy, regular no m/r/g   RESP: RLL crackles ABD: markedly distended Diminished bowel sounds, + guarding, + rebound, but abdomen is  NOT rigid  EXTR:no c/c/e 2+pulses  b/l DERM: no rash   NEURO: face symmetric speech fluent   PSYCH: calm, cooperative',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


