VALUES (
    '29157418', '11744921', 'PRIMARY DIAGNOSES: 1. Mild Acute Pancreatitis 2. Cholelithiasis without cholecystitis  SECONDARY DIAGNOSES: 1. Type 2 diabetes mellitus 2. Coronary artery disease 3. Benign Hypertension 4. Asthma', 'PANCREATITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via eu observation for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute pancreatitis.', 'This is a ___ yo woman with CAD, diabetes mellitus who p/w 1 week  of RUQ abdominal pain that radiates to her back. She notes a  couple episodes of nausea last week and one episode of vomiting  without blood or bile, but none in several days. She does feel  the pain is worse with eating. She denies associated fevers,  chills, nausea, vomiting, diarrhea, constipation, melena, brbpr.  She notes after the medication in the ed (toradol) she has no  pain and would like to go home. She denies B symptoms but does  note decreased appetite for 3 weeks with subjective weight loss.  She has occasional constipation, but none recently.  In the ED: VS: 98 70 184/68 18 98% RA. She was given toradol  15mg iv. Also in the ED her BG fell to 69, asymptomatic, she was  given ___ amp d50.  ROS: 10 point review of systems otherwise negative except as  noted above.', 'CAD, s/p stent DM, type II, insulin dependent with microalbuminuria Osteoarthritis Sarcoidosis Asthma Obesity Hypertension    Social History: ___ Family History: Diabetes', '[VITALS] Temp: 97.7 BP: 133/76 HR: 68 O2Sat: 97 Weight: NA  [EXAM] VS: T 97.7 HR 68 BP 133/76 RR 20 Sat 98% RA Gen: Well appearing woman in NAD Eye: extra-ocular movements intact, pupils equal round, reactive  to light, sclera anicteric, not injected, no exudates ENT: mucus membranes moist, no ulcerations or exudates Neck: no thyromegaly, JVD: flat, + acanthosis nigricans Cardiovascular: regular rate and rhythm, normal s1, s2, no  murmurs, rubs or gallops Respiratory: Clear to auscultation bilaterally, no wheezes,  rales or rhonchi Abd: Soft, mildly tender to palpation RUQ wihtout rebound or  guarding, non distended, no hepatosplenomegaly, bowel sounds  present Extremities: Trace pedal edema bilaterally, no cyanosis,  clubbing, joint swelling Neurological: Alert and oriented x3, CN II-XII intact, normal  attention, asterixis absent, speech fluent Integument: Warm, moist, no rash or ulceration   Psychiatric: appropriate, pleasant, not anxious Hematologic: no cervical or supraclavicular LAD',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


