VALUES (
    '24797227', '11761621', 'appendicitis esrd', 'APPENDICITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute appendicitis.', '___ with history of type I DM with associated ESRD, HD dependent presenting with one day of abdominal pain. Patient states symptoms yesterday, with pain in both lower quadrants, but is now worse in the RLQ. He also notes diarrhea with some nausea but no vomiting.  He denied any blood per rectum.  As noted, he is HD dependent, and had dialysis as scheduled two days ago ___, on ___ schedule) without issue. He denied any chest pain or shortness of breath.', '1. End-Stage Renal Disease (anuric) on HD TuThSa (___  ___ 2. Type 1 DM complicated by gastroparesis (A1c: 6.7 on ___ 3. Recurrent HTN emergency/urgency 4. Chronic L flank pain (poss diabetic polyneuropathy) 5. Chronic Diastolic CHF 6. Esophagitis/Gastritis/Duodenitis on EGF ___ with negative  h.pylori 7. Depression, prior suicide attempt 8. Fibromyalgia 9. Mod/severe cognitive deficits per OMR, neuropsych testing in  ___ 10. Migraine Headaches (per previous discharge record)      Social History: ___ Family History: Mother: diabetes, ovarian cancer. Two brothers: diabetes. Three  sisters: one with hypertension and one with gestational  diabetes. No history of CAD.', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 97/45 HR: NA O2Sat: 97 Weight: NA  [EXAM] VS: 97.6 88 97/45 18 96% RA  General: sleeping in stretcher, easily arousable. HEENT: mucus membranes slightly dry, nares clear, trachea at midline CV: regular rate, rhythm.  Radiating murmur from left axilla.  Pulm: clear to auscultation bilaterally Abd: + bowel sounds, tender to palpation in infraumbilical area and RLQ without rebound tenderness. Obese. MSK: warm, well perfused. Palpable thrill overlying LUE AVF. Neuro: alert, oriented to person, place, time  Labs: 135  99  38    -------------<250  4.3  20  8.2 ___       ALT: 24 AP: 138 Tbili: 0.3 Alb: 4.7  AST: 22 LDH:  Dbili:  TProt:   ___:  Lip:          9.6>36.7<152  N:74.1 L:17.4 M:5.8 E:2.3 Bas:0.4   Diagnostics: CT A/P (prelim): ____. Surrounding fat stranding and small amount of fluid, no abscess. No extraluminal free air.',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
    clinicalcaseid, patientid, title, type,
    description, symptom, medicalhistory, pe,
    status, createdBy
)
VALUES (
    '24590497', '11761802', 'Diverticulitis Left frontal lobe lesion', 'OTHER_ABDOMINAL',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with abdominal pathology.', 'The pt is a ___ year-old right-handed woman who presents with 3 days of left-sided neck pain and fever and chills. She came to the ED last night as the pain became so severe that she could  not stop crying. The neck pain starts at the left base of the skull and shoots forward. It is constant with a throbbing quality. It is worse when she turns her head to the left or if she exhales deeply. Nothing seems to make it worse. She denies any injuries. She does have a history of an episode of "torticollis" a few years ago that resolved. Although she initially thought this  pain may be related to torticollis, in retrospect this pain is very different. She denies any other neurological symptoms such as vertigo, incoordination, weakness, numbness, speech or vision changes. She does not typically have headaches.  Other than fever, the only infectious symptom she endorses is a few episodes of diarrhea, which is new. No sick contacts or travel outside of the country.    On neuro ROS, the pt denies loss of vision, dysarthria, dysphagia, lightheadedness, tinnitus or hearing difficulty. Denies difficulties producing or comprehending speech.  Denies focal weakness, numbness, parasthesiae. No bowel or bladder incontinence or retention. Denies difficulty with gait.  On general review of systems, the pt denies cough, shortness of breath.  Denies chest pain or tightness, palpitations.  Denies nausea, vomiting, constipation or abdominal pain.  No dysuria. Denies rash.', 'seasonal and food allergies   Social History: ___ Family History: No neurological history', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 121/77 HR: NA O2Sat: 99 Weight: NA  [EXAM] Vitals: Ti: 99.1, Tm 102.6 P:122  BP:121/77  RR: 16 SaO2: General: Awake, cooperative, appears in pain, mild distress. HEENT: NC/AT, no scleral icterus, MMM, clear oropharynx Neck: No meningismus, but pain on neck extension and left rotation. Pinpoint tenderness over left paraspinal cervical muscules. No carotid or vertebral bruits Pulmonary: Lungs CTA bilaterally without R/R/W Cardiac: RRR, nl. S1S2, no M/R/G Abdomen: soft, NT/ND, normoactive bowel sounds. Extremities: No C/C/E bilaterally Skin: no rashes or lesions  Neurologic: -Mental Status: Alert, oriented x 3.  Attentive, able to name  ___ backward without difficulty. Able to relate history without difficulty.  Language is fluent with intact repetition and comprehension.  Normal prosody.  There were no paraphasic  errors. Pt. was able to name both high and low frequency objects.  Able to read without difficulty.  Speech was not dysarthric. Able to follow both midline and appendicular commands. The pt. had good knowledge of current events.  There was no evidence of apraxia  or neglect.  -Cranial Nerves: I: Olfaction not tested. II: PERRL 4 to 2mm and brisk.  VFF to confrontation. Funduscopic exam unable to be completed due to light sensitivity III, IV, VI: EOMI without nystagmus.  Normal saccades. V: Facial sensation intact to light touch. VII: No facial droop, facial musculature symmetric. VIII: Hearing intact to finger-rub bilaterally. IX, X: Palate elevates symmetrically. XI: ___ strength in trapezii and SCM bilaterally. XII: Tongue protrudes in midline and has symmetric strengh.  -Motor: Normal bulk, tone throughout. No pronator drift. No adventitious movements. No asterixis.   Delt Bic Tri WrE FFl FE IO IP Quad Ham TA ___ L  5    ___   ___  5   5    5  5     5     5 R  5    ___   ___  5   5    5  5     5     5  -Sensory: No deficits to light touch, pinprick, proprioception throughout.   -DTRs:   Bi Tri ___ Pat Ach L  2  2    2    2   2 R  2  2    2    2   2 Plantar response was flexor bilaterally.  -Coordination: No dysmetria on FNF or HKS bilaterally. UE RAMs symmetric.  -Gait: Good initiation. Narrow-based, normal stride and arm swing.',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
    clinicalcaseid, patientid, title, type,
    description, symptom, medicalhistory, pe,
    status, createdBy
)
VALUES (
    '22483021', '11765822', 'perforated appendicitis', 'APPENDICITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute appendicitis.', 'This is a pleasant, otherwise healthy, ___ year-old female with a two-week history of abdominal pain. Patient states that she  first experienced symptoms two weeks ago, mainly as vague abdominal discomfort, malaise and loose, non-bloody stools. She attributed her symptoms to a tempura she had for dinner back then, a type  of food she does not usually have. The diarrhea subsided after 24 hours, however the abdominal discomfort persisted. Given no resolution of her symptoms, she decided to be seen by her chiropractor one week ago, who prescribed some herbal remedies. Patient states that pain did not improve, but rather became severe and localized to the right lower quadrant three days  prior to presentation. She now describes the pain as stabbing, continuous, worsened with movement and activity, improved with Tylenol. Concomitantly, she endorses intermittent diarrhea, low-grade fevers, chills, and anorexia. Even though her symptoms improved slightly yesterday, she awoke this morning with worsening pain, for which reason she decided to seek medical care.', 'None   Social History: ___ Family History: Significant for prostate cancer in father, breast cancer in  cousin, pancreatic cancer in grandfather.', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 103/59 HR: NA O2Sat: 100 Weight: NA  [EXAM] Vital signs - 100.5  88  103/59  16  100% RA Constitutional - Well appearing, in no acute distress Cardiopulmonary - RRR, normal S1 and S2. No murmurs. CTAB Abdominal - Soft, slightly distended, right lower quadrant  tenderness with palpation Extremities - Atraumatic. No clubbing, cyanosis or edema Neurologic - Grossly intact. Alert and oriented x 3. Ambulates  normally without assistance.',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


