VALUES (
    '28672604', '11802081', 'Acute appendicitis', 'APPENDICITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute appendicitis.', '___ PMHx for ETOH, gallstone pancreatitis, recent laparoscopic  converted to open cholecystectomy who presents with abdominal  pain. Of note, patient has a history of Alcohol abuse, and  gallstone pancreatitis s/p stent placement/removal and  sphincterotomy recurrent episodes of cholecystitis s/p laparoscopic converted to open cholecystectomy ___. However,  post-operatively patient had multiple hospital visits mostly for  request for pain medications. There is strong evidence of pain  seeking as patient recently went to ___ on  ___ for pain meds.   Patient comes to the ED today for significant per-incisional  pain as well as inability to tolerate oral intake. Patient  states that he has not been able to get out of bed today with a  dozen episodes of bilious emesis. Patient also complains of pain  mostly around his umbilical incision site. Also of note, patient  was at a ___ rehab, but started to drink again and 4  shots of Vodoka on ___.', 'PMH:  - EtOH abuse--had been admitted ___ to ICU; had paradoxical  reaction to lorazepam and was managed on phenobarbital protocol  - Gallstone pancreatitis ___ and ___ s/p ERCP ___  with stent placement and ___ ERCP with sphincterotomy and  stent removal (___). - Cholecystitis - Asthma - Alcoholic hepatitis    PSH:  laparoscopic converted to open cholecystectomy  (___)    Social History: ___ Family History: No CAD/HTN/DM/bleeding disorders', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: NA HR: NA O2Sat: NA Weight: NA  [EXAM] Admission   Vitals: Stable General: AAOx3 HEENT: EOMI Cardiac: WNL Respiratory: Breathing comfortably on room air Abdomen: Soft, mildly distended, incision site clean/dry/intact. Mild epigastric pain along ___ incision site.',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


