VALUES (
    '20001800', '11828074', 'Acute pancreatitis', 'PANCREATITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via eu observation for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute pancreatitis.', '___ yo male with hyperlipidemia, chronic gout, presents with one  day of epigastric pain.  Noted some reflux symptoms after eating fish two nights ago.   Yesterday, spent time with friends at a ___, noticed  relatively sudden onset of mid-epigastric pain, radiating to  back, that progressed throughout the afternoon, associated with  mild pleurisy.  No vomiting, no diarrhea, no fevers/chills.   Pain worse with movement, Tums did not provide relief.  Given  progression of pain to ___, presented to ___ ED.  Does note  increased alcohol intake (beers) over past few weeks.  No recent  medication changes.  In ED, VS: 97.7  61  166/103  18  100% RA RUQ ultrasound performed, admitted for further management  Upon arrival to the floor, patient noted ___ abdominal pain,  no nausea, no other complaints.  Acknowledges that he may have  been drinking too much alcohol recently.  12 ROS as noted above, also notable for lack of chest pain,  dyspnea, diarrhea.  All other systems negative.', '1.  Hyperlipidemia 2.  Gout    Social History: ___ Family History: alcohol dependence and CAD in family', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 154/82 HR: 52 O2Sat: 98 Weight: NA  [EXAM] VS:  98.6  154/82  HR 52  RR 18  96% RA General:  pleasant, well-appearing, no distress HEENT:  anicteric sclerae Cardiovascular:  RRR, normal S1, S2, II/VI systolic murmur best  heard at the apex, no radiation Pulmonary:  lungs clear to auscultation bilaterally Abdomen:  soft, mild tenderness in epigastrium, no rebound or  guarding Ext:  2+ radial pulses, no clubbing or edema Skin:  no telangiactasias or palmar erythema Neuro:  CNs ___ intact, no gross motor deficits Psych:  appropriate',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


