VALUES (
    '20639685', '11833713', 'gangrenous perforated cholecystitis, choledocholithiasis, &  pancreatitis', 'CHOLECYSTITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via observation admit for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute gallbladder disease.', 'We are seen Mrs ___ in consultation for gallstone pancreatitis.  She is a ___ year old female with history of obesity with known fatty liver, GERD, hiatal hernia. Her medical history is also pertinent for prior EUS with known CBD dilation (6.7 mm ___.  She presented to outside hospital this afternoon with complain  of 12 hours of acute diffuse abdominal pain radiated to her back. She endorses that she has similar episodes of this pain over the past 4 months but not as intense as this episode. The pain associates with emesis (NBNB), choluria, subjective fevers and diaphoresis. She denies acholia. Upon presentation to OSH, she was afebrile. Tachycardic to 122 and BP to 155/65. Laboratory work up at this institution demonstarted a leukocytosis to 16.6k and LFTs with biliary obsructive pattern (Tbil 2.1, Direct: 1.6, AST: 91, ALT: 47, Alphos: 196, Lipase 3.824). US demonstrated a CBD measuring 8.4mm with a stone in proximal CBD of 1.9cm. The gallbladder has wall thickening with pericholecystic fluid. She received one dose of Zosyn and transferred to ___ for further ___.', 'obesity, NASH, GERD, hiatal hernia; prior EUS w known CBD  dilation (6.7 mm ___    Social History: ___ Family History: N/C', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: NA HR: NA O2Sat: NA Weight: NA  [EXAM] General Adult Exam GENERAL APPEARANCE: Well developed, well nourished, alert and  cooperative, and appears to be in no acute distress. HEAD: normocephalic. EYES: PERRL, EOMI. Fundi normal, vision is grossly intact. EARS: External auditory canals and tympanic membranes clear,  hearing grossly intact. NOSE: No nasal',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


