VALUES (
    '22362400', '11887722', 'Acute Appendicitis', 'OTHER_ABDOMINAL',
    'A patient was admitted via eu observation for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with abdominal pathology.', 'Ms. ___ is a ___ female with a hx of stage IIA triple negative invasive ductal carcinoma of the right breast  s/p bilateral partial mastectomy and C3d1 of ddAC, who now presents with RLQ pain, nausea, and vomiting.  She reports that she was well until 3 AM this morning when she woke up with severe RLQ pain. She experienced this pain at rest and characterized it as constant, "sharp/throbbing", with radiation to her right flank in association with chills, diaphoresis, nausea and 1 episode of non-bloody emesis. She subsequently reported no appetite. Prior to being brought to the ED by ambulance she had a low-grade fever to 100.9 PO. She has not had a BM or passed flatus since last night. Otherwise she denies chest pain, shortness of breath, and/or dysuria.  Currently her pain persists yet she has had no further nausea or emesis since this morning. No history of similiar symptoms and no sick contacts.', 'PMH: HTN, uterine fibroids, stage IIA triple negative invasive ductal carcinoma of the right breast, L breast fibroadenoma, thyroid nodule, nephrolithiasis  PSH: Right axillary sentinel node biopsy ___ Dr. ___, Bilateral partial mastectomies with wire localization, left breast ___ Dr ___, Right ovarian cystectomy with bilateral ovarian cystotomies ___ Dr. ___, partial thyroidectomy for benign nodule (___), Evacuation of vaginal hematoma ___- Dr. ___, right sided electrohydraulic lithotripsy ___- Dr. ___, D&C ___ Dr. ___   Social History: ___ Family History: Adopted with no knowledge of family history.', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 96/58 HR: NA O2Sat: 97 Weight: NA  [EXAM] Vitals 97.8 70 96/58 16 94RA General-AAOx3, in no acute distress HEENT-AT, NC, sclera non icteric, neck supple, no JVD Heart-RRR, normal S1, S2 Lungs-CTA B/L Abdomen-soft, non distended, slight incisional discomfort,  dressing dry Extr.-non edema or cyanosis, B/L palpable distal pulses',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


