    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute gallbladder disease.', 'Ms. ___ is an ___ who presented to the hospital with a  one week history of malaise and non specific abdominal pain. The patient was accompanied to the emergency department by her friend. Last ___ her friend noticed that Ms. ___  looked fatigued and when she saw her again today she looked worse. When Ms. ___ had a loose bowel movement today, they decided to come to the emergency department for further management.   Ms. ___ indicates that she has been having abdominal  pain for the last week. It originally started in the right lower quadrant then went to the mid abdomen. She has also noticed decreased appetite but denies any nausea or vomiting or increase pain following meals. She also denies prior abdominal pain following meals.', '1.  Coronary artery disease status post anterior wall myocardial infarction in ___. 2. History of esophageal spasm   Social History: ___ Family History: No history of coronary artery disease.', '[VITALS] Temp: 97.3 BP: 131/61 HR: 76 O2Sat: 97 Weight: NA  [EXAM] On admission:   Vitals: T 97.3  BP 131/61  HR 76   RR 16     98% oxygen RA GEN: A&O HEENT: No scleral icterus, mucus membranes moist CV: RRR PULM: No respiratory distress ABD: Soft, nondistended, tender in the RUQ, no rebound or guarding, Ext: No ___ edema, ___ warm and well perfused',
