VALUES (
    '21703487', '11951469', 'Pancreatitis', 'PANCREATITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via observation admit for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute pancreatitis.', '___ s/p lap chole on ___ at ___ presents with abdominal pain unremitting since 10AM this morning. She has not felt back to normal since her surgery. Has had intermittent RUQ/epigastric pain associated with nausea and vomiting. She notes low grade temp and chills at home with a Tmax at home of 99.5 per her report. However, the pain became unremitting today starting at 10AM, which prompted her to seek medical care. She  is unable to tolerate PO with the exception of a few Cheerios occasionally. She endorses loose stools (not frank diarrhea) and continues to pass flatus.   Of note, she was admitted to ___ service at ___ from ___ for similar symptoms. She had a negative HIDA scan at this time, and she was eventually discharged at this time with a PO challenge. There was concern for a retained stone per the notes from this hospitalization; however, per the patient, she had begged to go home and she was instructed to return if her symptoms continued or worsened.', 'Stage III invasive ductal carcinoma HER 2+ BRCA 1+    GERD    migraine    psoriasis    depression    gallstones    Past Surgeries:    C section    hysterectomy ___    double mastectomy w/ reconstruction   lap chole ___ (Dr. ___ ___ office, cell ___      Social History: ___ Family History: non-contributory', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: NA HR: 120 O2Sat: NA Weight: NA  [EXAM] GENERAL: AAOx3 NAD   HEENT: NCAT, EOMI, PERRLA, No scleral icterus, mucosa moist  CARDIOVASCULAR: RRR  PULSES: 2+ radial pulses b/l   PULMONARY: breathing comfortably on room air GASTROINTESTINAL: previous laparoscopic incisions well healed,  C/D/I, soft, minimal TTP, non-distended, no guarding, rebound,  or peritoneal signs  NEUROLOGICAL: strength, and sensation grossly intact',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


