VALUES (
    '27071073', '11969588', 'acute cholecystitis', 'CHOLECYSTITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute gallbladder disease.', '___ s/p recent SVD ___ presents with RUQ abdominal pain and nausea since late ___ afternoon. Patient reports she was  lying in bed when pain started suddenly. She describes it as a  pressure localized to the right upper quadrant with no alleviating or aggravating factors. Pain has occurred at least 3 times in the past 2 weeks during various times of the day and never  associated with eating. She has associated nausea, but no vomiting. Pain  has always subsided, but tonight it did not and she decided to present to the ED for evaluation. She denies any fevers or chills. Pain has subsided since arrival to the ED although she remains significantly tender to palpation.', 'PNC:  - ___ ___ by certain LMP confirmed by office US - Labs Rh neg/Abs neg/Rub equivocal/RPR NR/HBsAg Neg/HIV Neg/GC/CT Neg - Screening: CF negative, low risk NIPT, msAFP low risk - FFS initially limited views of spine otherwise normal, posterior/fundal placenta. Last U/S ___ with normal and complete survey, placenta posterior, AFV nl - GTT not yet done - GBS not yet done   OBHx: - G1   GynHx: - regular menses until ___, hx PCOS, ?tubal blockage(per workup in ___, infertility - denies hx OCP use - denies abnormal Pap, fibroids, Gyn surgery, STIs    PMH:  - migraine headaches, improved during pregnancy - hemorrhoids with anal fissure - pituitary microadenoma/hyperprolactinemia, per pt PRL has been normal - kidney stones ___ ago - hyperlipidemia, no medications - saphenous vein narrowing, stable   PSH:  - hemorrhoidectomy ___    Social History: ___ Family History: -NC', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: NA HR: 120 O2Sat: NA Weight: NA  [EXAM] GEN: NAD HEENT: EOMI, MMM, sclera anicteric CV: RRR PULM: non-labored breathing ABD: soft, non-distended, no rebound, no guarding. incision  sites c/d/i EXT: bilateral lower extremity edema NEURO: A&Ox3 PSYCH: appropriate mood, appropriate affect',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


