VALUES (
    '29282744', '11977174', 'Acute Appendicitis', 'APPENDICITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via eu observation for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute appendicitis.', '___ is a ___ year old otherwise healthy female who  presents with worsening abdominal pain. The pain began at  approximately 6pm yesterday as diffuse abdominal pain. Ms.  ___ eventually developed nausea, vomiting, and subjective  fevers and chills. Her pain progressed to localize in her right side and became significantly worse with movements, especially  sitting and standing. This prompted her to seek care at the  ___ ED.  At time of our evaluation, the patient reports her pain has  improved with the narcotics. She also reports ongoing nausea.  She continues to have right sided abdominal pain and states it  bothers her most when she sits up to use the commode. She denies  any ongoing fevers or chills since her arrival. She denies dysuria, urinary hesitancy or frequency. She denies diarrhea or  other changes with her bowel movement.', 'PMHx: none  PSHx: Left elbow and knee surgery   Family History: Non-contributory', '[VITALS] Temp: 98.3 BP: 135/57 HR: 86 O2Sat: 98 Weight: NA  [EXAM] ADMISSION PHYSIAL EXAM: Vitals: T 98.3 HR 86 BP 135/57 RR 18 O2 99% RA Gen: Well appearing, AAOx3, NAD HEENT: No scleral icterus, midline trachea, neck supple CV: RRR Pulm: Breathing unlabored on room air Abd: Soft, nondistended. Focally tender to palpation in the  right lower quadrant with guarding. No rigidity, no rebound  tenderness. No abdominal incisional scars. Ext: Warm and well perfused, no edema',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
    clinicalcaseid, patientid, title, type,
    description, symptom, medicalhistory, pe,
    status, createdBy
)
VALUES (
    '26903059', '11981239', 'Primary Diagnosis ================= Pancreatitis Community Acquired Pneumonia Bradycardia  Secondary Diagnosis =================== Constipation', 'PANCREATITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via observation admit for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute pancreatitis.', 'Mr. ___ is a ___ male w/ remote h/o recurrent pericarditis and tularemia who presents  with abdominal pain. Patient was in usual state of health until yesterday morning when he awoke with severe pain in his "solar plexus." Pain is constant and "dull" in nature and radiates to his back. He trialed ibuprofen 600 mg yesterday evening before bed, slept briefly, but then awoke around midnight with resurgence of pain worse than prior. This persisted throughout early morning, prompting him to seek medical attention. He adds that he ate a large steak dinner and drank one glass of red wine and two to three shots of cognac the evening prior to the onset of his symptoms. He otherwise rarely consumes meat or alcohol since his diagnosis of gout one year ago. With regard to respiratory symptoms, patient reports daily productive cough on the order of weeks to months. He thinks URI symptoms predated  his cough. He endorses lightheadedness, generalized weakness, anorexia, suboptimal oral intake, nausea, and one loose stool in the ED. He otherwise denies fevers/chills, chest pain, shortness of breath, palpitations, or vomiting.   In the ED, morphine 4 mg IV reduced his pain from ___ -> ___  in severity. He suspects he is improving overall, but still has no appetite.', '-Hospitalized for ___ in ___ thought to be related to dehydration; intermittent chest pain unremarkable cardiac  work-up -Gout; allopurinol discontinued for transaminits -Pericarditis: First episode at ___ y/o (thought to be viral),  ___ recurrent episodes, last episode ___ years prior. -Tularemia (___) -Babesiosis -Appendectomy   Social History: ___ Family History: -Maternal hx intracranial aneurysm -Paternal hx kidney disease, unspecified, bladder cancer, and prostate cancer -Maternal GF hx AAA', '[VITALS] Temp: 98.3 BP: 139/82 HR: 50 O2Sat: 98 Weight: NA  [EXAM] ADMISSION PHYSICAL EXAM VITALS: T 98.3, HR 50, BP 139/82, RR 18, O2 98% RA GENERAL: NAD, well-appearing HEENT: PERRL, EOMI, anicteric sclerae, no conjunctival pallor,  MM dry, oropharynx clear NECK: supple, no LAD, no JVD  CV: bradycardic, regular rhythm, S1/S2, no m/r/g  PULM: unlabored, good air entry, CTAB GI: soft, normoactive, non-distended, epigastric and periumbilical tenderness, no organomegaly, no rigidity/guarding/rebound   EXT: WWP, without edema NEURO: non-focal',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
    clinicalcaseid, patientid, title, type,
    description, symptom, medicalhistory, pe,
    status, createdBy
)
VALUES (
    '26078032', '11982995', 'Pancreatitis ___ Hyponatremia', 'OTHER_ABDOMINAL',
    'A patient was admitted via observation admit for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with abdominal pathology.', 'Mr. ___ is a ___ male with h/o kidney cancer s/p nephrectomy, TCC of the bladder on BCG, new diagnosis of pancreatic cancer diagnosed on EUS on ___ c/b ? splenic vein thrombus for which he is on lovenox who presents with with worsening diffuse epigastric pain x 1 week. He had had diarrhea, gas and flatulence for the past two weeks. He flew to ___ the day after the EUS and there was noted to have weakness, unsteady gait and decreased appetite along with diffuse  abdominal pain that worsened with eating. He has had darker urine but no light colored stools. + subjective fevers resolved with Tylenol. No objective fevers or shaking chills. He had two episodes of emesis yesterday. He has lost 5lbs. He has had anoxrexia and decreased appetite. He does not report chest pain, shortness of breath, back pain, neuro sx or focal weakness.   He flew back from ___ yesterday and then went to his PCP today  who referred him to ___.  There he was found to have a lipase of 1069 and elevated WBC.  Upon arrival to the ED VS: Pain = ___, T = 98.7, HR = 82, BP = 142/76, O2sat = 98% on RA,  Na = 129, K= 4.6, Cr = 1.1, BS = 99 Lipase = 252 WBC = 17.0 with 85% PMNS.', 'TA grade  TCC of the bladder treated with BCG infusions-  - Renal cancer s/p R nephrectomy- Clear cell, renal cell carcinoma, 3.9-cm, G3, pT3a, margins negative - HTN - ? Splenic vein thrombus on lovenox   Social History: ___ Family History: His father died of throat cancer. His mother died of a stroke.', '[VITALS] Temp: 99.3 BP: NA HR: 132 O2Sat: 99 Weight: NA  [EXAM] Admission EXAM(8) 99.3 PO 132 / 80 L Lying 82 18 94 RA  VITALS: Afebrile and vital signs stable (see eFlowsheet) GENERAL: Alert and in no apparent distress EYES: Anicteric, pupils equally round ENT: Ears and nose without visible erythema, masses, or trauma.  Oropharynx without visible lesion, erythema or exudate CV: Heart regular, no murmur, no S3, no S4.  No JVD. RESP: Lungs clear to auscultation with good air movement bilaterally.  Breathing is non-labored GI: Abdomen soft, non-distended, LLQ tendernes at the site of  the lovenox shots. Diminished bowel sounds are present. There is no rebound or guarding. Diffuse ecchymoses b/l lower quadrants at the site of the lovenox injections.  GU: No suprapubic fullness or tenderness to palpation MSK: Neck supple, moves all extremities, strength grossly full and symmetric bilaterally in all limbs SKIN: No rashes or ulcerations noted NEURO: Alert, oriented, face symmetric, gaze conjugate with  EOMI, speech fluent, moves all limbs, sensation to light touch grossly intact throughout PSYCH: pleasant, appropriate affect  Patient examined on day of',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


