INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
    clinicalcaseid, patientid, title, type,
    description, symptom, medicalhistory, pe,
    status, createdBy
)
VALUES (
    '21906103', '11992252', '#Diverticulitis #Constipation #Esophagitis  #Dysphagia  #CAD  #Chronic Back Pain  #Traumatic brain injury #Muscle Spasm/Contracture', 'OTHER_ABDOMINAL',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with abdominal pathology.', 'Mr. ___ is a ___ ___ male from ___  with a past medical history significant for a traumatic brain    injury complicated by right upper and right lower extremity    contractures and limited verbal ability ___ years ago,    hypertension, osteoarthritis, coronary artery disease,  dysphagia, constipation, and anorexia who was recently  hospitalized at ___ from ___ for acute on chronic  failure to thrive and  hypotension who presents today with  complaint of abdominal pain  and n/v.    Patient was hospitalized in ___ after being found to be  profoundly hypotensive and hypothermic on presentation to the ED   and was subsequently transferred to the FICU due to pressor   requirement. His blood pressures remained stable after fluid    resuscitation. The patient was treated for an hypovolemic ___     with an admission creatinine of 2.5 that eventually normalized.     The patient was thought to have coronary artery disease as  inferior wall hypokinesis was noted on TTE but there was no   evidence of acute ischemia on EKG and lab data. On the floor,  the patient was treated for possible diabetes, dysphagia,   coronary artery disease, and hyperkalemia.    Since his discharge, the patient has continued to have poor po  intake at home. He has remained bed bound in his sister''s living   room. Per his sister, he has not had a BM in the past several  days and started having emesis yesterday. He was also noted to  be complaining of abdominal pain. EMS was called and the patient  was  brought to the ED.    In the ED, initial vital signs were: 96.8 70 18 129/64 99 RA   - Exam notable for: Tired-appearing, Abdominal tenderness L>R  lower>upper, Coughing, transmitted upper airway sounds,   difficulty clearing secretions   - Labs were notable for Hb 12.6, WBC 6.2, AST 46, ALP 163   - Studies performed include CT A/P which demonstrated stranding  in LLQ representing early uncomplicated diverticulosis, stool  ball, and diffuse stool burden. CXR demonstrated subsegmental   atelectasis at right cardiophrenic angle, slightly more   pronounced than on ___. An early infiltrate in this   area is considered unlikely, but not entirely excluded.   - Patient was disimpacted in ED with productive of thick  stoolwithout pellets   - Patient was given Lactulose 30 mL, Aspirin 81 mg, and IV  Ciprofloxacin (400 mg ordered)   - Vitals on transfer: 97.6 85 18 119/74 98 RA   Upon arrival to the floor, the patient is minimally verbal which  is at baseline per his sister. The majority of the history is   obtained from his sister. He has had right upper and right lower   extremity contractures and limited verbal ability for the past  ___ years after a traumatic brain injury. He was mugged while in  ___, causing the TBI. He moved back to ___ to live  with his sister after the event who has been taking care of him  since. He used to be fairly mobile until ___ of this year, when  his mobility decreased and he remained in bed. He remained in  ___ through the recent hurricanes and ___ back to  ___ due to lack of electricity and running water. By the time  he made it to ___, he was very ill, with limited po intake.  He was admitted to ___ as noted above. Since his discharge, he  has continued to have minimal po intake. She notes that he was  having poor po intake while in ___ but that it is worse  now. He has been unable to mobilize. He continues to endorse  abdominal pain and has not had a BM in the past several days  until he was dsimpacted in the ED.    REVIEW OF SYSTEMS: Positive per HPI. Limited due to patient''s   mental status.', 'Remote TBI c/b chronic right-sided contractures and limited  verbal ability Increasing debility over the past year Diabetes Hypertension    Social History: ___ was born in ___ and moved to ___ when he was ___. He lived here until his TBI in his mid-___ that was a result of a brutal physical confrontation that left him in a coma then resultant right sided and mental deficits upon waking. After rehabilitation he moved to ___ with his parents where he lives semi-independently in his own home walking with a walker. His mother would help him with his IADLs until her passing in ___ and his sisters ___ and ___ took over, but he was independent in his ADLs. After hurricane ___ in ___ his family was unable to take care of him with limited resources and no water so they moved to ___ where ___, his other sister lived. The travel was very hard and he was extremely weak so  upon landing they took him to the hospital (___) on ___. He has been bed bound since this hospitalization and his family is working on getting him insurance so he can undergo rehabilitation. Prior medical care has been intermittent private-pay visits by a home-call doctor every 3 months.  The patient smoked 1ppd since the age of ___ and has not smoked since ___ when he moved here. He drank one bottle of rum daily from his teens until ___, after which he drank ___ beers daily. NO marijuana or illicit drugs.     Family History: Reviewed.  None pertinent to this hospitalization', '[VITALS] Temp: 97.4 BP: NA HR: 103 O2Sat: 97 Weight: NA  [EXAM] =================== EXAM ON ADMISSION  =================== Vitals- 97.4 103 / 61 78 18 99 RA   GENERAL: Ill appearing male, NAD, difficult to assess mental  status as minimally verbal, ___ speaker   HEENT: Normocephalic, atraumatic. PERRL. Sclera anicertic, MMM.    NECK: No elevation of JVP, no LAD   CARDIAC: Regular rhythm, normal rate, no murmurs/rubs/gallops.   LUNGS: Clear to auscultation bilaterally w/appropriate breath  sounds appreciated in all fields. No wheezes, rhonchi or rales.    ABDOMEN: Normal bowels sounds, non distended, tender to  palpation in LLQ.   EXTREMITIES: No clubbing, cyanosis, or edema, no sign of  atrophy/hypertrophy. Pulses DP/Radial 2+ bilaterally.   SKIN: Dark pigmented patches in bilateral axillas with  excoriations.   NEUROLOGIC: Difficult to assess due as minimally verbal.  ============ DISPO EXAM  ============ Vitals- 97.0 115 / 67 62 18 99 Ra  GENERAL: Ill appearing male, NAD, ___ speaker, answers  questions appropriately and able to follow simple commands HEENT: Normocephalic, atraumatic. PERRL. Sclera anicertic, MMM.  NECK: No elevation of JVP, no LAD   CARDIAC: Regular rhythm, normal rate, no murmurs/rubs/gallops.  LUNGS: Nonlabored respirations. Loud upper airways sounds but do  not appreciate any crackles or wheezes.  ABDOMEN: Normal bowel sounds, non distended, nontender to  palpation. BACK: Tenderness to palpation in lumbar spine.  EXTREMITIES: No clubbing, cyanosis, or edema. Contractures of  right upper/lower extremities.  NEUROLOGIC: Answers questions appropriately and able to follow commands. Contractures of right upper/lower extremity. Able to  perform handgrip with right hand when prompted. Unable to  dorsiflex/plantarflex right foot. Normal ROM in left upper/lower  extremities.',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


