VALUES (
    '20789134', '12008843', 'Acute appendicitis with perforation and phlegmon.', 'APPENDICITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute appendicitis.', '___ with no significant past medical history presented to ED today with RLQ pain x 1 day with nausea. Patient reports pain began last night suddenly, which was sharp, constant and localized to RLQ. He at first thought it was a pulled muscle as he participated in an intense Pilate''s class the day before.  However pain then radiated ___ hours later towards the umbilicus and epigastrium. This morning it then localized again to only  the RLQ, non-radiating. He experienced loss of appetite and nausea overnight after onset of pain, denies vomiting. Also reportedly had fever to 101.2 at home last night. He denies dysuria,  changes in bowel habits, unexplained weight loss, shortness of breath,  or chest pain.   Only prior abdominal surgery was a left inguinal hernia repair ___ years ago. Denies prior history of sexually transmitted disease or testicular trauma. Denies personal or family history of bleeding disorders or cardiopulmonary disease.', 'Past Medical History: - exercise-induced asthma  Past Surgical History: - L inguinal hernia repair w mesh ___ (___) - excision of R posterior neck lipoma ___ (___)    Social History: ___ Family History: non-contributory', '[VITALS] Temp: 98.5 BP: 141/93 HR: 81 O2Sat: 98 Weight: NA  [EXAM] Vitals: T 98.5 HR 81 BP 141/93 RR 18 O2Sat 95 RA GEN: A&O, NAD HEENT: No scleral icterus, mucus membranes moist CV: RRR, No M/G/R PULM: Clear to auscultation b/l, No W/R/R ABD: Soft, mildly distended; non tender, midline incision intact  with stri-strips over.   Ext: No ___ edema, ___ warm and well perfused',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
