VALUES (
    '21543797', '12017780', 'Acute appendicitis', 'APPENDICITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via observation admit for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute appendicitis.', 'Ms. ___ is a ___ female with dementia, DM, HTN,  hypothyroidism, no prior abdominal operations, who presents to  the ED with complaint of confusion and abdominal pain for 1 day.  She does not speak ___, and translation was obtained from  her son ___ (who is also her HCP) who accompanied her. He reports that over the past 1 day, she has become progressively  confused and somnolent (whereas she is reportedly normally  interactive and energetic), and reporting worsening lower  mid-abdominal pain and nausea. She has also been nauseated but  has not had any emesis. She has had a poor PO intake and  appetite since onset of symptoms, but has been passing flatus  and had a bowel movement the day prior. No fevers/chills. No  similar prior such episodes.', '- Hypertension - DM2 - Hypercholesterolemia - History of depression (see medications below) - Hypothyroidism - Osteoarthritis - Osteoporosis - Insomnia - Anxiety - Hearing loss - Dementia-health care proxy invoked  PAST SURGICAL HISTORY:   - Bilateral cataract surgery.    Social History: ___ Family History: Father deceased at age ___.  Mother deceased at age ___.  The  patient does not know what their health conditions were.   Multiple children with DM2.', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 119/44 HR: NA O2Sat: 99 Weight: NA  [EXAM] PHYSICAL EXAM ON ADMISSION  Vitals: 99.3/98.0  103  119/44  18  100%RA  GEN: somnolent but easily arousable, appropriate upon  conversation HEENT: No scleral icterus CV: RRR PULM: Clear to auscultation b/l ABD: Soft, mildly distended, tender to palpation in lower  abdomen R>L, no rebound/rigidity/guarding Ext: No ___ edema, ___ warm and well perfused  PHYSICAL EXAM',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
