VALUES (
    '20026493', '12027666', 'Acute pancreatitis due to presume choledocholithiasis Syncope with orthostatic hypotension', 'CHOLECYSTITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via observation admit for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute gallbladder disease.', '___ with hx of CAD s/p MI, s/p CABG x3, then redo sternotomy  with AVR ___ Bicor tissue valve), DM, afib, ___  presenting with one day history of RUQ abdominal pain, N/V, and  diarrhea, and syncope. Epigastric pain woke her from sleep,  aching pain, reached ___, associated with nausea and nonbloody, nonbilious emesis, worse with palpation. She did not have  lightheadedness, chest pain, or SOB. She did have diarrhea on  the morning of admission x4, with small amount of bright red  blood in later episodes of diarrhea that she attributes to  hemorrhoids. She presented to her PCP''s office, where she  apparently had witnessed LOC. Per notes (___ and ED) pt was seated in  wheelchair with PCP, when she felt sick, vomited, then lost  consciousness. A code was called at clinic, and pt quickly  regained consciousness. Per notes, VS were 156/87, 80, 97% RA,  glucose 199. EMS was called to take the patient to the ED. She  denies chest pain, SOB, weakness, numbness, seizures.', 'Aortic stenosis MI (___) CAD - s/p CABG x3 ___ ___, SV-OM2,  SV-PDA Remote atrial fibrillation HTN DM x ___ years CRI Gout Appendectomy bilateral cataract surgery artificial eye lens (pseudophakia)    Social History: ___ Family History: Father deceased age ___, CAD. Mother deceased age ___, CAD, DM.  Three sisters and one brother alive and well. One brother  deceased due to trauma. Two daughters, two sons alive and well.', '[VITALS] Temp: 98.6 BP: NA HR: 126 O2Sat: 98 Weight: NA  [EXAM] ADMISSION  VS: 98.6 PO 126 / 62 72 18 96 RA  GEN: Delightful elderly female, alert, interactive, hard of  hearing, comfortable, no acute distress HEENT: PERRL, anicteric, conjunctiva pink, oropharynx without  lesion or exudate, moist mucus membranes LYMPH: no anterior/posterior cervical, supraclavicular  adenopathy CARDIOVASCULAR: Irregularly irregular without murmurs, rubs, or  gallops, JVP is 10 cm H20 LUNGS: clear to auscultation bilaterally without rhonchi,  wheezes, or crackles GI: soft, nontender, without rebounding or guarding, non  distended with normal active bowel sounds, no hepatomegaly EXTREMITIES: trace pitting edema bilaterally, no clubbing or  cyanosis GU: no foley SKIN: Fungal rash beneath bilateral breasts NEURO: alert and oriented, moving all extremities spontaneously,  face symmetric PSYCH: normal mood and affect',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
