VALUES (
    '22360162', '12035989', 'Ruptured appendicitis  Secondary:  atrial fibrillation   RV thrombus  hypernatremia', 'APPENDICITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via observation admit for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute appendicitis.', '___ is a ___ year old female with a previous medical  history of T2DM and CHF complicated by left mural thrombus who  presents with acute abdominal pain. The pain began last night  around midnight and was accompanied with nausea. She had one  episode of emesis and subjective chills without fever. She was  unable to tolerate food and drink today due to the abdominal  pain, prompting her to seek care ___ the ED.', '1. CARDIAC RISK FACTORS   - IDDM c/b retinopathy and ?neuropathy  - Hypertension   - Hyperlipidemia   2. CARDIAC HISTORY  - Negative ETT ___ - Non-ischemic cardiomyopathy with recovered EF (EF ___  ___ most recently 50-55% ___ - NSR, hx of junctional bradycardia   3. OTHER PAST MEDICAL HISTORY   -Left breast cancer, DCIS ___ s/p lumpectomy and chemo XRT (including Adriamycin) -cutaneous sarcoidosis: she had a lesion on her left elbow which was biopsied and was found to be consistent with sarcoid. Followed by pulm who has noted calcified mediastinal and hilar lymphadenopathy -CKD IV -Hypercholesterolemia -Hypothyroidism -Sleep apnea on CPAP -OA -Depression -Anemia    Social History: ___ Family History: No family history of early MI, arrhythmia, cardiomyopathies, or  sudden cardiac death.', '[VITALS] Temp: 98.8 BP: 159/65 HR: 81 O2Sat: 98 Weight: NA  [EXAM] Physical Exam on Admission: Vitals: T 98.8 HR 81 BP 159/65 RR 18 O2 97% RA Gen: Well appearing, AAOx3, NAD HEENT: No scleral icterus, midline trachea, neck supple CV: RRR Pulm: Breathing unlabored on room air Abd: soft, obese, TTP ___ the right and left lower quadrants with  guarding, without rigidity or rebound tenderness Ext: Warm and well perfused, no edema  Physical Exam',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
