    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute pancreatitis.', '___ healthy man presents with severe abdominal pain since yesterday after consuming ___ pints ___ on ___.  States has never had pain like this before, thought it was heartburn  but would not go away, was epigastric and radiating around to back, ___ stabbing, associated with nausea and vomiting.  Last  emesis at 4pm today.  Last BM this afternoon, normal no blood. Ne  fevers or chills.  States does not usually drink ETOH (about every ___ months), but when does the amount stated is about how much and sometime even more. No chest pain or shortness or breath.', 'PMH:obesity PSH: none   Social History: ___ Family History: NC', '[VITALS] Temp: 98.6 BP: 187/87 HR: NA O2Sat: 60 Weight: NA  [EXAM] On admission T98.6 60 187/87 16 100%RA  Gen: pleasant uncomfortable man in NAD, A+O x 3 HEENT: no scleral icterus, MMdry CV: RRR Lungs: CTAB Abd: obese, soft, minimal epigastric pain with deep palpation,  no rebound or guarding, no RUQ pain neg ___ ext: no c/c/e',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
    clinicalcaseid, patientid, title, type,
    description, symptom, medicalhistory, pe,
    status, createdBy
)
VALUES (
    '22429578', '12043129', 'Primary:  Diverticulitis  Secondary:  Hyperthyroidism', 'DIVERTICULITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via eu observation for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with diverticular disease.', '(From Nightfloat Admission H&P): This is a ___ w/Hx of  thyrotoxicosis on propranaol and methimizole who complains of  fever. She has had fever, sore throat nausea nad vomiting x1d.  She developed some periumbilical pain today. She denies urinary  sympotms. Pt saw her PCP for the first time recently on ___.  she was found to have an enlarged thyroid. blood test showed her to have hyperthyroidism. Her TSH was below the measurement in  the lab. T3 was 378 and T4 was 3.6. She was started on  methimazole as well as propranolol by her endocrinologist. She was seen at ___ clinic again today. Per PCP note, pt felt  well up until yesterday when suddenly she her heart rate became  very fast and she had a fever to 103. She called PCP, who  instructed her to stop taking the methimazole and take as much  propranolol as needed to control her pulse. It was initially  thought to be an allergic to methimazole. Routine lab showed WBC  up with increased neutrophils and with the mild right lower  quadrant the patient was sent to the ER for evaluation. In the ED initial vitals were: 102.8 126 119/61 20 96% - Labs were significant for WBC 12.2 (N80.6), normal lacte,  blend UA - CT abd/pelvis w/o con showed: 1. Normal appendix, no evidence of acute appendicitis. 2. Innumerable retroperitoneal and pelvic lymph nodes, none of  which appear particularly enlarged, however given the amount are  somewhat concerning. Although these could reflect reactive lymph nodes, given the  number findings also raise concern for lymphoproliferative  disorder. - Patient was given 2L NS, Methimazole 10 mg, Propranolol 20 mg Vitals prior to transfer were: 98.0 ___ > recheck 103/52  16 100% RA On the floor, pt reports feeling better, but c/o LLQ and RLQ  pain. no d/c, n/v, brbpr, cough, dysuria. + joint pain, myalgia.', '-No previous surgeries -Normal childbirth ___ -hyperthyroidism ___: T4: 3.6 TSH: less than 0.2. likely Grave''s disease   Social History: ___ Family History: Father: alive and well but has some coronary artery disease Mother: alive and well but has type II diabetes. No family history of any thyroid disturbances.', '[VITALS] Temp: NA BP: 106/57 HR: NA O2Sat: 98 Weight: NA  [EXAM] EXAM ON ADMISSION:  Vitals - 98 106/57 103 18 99RA GENERAL: NAD HEENT: AT/NC, EOMI, PERRL, anicteric sclera, pink conjunctiva,  MMM, good dentition NECK: nontender supple neck, no LAD, no JVD, thyroid gland  mildly englarged w/o nodules. CARDIAC: RRR, S1/S2, no murmurs, gallops, or rubs LUNG: CTAB, no wheezes, rales, rhonchi, breathing comfortably  without use of accessory muscles ABDOMEN: nondistended, +BS, tender in LLQ and RLQ, no  rebound/guarding, no hepatosplenomegaly EXTREMITIES: no cyanosis, clubbing or edema, moving all 4  extremities with purpose PULSES: 2+ DP pulses bilaterally NEURO: CN II-XII intact SKIN: warm and well perfused, no excoriations or lesions, no  rashes   EXAM',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


