VALUES (
    '24639523', '12109423', 'Primary diagnosis: 1. Pancreatitis 2. Gastric ulcers, duodenal ulcer 3. Low magesium (hypomagnesemia)  Secondary diagnosis: 1. Atrial tachycardia 2. Anemia 3. Alcohol use', 'PANCREATITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via ew emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute pancreatitis.', '___ female with congenital complete heart block s/p  pacemaker in ___, CHF EF 40%, AV stenosis and insufficiency s/p  bioprosthetic AVR in ___ now presents with feeling unwell x1  week with evidence of arrhythmia on pacemaker evaluation.   .   The patient was in her usual state of health until around 1 week  ago. At that time she was placing curtains and fell from a  height of 5 feet. She reports that she slipped due to wearing  slippers and denies any prodromal sypmtoms, loss of  consciousness, palpitations, chest pain, lightheadedness, nausea  or vomiting. Since the fall she has felt unwell with complaints  of diffuse fatigue, weakness, headache, abdominal discomfort and  occasional lightheadedness, nausea and one episode of emesis. 2  days prior to admission she presented to ___  ___ where she was evaluated and diagnosed with concussion  and discharged. She continued to feel unwell with similar  complaints and presented to ___ EW.   .   In the EW, initial vitals were: T 98.6, HR 95, BP 79/60, RR 18,  SaO2 100% RA. She was given 1L IVF with response in her blood  pressure to systolic ___ (apparently her baseline per patient  but history of HTN). There was some question as to when the fall  occured so the patient underwent a complete trauma work up  including CT torso, head and c-spine which prelim reports are  with acute abnormalities. Labs were unremarkable. EP was  consulted for pacemaker interogation. Interrogation revealed "3  atrial high-rate episodes", "EGMs with 1:1 tachycardia at 120  BPM on ___ and twice on ___ lasting for up to 2 minutes in  duration." During evaluation, the patient developed a "slow  ventricular rhythm at 85 BPM with 1:1 retrograde conduction  confirmed by atrial electrogram." The patient was asymptomatic  during this episode and no blood pressure was taken. Dr.  ___ was contacted without response regarding if  this patient should be admitted to ___ attending or Dr. ___.  She was admitted to ___ for further evaluation and management.  Vitals at transfer were: HR 63, BP 97/61, RR 16 , SaO2 98% RA.   .   Currently, the patient reports headache (diffuse throbbing,  constant for last few days, denies weakness or numbness),  abdominal pain (periumbilical, non-radiating) and thirst.  Otherwise no symptoms.   .   On review of systems, she denies any prior history of stroke,  TIA, myalgias, joint pains, cough, hemoptysis, black stools or  red stools, recent fevers, chills or rigors. All of the other  review of systems were negative.   .   Cardiac review of systems is notable for absence of chest pain,  dyspnea on exertion, paroxysmal nocturnal dyspnea, orthopnea,  ankle edema, palpitations, syncope.', 'Aortic Valve Stenosis and Insufficiency, Congestive heart  failure, Hypertension, Hyperlipidemia, Congenital Complete heart  block s/p PPM ___, Apical LV thrombus, Peptic ulcer disease,  Osteopenia, s/p Hysterectomy, s/p Appendectomy, s/p  Cholecystectomy, s/p Repair of right rotator cuff tear x 3, s/p  Cataract surgery   Social History: ___ Family History: There is no family history of premature coronary artery disease  or sudden death.', '[VITALS] Temp: 97.5 BP: 140/88 HR: 69 O2Sat: 97 Weight: NA  [EXAM] On admission: VS: T 97.5, BP 140/88, HR 69, RR 18, SaO2 98% RA   GENERAL: Pleasant, no apparent distress, AOx3   HEENT: NCAT. Sclera anicteric. PERRL (5 to 3 bilateral), EOMI.  Conjunctiva were pink, no pallor or cyanosis of the oral mucosa.  Dry MM.   NECK: Supple with low JVD.   CARDIAC: Normal rate, regular rhythm, II/VI systolic murmur at  base, no S3 or S4 appreciated. Anterior scar. Pacemaker.   LUNGS: Mild kyphosis. Resp were unlabored, no accessory muscle  use. CTAB, without crackles or wheeze.   ABDOMEN: Soft, mild tenderness ___ region. No HSM or  tenderness. Abd aorta not enlarged by palpation. No abdominial  bruits.   EXTREMITIES: No c/c/e. Warm. Evidence of recent trauma to shins.    SKIN: No stasis dermatitis, ulcers, scars, or xanthomas.   NEURO: CNII-XII grossly intact, ___ strength bilateral upper and  lower extremities, sensation grossly intact   .',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
    clinicalcaseid, patientid, title, type,
    description, symptom, medicalhistory, pe,
    status, createdBy
)
VALUES (
    '28951548', '12120702', 'acute cholecystitis', 'CHOLECYSTITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via direct emer. for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute gallbladder disease.', 'Mr. ___ is a ___ yo male s/p RNY gastric bypass ___ with a  remote history of a marginal ulcer who was in his usual state of   health until he awoke from sleep with severe abdominal pain and  subsequently presented to an OSH on ___.  Upon  arrival to ___ he was placed on bowel rest, given  intravenous fluids and underwent CT scan, which suggested some  stranding of mesenteric fat in close proximity to the  gastrojejunal anastomosis.  The patient was then transferred to  ___ and admitted to the ___ surgery service for further  evaluation and monitoring.   Overnight on HD1, the patient vomited contrast from the CT  obtained at the OSH and reported complete resolution of his  symptoms.  His diet was advanced the following day to a  bariatric stage II which he initially tolerated without pain,  nausea or vomiting.  Given that he remained hemodynamically  stable and had tolerated oral intake, he was discharged.   However, just prior leaving the hospital, Mr. ___ vomited a  small amount of broth, which he attributed to the taste and  reported feeling well overall.  It was reviewed with the patient   that the second read for the OSH CT was still pending and if he  wished to leave, he must return to the hospital immediately if  he were to experience any recurrence of his symptoms.  On his way home developed severe vomiting and returned to the  hospital where he was re-admitted.', 'Hypertension Hyperlipidemia Hypothyroidism Peripheral neuropathy Kidney stones Papillary urethral cancer Marginal ulcer s/p Roux-en-Y gastric bypass ___ s/p thyroidectomy s/p R ACL repair   Social History: ___ Family History: Father: deceased, CAD Mother: deceased, COPD Brother: MI, cerebral palsy', '[VITALS] Temp: 97.7 BP: 133/58 HR: 77 O2Sat: 97 Weight: NA  [EXAM] VS: Temp 97.7, HR 77, BP 133/58, RR 16, O2Sat 97%RA GENERAL: A&Ox3 NAD.  HEENT: MMM. Anicteric, No oral lesions or jaundice ___: RRR, no m/r/g   LUNGS: CTAB, no w/r/c   ABDOMEN: soft, mild/appropriate tenderness to palpation,  nondistended, no rebound or guarding, incisions clean and dry,  no erythema or induration Ext: warm and well perfused, no edema',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);


INSERT INTO clinicalcases (
    clinicalcaseid, patientid, title, type,
    description, symptom, medicalhistory, pe,
    status, createdBy
)
VALUES (
    '22891222', '12121983', 'acute appendicitis', 'APPENDICITIS',
    'A patient was admitted via eu observation for evaluation of abdominal symptoms, later diagnosed with acute appendicitis.', '___ year old female present with  1 day of lower abdominal pain.   Pt reports crampylower abdominal pain which started yesterday  morning.  Patient reports pain started in the AM yesterday and has gradually  gotten worse.  The pain is now more localized in the RLQ.  Her only associated symptom is chills which she had last night.  She reports otherwise feeling well.  Denies fevers, diarrhea, constipation, BRBPR, melena or weight changes.', 'diverticulitis, diet controlled DM, HTN, h/o breast CA    Social History: ___ Family History: NC', '[VITALS] Temp: 98.8 BP: 121/74 HR: 91 O2Sat: 98 Weight: NA  [EXAM] upon admission ___   Temp: 98.8 HR: 91 BP: 121/74 Resp: 18 O(2)Sat: 99 Normal   Constitutional: Comfortable HEENT: Normocephalic, atraumatic Chest: Clear to auscultation Cardiovascular: Regular Rate and Rhythm Abdominal: Soft tenderness to palpation of the lower abdomen, voluntary guarding, no rebound GU/Flank: No costovertebral angle tenderness Extr/Back: No cyanosis, clubbing or edema Skin: No rash Neuro: Speech fluent Psych: Normal mood  Physical examination',
    'active', 'system_generator'
);

