INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '23919775',
    '10139369-RR-16',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT axial images of the abdomen and pelvis were obtained with intravenous contrast.  Coronal and sagittal reformations were prepared.  CT ABDOMEN WITH INTRAVENOUS CONTRAST: Minimal pleural thickening is seen within the left lung base.  No suspicious pulmonary nodule or mass is identified.  The cardiac apex is within normal limits.  The liver demonstrates homogenous parenchymal enhancement without suspicious focal lesion.  Mild periportal edema is identified.  Hepatic veins and portal venous system are grossly patent.  No intra- or extra-hepatic biliary ductal dilatation is identified.  The gallbladder, spleen, pancreas, and adrenal glands are normal.  There is symmetric enhancement and excretion fdrom both kidneys without suspicious focal lesion or hydronephrosis.  Abdominal aorta and branch vessels are non-aneurysmal and grossly patent.  No concerning adenopathy is identified.  There is an 11 mm dilated fluid-filled appendix within the right lower quadrant with hyperemic walls, findings compatible with ____.  There is a small pocket of free fluid adjacent to the appendix, however, no extraluminal free air is identified to suggest perforation.  Minimal free fluid is also identified within the deep pelvis.  Stomach and small bowel loops are normal in caliber and configuration without evidence of obstruction or inflammation.  CT PELVIS WITH INTRAVENOUS CONTRAST: Rectum and colon are normal in caliber and configuration without evidence of obstruction or inflammation.  The bladder is distended and appears normal.  Prostate and seminal vesicles are unremarkable.  BONES AND SOFT TISSUES: No bone destructive lesion or acute fracture is identified.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '27022201',
    '10154376-RR-22',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT contrast-enhanced axial images obtained from the lung bases to the pelvic outlet.  Coronal and sagittal reformations were performed.  FINDINGS: The visualized portions of the lungs and mediastinum are unremarkable.  The liver is homogenous in attenuation without discrete masses or lesions.  The gallbladder, pancreas, and spleen are unremarkable.  The bilateral adrenal glands have normal limb thickness without convex margin to suggest mass.  The kidneys are normal in size and excrete contrast symmetrically.  The stomach is unremarkable.     In the right lower quadrant, a dilated appendix measures 12 mm in diameter (300B:29, 2:62), full course not optimally seen, but with a hyperdense focus at the distal aspect which may represent an appendicolith.  Periappendiceal fluid is seen.  The adjacent terminal ileum is markedly thickened, likely reactive.  A small amount of free fluid is noted within the pelvis with minimal enhancement of the adjacent peritoneum (2:69) which may represent early peritonitis. Overall, findings are suspicious for perforated ____ with adjacent reactive changes within the ileum.  The large bowel is unremarkable.  No diverticula are identified.  No drainable fluid collections or free air identified. Multiple mesenteric lymph nodes are identified, none of which meet CT criteria for pathologic enlargement.  No portacaval or retroperitoneal lymphadenopathy identified.   The uterus, adnexa, bladder, distal ureters and rectum are unremarkable.  The aorta, vena cava, main portal vein and their major branches are patent.  OSSEOUS STRUCTURES: No suspicious lytic or blastic lesions are identified.'
);


