INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '21159619',
    '10298888-RR-11',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'EXAMINATION: CT ABD AND PELVIS WITH CONTRAST:  TECHNIQUE: Axial helical MDCT scan of the abdomen and pelvis was obtained following the intravenous administration of 150 cc of Omnipaque in a split bolus .  Coronal and sagittal reformatted images were also generated for review.  DOSE: 936 mGy-cm  FINDINGS:   LOWER CHEST: The lung bases are clear. A calcified granuloma is seen in the right lower lobe. The visualized portions of the heart and pericardium are unremarkable. There is no pleural effusion.  LIVER: The liver enhances homogeneously, with no focal lesions or intrahepatic biliary duct dilatation. The gallbladder is unremarkable and the portal vein is patent.  PANCREAS: The pancreas does not demonstrate focal lesions or peripancreatic stranding or fluid collection.  SPLEEN  The spleen is homogeneous and normal in size.  ADRENALS: The adrenal glands are unremarkable.  KIDNEYS: The kidneys do not show solid or cystic lesions and demonstrate symmetric nephrograms and excretion of contrast.  No pelvicaliceal dilatation or perinephric abnormalities are present.  GI TRACT: The stomach, duodenum, and small bowel are within normal limits, without evidence of wall thickening or obstruction. The colon is non-dilated without obstructive lesions. The appendix is mildly dilated measuring up to 8 mm with hyperemia.  There is mild surrounding fat stranding, particularly at the appendiceal tip.  VASCULAR: The aorta is normal in caliber without aneurysmal dilatation. The origins of the celiac axis, SMA, bilateral renal arteries, and ___ are patent.  RETROPERITONEUM AND ABDOMEN: There is no retroperitoneal or mesenteric lymph node enlargement.  No ascites, free air, or abdominal wall hernias are noted.  PELVIC CT: The urinary bladder and distal ureters are unremarkable.  No pelvic wall or inguinal lymph node enlargement is seen. There is no pelvic free fluid.  The uterus and bilateral adnexa are unremarkable. An IUD is seen within the uterus.  OSSEOUS STRUCTURES: No blastic or lytic lesions suspicious for malignancy is present.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '26196412',
    '10305345-RR-8',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT images were acquired from the lung bases to the pubic symphysis after administration of IV contrast.  No oral contrast was administered.  Multiplanar reformatted images were obtained for evaluation.  CT ABDOMEN WITH IV CONTRAST: The visualized lung bases are clear without pleural effusions.  The liver enhances homogeneously without focal lesions.  There is no intrahepatic or extrahepatic biliary ductal dilatation.  The gallbladder, spleen, pancreas, adrenal glands and kidneys are normal.  There is prompt excretion of IV contrast into the collecting system bilaterally, without hydronephrosis or hydroureter.  The stomach, duodenum and loops of small bowel are normal.  There is no free air, fluid or intra-abdominal lymphadenopathy.  CT PELVIS WITH CONTRAST: The fluid-filled, retrocecal appendix measures up to 10 mm in diameter, with moderate periappendiceal fat stranding, compatible with ____ (image 2:46).  There is no free air or abscess.  The colon is grossly unremarkable with normal bowel gas and fecal matter.  The uterus is normal in size for female of childbearing age.  The urinary bladder is normally distended without focal abnormalities.  The distal ureters are patent with excreted IV contrast.  There is no free air, fluid or lymphadenopathy.  BONE WINDOW: There are no suspicious osteolytic or sclerotic lesions.'
);


