VALUES (
    '24862340',
    '10373195-RR-10',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABDOMEN W/CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: Multidetector CT images of the abdomen and pelvis after administration of IV contrast with coronal and sagittal reformats were submitted for interpretation.  FINDINGS: Lung bases are unremarkable.  Heart is not enlarged.  There is no pericardial effusion.  Liver, gallbladder, spleen, pancreas, adrenals, kidneys are unremarkable.  The abdominal aorta and iliac vessels are unremarkable.  There is no lymphadenopathy.  The appendix is dilated with wall hyperemia and mild surrounding fat stranding, most compatible with ____.  There is no drainable fluid collection.  There is small amount of free pelvic fluid.  Uterus, urinary bladder, distal ureters and rectum are unremarkable.  OSSEOUS STRUCTURES: There is no bony lesion to suggest malignancy or infection.'
);


