INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '22571105',
    '10379372-RR-21',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: Multi detector CT images were obtained after the administration of intravenous and oral contrast.  Coronal and sagittal reformations were generated and reviewed.  Dose:  DLP 380 mGy-cm.  FINDINGS: Chest:  The base of the lungs are clear bilaterally.  Visualized heart and pericardium are unremarkable.  The liver enhances homogeneously with no focal lesion identified.  There is no intrahepatic biliary dilatation.  The portal vein is patent.  The gallbladder is without radiopaque cholelithiasis.  The pancreas, spleen, and bilateral adrenal glands are unremarkable.  Kidneys present symmetric nephrograms and excretion of contrast with no evidence of hydronephrosis.  No focal lesions are identified.  There is no perinephric stranding.  The stomach, duodenum, and loops of small bowel are unremarkable.  The appendix is enlarged measuring 7 mm proximally and more dilated distally to 1.4 cm.  There is an appendicolith at the transition point as well as periappendiceal stranding, findings compatible with ____. No evidence of perforation. The colon is unremarkable.  No evidence of obstruction or abdominal free fluid. The abdominal aorta is normal in caliber without aneurysmal dilatation.  There is no retroperitoneal or mesenteric adenopathy.  Pelvis:  The bladder is moderately well distended.  Distal ureters are opacified and within normal limits.  Prostate gland and seminal vesicles are normal in appearance.  There is no inguinal or pelvic adenopathy.  Osseous structures:  There is no suspicious lytic or blastic lesion.'
);


