INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '21782521',
    '10472364-RR-15',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'ABDOMEN US (COMPLETE STUDY)',
    'TECHNIQUE: Grayscale and Doppler ultrasound images of the abdomen were obtained.  FINDINGS: There is an infrarenal abdominal aortic aneurysm measuring 4.4 (transverse) x 3.8 (AP) x 6.5 (CC) cm.  There is a large right common iliac artery aneurysm measuring 4.9 x 6.3 cm.  The left common iliac artery is also aneurysmal measuring 2.2 x 1.9 cm.   The liver is normal in echotexture and no focal liver lesions are identified.  No intra or extrahepatic duct dilatation.  The common bile duct measures 3 mm. Doppler examination of the main portal vein demonstrates patency with normal hepatopetal flow.  There is a 3 mm polyp within the neck of the gallbladder.  The gallbladder is otherwise unremarkable.  No gallstones.  No ascites.   The right kidney measures 10.9 cm and the left kidney measures 10.5 cm.  No hydronephrosis, masses or stones.  The spleen is minimally enlarged measuring 13.6 cm.  The spleen is homogeneous in echotexture.  The pancreas is within normal limits.  The tail of the pancreas is not well visualized due to overlying bowel gas.  The visualized portions of the inferior vena cava are unremarkable.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '21782521',
    '10472364-RR-16',
    'CT',
    'Chest',
    'CTA CHEST W&W/O C&RECONS, NON-CORONARY',
    'TECHNIQUE: Axial helical MDCT images were obtained of the chest, abdomen and pelvis before and after the administration of IV contrast in the arterial phase.  Multiplanar reformatted images were generated in the coronal and sagittal planes.  DLP: 1501.57 mGy-cm.  FINDINGS:   CT CHEST: The thyroid is unremarkable in appearance.  Heart size is normal without pericardial effusion.  The thoracic aortic arch and main pulmonary artery are normal in caliber.  The ascending aorta measures 2.9 cm in maximum diameter at the level of the pulmonary artery.  There is no central pulmonary embolus.  There is no supraclavicular, axillary, hilar or mediastinal lymphadenopathy by CT size criteria.  Bi-apical scarring is minimal.  Bibasilar atelectasis is small.  Note is made of a small right-sided Bochdalek hernia containing fat.  Lungs are clear without nodule or focal consolidation.  Pleural surfaces are clear without effusion or pneumothorax.  CT ABDOMEN: The liver enhances homogeneously without focal lesion, intra- or extra-hepatic biliary duct dilatation.  The gallbladder is decompressed, thin-walled and unremarkable.  The portal vein is patent.  The spleen, pancreas, and adrenal glands are unremarkable in appearance.  The kidneys present symmetric nephrograms and excretion of contrast without focal solid or cystic lesions, pelvicaliceal dilatation or perinephric abnormalities.  The stomach, duodenum, and small bowel are unremarkable in appearance without evidence of obstruction.  There is significant phlegmonous change and mesenteric fat stranding in the right lower quadrant surrounding a thick hyperemic appendix with thickened walls measuring up to 1.5 cm in diameter (3:222), likely perforated at its base with an adjacent organizing 2.5 x 2.3 cm dense fluid collection containing gas and a couple of calcified stones.  Smaller adjacent collection up to 1.5 cm seen slighly more laterally.  Of note, the transverse colon which is decompressed is seen to traverse just anterior to this region, deep to the anterior abdominal wall.  There is no mesenteric or retroperitoneal lymphadenopathy by CT size criteria. There is no pneumoperitoneum or hernia.  CT PELVIS: The bladder is decompressed and unremarkable.  The rectum and prostate are unremarkable.  There is no pelvic free air or free fluid.  There is no inguinal or pelvic wall lymphadenopathy by CT size criteria.  CTA RUNOFF: Evaluation is somewhat limited by suboptimal contrast bolus timing.  The upper abdominal aorta is normal in caliber with patent celiac axis, SMA, and bilateral renal arteries.  There is an infrarenal abdominal aortic aneurysm measuring 3.9 x 3.0 cm in greatest dimension, which dissects at the distal abdominal aorta with both aneurysm and dissection extending through the right common iliac artery with a larger aneurysmal segment in the mid right common iliac artery measuring 5.2 x 3.9 cm with both aneurysm and dissection extending into the proximal portion of the right external iliac artery as well.  The left common iliac artery is mildly ectatic with a maximum diameter of 1.7 cm, without frank aneurysm.  Arterial opacification is preserved distally to the mid thigh in the common femoral and to the superficial and deep femoral arteries.  OSSEOUS STRUCTURES: Ectasia of the thecal sac with posterior vertebral body scalloping at the level of L4 and S1 compatible with dural ectasia.  Additional areas of dural ectasia seen at the neural foramen in the thoracic spine as well.  There is grade 1 anterolisthesis of L5 on S1.  There are no focal blastic or lytic lesions in the visualized osseous structures concerning for malignancy.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '23520146',
    '10482767-RR-5',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT images were acquired through the abdomen and pelvis with IV contrast.  Multiplanar reformations were obtained and reviewed.  The partially imaged lungs and heart are unremarkable.  CT OF THE ABDOMEN WITH IV CONTRAST: The liver, spleen, both adrenals, both kidneys, pancreas and gallbladder are normal.  Small and large bowel loops are normal.  Duplicated renal collecting system noted bilaterally.  There is an abnormal appearance of the appendix which measures up to 9-mm in diameter. The appendix is fluid-filled with mucosal hyperenhancement and periappendiceal stranding.  No free fluid or definite evidence of perforation is noted.  CT OF THE PELVIS WITH IV CONTRAST: The rectum, sigmoid colon, bladder, both adnexa and uterus are unremarkable.  No pelvic free fluid, pelvic or inguinal lymphadenopathy by CT size criteria is present.  OSSEOUS STRUCTURES: No suspicious lytic or blastic lesions or fracture.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '28712418',
    '10511804-RR-19',
    'CT',
