    '10652831-RR-11',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'PELVIS, NON-OBSTETRIC',
    'TECHNIQUE: Transabdominal and transvaginal sonography was performed.  Transvaginal sonography was performed for further delineation of endometrium and adnexa.  FINDINGS:   LMP: ___.  The uterus measures 8.0 x 4.7 x 6.2 cm (previously 8.2 x 4.4 x 5.6 cm).  The endometrium is homogeneous and measures 10 mm.  The ovaries are normal and color Doppler was performed to assess for ovarian torsion.  Arterial and venous waveforms of bilateral ovaries are normal.  Trace amount of free pelvic fluid is seen.  Focused transabdominal evaluation of the right lower quadrant at the site of patient''s pain demonstrates what appears to be a blind-ending loop which is non-compressible and measures up to 7 mm in diameter distally.  Proximally, this loop is normal in caliber.  Connection to the cecum cannot be confirmed; however, this is concerning for possible distal ____.  Hyperechoic structure within the lumen in the distal aspect of this tubular structure is suggestive of an appendicolith.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
