)
VALUES (
    '28417762',
    '10781847-RR-18',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT PERITINEAL DRAIN EXCLUDING APPENDICEAL',
    'PROCEDURE: CT-guided percutaneous drainage of right lower quadrant abscess. Written informed consent was obtained prior to procedure.  Timeout was performed using two patient identifiers.  Under CT fluoroscopy guidance and after local anesthesia with 1% lidocaine an ___ ___ catheter was introduced in the right lower quadrant.  Sterile technique was used throughout the procedure.  20 cc of foul-smelling thick yellowish fluid was aspirated and sent for Gram stain, culture and sensitivity.  The patient tolerated the procedure well with no evidence of immediate complications.  A nurse was present throughout the procedure for conscious sedation and the patient has received 2.5 mg Versed and 175 mg of fentanyl.  The staff radiologist is Dr. ___ who was supervising and participating throughout the procedure.'
);


