INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '24456557',
    '11242610-RR-4',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT axial imaging was obtained from the lung bases to the pubic symphysis following the administration of intravenous contrast material.  Coronal and sagittal reformats were completed.  DLP: 352.06 mGy-cm.  FINDINGS:   CT ABDOMEN WITH CONTRAST: The lung bases are clear.  The visualized heart and pericardium are unremarkable.  The liver enhances homogenously without any focal lesions or intra- or extra-hepatic biliary dilatation.  The portal vein is patent.  The gallbladder, pancreas, spleen and adrenal glands are unremarkable.  The kidneys enhance and excrete contrast symmetrically without any focal lesions or hydronephrosis.  The stomach, small and intra-abdominal large bowels are unremarkable.  There is no free fluid or free air or lymphadenopathy within the abdomen.  CT PELVIS: The appendix is visualized in the right pelvis.  It appears prominent in size, measuring approximately 8 mm (601B:23, 2:67).  There is air seen within the tip of the appendix; however, the tip appears slightly thickened and hyperenhancing.  Although, there is no mesenteric stranding in the region, these findings are concerning for early or tip ____.  The bladder, this is partially distended and unremarkable.  The uterus and adnexa are unremarkable.  The rectum and sigmoid colon are unremarkable.  The sigmoid colon is redundant.  There is no free fluid, free air or lymphadenopathy within the pelvis.  OSSEOUS STRUCTURES: There are no concerning lytic or sclerotic lesions.'
);


