INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '29861952',
    '11251623-RR-16',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT-acquired axial images from the lung bases through the pubic symphysis were obtained after administration of 150 mL Omnipaque intravenous contrast material.  Enteric contrast was not given.  Coronal and sagittal reformats prepared and reviewed.  DLP: 941.53 mGy-cm.  FINDINGS: The lower chest is unremarkable.  ABDOMEN: The liver enhances homogeneously and again noted is curvilinear calcifications likely outlining a hemangioma or the prior focus of injury or inflammation.  The gallbladder and biliary tree appear normal.  The pancreas, spleen, and adrenal glands appear normal.  The kidneys enhance normally and excrete contrast symmetrically.  There are several parapelvic cysts on the left.  The stomach, duodenum, and abdominal loops of small and large bowel are of normal caliber, without wall thickening, or associated mass.  The appendix is dilated up to 11 mm in thickness, with mural hyperemia and surrounding fat stranding.  The location of the appendix is retrocecal and it abuts the inferior liver edge.  There is no ascites, fluid collection, or pneumoperitoneum.   The portal, splenic, and mesenteric veins are patent.  The abdominal aorta is not enlarged and its main branches are patent.  There is no retroperitoneal, periportal, or mesenteric lymphadenopathy.  PELVIS: The rectum and urinary bladder are normal.  The prostate and seminal vesicles are normal.  There is no pelvic free fluid or mass.  There is no pelvic or inguinal lymphadenopathy.  MUSCULOSKELETAL: There are no lytic or sclerotic osseous lesions concerning for malignancy.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '23768370',
    '11271666-RR-20',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: Axial MDCT images through the abdomen and pelvis were obtained after administration of intravenous contrast.  Axial, coronal, and sagittal reformats were obtained.  FINDINGS:   CT OF THE ABDOMEN: The lung bases are clear.    The liver and gallbladder are normal.  There is no intra- or extra-hepatic biliary dilatation.  The pancreas, spleen, and bilateral adrenal glands are normal.  The kidneys are homogeneously enhancing and excreting urine without evidence of hydronephrosis, stones, or masses.  The portal venous, systemic venous and systemic arterial system of the abdomen and pelvis are normal.  There is no free air and no free fluid.  The esophagus, stomach, and small bowel are normal.  The appendix is dilated measuring up to 13 mm and fluid filled, with no periappendiceal fat stranding. No evidence of perforation or abscess formation.  The remainder of the large bowel is normal.  CT OF THE PELVIS: The uterus, bilateral ovaries, and the urinary bladder are normal. There is no retroperitoneal or mesenteric lymphadenopathy.  There are no pelvic hernias.  BONES: There are no suspicious lytic or sclerotic bony lesions.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '22023122',
    '11353978-RR-58',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS W/O CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT images were obtained from the lung bases to the pelvic outlet after the administration of oral contrast.  IV contrast was not administered due to the patient''s history of allergy.  Coronal and sagittal reformations were acquired.  FINDINGS:   CT ABDOMEN: The lung bases are clear.  The visualized portions of the heart and pericardium are unremarkable.  Evaluation of the liver is limited due to absence of intravenous contrast, but there is no gross or diffuse or focal abnormality.  The gallbladder, pancreas, spleen, and adrenals are normal.  The kidneys are grossly unremarkable and there is no nephrolithiasis or hydronephrosis.  The stomach and small bowel are unremarkable.  There is no portacaval, mesenteric, or retroperitoneal lymphadenopathy.  There is no free air or free fluid.  CT PELVIS: The appendix is enlarged, measuring 10 mm with trace surrounding fat stranding and fascial thickening (2:67, 601B:31).  Oral contrast does not fill the appendix.  Polypoid thickening is noted at the appendiceal origin bulging into the cecum.  The appendix measured approximately 6 mm on ___.    Exophytic uterine fibroids are again noted.  There is also apparent edema at the cecal origin of the appendix.  The appendix also appears to have a somewhat polypoid appearance in its origin, similar to prior CT.  The left gonadal vein is prominent.  The colon, rectum, and urinary bladder are unremarkable.  There is no pelvic lymphadenopathy or free fluid.  OSSEOUS STRUCTURES: A linear hyperdense lesion in the proximal right vastus lateralis is stable from ___.  There is no lytic or blastic lesion suspicious for malignancy.  There is disc space narrowing at L2-3 with endplate sclerosis.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '27676824',
    '11354070-RR-38',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: Multidetector helical CT scan of the abdomen and pelvis was obtained after the administration of 130 mL IV Omnipaque contrast.  Coronal and sagittal reformations were prepared.  DLP: 637 mGy-cm.  FINDINGS:   CT ABDOMEN AND PELVIS WITH CONTRAST: The included portions of the lung bases are clear.  In the right lower quadrant, the appendix is hyperemic, fluid-filled and dilated measuring up to 11 mm in diameter with periappendiceal fluid and inflammation.  No free air is identified.  An adjacent reactive lymph node is noted.  The liver contains a hypodensity in the left lobe measuring 6 mm, too small to characterize (2A:14) however most likely a simple cyst or ciliated foregut cyst.  The gallbladder, pancreas, spleen, and left adrenal gland are unremarkable.  The right adrenal gland contains a 2.5 x 1.5 (2A:15) x 2.7 (601B:41) cm lesion, incompletely characterized on this single-phase contrast-enhanced examination.  The renal collecting systems are partially duplicated, a normal variant.  Intra-abdominal loops of small and large bowel are normal in size and caliber.  Within the pelvis, there is previously noted dilation of the appendix with inflammation surrounding the appendix and possibly secondarily involving the cecal tip.  Distal loops of large bowel and rectum are normal in size and caliber.  The uterus, adnexa, bladder and distal ureters appear grossly unremarkable.  Small amount of pelvic free fluid is noted within the cul-de-sac as well as surrounding the appendix.  No free air or lymphadenopathy is identified.  No concerning osseous lesion is seen.'
);


