    '11552008-RR-5',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT images are obtained through the abdomen and pelvis following administration of IV and oral contrast.  Coronal and sagittal reformations were performed.  FINDINGS: The lung bases are clear.  The visualized heart and pericardium are unremarkable.  ABDOMEN: The liver enhances homogeneously and there are no focal liver lesions.  There is some focal fatty deposition adjacent to the falciform ligament.  The gallbladder is normal.  There is no intrahepatic or extrahepatic biliary duct dilatation.  The portal vein is patent.  The pancreas is normal.  The spleen, adrenal glands, and kidneys are normal.  The stomach and small bowel are normal.  The colon is normal.    Appendix is dilated up to 1.4 cm in diameter and there is an appendicolith seen at the proximal appendix (601 b, 25).  There is no  free air.  There is free fluid, inflammatory fat stranding surrounding the appendix with indistinctness of the structures adjacent to the appendix compatible with phlegmon.  There is no fluid collection. There are prominent right external iliac lymph nodes, likely reactive.  PELVIS: The uterus and adnexa are unremarkable.  There is an IUD in place in the uterus.  There is some free fluid in the pelvis.  Mildly prominent lymph nodes are seen in the right pelvis.  The rectum is normal.  The bladder and terminal ureters are normal.  There is no hernia identified.  Prominent veins in the right adnexa, may indicate chronic venous congestion.   The aorta is normal in caliber.  There is no acute bone abnormality.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '23910362',
    '11557394-RR-16',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: Axial helical MDCT images were obtained of the abdomen and pelvis after the administration of IV contrast.  Multiplanar reformatted images were generated in the coronal and sagittal planes.  DLP: 492.56 mGy-cm.  FINDINGS: The imaged lung bases are clear.  Heart size is normal.  CT ABDOMEN: The liver enhances homogeneously without focal lesion, intra- or extra-hepatic biliary duct dilatation.  The portal vein is patent.  The gallbladder is thin-walled and unremarkable.  The spleen, pancreas and adrenal glands are unremarkable in appearance.  The kidneys present symmetric nephrograms and excretion of contrast without focal solid or cystic lesion, pelvicaliceal dilatation or perinephric abnormality.  The stomach, duodenum and remainder of the small bowel is unremarkable in appearance without evidence of obstruction.  The appendix is clearly visualized in the right lower quadrant and is thickened to a maximum diameter of 1.2 cm with wall thickening, periappendiceal stranding as well as mild thickening of the adjacent peritoneal wall compatible with ____. The remainder of the large bowel is unremarkable in appearance.  The abdominal aorta is normal in caliber with patent celiac axis, SMA, bilateral renal arteries and ___.  There is no mesenteric or retroperitoneal lymphadenopathy by CT size criteria.  There is no ascites, pneumoperitoneum or hernias noted.  CT PELVIS: The bladder, uterus, ovaries and the rectum are unremarkable in appearance.  There is small physiologic free pelvic fluid.  There is no free pelvic air.  There is no inguinal or pelvic wall lymphadenopathy by CT size criteria.  OSSEOUS STRUCTURES: There are no focal blastic or lytic lesions within the visualized osseous structures concerning for malignancy.  There is transitional anatomy of L5 with partial right sided fusion and degenerative change.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
