INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '26806036',
    '11595084-RR-23',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABDOMEN W/CONTRAST',
    'CT ABDOMEN AND PELVIS WITH CONTRAST.:   TECHNIQUE: MDCT axially acquired images through the abdomen and pelvis were obtained.  IV contrast was administered.  Coronal and sagittal reformats were performed.  FINDINGS: There is paraseptal emphysematous changes at the lung bases.  There is bibasilar atelectasis.  There is no pleural effusion or pericardial effusion identified.  The liver, gallbladder, spleen, pancreas, adrenal glands, and kidneys are unremarkable.  The kidneys enhance and excrete contrast symmetrically.  Small bowel loops are normal in caliber and without focal wall thickening. There is extensive atherosclerotic calcification of the abdominal aorta and its branches.  There is focal aneurysmal dilatation of the infrarenal abdominal aorta which has a bilobed appearance measuring approximately 3.0 x 3.7 cm (2, 48) with mural plaque and penetrating atherosclerotic ulcer. There is no free fluid or free air.  CT OF THE PELVIS: The appendix is dilated measuring up to 8 mm with adjacent inflammatory fat stranding and hyperenhancing mucosa (2, 60).  Small foci of air within the appendix is noted.  No definite evidence of perforation or abscess formation, although tiny specs of extraluminal air may represent microperforation. The rectum, sigmoid colon, and bladder are unremarkable. There is no pelvic or inguinal lymphadenopathy.  BONE WINDOWS: There are no suspicious lytic or sclerotic lesions identified.'
);


