INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '29646721',
    '11712125-RR-4',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABDOMEN W/CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: Helical CT-acquired contiguous axial slices were obtained from the lung bases to the pubic symphysis without administration of oral contrast. 100 cc of intravenous contrast was administered uneventfully intravenously. Multiplanar reformations were generated.  FINDINGS:   CT OF THE ABDOMEN WITH INTRAVENOUS CONTRAST: The lung bases are clear without focal consolidation, pleural effusion, or pneumothorax.  The imaged portion of the base of the heart is unremarkable.  The liver, spleen, gallbladder, pancreas, adrenals, and bilateral kidneys are normal.  There is no intraperitoneal free air.  There are multiple prominent mesenteric and retroperitoneal lymph nodes along the celiac axis, in the paraaortic region, measuring up to 4 mm in short axis, not enlarged by CT criteria.  CT OF THE PELVIS WITH INTRAVENOUS CONTRAST: There is marked inflammatory fat stranding in the pericecal area with a large soft tissue mass that measures 3.2 x 5.4 cm and demonstrates areas of low attenuation more centrally which are approximately 28.5 Hounsfield units in attenuation.  The appendix is not visualized as a separate structure to this mass and the Terminal ileum is intimately related to it and demonstrates bowel wall thickening. Overall appearance raises the possibility of a ruptured ____ with inflammatory phlegmon in the pericecal area. There is no drainable fluid collection or abscess.  The rectum, sigmoid colon, uterus, adnexa, distal ureters, urinary bladder are unremarkable.  Trace free fluid is noted.  There is no inguinal or iliac chain adenopathy.  OSSEOUS STRUCTURES: There are no suspicious lytic or sclerotic osseous lesions.'
);


