VALUES (
    '20276429',
    '11746236-RR-20',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT images were acquired from the lung bases to the pubic symphysis after administration of IV contrast.  No oral contrast was administered.  Multiplanar reformatted images were obtained for evaluation.  CT ABDOMEN WITH IV CONTRAST: The visualized lung bases are clear.  The liver is normal with homogeneous enhancement.  There is no intrahepatic or extrahepatic biliary ductal dilatation.  The gallbladder, spleen, pancreas, adrenal glands are normal.  The kidneys enhance symmetrically, with prompt excretion of IV contrast bilaterally.  There is no hydronephrosis.  The duodenum and loops of small bowel are unremarkable.  There is no free fluid or air in the intra-abdominal cavity.  CT PELVIS WITH IV CONTRAST: There is a dilated, fluid-filled appendix, measuring up to 9 mm in diameter, representing ____.  There is no evidence of free air, abscess, or bowel obstruction.  There is normal fecal loading in the colon.  The uterus is normal in size for a patient of childbearing age.  There is bilateral follicular activity in the adnexae.  The urinary bladder is moderately distended.  There is no free air or fluid in the pelvis.  BONE WINDOW: There are no suspicious osteolytic or sclerotic lesions.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '22738192',
    '11756787-RR-16',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'EXAMINATION: CT ABD AND PELVIS WITH CONTRAST:  TECHNIQUE: MDCT images were obtained from the lung bases to the pubic symphysis after the administration of intravenous contrast.  Axial images were interpreted in conjunction with coronal and sagittal reformats.  Oral contrast was not administered.  DLP: 651 mGy-cm  FINDINGS:   CHEST: The visualized lung bases are clear. There is no pericardial or pleural effusion.  ABDOMEN: There are no focal liver lesions identified. There is mild periportal edema. The portal venous system is patent. There is no evidence of intrahepatic or extrahepatic biliary dilatation. The gallbladder is normal and without gallstones.  Mild gallbladder wall edema is noted. The inferior vena cava has a plump appearance.  The spleen and adrenal glands are unremarkable.  The pancreas enhances homogenously and is without focal lesions.  The kidneys display symmetric nephrograms and excretion of contrast. There are no focal renal lesions. There is no hydronephrosis. The ureters are normal in caliber and course to the bladder.  The stomach is decompressed. The small bowel is normal in caliber without focal wall thickening. The large bowel is normal in caliber. There is high-density material within portions of small and large bowel, which may be related to ingested material.  The appendix is dilated measuring up to 14 mm and is air and fluid filled with extensive surrounding fat stranding (601b:31). An appendicolith is noted in the body of the appendix (601b:25). There is mild thickening of the proximal ascending colon/cecum (601b:29).  There is no extraluminal air or drainable fluid collection.  The abdominal aorta and its major branches are patent . The aorta and iliac branches are normal in course and caliber. There is no retroperitoneal or mesenteric lymphadenopathy by CT size criteria.  PELVIS: The bladder is well distended and normal.  There is no pelvic side-wall or inguinal lymphadenopathy by CT size criteria. There is trace pelvic free fluid, likely reactive.  OSSEOUS STRUCTURES: No focal lytic or sclerotic lesion concerning for malignancy.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
