VALUES (
    '24797227',
    '11761621-RR-194',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT images were obtained through the abdomen and pelvis following the administration of oral contrast only.  Coronal and sagittal reformations were performed.  FINDINGS: The lung bases are clear.  The visualized heart and pericardium demonstrate mild annular calcifications.  There is no pericardial effusion.  Lack of IV contrast limits evaluation of the intra-abdominal organs.  The liver is normal in contour.  There are no focal liver lesions.  The gallbladder, pancreas, spleen, and adrenal glands are normal.  The kidneys are small with multiple subcentimeter hypodensities that are too small to characterize.  There is no mesenteric or retroperitoneal lymphadenopathy.  The appendix is enlarged, measuring 1.2 cm in diameter with surrounding fat stranding and small amount of surrounding fluid consistent with ____.  There is no evidence of abscess or extraluminal free air.  The remainder of the colon is unremarkable.  PELVIS: The prostate and seminal vesicles are normal.  The rectum is normal.  The bladder and terminal ureters are normal.  The intra-abdominal vasculature has normal contours.  BONES: Bones are grossly unremarkable.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '22483021',
    '11765822-RR-21',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'EXAMINATION: CT ABDOMEN AND PELVIS:  TECHNIQUE: Axial MDCT images were obtained through the abdomen and pelvis after the uneventful administration of IV and oral contrast.  Sagittal and coronal reformats were generated.  TOTAL EXAM DLP: 320 mGy-cm.  FINDINGS: There is mild bibasilar atelectasis.  There is no pleural or pericaridal effusion.  CT of the abdomen:  The liver enhances homogeneously with no focal hepatic lesions. The gallbladder is decompressed.  The adrenal glands, pancreas and spleen are normal. The kidneys enhance symmetrically and excrete contrast without hydronephrosis or worrisome renal lesion.  Multiple appendicoliths are seen at the base of the appendix seen on series 2, image 61. The adjacent appendix appears contiguous with a fluid collection in the right lower quadrant suggesting ____ with rupture. This fluid collection is rim enhancing best seen on series 2, image 60 measuring 3.1 x 3.2 x 4.8 cm. There is associated inflammatory fat stranding and small free fluid as well as mild phlegmonous changes. The terminal ileum is thickened, likely reactive. There is no significant intraabdominal free air.  There is small volume ascites. Remaining portions of small and large bowel are unremarkable. The abdominal aorta is of normal diameter. The celiac axis, SMA, bilateral renal arteries and ___ are patent.  CT of the pelvis: The urinary bladder and terminal ureters are normal. There is a small amount of pelvic free fluid.  The rectum is normal.  Ovaries and uterus are normal.  Osseous structures: No blastic or lytic lesion concerning for malignancy.  Focal degenerative changes are noted at the L5-S1 level with endplate sclerosis and anterior osteophytosis.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
