VALUES (
    '24423127',
    '11853064-RR-24',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT helical images were acquired through the abdomen and pelvis after the administration of 130 cc of Omnipaque intravenous contrast.  Sagittal and coronal reformats were generated and reviewed.  FINDINGS: The imaged lung bases are clear of pulmonary nodules or pleural effusions.  The imaged portion of the heart and pericardium are normal.  The liver enhances homogeneously, without focal lesions or biliary dilatation. The gallbladder is normal.  Both adrenal glands, spleen and pancreas are normal.  The stomach and small bowel loops are normal.  The appendix is dilated measuring up to 14 mm, with extensive periappendiceal fat stranding, consistent with ____.  The appendix is in a retrocecal position. High-density material within the base of the appendix, may represent a appendicolith. There is no evidence of perforation or periappendiceal abscess. The abdominal aorta is normal in course and caliber. Small scattered retroperitoneal lymph nodes are too small to meet criteria for significant adenopathy.  CT OF THE PELVIS WITH INTRAVENOUS CONTRAST: The urinary bladder, uterus, and adnexa are normal.  Trace pelvic free fluid is within physiologic range.  The rectum and sigmoid colon are normal.  BONES AND SOFT TISSUES: No bone lesions suspicious for infection or malignancy are detected. Note is made of ___''s cysts within the sacrum.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
