VALUES (
    '24528064',
    '11864955-RR-2',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'ABDOMEN U.S. (COMPLETE STUDY)',
    'ABDOMINAL ULTRASOUND: The liver is normal in echogenicity without focal lesions.  There is normal hepatopetal flow in the portal vein.  The IVC is patent.  There is no intrahepatic biliary dilation.  The common duct measures 3 mm.  The gallbladder is partially collapsed without stones, sludge, wall edema, or pericholecystic fluid.  Ultrasonographic ___ sign was negative.  The pancreas is normal, without ductal dilation.  The spleen measures 8.9 cm.  The right kidney measures 11.3 cm, and the left kidney measures 10.8 cm.  There are no renal stones, masses, or hydronephrosis.  The appendix was well visualized in the right lower quadrant, measuring 5 mm without evidence of wall thickening or hyperemia.  It was fully compressible, with no focal tenderness elicited during graded compression maneuvers.    There is no free fluid.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '24528064',
    '11864955-RR-3',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: Helical MDCT images were acquired from the lung bases through the greater trochanters with intravenous and oral contrast.  The patient tolerated only one bottle of oral contrast before vomiting.  5-mm axial, coronal, and sagittal multiplanar reformats were generated.  FINDINGS: Sub-2-mm pulmonary nodules are noted at the lung bases ___ and 10).  There are no pleural effusions.  The heart is normal in size, without pericardial effusion.  Note is made of a small sliding hiatal hernia.  ABDOMEN: The liver enhances homogeneously on this single phase examination.  The gallbladder is partially collapsed.  The pancreas is normal.  There is no intra- or extra-hepatic biliary ductal dilation.  The spleen is normal in size.  The adrenals are normal.  The kidneys enhance and excrete contrast promptly and symmetrically, without masses or hydronephrosis.  No bowel obstruction is seen.  PELVIS: The appendix has increased in size from prior ultrasound, now measuring 8-9 mm.  There is apparent mild wall thickening, hyperemia, and suggestion of minimal to mild periappendiceal haziness.  No extraluminal fluid collections are seen to suggest perforation.  There is no free air.  Prominent lymph nodes in the right lower quadrant measure up to 7 mm, likely reactive.  The colon and rectum are unremarkable.  The bladder is normal, with bilateral ureteral jets identified.  The uterus and ovaries are normal.  There is trace physiologic free fluid in the pelvis.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
