VALUES (
    '23447345',
    '11871323-RR-3',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABDOMEN W/CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT images were acquired from the lung bases through the pubic symphysis following administration of intravenous contrast.  Multiplanar reformations were generated.  CT ABDOMEN: The lung bases are clear without pleural effusion.  The heart is normal in size without pericardial effusion.  The liver demonstrates no focal lesion.  There is no biliary dilatation.  The gallbladder is collapsed.  The spleen, pancreas, and adrenal glands are unremarkable.  Bilateral kidneys demonstrate symmetric nephrogram without hydronephrosis or hydroureter.  Small and large bowel loops are normal in caliber.  There is no free air or free fluid.  The appendix appears hyperemic, measuring up to 7 mm in diameter, with adjacent fat stranding, consistent with ____.  There is no evidence of free air to suggest perforation.  There is no periappendiceal fluid collection or abscess. Adjacent cecum appears within normal limits.  Great vessels are patent and normal in caliber.  Circumaortic left renal vein is incidentally noted.  Scattered small mesenteric lymph nodes do not meet CT size criteria for pathologic enlargement.  CT PELVIS: The bladder, distal ureters, prostate, and rectum appear unremarkable.  Hernia repair mesh is seen in the lower anterior abdomen; extending laterally bilaterally.  There is no inguinal or pelvic lymphadenopathy.  There is no free fluid within the pelvis.  BONE WINDOW: No suspicious focal lesions.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '21808474',
    '11876479-RR-48',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABDOMEN W/CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: Contiguous axial MDCT-acquired images of the abdomen and pelvis were obtained after uneventful administration of oral and 130 cc of intravenous contrast.  Coronal and sagittal reformats were reviewed.  CT ABDOMEN: Imaged lung bases are clear.  The visualized heart and pericardium are normal.  There is no pleural or pericardial effusion.  The liver enhances homogeneously without concerning focal lesion.  There is a subcentimeter calcification in the lateral segment of the left hepatic lobe (2:14) is stable since ___, likely representing granuloma.  There is no intra- or extra-hepatic biliary dilatation.  The gallbladder is normal without gallstones within.  The pancreas, spleen, and adrenal glands are unremarkable.  Gastric bypass changes with suture lines in the left hemi-abdomen are noted.  Oral contrast is seen within the excluded stomach and duodenum/afferent limb, concerning for gastro-gastric fistula, or alternatively reflux proximally through the afferent limb.  Loop of small bowel in the left abdomen, near the anastomosis is mildly dilated.  Contrast is seen distally and findings may be post-surgical.  Small bilateral subcentimeter renal hypodensities are too small to further characterize. There is no hydronephrosis bilaterally.    There is no free air or free fluid.  No mesenteric or retroperitoneal lymphadenopathy is noted.  PELVIS: The appendix is fluid-filled and dilated measuring up to 9 mm in maximum diameter.  There is mild enhancing appendiceal wall thickening with mild adjacent periappendiceal fat stranding.  The appendix does not fill with oral contrast.  No adjacent fluid collection is noted.  The loops of large bowel, sigmoid and rectum are normal.  The uterus is enlarged and with fibroids within, similar in appearance from ___.  A 3.2 cm left hypodense adnexa lesion is not well characterized in this study and may represent a cyst. The bladder, distal ureters, sigmoiod and rectum are normal. Mild amount of free fluid is noted in the cul-de-sac.  No free air is noted.  A few prominent ileocolic lymph nodes are noted.   The aorta is normal without aneurysm formation or calcified atherosclerosis.  BONE WINDOWS: There are mild multilevel degenerative changes throughout the thoracic and lumbar spine with grade 1 retrolisthesis of L5 over S1.  No concerning osseous lesions for infection or malignancy is noted.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '22362400',
    '11887722-RR-70',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT images were obtained from the lung bases to the pubic symphysis after administration of 130 cc of IV Omnipaque contrast.  Oral contrast was administered. Axial images were interpreted in conjunction with coronal and sagittal reformats.  FINDINGS: The visualized heart is normal.  There is small bibasilar atelectasis.  No pleural or pericardial effusion.  ABDOMEN: The liver is normal without focal or diffuse abnormality. The gallbladder, intra- and extra-hepatic bile ducts, pancreas, spleen, and adrenal glands are normal.  The kidneys enhance symmetrically and excrete contrast promptly.  The ureters are normal in course and caliber.  5.0 x 2.7 cm hypodense cystic lesion in the right anterior abdomen with local mass effect on the left hepatic lobe is unchanged and consistent with a lymphangioma or peritoneal inclusion cyst.    The stomach is normal.  The small and large bowel enhance homogeneously and have a normal course and caliber.  The appendix is dilated to 11 mm with hyperemia and adjacent fat stranding, consistent with ____, predominantly involving the distal appendix.  No substantial cecal edema.    No retroperitoneal or mesenteric lymphadenopathy.  The portal and intra-abdominal systemic vasculature are normal.  No abdominal wall hernia, pneumoperitoneum, or free abdominal fluid.  PELVIS: The bladder and terminal ureters are normal.  The uterus is unremarkable.  No pelvic side-wall or inguinal lymphadenopathy. No free pelvic fluid or inguinal hernia.  OSSEOUS STRUCTURES: No focal lytic or sclerotic lesion concerning for malignancy.'
);


