)
VALUES (
    '27374950',
    '11909152-RR-13',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'PELVIS, NON-OBSTETRIC',
    'PELVIC ULTRASOUND: LMP ___.  Transabdominal and transvaginal ultrasound examinations were performed, the latter for better visualization of the endometrium and adnexa.  The uterus measures 9.3 x 3.4 x 4 cm.  Minimal free fluid is noted within the cervix.  The endometrium measures 0.5 cm and is within normal limits.  The right ovary measures 3.2 x 3.2 x 1.8 cm.  The left ovary measures 2.1 x 3.9 x 1.7 cm.  Both ovaries showed normal arterial and venous waveforms.  Ultrasound examination over the localized region of pain in the right lower quadrant revealed a tubular structure, which was non-compressible which may represent the appendix measuring up to about 6 mm in maximum diameter.  There were a few echogenic foci within this structure which may represent appendicoliths.  Further evaluation with a CT is recommended to rule out ____.  Please note normal arterial waveforms preclude ovarian torsion at the time of study; however, intermittent torsion cannot be completely excluded.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '27374950',
    '11909152-RR-14',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT axial imaging was obtained from the lung bases to the pubic symphysis following the administration of intravenous contrast material.  Coronal and sagittal reformats were completed.  FINDINGS:   CT ABDOMEN WITH CONTRAST: Visualized heart and pericardium are unremarkable.  There is no pericardial effusion.  There is minimal bibasilar atelectasis.  The liver enhances homogeneously without any focal lesions.  There is no intra- or extra-hepatic biliary dilatation.  Portal vein is patent.  The gallbladder, pancreas and adrenal glands are unremarkable.  The spleen is top normal in size measuring 13 cm.  The kidneys enhance and excrete contrast symmetrically without any focal lesions or hydronephrosis.  The stomach, intra-abdominal small and large bowel are unremarkable.  There is no free fluid, free air or lymphadenopathy within the abdomen.  CT PELVIS WITH CONTRAST: There is a dilated fluid-filled appendix measuring 10 mm with a proximal obstructing appendicolith (image 601B:14) consistent with ____.  There is no associated drainable fluid collection or extraluminal gas.  Of note is some adjacent soft tissue thickening, best seen on coronal image (601B:14).  There is a trace amount of free fluid within the pelvis which may be physiologic and/or reactive.  The rectum, sigmoid colon, bladder, uterus, and adnexa are unremarkable.  OSSEOUS STRUCTURES: There is mild sclerosis of the right sacroiliac joint that might represent sacroiliitis.'
);


