    '11972669-RR-17',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT images were obtained from the lung bases to the pubic symphysis without administration of IV contrast.  Axial images were interpreted in conjunction with coronal and sagittal reformats.  DLP: 402 mGy-cm.  FINDINGS:   ABDOMEN: The visualized heart is unremarkable.  There is trace bibasilar dependent atelectasis.  The lung bases are otherwise clear.  No pleural or pericardial effusion is seen.  The liver is normal without focal or diffuse abnormality.  The gallbladder, intra- and extra-hepatic bile ducts, pancreas, spleen and bilateral adrenal glands are normal.  Two small splenules are incidentally noted.  Bilateral kidneys enhance symmetrically and excrete contrast promptly.  Bilateral ureters are normal in course and caliber.  The stomach is unremarkable.  The small and large bowel are normal in course and caliber.  The appendix is dilated to 13 mm, is fluid filled, and has a hyperemic wall.  There is no evidence of perforation or abscess.  The adjacent cecum is unremarkable.  No pathologically enlarged retroperitoneal or mesenteric lymph nodes.  The portal and intra-abdominal systemic vasculature are unremarkable.  No abdominal wall hernia, pneumoperitoneum, or free abdominal fluid.  PELVIS: The bladder and terminal ureters are normal.  Normal bilateral ureteral jets.  The prostate and seminal vesicles are unremarkable.  No pelvic sidewall or inguinal lymphadenopathy.  No inguinal hernia or free pelvic fluid.  OSSEOUS STRUCTURES: No focal lytic or sclerotic lesion concerning for malignancy.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '22388615',
    '11975241-RR-12',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'ABDOMEN U.S. (COMPLETE STUDY)',
    'TECHNIQUE: Abdominal ultrasound.  FINDINGS: The hepatic echotexture is within normal limits.  In segment V of the liver, a 1.1 x 1.1 x 0.8 cm echogenic lesion is seen, which has no internal vascularity and is consistent with a hemangioma.  There is no intra- or extra-hepatic biliary ductal dilation.  The common hepatic duct measures 2 mm.  The portal vein is patent with flow in the appropriate direction.  Pancreas appears within normal limits.  The gallbladder is nondistended and contains no stones.  There is no abnormal gallbladder wall thickening or pericholecystic fluid.  The right kidney measures 10.7 cm.  Left kidney measures 11.6 cm.  No stones, masses, or hydronephrosis are identified in either kidney.  The spleen measures 9.6 cm.  Abdominal aorta and IVC are normal in caliber.  There is no ascites.  Targeted imaging was performed of the region of patient''s pain in the right lower quadrant.  There is a blind-ending tubular structure representing the patient''s appendix with echogenic indurated fat surrounding its tip.  The appendix is directed laterally towards the right iliac wing from its insertion at the cecal tip.  Two shadowing appendicoliths are seen within the appendiceal lumen, including one which is situated towards the junction of the appendix and the cecum.  There is no evidence of abscess.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '24854222',
    '11991721-RR-7',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABDOMEN W/CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: Post-contrast axial images were obtained through the abdomen and pelvis.  Multiplanar reformatted images were generated.  CT ABDOMEN WITH IV CONTRAST: At the lung bases, there is moderate dependent atelectasis, with no consolidation or pleural effusion.  The heart size is normal without pericardial effusion.  Linear high-density material layering along the posterior right pleural space may represent minimal focal pleural calcification.  In the abdomen, the liver contains a tiny focal hypodensity in the posterior right lobe, too small to characterize, and is otherwise unremarkable.  The gallbladder, pancreas, spleen, adrenal glands, stomach, and duodenum are unremarkable.  The kidneys enhance and excrete contrast symmetrically without hydronephrosis, stones, or renal masses.  The abdominal aorta and its major branches are normal.  There is no free air or free fluid in the abdomen.  Mesenteric and retroperitoneal lymph nodes are not enlarged by size criteria.  CT PELVIS WITH IV CONTRAST: The appendix is distended up to 11 mm, with surrounding inflammatory change and a small amount of pericecal fluid.  The tip of the appendix appears to abut the otherwise normal-appearing right ovary.  There is no evidence of perforation or abscess.  Loops of bowel otherwise demonstrate scattered diverticula in the colon without diverticulitis.  Small bowel is normal in caliber.  The uterus appears slightly heterogeneous which could indicate underlying fibroids.  The ovaries are unremarkable with a corpus luteum on the left.  There is a physiologic amount of fluid in the cul-de-sac.  There is no pelvic or inguinal lymphadenopathy by size criteria.  OSSEOUS STRUCTURES: There is no fracture or worrisome bony lesion. There is partial sacralization of the L5 vertebra.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '20789134',
    '12008843-RR-19',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: Axial helical MDCT images were obtained through the abdomen and pelvis after the uneventful administration of 130 cc of Omnipaque intravenous contrast.  Coronal and sagittal reformats were generated.  FINDINGS: There is mild atelectasis at the right lung base.  No pericardial or pleural effusion is noted.  CT ABDOMEN: The liver demonstrates decreased attenuation, compatible with mild fatty deposition.  No focal hepatic lesions identified. No intra or extrahepatic biliary duct dilatation.  The gallbladder, pancreas, adrenal glands and spleen are normal.  There is a subcentimeter hypodensity in the lower pole of the right kidney, which is too small to further characterize.  Otherwise, the kidneys enhance symmetrically and excrete contrast with no evidence of hydronephrosis or mass.   The stomach is collapsed.  There is no bowel obstruction.  There is a hyperenhancing dilated tubular structure arising from the cecum, consistent with ____. There is an extensive amount of surrounding fat stranding and thickening of the lateral conal fascia, likely due to microperforation (2:63). There is no abscess. There is a small amount of associated free fluid. The aorta is of normal caliber. The celiac axis, SMA, bilateral renal arteries and ___ are patent.  CT PELVIS: The urinary bladder and terminal ureters are within normal limits. The prostate is normal.  There is no inguinal or pelvic lymphadenopathy.  There is a small amount of pelvic free fluid.  OSSEOUS STRUCTURES: No blastic or lytic lesion concerning for malignancy.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
