e in the mid appendix and the other near the tip, may reflect appendicoliths (601:30).  There is trace periappendiceal stranding.  No organized collections, free fluid, or signs of pneumoperitoneum are noted.  PELVIS: Circumferential urinary bladder wall thickening, likely due to underdistention.  There is no free fluid in the pelvis.  REPRODUCTIVE ORGANS: The visualized reproductive organs are unremarkable.  LYMPH NODES: There is no retroperitoneal or mesenteric lymphadenopathy.  There is no pelvic or inguinal lymphadenopathy.  VASCULAR: There is no abdominal aortic aneurysm.  No atherosclerotic disease is noted.  BONES: Sclerotic focus in the right sacrum, likely a bone island.  There is no evidence of worrisome osseous lesions or acute fracture.  SOFT TISSUES: The abdominal and pelvic wall is within normal limits.  NOTIFICATION: Findings were discussed with the ___ team on ___ at 2340.  Findings were also reviewed with ACS.'
