ere is no free air or focal fluid collection.  There is no evidence of mesenteric lymphadenopathy.  RETROPERITONEUM: There is no evidence of retroperitoneal lymphadenopathy.  PELVIS: The urinary bladder and distal ureters are unremarkable.  There is no evidence of pelvic or inguinal lymphadenopathy.  There is no free fluid in the pelvis.  REPRODUCTIVE ORGANS: The uterus and bilateral adnexae are within normal limits.  BONES: There is no evidence of worrisome osseous lesions or acute fracture.  SOFT TISSUES: The abdominal and pelvic wall is within normal limits.  NOTIFICATION: The findings were discussed with ___, M.D. by ___ ___, M.D. on the telephone on ___ at 1:23 pm, 45 minutes after discovery of the findings.'
