ss, and enhancement. The colon and rectum are within normal limits. The patient is status post laparoscopic ____.  Mild fat stranding is noted in the surgical bed without evidence of a discrete fluid collection or abnormal enhancement.  PELVIS: There is no free fluid in the pelvis.  Surgical changes are as described above.  REPRODUCTIVE ORGANS: The uterus and bilateral adnexae are grossly within normal limits.  LYMPH NODES: There is no retroperitoneal or mesenteric lymphadenopathy.   There is no pelvic or inguinal lymphadenopathy.  VASCULAR: No significant atherosclerotic disease is noted.  There is no abdominal aortic aneurysm.  BONES: There is no evidence of worrisome osseous lesions or acute fracture.  There is incidental note of a transitional type 4 L5 vertebra.  SOFT TISSUES: A small fluid collection measuring 2.7 x 1.7 cm is identified at the site of the umbilical laparoscopic port.  No significant associated enhancement is identified.  Minimal fat stranding in the right lateral lower abdominal subcutaneous tissues also likely relates to a port site.  Otherwise no gross abnormality of the abdominopelvic walls identified.'
