ll abscess (2:75).  An appendicolith is visualized adjacent to the expected course of the appendix at its tip (2:72) noting that the wall of the appendix in this location is not clearly delineated and findings are suspicious for an extraluminal appendicolith.  There is dilation of the small bowel loops, measuring up to 3.3 cm in transverse diameter, with air-fluid levels, with decompression in the mid pelvis in the region of significant right lower quadrant stranding.  There is reactive wall thickening of the sigmoid colon.  There is a small amount of free-fluid in the pelvis and enhancement of the adjacent peritoneum.  REPRODUCTIVE ORGANS: Prostate and seminal vesicles are unremarkable.  LYMPH NODES: There is no retroperitoneal or mesenteric lymphadenopathy.  There is no pelvic or inguinal lymphadenopathy.  VASCULAR: There is no abdominal aortic aneurysm.  No atherosclerotic disease is noted.'
