ower quadrant.  PELVIS: The urinary bladder and distal ureters are unremarkable.  There is no free fluid in the pelvis.  REPRODUCTIVE ORGANS: The visualized reproductive organs are unremarkable.  LYMPH NODES: Prominent right lower quadrant mesenteric nodes are visualized likely reactive in nature and without evidence of lymphadenopathy by CT size criteria.  There is no retroperitoneal lymphadenopathy.  There is no pelvic or inguinal lymphadenopathy.  VASCULAR: There is no abdominal aortic aneurysm.  No atherosclerotic disease is noted.  BONES: There is no evidence of worrisome osseous lesions or acute fracture.  SOFT TISSUES: The abdominal and pelvic wall is within normal limits.'
