INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '22360162',
    '12035989-RR-142',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'EXAMINATION: CT ABD AND PELVIS WITH CONTRAST:  TECHNIQUE: Single phase contrast: MDCT axial images were acquired through the abdomen and pelvis following intravenous contrast administration. Oral contrast was not administered. Coronal and sagittal reformations were performed and reviewed on PACS.  DOSE: Acquisition sequence:    1) Spiral Acquisition 4.5 s, 59.7 cm; CTDIvol = 23.1 mGy (Body) DLP = 1,375.0 mGy-cm.    2) Stationary Acquisition 0.6 s, 0.5 cm; CTDIvol = 3.4 mGy (Body) DLP = 1.7 mGy-cm.    3) Stationary Acquisition 10.2 s, 0.5 cm; CTDIvol = 57.0 mGy (Body) DLP = 28.5 mGy-cm.  Total DLP (Body) = 1,405 mGy-cm.  FINDINGS:   LOWER CHEST: There is a small amount of likely atelectasis at the right lung base which is increased from prior.  There is no evidence of pleural or pericardial effusion.  There are extensive calcified mediastinal and hilar lymph nodes.  ABDOMEN:   HEPATOBILIARY: The liver demonstrates homogenous attenuation throughout.  There is no evidence of focal lesions. There is no evidence of intrahepatic or extrahepatic biliary dilatation.  There is vicarious excretion of contrast in the gallbladder.  No gallstones or evidence of acute cholecystitis.  There is trace perihepatic ascites.  PANCREAS: The pancreas has normal attenuation throughout, without evidence of focal lesions or pancreatic ductal dilatation.  There is no peripancreatic stranding.  SPLEEN: The spleen shows normal size and attenuation throughout, without evidence of focal lesions.  ADRENALS: The right and left adrenal glands are normal in size and shape.  URINARY: The kidneys are of normal and symmetric size with normal nephrogram.  There is no evidence of focal renal lesions or hydronephrosis.  There is no perinephric abnormality.  GASTROINTESTINAL: The stomach is unremarkable.  The proximal small bowel loops are fluid-filled and dilated to 5.5 cm.  There is a transition point in the left lower quadrant, with the small bowel loops distal to this collapsed (2:76; 601:33).  There is wall thickening of the sigmoid colon with surrounding fat stranding, as well as fat stranding in the right lower quadrant surrounding the base of the cecum where there are two calcified densities in a somewhat tubular structure with surrounding small locules of air, again concerning for appendicoliths within a ruptured appendix (2:68).  There is increased inflammation extending from the right lower quadrant in the region of the appendicoliths towards the midline of the abdomen where there is a locule of fluid spanning 3.5 x 2.3 cm in the midline of the posterior lower mesentery (2:63; 602:43; 601:38).  Additionally, inflammation extends into the right lower pelvis where there is a 2.8 x 2.3 cm locule of fluid posterior to the uterus and to the right of the sigmoid colon which is increased in size from prior (2:83; 601:56)  PELVIS: The urinary bladder and distal ureters are unremarkable.  There is a small amount of fluid in the pelvis surrounding the uterus.  REPRODUCTIVE ORGANS: There is a fibroid uterus with numerous calcified fibroids, not significantly changed.  There is increased fluid surrounding the uterus.  The locule of fluid on the superior aspect of the fibroid uterus spans approximately 3.7 x 2.6 x 1.6 cm (2:77).  This is continuous with a locule of fluid along the inferior aspect of the uterus which spans approximately 5.2 x 2.1 by 4.2 cm (601:39; 602:40).  Additionally, left adnexa appears slightly enlarged with more low-density fluid within, likely secondary inflammation (2:77).  The largest locule fluid within the left ovary spans approximately 2.1 cm.  LYMPH NODES: There is no retroperitoneal or mesenteric lymphadenopathy.  There is no pelvic or inguinal lymphadenopathy.  VASCULAR: There is no abdominal aortic aneurysm.  Moderate atherosclerotic disease is noted.  The portal vein, splenic vein, and SMV are patent.  BONES: There are degenerative changes in the lumbar spine.  There is no evidence of worrisome osseous lesions or acute fracture.  SOFT TISSUES: There is an umbilical hernia containing a nonobstructed loop of small bowel as well as trace fluid.  Multiple soft tissue nodules along the anterior abdominal wall likely injection site granulomas.  There is adjacent stranding, muscle likely related to injection sites.  NOTIFICATION: The findings were attempted to be communicated via telephone, however multiple members of the ___ team paged without a return phone call.'
);


