    'TECHNIQUE: CT abdomen with IV and oral contrast.  Coronal and sagittal reformatted images provided.  FINDINGS: There is no pneumonia or pleural effusion at the lung bases, minimal atelectasis is seen at the right lung base, 2:18.  The gallbladder wall is thick and edematous, measuring 6 mm, with fat stranding in the surrounding tissue, concerning for ____. No focal lesions are seen in the liver.  The spleen, adrenal glands and kidneys are normal in appearance.  The pancreas is atrophic.  There is a biliary stent in place.  There is no periportal, mesenteric or retroperitoneal lymphadenopathy. The abdominal aorta is within normal limits. No free fluid. No free air. The large and small bowel appear within normal limits.  OSSEOUS STRUCTURES: Again seen are two well-circumscribed lytic lesions within the L4 vertebral body adjacent to the superior endplate with surrounding sclerosis, as seen on prior CT.  Seen again is an elongated lucent lesion along the inferior endplate of L3 vertebral body, similar in appearance.  Degenerative changes are seen in the lumbar spine.'
