VALUES (
    '26024119',
    '10101174-RR-21',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'LIVER OR GALLBLADDER US (SINGLE ORGAN)',
    'EXAMINATION: LIVER OR GALLBLADDER US (SINGLE ORGAN):  TECHNIQUE: Gray scale and color Doppler ultrasound images of the abdomen were obtained and reviewed.  FINDINGS:   LIVER: The liver is diffusely echogenic. The contour of the liver is smooth.  Irregularly-shaped hypoechoic regions of hepatic parenchyma adjacent to the gallbladder fossa are compatible with focal fatty sparing. There is no concerning focal liver mass.  The main portal vein is patent with hepatopetal flow. There is no ascites.  BILE DUCTS: There is no intrahepatic biliary dilation. The CBD measures 3 mm.  GALLBLADDER: Multiple mobile echogenic shadowing foci are seen within the gallbladder lumen, compatible with gallstones. A single stone which is not mobile appears situated in the gallbladder neck.  There is borderline gallbladder wall thickening.  There is an equivocal sonographic ___ sign.  PANCREAS: The head and body of the pancreas are within normal limits. The tail of the pancreas is not visualized due to the presence of gas.  SPLEEN: Normal echogenicity, measuring 10.4 cm.  KIDNEYS: The right kidney measures 11.1 cm. The left kidney measures 10.4 cm. Normal cortical echogenicity and corticomedullary differentiation is seen bilaterally.  There is no evidence of concerning solid renal mass, stones, or hydronephrosis in the kidneys.  RETROPERITONEUM: The visualized portions of the aorta and the IVC are within normal limits.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '26024119',
    '10101174-RR-22',
    'CT',
    'Chest',
    'CTA CHEST W&W/O C&RECONS, NON-CORONARY',
    'EXAMINATION: CHEST CTA:  TECHNIQUE: Axial helical MDCT images were obtained from the suprasternal notch to the upper abdomen in early arterial phase scanning after the administration of 100 cc of Omnipaque.  Reformatted coronal, sagittal, thin slice axial images, and oblique maximal intensity projection images were submitted to PACS and reviewed.  DLP: 382.29 mGy-cm.  FINDINGS:   CTA THORAX: The aorta and main thoracic vessels are well-opacified. The aorta is normal caliber throughout, without evidence of dissection or intramural hematoma. The main aortic arch branches are normal. The main, right, and left pulmonary are well-opacified. The pulmonary arterial tree is patent without evidence of lobar or segmental intraluminal filling defect. No arteriovenous malformation is seen.  CT OF THE THORAX: The airways are patent to the subsegmental level.  A single enlarged anterior mediastinal lymph node measures 1.2 cm in short axis. There is no hilar or supraclavicular lymphadenopathy. The heart, pericardium, and great vessels are within normal limits. No hiatal hernia or other esophageal abnormality is present.  Lung windows demonstrate streaky opacities in the dependent portions of lung, compatible with subsegmental atelectasis.  There is a left lower lobe subpleural lung nodule measuring 5 mm in short axis (series 2, image 67). Otherwise, the lungs are clear, and there is no pleural effusion or pneumothorax.  The imaged upper abdomen demonstrates a diffusely hypodense liver, consistent with hepatic steatosis.  OSSEOUS STRUCTURES: There is no focal osseous lesion concerning for malignancy.  NOTIFICATION: Addition to wet read regarding left lower lobe lung nodule and recommended ___ follow-up chest CT were discussed over the phone with Dr. ___ by Dr. ___ on ___ at 16:58.'
);


