INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '20269467',
    '10132759-RR-16',
    'MRCP',
    'Abdomen',
    'MRCP (MR ABD W&W/OC)',
    'EXAM: MRCP obtained, ___.  TECHNIQUE: Multiplanar T1- and T2-weighted images were acquired on a 1.5 Tesla magnet, including dynamic 3D images obtained prior to, during, and after the uneventful intravenous administration of 20 mL of Magnevist.  Multiplanar 2D and 3D reformations and subtraction images were generated on an independent workstation.  FINDINGS: The liver demonstrates homogeneous signal intensity.  Mild diffuse loss of signal intensity on out-of-phase images is secondary to diffuse fatty infiltration.  A few tiny T2 hyperintense nonenhancing lesions are consistent with simple cysts. No abnormal enhancing masses are identified. There is no intrahepatic biliary ductal dilatation.  THe common bile duct is of normal caliber without filling defect to suggest stone/sludge.   Main portal vein and hepatic veins are patent.  The spleen, pancreas, and adrenal glands are unremarkable in appearance. Kidneys demonstrate prompt and symmetric uptake and excretion of contrast.  T2 hyperintense lesion within the upper pole of the left kidney is consistent with a simple cyst.  Within the neck of the gallbladder is a large 2 cm calculus, impacted in the neck.  Adjacent to this large calculus is a subtly hypointense area which likely represents layering stones or sludge.  There is significant gallbladder wall edema with pericholecystic fluid, findings consistent with acute ____.  Of note, there is no hyperemia within the surrounding hepatic parenchyma.  At the level of the ampulla is a tiny cystic area, which measures approximately 2.3 cm in size.  This most likely represents a duodenal diverticulum, as it appears to have an air-fluid level on the axial images. However, other considerations includes choledochocoele or a pancreatic cyst or IPMN.  These seem less likely.  No enlarged intra-abdominal lymph nodes are identified.  The visualized bowel loops are unremarkable.  Multiplanar 2D and 3D reformations provided multiple perspectives for the dynamic series.'
);


