VALUES (
    '28446121',
    '10234917-RR-30',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABDOMEN W/CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: Multidetector helical CT scan of the abdomen and pelvis was obtained after the administration of 130 mL IV Optiray contrast.  Axial, coronal, and sagittal reformations were prepared.  FINDINGS: Within the lung bases, there is bilateral dependent atelectasis.  There are calcifications of the aortic and mitral valves.  Within the abdomen, the gallbladder is moderately distended with gallbladder wall edema and pericholecytic fluid.  The CBD does not appear dilated.  The surrounding liver demonstrates normal enhancement.  The liver, spleen, and bilateral adrenal glands appear normal.  The left kidney contains a hypodensity too small to characterize (2:34).  The right kidney also contains hypodensities too small to characterize (2:35).  Incidental note is made of a splenule (2:27).  The pancreas contains hypodensities (2:26, 28), previously characterized as an IPMN by MRI.  Loops of small and large bowel are of normal size and caliber.  No abdominal free air, free fluid, or pathologically enlarged lymph nodes are seen.  Within the pelvis, distal loops of large bowel and rectum are normal in size and caliber.  There is sigmoid diverticulosis without secondary signs of inflammation.  No pelvic free air, free fluid, or lymphadenopathy is seen.  The bladder and distal ureters appear normal.  BONE WINDOWS: No concerning osseous lesion is seen.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '28446121',
    '10234917-RR-31',
    'MRCP',
    'Abdomen',
    'MRCP (MR ABD W&W/OC)',
    'MRCP:   TECHNIQUE: Multiplanar T1- and T2-weighted images were acquired on 1.5 Tesla magnet including dynamic 3D imaging obtained prior to, during, and after the uneventful intravenous administration of 0.1 mmol/kg (15 cc) of gadolinium-DTPA.  Imaging was performed using non-breathhold technique, which somewhat limits the examination, as the patient was unable to sustain breathhold throughout this examination.  FINDINGS: The liver, spleen, and bone marrow demonstrate diffuse drop out of signal intensity on the longer echo time in-phase imaging compared to the out-of-phase imaging consistent with hemosiderosis.  There is no evidence of focal lesions in the liver or spleen.  There is no evidence of intrahepatic or extrahepatic biliary dilatation.  There is no evidence of filling defects in the biliary tree.    The gallbladder appears distended with debris and small stones in it.  The wall of the gallbladder is mildly edematous and there is a trace of pericholecystic fluid.  Findings are in keeping with diagnosis of acute ____.  The pancreas demonstrates diffuse atrophy, with multiple oblong cystic lesions without evidence of internal icenhancement on the post-contrast imaging.  The size and appearance of these lesions are essentially unchanged as compared to the prior MRCP study. The largest cystic lesion is seen in the tail of pancreas measuring 1.2 cm (series 8, image 25).  The adrenals are unremarkable bilaterally.  The left kidney demonstrates normal size and signal intensity without evidence of focal lesions.  The right kidney demonstrates a small simple cortical cyst in the lateral interpolar portion (series 8, image 33).  There is no evidence of retroperitoneal or mesenteric lymphadenopathy.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
