);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '22596275',
    '10313992-RR-6',
    'MRCP',
    'Abdomen',
    'MRCP (MR ABD W&W/OC)',
    'TECHNIQUE: Multiplanar T1 and T2 weighted imaging were obtained on a 1.5 tesla magnet including dynamic 3D imaging prior to and during and following the administration of 8 mL of intravenous gadolinium contrast material.  FINDINGS: The gallbladder is distended measuring 16.2 x 5.4 x 5.4 cm with significant gallbladder wall edema and associated inflammation.  There are 4 large gallstones layering dependently and  1 stone measuring 1.8 cm impacted in the neck of the gallbladder.  This stone is causing intrinsic compression of the proximal common hepatic duct resulting in mild intrahepatic biliary dilatation, consistent with ___''s syndrome.  The common bile duct is of normal caliber and there is no evidence of choledocholithiasis.  The liver demonstrates normal signal intensity without any focal lesions.  There is some increased perfusion around the gallbladder fossa due to hyperemia from gallbladder inflammation.    The pancreas is of normal signal intensity without any focal lesions or ductal dilatation.  The spleen is not enlarged and is unremarkable.  The adrenal glands are unremarkable. The kidneys enhance and excrete contrast as expected without any hydronephrosis or focal lesions.  The stomach and visualized abdominal bowel loops are unremarkable.  There is a trace amount of perihepatic ascites.  Atelectasis is noted at the right lung base.  No abnormal bone marrow signal.'
);


