INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '20544652',
    '10347234-RR-39',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: Axial CT images through the abdomen and pelvis were acquired after administration of intravenous contrast.  Coronal and sagittal reformatted images were reviewed.  FINDINGS:   CT OF THE ABDOMEN WITH CONTRAST: There is minimal bibasilar atelectasis.  There are no pleural or pericardial effusions.  Minimal visualization of the inferior portion of the heart is unremarkable.  The liver demonstrates hyperemia in the gallbladder fossa.  The gallbladder is distended, concerning for ____.  The common bile duct measures up to 8 mm.  There is small amount of pericholecystic fluid.  There is a prominent periportal lymph node which does not meet criteria for enlargement.    There is a large unchanged hiatal hernia.  There is no free air.  Visualized loops of small and large bowel are unremarkable.  The spleen is unremarkable.  The pancreas contains a pancreatic head cyst measuring up to 1 cm which is similar-appearing compared to prior.  There is also a cyst in the pancreatic tail which was previously visualized and measures 2.2 x 1.7 cm. Multiplicity of these cysts likely represents IPMN; however, other neoplasms cannot be excluded.  The adrenal glands are unremarkable.  There are multiple bilateral renal hypodensities which likely represent cysts.  A very large cyst on the right herniates through the diaphragm in two locations; one of these locations of herniation is new compared to prior.  There is infrarenal aortic aneurysmal dilatation measuring 3.2 x 3.2 cm.  The aorta is tortuous, likely secondary to scoliosis.  Atherosclerotic calcification is seen.  CT OF THE PELVIS WITH CONTRAST: There is sigmoid diverticulosis without evidence for diverticulitis.  The uterus and adnexal structures are not visualized and are likely surgically absent.  Surgical suture material is visualized in the pelvis.  The bladder and visualized portions of small bowel are unremarkable.  The appendix is not definitively visualized but there is no right lower quadrant fat stranding or fluid collection.  MRCP.: 3.  Infrarenal aortic aneurysmal dilatation up to 3.2 cm.  Preliminary findings were communicated by wet read at 12:45 p.m. on ___.  Additional findings and recommendations were reported to the radiology communication dashboard at 5:15 p.m. on ___.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
