    'RIGHT UPPER QUADRANT ULTRASOUND PERFORMED ON ___: Comparison with a CT abdomen and pelvis performed earlier today as well as a prior abdominal ultrasound from ___.  FINDINGS: The liver appears normal in size and echotexture without focal lesion.  The gallbladder is markedly distended with a thickened wall and trace pericholecystic fluid.  Sonographic ___ sign could not be determined given patient''s medicated status.  There is a small amount of sludge within the gallbladder lumen.  No definite stones could be visualized.  Please note, patient had a stone on the prior study.  The common bile duct measures 8 mm in diameter and no definite sign of choledocholithiasis is seen.  Pancreatic cystic lesion in the head is better assessed on the preceding CT.  Main portal vein is patent with hepatopetal flow.  No definite intrahepatic biliary ductal dilation is seen.'
);


