INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '29565262',
    '10522176-RR-47',
    'MRCP',
    'Abdomen',
    'MRCP (MR ABD W&W/OC)',
    'TECHNIQUE: Multiplanar MR imaging of the abdomen was performed, including dynamically acquired images obtained prior to, during, and after administration of IV contrast.  A total of 8 cc of Gadavist was administered for this examination.  In addition, in order to opacify proximal bowel loops, 2.5 cc of Gadavist diluted with 75 cc of water was also orally administered.  FINDINGS: The gallbladder wall is notably edematous.  There is a gallstone seen within the gallbladder (series 5, image 13), which measures approximately 6 mm.  There are no stones seen within the common duct.  The common duct measures 3 mm in diameter.  There is no pancreatic ductal dilation.  Pancreatic parenchyma appears unremarkable without evidence of complications related to pancreatitis.  The SMV appears somewhat narrow, of uncertain clinical significance.  There is no evidence of thrombus.    A 2.3 cm cystic focus which has a somewhat thick wall is seen arising from the inferior aspect of the spleen (series 3, image 34).  The liver demonstrates mild drop of signal on the out of phase images compared with the in phase images, consistent with hepatic steatosis.  Multiple renal pelvic cysts are seen on the left.  Punctate nonenhancing foci are seen within the kidneys, less than 4 mm in diameter, probably representing cysts although more difficult to see on T2 weighted images.  No evidence of hydronephrosis or renal mass.  The bilateral adrenal glands appear unremarkable.'
);


