    'EXAMINATION: LIVER OR GALLBLADDER US (SINGLE ORGAN):  TECHNIQUE: Grayscale and color Doppler ultrasound examination of the abdomen was performed.  FINDINGS:   LIVER: The liver echotexture is normal and the contour is smooth. There is no focal liver lesion. The main portal vein is patent with hepatopetal flow. There is no ascites.  BILE DUCTS: There is no intrahepatic bile duct dilation. The CBD measures 6 mm, tapering smoothly as it nears the papilla.  GALLBLADDER: There are multiple mobile gallstones with a larger, 17 mm stone which is immobile and located within the phrygian cap.  The gallbladder is nondistended, without wall thickening.  PANCREAS: The head and body of the pancreas are normal.  The tail was not well seen due to overlying bowel gas.  SPLEEN: Normal echogenicity, measuring 8.4 cm.  RETROPERITONEUM: The imaged portions of the aorta and IVC are within normal limits.'
