    'EXAMINATION: MRCP ABDOMEN:  TECHNIQUE: Multiphasic multi sequence MRCP of the abdomen was performed on ___. 9 cc of Gadovist iodinated contrast was administered intravenously without reported complication.  FINDINGS: Abnormal T2 signal prolongation centered around the pancreatic tail with associated enhancement and diffusion restriction is compatible with pancreatitis. There is a small amount of hemorrhagic peripancreatic fluid and ascites, as well as adjacent thickening of Gerota''s fascia. There is no evidence of necrosis.  Multiple gallstones layer within the gallbladder. There is no choledocholithiasis. The common bile duct is normal caliber measuring 5 mm. There is no intra or extrahepatic biliary ductal dilatation. The portal vein, SMV and splenic veins are patent.  The spleen, kidneys, and liver are notable only for a small left renal cyst. There is no hydronephrosis. Both kidneys enhance symmetrically.  The image portions of the abdominal aorta are normal caliber. There is no upper abdominal lymphadenopathy. Imaged portions of the bowel are unremarkable.  The visualized heart, lung bases, bones and soft tissues are unremarkable.'
);


