INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '26286187',
    '10734159-RR-90',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT-acquired axial images were obtained from the base of the lungs to the pubic symphysis after the administration of IV contrast.  Multiplanar reformatted images were prepared and reviewed.  FINDINGS:   CT ABDOMEN WITH IV CONTRAST: Mild atelectatic changes are noted at both lung bases.  The visualized heart is normal in size without a pericardial effusion.   The gallbladder contains stones and is distended with evidence of wall edema.  There is hyperemia also noted in the hepatic parenchyma adjacent to the gallbladder.  These findings are highly concerning for ____. No intra- or extra-hepatic biliary dilatation is present.  Again visualized throughout the the liver are multiple hypodense lesions which appear stable compared to prior study and likely representative of hepatic cysts (2:14, 42).  The portal and hepatic veins are patent.   Bilateral kidneys contain multiple hypodense foci which are too small to characterize and others consistent with cysts. Overall, these findings are stable in comparison to the prior study.  No evidence of hydronephrosis or stones.  The stomach, visualized loops of small bowel, spleen, pancreas, and bilateral adrenal glands, are within normal limits. There is a small hiatal hernia.  There is dilatation of the left gonadal vein (2:36).  The abdominal aorta is normal in caliber and contour.  There is no free fluid or free air in the abdomen.  CT PELVIS WITH IV CONTRAST: There is colonic diverticulosis but no evidence of diverticulitis.  The uterus appears to contain a fundal fibroid.  The bladder and rectum are within normal limits. Again noted is 3.1 x 2.2 cm right adenxal hypodense lesion, stable in comparison to the prior studies. Left sided pelvic varices are present. Varices are again noted in the right inguinal region as well.  There is no free fluid or free air.  There is no pelvic or inguinal lymphadenopathy.    Osseous Structures:  There are no lytic or sclerotic osseous lesions suspicious for malignancy.  Extensive degenerative changes are again noted in the right hip.'
);


