    '25529120',
    '10758777-RR-51',
    'MRCP',
    'Abdomen',
    'MRCP (MR ABD W&W/OC)',
    'TECHNIQUE: Multiplanar T1- and T2-weighted images of the abdomen acquired on a 1.5 Tesla magnet including dynamic 3D imaging obtained prior to, during, and after the uneventful IV administration of 15 mL Magnevist gadolinium contrast. Prior to the examination, 100 mL of GastroMARK and 100 mL Redicat were administered by mouth.  Multiplanar 2D and 3D reformations and subtraction images were generated on an independent workstation.  MR OF THE ABDOMEN WITH IV GADOLINIUM (MRCP):  The gallbladder is distended and contains several small dependent gallstones, although the wall is not thickened and there is no adjacent fluid.  The biliary tree is normal in caliber, and there is no evidence of choledocholithiasis.  Note is made of a linear structure that courses along the cephalad aspect of the gallbladder, low in singal on postcontrast T1 imaging and high in signal on pre-contrast T2-weighted imaging - this is most consistent with an aberrant bile duct which courses along the cephalad aspect of the gallbladder. It is difficult to define the origin and insertion of this duct, but it appears to arise from the gallbladder (___) and insert into the common hepatic duct near the cystic duct insertion (4:20). These findings are suported  on the thick slab cholangiogram graphic images (8:4).  The spleen is markedly enlarged measuring 20 cm in craniocaudal length.  There are two small non-enhancing cystic lesions of the pancreatic body which measure up to 6 mm. There is no peripancreatic inflammatory change or fluid. There are no enlarged lymph nodes.  Relative to the spleen, the hepatic parenchyma drops signal intensity on T1-weighted out-of-phase images relative to in-phase images indicating fatty infiltration.  A small area of subcapsular arterial enhancement of segment V has a tubular branching morphology, consistent with a perfusion anomaly.  There are no concerning hepatic lesions or ascites.  Centered in the collecting system of the lower pole of the right kidney is a nonenhancing 11 mm area which is low signal intensity on T1- and T2-weighted images, likely a non- obstructing calculus. There is no hydronephrosis of either kidney. There is a 2.5 cm simple cyst of the lower pole of the left kidney.  The celiac trunk, SMA, and renal arteries are patent.  There is no focal bone lesion.  Multiplanar 2D and 3D reformations and subtraction images were essential in evaluation of the biliary tree.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
