VALUES (
    '25323331',
    '10819799-RR-49',
    'CT',
    'Head',
    'CT HEAD W/O CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: Axial CT images were acquired of the head without contrast and reformatted into coronal and sagittal planes.  FINDINGS: There is no evidence of  hemorrhage, abnormal fluid collections, mass effect or recent infarction.  The ventricles and sulci remain mildly enlarged, consistent with age-appropriate atrophy.  Encephalomalacia in the left frontal and parietal lobes is likely the result of prior infarction.  Gray matter/white matter differentiation is otherwise preserved.  There is mild periventricular white matter hypodensity consistent with chronic small vessel ischemic change. There is no osseous abnormality.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '25323331',
    '10819799-RR-54',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS W/O CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: Helically acquired axial MDCT images were obtained from the lung bases to the pubic symphysis without intravenous or oral contrast.  Coronal and sagittal reformatted images are provided.  CONTRAST: None.  CT OF THE ABDOMEN WITHOUT INTRAVENOUS CONTRAST: There is a trace right-sided pleural effusion and bilateral lower lobe atelectasis that is new from the CT ___.  Imaged portion of lung bases appear otherwise unchanged.  Coronary artery calcifications and aortic valvular calcifications again noted.  There has been interval placement of a percutaneous ____ tube which is in appropriate position with pigtail in the gallbladder lumen surrounded by multiple stones.  A trace amount of fluid is seen along the right hepatic capsule and inferior to the right hepatic lobe and is of low density, without evidence of hematoma.  There is no evidence of hematoma elsewhere in the abdomen or pelvis.  The gallbladder itself is contracted around multiple stones and shows wall edema consistent with known ____.  There is no evidence of biliary dilation.  Fatty atrophy of the pancreas again noted.  Multiple prominent peripancreatic lymph nodes are stable.  Focal calcifications in the spleen are consistent with granulomas.  Two hypodense lesions in the left adrenal gland are unchanged and consistent with adenomas.  The non-contrast appearance of the kidneys appears within normal limits.  There is atherosclerotic calcification of the aorta.  Large and small bowel loops are normal in caliber and contour.  There is no free intraperitoneal air.  CT OF THE PELVIS WITHOUT INTRAVENOUS CONTRAST: There is no evidence of hematoma in the pelvis or inguinal regions.  Bladder is collapsed around a Foley catheter.  Prostate, seminal vesicles, rectum, and sigmoid colon appear unremarkable.  Diffuse vascular calcifications are consistent with atherosclerotic change.  BONE WINDOWS: There is severe degenerative change of the right hip and multilevel degenerative change of the thoracic and lumbar spine with no suspicious lytic or sclerotic osseous lesions identified.  An L2 upper endplate vertebral compression deformity is unchanged.'
);


