INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '23898699',
    '10830214-RR-4',
    'MRCP',
    'Abdomen',
    'MRCP (MR ABD W&W/OC)',
    'MRCP ___:   TECHNIQUE: Multiplanar T1- and T2-weighted imaging was performed on a 1.5 T magnet, prior to, during, and subsequent to the administration of 0.1 mmol/kg of Gadovist (7 mL).  2.5 mL of Gadovist with 75 mL of water was administered orally prior to the procedure.  Images (particularly the dynamic post contrast sequences) are degraded by breath-hold artifact.  FINDINGS: The liver is of normal signal on T2-weighted imaging, no significant signal dropoff on out-of-phase imaging when compared to the T1-weighted in-phase imaging to suggest fatty deposition.  No focal liver lesion within the limitations of this scan.  The portal and hepatic veins are patent.  There is conventional hepatic arterial anatomy.  No intra- or extra-hepatic biliary dilatation, the common bile duct measures 5 mm.  The pancreatic duct measures 2 mm.  Post contrast images are non-diagnostic at the level of the ampulla however there is no evidence of an ampullary mass on T2 weighted imaging.  No intraductal filling defects.  The gallbladder is slightly thick-walled but non distended. There is a small amount of high T2 signal adjacent to the gallbladder either representing some fluid adjacent to the gallbladder or possible folding of gallbladder wall.  Gallstones from prior sonography are less evident now.   The pancreas enhances normally.  No focal pancreatic lesion.  No pancreatic duct dilatation.  There is a 1.4-cm lobulated cystic lesion at the lower pole of the right kidney. Images are degraded by motion artifact however there appears to be some internal septae/peripheral nodular enhancement post-administration of contrast.  The appearanced are indeterminate and a followup scan is advised in six months'' time.  Several other simple cysts are noted within both kidneys.  The spleen and adrenal glands are unremarkable.  The small and large bowel are also within normal limits.  No upper abdominal or retroperitoneal lymphadenopathy.'
);


