    'FINDINGS: The liver appears mildly coarsened without focal lesion.  There is no biliary dilatation.  The gallbladder contains multiple shadowing stones, but does not appear distended.  There are areas of ring-down artifacts along the anterior wall, raising question of adenomyomatosis.  There is no pericholecystic fluid.  There is no biliary dilatation.  The common duct measures 4 mm.  There is normal hepatopetal flow in the portal vein.  The spleen measures 12 cm.  Partially visualized pancreas, aorta, and IVC are within normal limits.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '21860863',
    '10880579-RR-20',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'LIVER OR GALLBLADDER US (SINGLE ORGAN)',
    'FINDINGS: The left hepatic lobe is heterogeneous compatible with known tumor infiltration, better seen on prior CT.  The right hepatic lobe is coarsened in echotexture.  There is no intrahepatic bile duct dilation. Two biliary stents are in place. Shadowing gallstones are seen with nonspecific wall thickening given the gallbladder is contracted on the current exam. There is no pericholecystic fluid. Unable to assess sonographic ___ sinus as the patient received morphine prior to the study. The pancreas is not seen due to overlying bowel gas.  The spleen is not well visualized but measures approximately 9.9 cm.  Single views of each kidney show no hydronephrosis.  There is no ascites.  DOPPLER ASSESSMENT: Color Doppler assessment with spectral analysis of the hepatic vasculature was performed.  The main portal vein is patent with normal hepatopetal flow.  There is normal forward flow in the left portal, right anterior and right posterior portal veins.  The middle, left and right hepatic veins are patent with normal waveforms.  The main hepatic artery is patent with a brisk systolic upstroke and forward flow in diastole.'
);


