INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '21860863',
    '10880579-RR-24',
    'CT',
    'Chest',
    'CT CHEST W/CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: Axial CT images through the chest, abdomen and pelvis were obtained following intravenous and oral contrast administration.  Three-minute delayed imaging through the abdomen was also obtained.  Sagittal and coronal reformats were reviewed.  FINDINGS:   CHEST: There is an enlarged 9-mm right pretracheal lymph node containing central necrosis (20:3). There is a 13.6 mm subcarinal node (24:3).  There is also significant amount of right-sided paracardiac lymphadenopathy, marker node measuring 1 cm (39:3).  Overall, these lymph nodes have increased in size compared to the previous exam. There is no abnormal axillary or hilar lymphadenopathy.  The heart and great vessels are unremarkable.  There is a new right-sided pleural effusion.  The central tracheobronchial tree is clear.  Atelectasis is seen at the right lung base as well as within the right middle lobe.  Superimposed consolidation is not excluded.  The right middle lobe atelectasis is stable compared to previous; however, the right lower lobe atelectasis is new.  ABDOMEN: There is a new large pericholecystic fluid collection containing locules of air.  There is also air seen within the gallbladder lumen. The gallbladder is decompressed and the gallbladder mucosa appears interrupted in several locations. The gallstone seen previously,  is no longer visualized within the gallballder.   There is additonally, inflammatory stranding surrounding the transverse mesocolon likely related to the spread of the pericholecystic inflammation. A fistula between the gallbladder and transverse colon is not excluded.   There is perihepatic fluid, which is indenting the liver capsule.  This tracks inferiorly where the largest pocket of fluid in the anterior abdominal wall measures 6.1 x 2.7 x 6.2 cm.   There are two CBD stents in situ filled with debris.  No air is seen within the intrahepatic biliary tree. Again appreciated are the significantly dilated bile ducts within the left lobe of the liver. There is an infiltrative mass in the left lobe of the liver with an atrophic left lobe. Appearances are not significantly changed. Fiducial seeds are also seen within the left lobe of the liver.   There is fatty atrophy of the pancreas.  The spleen, left adrenal, right kidney are unremarkable.  There is a small left upper pole renal cyst.  There are multiple enlarged periportal nodes, marker measuring 11 mm (53:3).  There is tubing within the stomach of uncertain etiology, possibly a displaced biliary stent. The visualized small and large bowels are unremarkable.  Otherwise, the visualized large and small bowels are unremarkable.  PELVIS: The bladder, uterus, adnexa and rectum appear unremarkable.  There is no free fluid layering in the pelvis.  BONES: A sclerotic T7 vertebral lesion is unchanged, from ___.'
);


