    'FRONTAL CHEST RADIOGRAPH: Sternal wires and mediastinal clips denote prior cardiac surgery.  The heart size is top normal.  Widespread coarse reticular opacities are increased since the ___ radiograph, particularly at the bases, verified via direct comparison between the abdominal CT examination performed this evening and a chest CT from ___, reflecting progressive interstitial lung disease in the setting of severe emphysema.    Bilateral upper zone calcified nodules are also seen on the CT from ___, likely the sequela of granulomatous disease.    There is no pneumothorax or pleural effusion.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '29994310',
    '10983866-RR-33',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'ABDOMEN (SUPINE & ERECT)',
    'ABDOMEN:   FINDINGS: Documentation is provided by two radiographic images.  No free intra-abdominal air.  Several small air-fluid levels projecting over nondistended bowel loops in the mid abdomen.  Colonic air filling and stool filling of the ascending and descending colon.  Contrast material in the bladder.  Diffuse gas feeling of small bowel loops without evidence of wall thickening.  No pathologic calcifications.  No foreign bodies.'
