INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '28501096',
    '11072749-RR-20',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'LIVER OR GALLBLADDER US (SINGLE ORGAN) PORT',
    'EXAMINATION: LIVER OR GALLBLADDER US (SINGLE ORGAN):  TECHNIQUE: Grey scale and color Doppler ultrasound images of the abdomen were obtained.  FINDINGS:   LIVER: The echogenicity of the liver is homogeneous. The contour of the liver is smooth. There is no focal liver mass. Main portal vein is patent with hepatopetal flow. There is no ascites.  BILE DUCTS: There is no intrahepatic biliary dilation. The CBD remains dilated, measuring 12.3 mm at the level of the hepatic artery.  GALLBLADDER: The gallbladder remains distended, however the gallbladder wall is now of normal thickness. There are several stones present, with a large stone within the gallbladder neck, which is not mobile. There is no pericholecystic free fluid. There is a small amount of sludge within the gallbladder.  PANCREAS: Visualized portions of the pancreas are normal  SPLEEN: Normal echogenicity, measuring 8.3 cm.  KIDNEYS: The right kidney measures 8.8 cm. The left kidney measures 9 cm. Limited imaging demonstrates no evidence of hydronephrosis.  NOTIFICATION: Findings discussed by Dr. ___ with Dr. ___ at approximately 15:00 on ___.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '28501096',
    '11072749-RR-22',
    'CT',
    'Chest',
    'CTA CHEST W&W/O C&RECONS, NON-CORONARY',
    'PE.:   TECHNIQUE: MDCT-acquired images through the chest were obtained at 1.25 mm slice thickness.  Coronally and sagittally reformatted images are provided.  DLP: 168 mGy-cm.  FINDINGS: The pulmonary arteries are well opacified without perfusion defects to suggest acute pulmonary embolus.  The main pulmonary artery is normal in size measuring 2.1 cm.  Intrathoracic aorta is normal in caliber without evidence of dissection or acute aortic syndrome.  The great vessels are unremarkable.  The heart is normal in size without pericardial effusion.  The tracheobronchial tree is patent to subsegmental levels.  There are small-to-moderate left and moderate right pleural effusions, which appear nonhemorrhagic.  Adjacent areas of compressive atelectasis are noted.  Centrilobular emphysema is mild in the upper lobes.  No pneumothorax or focal consolidation.  Linear opacities in the lingula and left lower lobe, likely reflect atelectasis.  No suspicious pulmonary mass is identified.  Ground-glass opacities are seen in bilateral lower lobes.  Thera are scattered central lymph nodes, which do not meet CT criteria for pathologic enlargement. There is no axillary lymphadenopathy.  The thyroid gland is heterogeneous in enhancement.    This study is not tailored for subdiaphragmatic evaluation, moderately large hiatal hernia is noted.  Partially visualized liver demonstrates pneumobilia, which most likely relates to recent percutaneous ____ drain placement.  OSSEOUS STRUCTURES: No suspicious lytic or sclerotic bony lesion is seen.'
);


