INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '29153618',
    '11132868-RR-58',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT-acquired axial images were obtained from the base of the lungs to pubic symphysis after administration of 130 mL of Omnipaque nonionic intravenous contrast.  Multiplanar reformatted images were prepared and reviewed.  FINDINGS:   CT OF THE ABDOMEN WITH IV CONTRAST: The visualized lung bases demonstrate bibasilar opacities, right greater than left, may represent atelectasis and possibly a component of pneumonia especially at the right base.  A 2.8 x 2.2 cm bulla is visualized in the right lower lobe (2:2).  The visualized heart is normal in size without pericardial effusion.  The gallbladder appears partially distended with significant gallbladder wall edema. A 2.8 x 2.2 impacted stone is noted at the gallbladder neck. A dependent stone is also noted in the fundus. Additionally, a small amount of free perihepatic fluid is identified and consistent with ascites from acute ____ (2:48). There is no intrahepatic biliary ductal dilation to suggest ___''s syndrome.  Otherwise, the liver, spleen, pancreas, stomach, visualized loops of small and large bowel are within normal limits.   The appendix is normal in appearance. The left adrenal gland and the left kidney are within normal limits. The right kidney appears low lying and malrotated. A lying down right adrenal gland is congenital given the pelvic right kidney.  Extensive atherosclerotic calcifications are visualized throughout the distal aorta and the origin of bilateral common iliac arteries.  A hypodense focus is also noted in the right external iliac artery (2:85) and may be representative of non-calcified plaque. The aorta is normal in caliber and contour.  There is no free air in the abdomen.  There is no mesenteric or retroperitoneal lymphadenopathy.  CT OF THE PELVIS WITH IV CONTRAST: The bladder, rectum, sigmoid colon, and prostate are within normal limits.  There is no free fluid or free air in the pelvis.  Prominent bilateral inguinal lymph nodes are identified, but there is no pelvic or inguinal lymphadenopathy by CT size criteria.  OSSEOUS STRUCTURES: There are no lytic or sclerotic osseous lesions suspicious for malignancy.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '29153618',
    '11132868-RR-59',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABDOMEN W/CONTRAST',
    'FINDINGS: There is dependent bibasilar atelectasis as well as mild ground-glass opacities.  Coronary artery disease is partially imaged.  The visualized portions of the heart and pericardium are otherwise unremarkable.  There is hyperemia surrounding the gallbladder fossa at the site of prior cholecystectomy as well as small amount of residual fluid, likely representing seroma.  The hepatic and portal veins are patent.  Oral contrast passes through the stomach and small bowel without any extravasation.  There is no retroperitoneal air or oral contrast to suggest a duodenal leak.  The pancreas, spleen, and adrenals are normal.  The kidneys enhance symmetrically. Of note, the right kidney is in a pelvic position and is only partially imaged.  The visualized portions of the large bowel are normal.  There is a tiny amount of free intraperitoneal air as well as some in the abdominal wall, consistent with recent open cholecystectomy.  Atherosclerotic calcifications are noted throughout the descending aorta.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '25972552',
    '11133971-RR-78',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS W/O CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: Helical MDCT images were acquired from the lung bases through the greater trochanters without intravenous contrast, due to the patient''s chronic renal failure.  No oral contrast was administered.  Coronal and sagittal multiplanar reformations were generated.  FINDINGS: Evaluation is suboptimal, due to lack of intravenous/oral contrast and patient motion.  Moderate cardiomegaly is present, with evidence of right-sided volume overload.  A small pericardial effusion is present.  Relative hypoattenuation of the blood pool is consistent with anemia.  Calcifications are noted in the descending aorta and mitral annulus.  Mild atelectasis is noted at the lung bases.  There are no pleural effusions.  Note is made of a small paraesophageal hiatal hernia.  ABDOMEN: The gallbladder is distended, with a partially visualized 2.4 cm hyperdense stone that appears to be impacted at the neck.  Additional rim- calcified stones in the body and fundus measure 1.5 and 1.6 cm.  There is a vague fluid level within the gallbladder, with dependent contents measuring ___ ___, and nondependent contents measuring 15 ___.  This is suggestive of mixed bilirubin and cholesterol contents, with possible superimposed hemorrhage.  Diffuse gallbladder wall edema is noted, with slight contour irregularity.  There is surrounding fat stranding and pericholecystic fluid tracking along the inferior margin of the liver.    The liver is unremarkable on this noncontrast examination.  The pancreas is slightly atrophic.  There is no high-grade intra- or extra-hepatic biliary ductal dilatation, although evaluation is suboptimal without intravenous contrast.  The spleen is normal in size.  Calcifications are noted in the splenic artery.  The adrenals appear slightly full bilaterally.  The kidneys are atrophic, with cortical thinning and lobulation reflecting prior infectious or ischemic injury.  There are no renal stones or hydronephrosis.  The stomach and small bowel are normal.  PELVIS: The appendix, colon and rectum are normal.  Bowel loops are normal in caliber, without evidence of transition point to suggest obstruction.  There is no evidence of inflammatory wall thickening or fat stranding.  There are no extraluminal air collections to suggest perforation.  There is no pneumatosis, portal or mesenteric venous gas to indicate ischemia.  There is a Foley catheter in the bladder.  The prostate is mildly enlarged.  Coarse calcifications are noted throughout the abdominal aorta and iliac arteries, with severe stenosis of the celiac, SMA, renal artery, and ___ ___.  Multiple prominent lymph nodes measure up to 7 mm in the mesentery and 6 mm in the retroperitoneum, and are likely reactive.  The bones are diffusely demineralized, with multilevel bridging osteophytes. No suspicious lytic or sclerotic osseous lesions are identified.  Mild diffuse body wall edema is present.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '25972552',
    '11133971-RR-79',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'LIVER OR GALLBLADDER US (SINGLE ORGAN)',
    'RIGHT UPPER QUADRANT ULTRASOUND: The gallbladder is markedly distended, with a 2.5 cm x 2.1 cm x 1.6 cm impacted stone at the neck.  Multiple additional stones are present in the gallbladder fundus, and demonstrate mobility with patient repositioning.  There is a large amount of layering sludge, with distinct hyper- and hypoechoic components suggesting combined cholesterol and bilirubin sediments, and possible superimposed hemorrhage.  Diffuse gallbladder wall edema is present, measuring up to 7 mm.  The wall appears slightly irregular, although no dirty shadowing is seen to indicate intramural air.  There is a small amount of pericholecystic fluid at the gallbladder fundus.  Ultrasonographic ___ sign is positive.  The liver is normal in echogenicity, without focal lesions.  There is normal hepatopetal flow in the portal vein.  There is mild intrahepatic biliary dilation.  The common duct measures 4 mm, and is not well seen beyond the level of the impacted gallstone.  The pancreatic head and body are normal, and the tail is not well visualized due to shadowing bowel gas.  There is no pancreatic ductal dilatation.  Incidental note is made of a 1.3 cm simple cyst in the right upper renal pole.'
);


