INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '22841113',
    '11275704-RR-22',
    'CT',
    'Chest',
    'CHEST (PA & LAT)',
    'CHEST, PA AND LATERAL:   FINDINGS: AP and lateral chest views have been obtained with patient in sitting upright position.  The heart size is difficult to determine related to asymmetric right-sided pulmonary hyperinflation with mediastinal shift towards the left and corresponding alteration of cardiac contours.  The aortic arch and descending contour is identified on the left side.  There is a prominent shadow in the right upper mediastinum occupying the right tracheal main bronchus angle usually the place of the azygos vein.  This prominent density, however, has a diameter of approximately 2 cm and coinciding with this finding, there exists a local narrowing of the trachea seen on the frontal view.  The possibility of a vascular abnormality is, therefore, entertained.  There exists an irregular vascular distribution pattern in the entire right lung, but there is no evidence for typical findings related to chronic pulmonary venous congestion.  Noteworthy is a concave contour in the mid portion of the right-sided mediastinum suggestive of some mediastinal shift towards the left which also could explain the unusual cardiac contour on the left side.  There are some local densities, poorly delineated in the right upper lobe area which could be infectious processes.  However, as we have no previous examination available for comparison, further followup is recommended.'
);


