INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '24636219',
    '11365171-RR-13',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABDOMEN W/CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: Multidetector CT acquisition was performed from the lung bases to the iliac crests with oral and 150 mL Omnipaque intravenous contrast.  Coronal and sagittal reformats were displayed with 5-mm slice thickness.  DLP: 656.38 mGy-cm.  FINDINGS: The visualized lung bases demonstrate nonhemorrhagic pleural effusions, small on the right and trace on the left.  There is mild adjacent bibasilar atelectasis.  The liver is normal.  The gallbladder is dilated with a small amount of pericholecystic fluid, but no wall hyperemia and no adjacent fat stranding.  A 12mm intra-luminal hyperdense focus may represent a gallstone.  There is moderate intrahepatic bile duct dilation and dilation of the common duct to 9 mm with prominence of the ampulla.  The pancreatic duct is not dilated and the pancreas is normal.  The spleen and adrenal glands are normal.  The kidneys enhance symmetrically and excrete contrast promptly without hydronephrosis.  The imaged portions of the stomach and bowel are normal.  The imaged aorta is of normal caliber throughout.  The main portal vein, splenic vein and SMV are patent.  A 12-mm aortocaval lymph node is more prominent than in ___.  There is no free fluid and no free air.  BONE WINDOWS: No bone finding suspicious for infection or malignancy is seen.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '24636219',
    '11365171-RR-14',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT imaging of the abdomen and pelvis with intravenous contrast was performed.  Multiplanar reformats were prepared and reviewed.  DLP: 1142.90 mGy-cm  FINDINGS:   ABDOMEN: Previously identified pleural effusions have mostly resolved.  The visualized lung bases are otherwise clear.    A small hyperenhancing liver lesion consistent in appearance with an hemangioma is seen in the lateral right lobe of the liver.  The liver is otherwise homogeneous in texture with no focal lesions.  A biliary stent is seen in appropriate position.  There is no intrahepatic or extrahepatic biliary ductal dilatation.  The CBD measures 6 mm.  The gallbladder wall is slightly edematous, but the gallbladder is not distended and there is no pericholecystic fat stranding.  A 12 mm intraluminal hyperdense focus is again seen within the gallbladder, which likely represents a gallstone.   The body and tail of the pancreas appear normal.  A hypodensity is seen within the head of the pancreas along the pancreaticoduodenal groove, consistent with groove pancreatitis.  There is adjacent lymphadenopathy in the porta hepatis measuring 2.3 x 1.8 cm.  The previously seen 12 mm aortocaval lymph node is unchanged from prior exam.  There is no evidence of duodenal perforation or inflammation.  The stomach, duodenum, and intra-abdominal loops of bowel are normal in caliber and unremarkable.  The spleen and adrenal glands are normal.  The kidneys are unremarkable with no contour irregularities, hydronephrosis, or nephrolithiasis.  The intra-abdominal aorta is normal in appearance.  PELVIS: The sigmoid colon and rectum are normal in appearance.  The distal ureters and bladder are normal.   An IUD is noted within the uterus. The uterus is otherwise unremarkable.  There is no pelvic or inguinal lymphadenopathy.  There is no free fluid in the pelvis.  BONE WINDOWS: No focal lytic or sclerotic osseous lesion suspicious for infection or malignancy is seen.  NOTIFICATION: These findings were communicated to Dr. ___ at 2:30 p.m. on ___ in person.'
);


