INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '26169546',
    '11490406-RR-25',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: Axial MDCT images were obtained through the abdomen and pelvis following the administration of 130 cc of Visipaque intravenous contrast material and without oral contrast material.  Reformatted coronal and sagittal images were obtained.  DOSE: DLP:  337 mGy-cm. CTDIvol:  7 mGy.  FINDINGS:   THORAX: The visualized lung bases are clear with no pleural effusions, pneumothorax or focal opacities. There is mild enlargement of the heart, and post-surgical changes following CABG are noted.  LIVER: The liver enhances homogeneously with no focal lesions. The portal and hepatic veins are patent, and there is no intra or extrahepatic biliary duct dilatation.  GALLBLADDER: The gallbladder is distended with multiple gallstones and a gallstone at the gallbladder neck (02:29). The gallbladder wall is thickened with mucosal hyperemia and adjacent fat stranding.  SPLEEN: The spleen is normal in size and shape.  PANCREAS: A 7 mm pancreatic tail cyst is smaller compared to ___ when it measured 1.1 x 1.2 cm (2:31). There is no pancreatic ductal dilation.  ADRENALS: The adrenal glands are normal in size and shape.  KIDNEYS: The kidneys are normal in size and shape.  Renal hypodensities are compatible with cysts, previously characterized on prior MR from ___. The kidneys have appropriate contrast enhancement and excretion bilaterally.  There is hydronephrosis or perinephric stranding.  BOWEL: Small hiatal hernia is present. The stomach is mildly distended and unremarkable.  There is wall edema within the duodenum adjacent to the inflamed gallbladder (2:38), likely reactive. The remaining small bowel is without obstruction or focal wall thickening.  The appendix is not visualized, but there are no secondary findings to suggest appendicitis. The large bowel contains feces without wall thickening or evidence of obstruction.  Suture material likely representing prior colonic resection and anastomosis is noted at the hepatic flexure (2:40). There is no intraperitoneal free air or free fluid.  LYMPH NODES: There are no pathologically enlarged retroperitoneal or mesenteric lymph nodes by CT size criteria.  PELVIS: The bladder is relatively well distended without focal wall thickening. There is no pelvic free fluid. There are no pathologically enlarged pelvic sidewall or inguinal lymph nodes by CT size criteria, and left inguinal surgical clip is seen (2:79). The rectum is unremarkable.  VESSELS & SOFT TISSUE:  There is extensiveatherosclerotic disease without aneurysmal dilatation of the abdominal aorta. The aorta and its major branches are patent.  BONES: There are no suspicious lytic or sclerotic osseous lesions to suggest malignancy. Degenerative changes within the thoracolumbar spine are noted along with scoliosis.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
