)
VALUES (
    '25629867',
    '11547436-RR-19',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'ABDOMEN U.S. (COMPLETE STUDY)',
    'ABDOMINAL ULTRASOUND:   FINDINGS: The liver is normal in echotexture without focal masses or lesions. There is no intra- or extra-hepatic biliary dilatation.  There is normal hepatopetal flow within the main portal vein.  There is a 1.8 x 1.5 x 1.2 cm hyperechoic structure with posterior shadowing in the neck of the gallbladder, likely an impacted stone. There is a second shadowing calculus in the fundus of the gallbladder which is not mobile. There is achogenic nonshadowing material in the gallbladder lumen which likely represents sludge. There is equivocal thickening of the gallbladder wall (1a:33) though this is likely a result of technique. The gallbladder is not distended. There is no pericholecystic fluid.  The common bile duct measures 5 mm.  There is a positive sonographic ___ sign.  The right and left kidneys are normal in echotexture without stones, masses or hydronephrosis.  The right kidney measures 9.8 cm, and the left kidney measures 8.6 cm.  The spleen is normal in echotexture measuring 10.3 cm.  The pancreas is poorly visualized due to overlying bowel gas.  The partially visualized proximal abdominal aorta is normal in appearance; however, evaluation is severely limited due to overlying bowel gas.'
);


