    'TECHNIQUE: Grayscale and color and spectral Doppler ultrasound images of the abdomen were obtained.  FINDINGS: The liver shows no evidence of focal lesions or textural abnormality.  Doppler assessment of the main portal vein shows patency and hepatopetal flow.  There is no ascites. There is no evidence of intrahepatic or extrahepatic biliary dilatation.  A small amount of pneumobilia is seen, consistent with history of sphincterotomy.  The CBD measures 3 mm.    The gallbladder is enlarged, similar prior exam, but not distended.  Gallbladder wall edema is seen with thickening of the wall to 7 mm, which is nonspecific.  No pericholecystic fluid is seen.  No ___ sign was detected during sonographic exam.  Gallstones and sludge are visualized within the gallbladder.    The tail of the pancreas is not well visualized due to overlying bowel gas, but the visualized portions of the pancreas are unremarkable.  Limited views of the right kidney are unremarkable.  The spleen measures 9.4 cm and demonstrates a homogeneous echotexture.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '21513149',
    '11573961-RR-39',
    'MRCP',
    'Abdomen',
    'MRCP (MR ABD W&W/OC)',
    'TECHNIQUE: Multiplanar T1 and T2 weighted MR images of the abdomen were performed in a 1.5 Tesla magnet, prior to and after uneventful intravenous administration of 8 mL of Gadavist.  FINDINGS: The liver is normal in signal intensity. Few tiny biliary hamartomas are seen. There is no intra or extrahepatic bile duct dilation. The CBD is normal in caliber. No obstructing intraductal stone or mass is seen. The gallbladder is distended with multiple gallstones/layering sludge.  There is marked gallbladder wall edema. There is heterogeneous arterial phase hyperenhancement in the gallbladder fossa. The findings are consistent with acute ____.    The pancreas is normal in signal intensity enhancement, without evidence of acute or chronic pancreatitis.  Few scattered sub 5 mm cystic lesions are seen in the body and tail of the pancreas (7:5), largest measuring 5 mm. The main pancreatic duct is not dilated.  The adrenal glands are normal. Multiple renal cortical cysts are seen in both kidneys, the largest in the upper pole of the left kidney, measuring 7.4 cm and lower pole of the right kidney measuring 1.6 cm. Few of the right renal cysts contain layering T1 hyperintense hemorrhage, without abnormal enhancement. (8:50, 64, 68, 73) There is no hydronephrosis or concerning renal mass.    Moderate atherosclerotic disease of the abdominal aorta is noted. The celiac trunk, superior mesenteric and bilateral renal arteries are patent. The portal, splenic and superior mesenteric veins are patent. No pathologic retroperitoneal or mesenteric lymphadenopathy seen. The stomach, imaged abdominal loops of small and large bowel are unremarkable, except for a small periampullary duodenal diverticulum.    There is no ascites. Trace right pleural effusion is noted.    Multiple sacral Tarlov cysts are seen (2:37). Scattered T2 hyperintense lesions in the thoracic and lumbar spine likely represent hemangiomas.  NOTIFICATION: Findings were discussed with ___ on ___ at 08:50 a.m via telephone by ___.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
