INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '27369388',
    '11593760-RR-22',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT axially acquired images were obtained from the dome of the liver to the pubic symphysis after the uneventful administration of 130 mL of Omnipaque and oral contrast.  Coronal and sagittal reformations were provided and reviewed.  DLP: 430.01 mGy-cm.  ABDOMEN: The visualized lung bases demonstrate bibasilar atelectasis.  There is no pleural effusion or pneumothorax.  A more rounded area of ground-glass opacity is noted in the right posterior lobe, but is incompletely imaged.  The heart size is top normal with slight enlargement of the left atrium.  A pacemaker is noted with wires terminating in the right atrium and right ventricle.  There is no pericardial effusion.  The liver enhances homogeneously without focal lesions.  A small granuloma is seen in segment VI.  The gallbladder is mildly distended with gallbladder wall edema; however, there is no surrounding inflammation to suggest ____. The common bile duct is prominent, measuring 7.5 mm and there is no intrahepatic biliary ductal dilation.  The spleen, pancreas, and adrenal glands are unremarkable.  The kidneys enhance symmetrically and excrete contrast without hydronephrosis.  There is no mesenteric or retroperitoneal lymphadenopathy.  The stomach, large and small bowel are unremarkable, without evidence of bowel wall thickening or obstruction.  A small fat-containing umbilical hernia is present.  There is no free air or free fluid.  The portal vein, splenic vein and superior mesenteric vein are patent.  There are dense calcifications seen throughout a non-aneurysmal aorta and at the origins of the renal and celiac arteries.  PELVIS: The bladder, uterus and rectum are normal.  The appendix is not visualized, although, there is no evidence of appendicitis.  There is trace free pelvic fluid.  No pelvic or inguinal sidewall lymphadenopathy is appreciated.  BONES: There are no suspicious osseous lesions.  Mild-to-moderate degenerative changes are seen within the hip.  A levoscoliosis of the lumbar spine with moderate-to-severe degenerative changes are appreciated.'
);


