INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '21948836',
    '11654859-RR-21',
    'MRI',
    'Abdomen',
    'MRI ABDOMEN W/O CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: Multiplanar T1- and T2-weighted images were acquired on a 1.5- Tesla magnet.  Given that the patient is pregnant, IV gadolinium was not administered.  Multiplanar 2D and 3D reformations were performed on an independent workstation.  MR ABDOMEN WITHOUT GADOLINIUM (MRCP):  The liver demonstrates normal signal with no focal lesions.  The gallbladder is diffusely edematous similar to prior ultrasound from ___.  There is a small amount of hyperintense T1-weighted signal along the dependent surface of the gallbladder suggesting a small amount of tiny stones or sludge.  There is no appreciable pancreatic edema or fluid collections.  The pancreas is normal in signal. The spleen is unremarkable.  The adrenal glands and kidneys are within normal limits.  The collecting systems are prominent, consistent with the physiology of pregnancy.  There is mild focal narrowing at the origin of the left hepatic duct with immediate distal dilatation to 9 mm. There is also mild narrowing at the origin of the right hepatic duct with no appreciable distal dilatation. The bommon hepatic and bile ducts are dilated to 9 mm. The distal common bile duct is moderately narrowed at the ampulla. There is no evidence of common bile duct stone or abnormal mass seen surrounding any of the above described areas of narrowing or dilatation.  Limited views of the bowel are unremarkable.  There is no free fluid within the upper abdomen.  There is normal marrow signal.'
);


