INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '23199260',
    '11808155-RR-39',
    'CT',
    'Chest',
    'CTA CHEST W&W/O C&RECONS, NON-CORONARY',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT-acquired axial images were obtained through the chest and abdomen without and with intravenous contrast.  No oral contrast was administered.  Coronal, sagittal, and oblique reformations were evaluated.  CT OF THE CHEST WITHOUT AND WITH INTRAVENOUS CONTRAST: There is no evidence of aortic dissection, pulmonary embolism, or intramural hematoma. Atherosclerotic disease is noted within the coronary circulation, aortic root, and aortic arch and there is mild-to-moderate left atrial enlargement.  No pericardial effusion is identified.  There is small right pleural effusion and trace left pleural effusion with low lung volumes and moderate atelectasis noted of the lower lobes bilaterally.  No pathologically enlarged central or axillary lymph nodes are identified.  The thyroid is noted to be markedly enlarged and contains multiple low-attenuation lesions within it, some of which display coarse peripheral calcifications.  The right lobe is noted to extend into the superior mediastinum and causes mild leftward deviation of the trachea without significant narrowing of the airway itself.  CT OF THE ABDOMEN WITHOUT AND WITH INTRAVENOUS CONTRAST: The gallbladder is distended with hyperenhancing mucosa and approximately 5-6 mm of wall edema/thickening.  Additionally there is suggestion of a focal area of mucosal discontinuity within the lower aspect of the fundus (3:11) which also appears present on the ___ examination.  Adenomyosis within the fundus is again noted. The extrahepatic common duct is mildly dilated measuring 9 mm with no definite choledocholithiasis (although the known gallstones are also not identified on this exam). There is new inflammation of the surrounding pericholecystic fat adjacent to redundant hepatic flexure which displays mild reactive changes/wall edema involving a 8-9cm decompressed segment. Other portions of the hepatic fexure are mildy dilated measuring 6cm.  Fatty replacement of the pancreas persists. Small left renal cyst and mild perinephric inflammatory changes are not significantly changed. Atherosclerotic disease is noted within the aorta.  No free air, free fluid, or pathologically enlarged lymph nodes are identified.  BONE WINDOWS: Old fracture of the right sixth rib with subtle probable fractures of the right fourth and fifth ribs appear to have been present on ___ exam.  No malignant-appearing osseous lesions are identified. Multilevel degenerative changes and degenerative disc disease are again noted. Wedge compression deformities with approximately 75% loss of intervertebral body height at T12 and 50% of anterior vertebral body height at L1 are new from ___.  Multilevel vertebral body hemangiomas are also present.'
);


