INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '25582981',
    '11902171-RR-38',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABDOMEN W/CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: Axially acquired images were obtained from the lung bases to the pubic symphysis after the administration of 100 cc of Optiray intravenous contrast.  In addition, three-minute delayed images for a venous phase study was performed through the lower extremities.  Coronal and sagittal reformatted images were also displayed.  FINDINGS:   CT OF THE ABDOMEN WITH IV CONTRAST: There is a punctate hyperdensity at the left lung base, likely a calcified granuloma.  Otherwise, the lung bases are clear bilaterally save for some linear atelectasis.  The heart size is normal. The spleen, kidneys, adrenal glands, pancreas, stomach are within normal limits.  The gallbladder is distended.  There is mild intrahepatic dilation.  Otherwise, the liver is normal in appearance.  There is no free air or free fluid.  There is no bowel obstruction.  There is retroperitoneal or mesenteric lymphadenopathy.  CT OF THE PELVIS WITH IV CONTRAST: The rectum, prostate, and bladder are within normal limits.  A Foley catheter is noted within a decompressed bladder.  There is no free fluid.  No pelvic or inguinal lymphadenopathy is present.  BONE WINDOWS: No concerning osseous lesions are identified.  There is no subcutaneous air throughout the torso.  CTV OF THE LOWER EXTREMITIES: Please note that the most lateral aspects of the legs bilaterally are excluded from view. No filling defects are noted within the common femoral, superficial femoral, popliteal, or posterior tibial or peroneal veins bilaterally.  There is diffuse soft tissue edema bilaterally.  There is no subcutaneous air.  Fluid is noted in the deep subcutaneous tissues surrounding the distal lower extremities bilaterally, predominantly around the ankles.'
);


