INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '24324099',
    '11990136-RR-20',
    'MRI',
    'Abdomen',
    'MRI ABDOMEN W/O CONTRAST',
    'EXAMINATION: MRI of the abdomen. MRCP.  TECHNIQUE: T2 weighted multiplanar sequences of the abdomen were acquired within a 1.5 Tesla magnet. 1 cc of Gadavist mixed with 50 cc of water were administered for oral contrast. Intravenous contrast was not administered due to renal insufficiency.  FINDINGS:   MRI OF THE ABDOMEN WITHOUT IV CONTRAST: Included views of the lung bases are clear. There is no pericardial or pleural effusion. The heart size is normal.  The hepatic parenchyma demonstrates normal signal intensity on T1 and T2 weighted sequences. No concerning hepatic mass is detected. There is no intra or extrahepatic bile duct dilation.  The gallbladder is distended, demonstrating a moderately thickened mildly irregular wall (series 4, image 23, 22). There is no pericholecystic fluid. Multiple stones reside within the gallbladder neck (series 4, image 22). The cystic duct is normal in caliber.  Multiple sub- 5 mm pancreatic cystic lesions are denoted by a high internal signal intensity on T2 weighted sequences (series 3, image 16, series 4, image 23). The main pancreatic duct is normal in caliber. The pancreas mildly atrophied, within normal limits for this patient''s age.  Arising from the upper and lower pole of the left kidney are well-circumscribed 7 mm and 4 mm cysts, respectively, denoted by a high internal signal intensity on T2 weighted sequences (series 3, image 28, series 4, image 25). The kidneys are otherwise normal.  The adrenal glands, spleen, stomach, and intra-abdominal loops of small and large bowel are normal. There is no mesenteric or retroperitoneal lymphadenopathy, and no ascites.  There are no bony lesions concerning for malignancy or infection.  NOTIFICATION: The initial findings were discussed by Dr. ___ with Dr. ___ telephone at the time of interpretation, 10:03 on ___.'
);


