INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '28951548',
    '12120702-RR-46',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: Single phase split bolus contrast: MDCT axial images were acquired through the abdomen and pelvis following intravenous contrast administration with split bolus technique. IV Contrast:  130 mL Omnipaque. Coronal and sagittal reformations were performed and reviewed on PACS. Oral contrast was administered.  DOSE: 847 mGy-cm.  D LP  FINDINGS: Status post Roux-en-Y gastric bypass.  There is interval decreased distention of the proximal stomach; however, it remains larger than expected for post bypass status.  There is oral contrast traversing through the gastrojejunal anastomosis, and into the small bowel.  Persistent fat stranding is appreciated surrounding the gastric jejunal anastomosis, with associated prominent regional reactive lymph nodes, maximally measuring up to 1.1 cm in short axis (02:28).  No oral contrast is seen entering the excluded stomach or biliary limb.  No obstruction appreciated in the current study.  The remainder of the alimentary tract is unchanged in appearance, including scattered colonic diverticulosis.  Normal appendix in the right lower quadrant.  No free air or free fluid.  Other findings within the abdomen are unchanged including mildly distended gallbladder with cholelithiasis, likely secondary to fasting state.  Atrophic right kidney, with mild hydronephrosis and hydroureter up to the anastomosis within the right anterior bladder.  Slightly delayed right nephrogram.  Multiple right anterior bladder diverticuli.  Right renal cyst.  Multiple small retroperitoneal and para-aortic lymph nodes, without pathologic enlargement.  Small left pleural effusion with associated subsegmental atelectasis, new from previous.  NOTIFICATION: Findings were discussed by Dr. ___ with Dr. ___ telephone at 08:45am.'
);


