ies 2, image 80). There is no free fluid in the pelvis.  LYMPH NODES: Multiple prominent lymph nodes adjacent to the gallbladder likely reactive and measure up to 0.9 cm (for example series 2, image 34 and 36).  VASCULAR: There is no abdominal aortic aneurysm.  Mild atherosclerotic disease is noted.  BONES: There is no evidence of worrisome osseous lesions or acute fracture.  SOFT TISSUES: The abdominal and pelvic wall is within normal limits.'
