e is no perinephric abnormality.  GASTROINTESTINAL: Small bowel loops demonstrate normal caliber, wall thickness and enhancement throughout. Colon and rectum are within normal limits.  Appendix contains air, has normal caliber without evidence of fat stranding.  Soft tissue density surrounding the ___ (series 4, image 122) has significantly improved compared to outside hospital CT from ___.  RETROPERITONEUM: Scattered prominent retroperitoneal lymph nodes are not enlarged by CT criteria.  PELVIS: The urinary bladder is distended.  The distal ureters are unremarkable.  There is no evidence of pelvic or inguinal lymphadenopathy.  There is no free fluid in the pelvis.  REPRODUCTIVE ORGANS: The prostate and seminal vesicles are unremarkable.  BONES: There is no evidence of worrisome osseous lesions or acute fracture.  SOFT TISSUES: The abdominal and pelvic wall is within normal limits.'
