    '10902160-RR-28',
    'MRCP',
    'Abdomen',
    'MRCP (MR ABD W&W/OC)',
    'EXAMINATION: MRCP:  TECHNIQUE: T1- and T2-weighted multiplanar images of the abdomen were acquired in a 1.5 T magnet. Intravenous contrast: 10 mL Gadavist. Oral contrast:  1 cc of Gadavist mixed with 50 cc of water was administered for oral contrast.  FINDINGS: Lower Thorax: Trace pleural effusions are noted bilaterally.  Heart is normal in size without pericardial effusion.  Liver: The liver enhances homogeneously without suspicious enhancing masses.  Biliary: No intrahepatic or extrahepatic biliary duct dilation.  The gallbladder demonstrates a fluid fluid level suggestive of biliary sludge.  There is no cholelithiasis or evidence of ____.  Pancreas: Peripancreatic stranding, predominantly around the body of the pancreas, is consistent with known pancreatitis.  There is no pancreatic duct dilatation.  No peripancreatic fluid collections are seen.  A 7 mm T2 hyperintensity in the neck of the pancreas (4:26) likely represents a side branch IPMN.  A smaller 5 mm T2 hyperintensity in the pancreatic tail (8:21) is also noted.  Spleen: The spleen is normal in size and signal intensity.  Adrenal Glands: The adrenal glands are normal in size in signal intensity.  Kidneys: A 10 mm lesion in the midpole in the left kidney (1202:86) demonstrates central enhancement.  The lesion is T1 isointense without evidence of bulk or intravoxel fat.  Bilateral renal cysts are noted.  Gastrointestinal Tract:  The stomach and intra-abdominal loops of small and large bowel are unremarkable without evidence of wall thickening or obstruction.  Lymph Nodes: No mesenteric or retroperitoneal lymphadenopathy.  Vasculature: The portal and hepatic veins are patent.  There is no abdominal aortic aneurysm.  Osseous and Soft Tissue Structures: The bones demonstrate normal signal intensity.  The abdominal wall is unremarkable.  NOTIFICATION: The findings were discussed with Drs.  ___ by ___, M.D. on the telephone on ___ at 9:20 AM, 15 minutes after discovery of the findings.'
);


