INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '21216421',
    '11438173-RR-48',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABDOMEN W/O CONTRAST',
    'EXAMINATION: CT abdomen without contrast.  TECHNIQUE: Multidetector CT images of the abdomen were acquired without intravenous contrast. Non-contrast scan has several limitations in detecting vascular and parenchymal organ abnormalities, including tumor detection. No oral contrast was administered. Coronal and sagittal reformations were performed and reviewed on PACS.  DOSE: Total DLP (Body) = 215 mGy-cm.  FINDINGS:   LOWER CHEST: Breathing artifact.  Bilateral septal thickening suggesting mild edema.  Bilateral subpleural reticular nodularity suggesting fibrotic changes. Calcified pleural plaques.  Sternotomy wires in situ.  Status post CABG.  ABDOMEN:   HEPATOBILIARY: Simple left hepatic cysts.  The largest measures 2.7 cm.  Sub cm hypodense foci in the right hepatic lobe, too small to characterize by noncontrast CT, likely biliary hamartoma or cysts. No ductal dilation.  Cholelithiasis with distended gallbladder.  Moderate gallbladder wall edema with adjacent fat stranding.  This appears to be evolved since the earlier today''s right upper quadrant ultrasound.  PANCREAS: Atrophic pancreas. No discrete lesion or ductal dilation.  SPLEEN: No splenomegaly.  ADRENALS: Unremarkable.  URINARY: No nephrolithiasis or hydronephrosis.No large mass.  No proximal hydroureter.  Left peripelvic cysts.  GASTROINTESTINAL: Focally dilated right upper quadrant small bowel loop measures 2.8 cm (03:33 ) without evidence of obstruction. Scattered colonic diverticula. No pneumoperitoneum.  LYMPH NODES: No adenopathy with noncontrast evaluation.  VASCULAR: Moderate arteriosclerosis.  3.9 cm fusiform abdominal aortic aneurysm.  Semi circular calcifications within the aneurysmal sac suggesting dissection/ intramural hematoma, likely chronic based on stable aneurysmal size.  No abdominal or retroperitoneal hematoma.  BONES AND SOFT TISSUES: Chronic moderate compression fracture of T12. No soft tissue mass.  NOTIFICATION: The findings were discussed by Dr. ___ with Dr. ___ on the ___ ___ at 6:46 ___, 30 minutes after discovery of the findings.'
);


