INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '21888122',
    '11487947-RR-16',
    'MRCP',
    'Abdomen',
    'MRCP (MR ABD W&W/OC)',
    'EXAMINATION: MRCP:  TECHNIQUE: T1- and T2-weighted multiplanar images of the abdomen were acquired in a 1.5 T magnet. Intravenous contrast: 8 mL Gadavist. Oral contrast:  1 cc of Gadavist mixed with 50 cc of water was administered for oral contrast.  FINDINGS: Lower Thorax: There trace pleural effusions bilaterally.  There is pericardial effusion.  Hepatobiliary: Liver is normal in signal intensity and morphology.  A simple cyst or biliary hamartoma is noted inferiorly within segment VI.  There is no suspicious liver lesion.  There is moderate intrahepatic and extrahepatic biliary ductal dilatation with the common bile duct measuring up to 11 mm in diameter (8:1).  The common bile duct tapers at the level of the ampulla.  There is are no filling defects to indicate choledocholithiasis (03:19).  There is mild narrowing of the right and left hepatic ducts at the confluence (07:23).  There is no abnormal enhancement of the bile duct walls.  There is no peribiliary enhancement or restricted diffusion in the liver.  The gallbladder is distended with mild wall edema, likely reactive.  There is no hyperemia of the adjacent hepatic parenchyma.  There are millimetric stones in the gallbladder lumen, though better appreciated on recent ultrasound.  Pancreas: The pancreas is normal in signal intensity and morphology without focal lesion or ductal dilatation.  There is mild stranding of the central mesentery just inferior to the pancreatic body, again suggesting acute interstitial edematous pancreatitis.  The pancreatic parenchyma enhances uniformly.  Spleen: Normal in size without focal lesion.  Adrenal Glands: Unremarkable.  Kidneys: A 1.6 cm T1 hyperintense, nonenhancing lesion in the posterior interpolar region of the left kidney is compatible with a proteinaceous or hemorrhagic cyst.  There are other subcentimeter hemorrhagic cysts in both kidneys.  There also a few tiny simple cortical cysts bilaterally.  There is no suspicious lesion or hydronephrosis.  Gastrointestinal Tract:  Visualized loops of large and small bowel are unremarkable.  Lymph Nodes: There is no lymphadenopathy.  Vasculature: Unremarkable.  Osseous and Soft Tissue Structures: No suspicious osseous lesion.'
);


