INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '24114990',
    '11532659-RR-88',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS W/O CONTRAST',
    'EXAMINATION: CT abdomen and pelvis  TECHNIQUE: Multidetector CT images of the abdomen and pelvis were acquired without intravenous contrast. Non-contrast scan has several limitations in detecting vascular and parenchymal organ abnormalities, including tumor detection. Oral contrast was not administered. Coronal and sagittal reformations were performed and reviewed on PACS.  DOSE: Acquisition sequence:    1) Spiral Acquisition 3.2 s, 51.2 cm; CTDIvol = 19.5 mGy (Body) DLP = 995.7 mGy-cm.  Total DLP (Body) = 996 mGy-cm.  FINDINGS:   LOWER CHEST: Partially visualized hazy, peribronchial nodular opacities in the right lower lobe is similar to prior study.  Nodular consolidation in the left lower lobe is new since prior study.  A 5 mm ground-glass nodule in the left lower lobe (2:6) is noted.  There is a trace left pleural effusion.  A prosthetic mitral valve is again noted.  There is no pericardial effusion.  ABDOMEN:   HEPATOBILIARY: The liver demonstrates homogeneous attenuation throughout. A hepatic artery embolization coil is noted.  A hypodensity measuring 1.4 cm in segment 7 of the liver, nonenhancing on prior contrast study, likely represents a cyst or biliary hamartoma.  There is increased perihepatic, perisplenic, and pelvic fluid of intermediate density compatible with hemorrhage. The fluid right lateral to the liver is of intermediate density, decreased in density compared to the prior study. The previously seen hematoma posterior inferior to the left lobe and medial to the gallbladder fossa measures approximately 6.5 x 5.8 in the gallbladder fossa, previously measuring 5.5 x 5.7cm.  Although the hematoma is increased in size, it contains mostly low density fluid with more hyperdense components consistent with increased clot.  No intrahepatic or extrahepatic biliary dilatation.  The gallbladder contains gallstones without wall thickening or surrounding inflammation.  An anterior approach percutaneous ____ tube is appropriately positioned and coiled within the fundus of the gallbladder.  Previously administered contrast remains within the gallbladder.  PANCREAS: The pancreas has normal attenuation throughout, without evidence of focal lesions within the limitations of an unenhanced scan.  There is no pancreatic ductal dilatation.  There is no peripancreatic stranding.  SPLEEN: The spleen shows normal size and attenuation throughout, without evidence of focal lesions.  ADRENALS: The right and left adrenal glands are normal in size and shape.  URINARY: The kidneys are of normal and symmetric size.  Multiple subcentimeter hypodensities are seen in bilateral kidneys, too small to characterize, likely simple cysts.    There is no hydronephrosis.  There is no nephrolithiasis.  There is no perinephric abnormality.  GASTROINTESTINAL: The stomach is unremarkable.  Small bowel loops demonstrate normal caliber and wall thickness throughout.  Diverticulosis of the colon is noted, without evidence of wall thickening and fat stranding.  The appendix is normal.  PELVIS: The urinary bladder is underdistended and contains a Foley catheter. The visualized reproductive organs are unremarkable.  LYMPH NODES: There is no retroperitoneal or mesenteric lymphadenopathy.  There is no pelvic or inguinal lymphadenopathy.  VASCULAR: There is no abdominal aortic aneurysm.  Mild atherosclerotic disease is noted.  Small pseudoaneurysm in the right femoral access site seen on ultrasound is not well evaluated on the current study.  Stranding anterior to the right femoral access site is likely postsurgical from recent catheterization without evidence of hematoma.  BONES: There is no evidence of worrisome osseous lesions or acute fracture. Minimal compression deformity of T10 is unchanged.  SOFT TISSUES: An umbilical hernia containing fat is noted.  NOTIFICATION: The findings were discussed with ___ the CCU resident, M.D. by ___, M.D. on the telephone on ___ at 12:15 pm, 10 minutes after discovery of the findings.'
);


