INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '29220175',
    '11620485-RR-62',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CTA ABD & PELVIS',
    'EXAMINATION: CTA ABD AND PELVIS:  TECHNIQUE: Abdomen and pelvis CTA: Non-contrast and post-contrast images were acquired through the abdomen and pelvis. Oral contrast was not administered. MIP reconstructions were performed on independent workstation and reviewed on  PACS.:   DOSE: Total DLP (Body) = 1,016 mGy-cm.  FINDINGS:   VASCULAR: There is no abdominal aortic aneurysm. There is minimal calcium burden in the abdominal aorta and great abdominal arteries.  No intramural hematoma or aortic dissection.  The celiac axis, SMA, ___ are patent.  Moderate atherosclerotic disease seen at the origin of the celiac axis and SMA without significant narrowing.  Bilateral renal arteries are patent.  Conventional hepatic anatomy.  LOWER CHEST: Minimal atelectasis is noted in the lung bases.  There is stable pleural based pulmonary nodule at the left lung base (03:34) with over ___ year stability.  There is no pleural or pericardial effusion.  Right atrial and right ventricular lead tips are noted.  There is a prosthetic aortic valve.  The heart is normal in size.  No pericardial effusion.  ABDOMEN:   HEPATOBILIARY: The liver demonstrates homogenous attenuation throughout. There is no evidence of focal lesions. There is no evidence of intrahepatic or extrahepatic biliary dilatation.  The gallbladder is mildly distended and contains stones and mild pericholecystic free fluid vs wall edema.  Main portal vein, SMV, splenic vein are patent.  PANCREAS: The pancreas has normal attenuation throughout, without evidence of focal lesions or pancreatic ductal dilatation. There is no peripancreatic stranding.  SPLEEN: The spleen shows normal size and attenuation throughout, without evidence of focal lesions.  ADRENALS: Left adrenal gland is unremarkable.  There is a 1.2 x 1.7 cm fatty lesion in the right adrenal gland compatible with a myelolipoma.  URINARY: Bilateral subcentimeter renal hypodensities are too small to characterize.  Largest hypodensity measures 5.6 x 4.8 cm in the left lower pole consistent with a simple cyst.  The kidneys otherwise are of normal and symmetric size with normal nephrogram. There is no evidence of stones or hydronephrosis.  There is no perinephric abnormality.  GASTROINTESTINAL: Small hiatal hernia noted the stomach is decompressed.  Small bowel loops demonstrate normal caliber, wall thickness and enhancement throughout.  Sigmoid diverticulosis seen without evidence of acute diverticulitis.  Colon and rectum are within normal limits.  Appendix is top-normal in size with small amount of fluid in the appendiceal tip which is unchanged in appearance since ___.  No adjacent fat stranding.  No mucosal hyper enhancement.  There is no evidence of mesenteric lymphadenopathy.  RETROPERITONEUM: Few scattered subcentimeter retroperitoneal lymph nodes do not meet CT size criteria for enlargement. Top-normal left common iliac artery nodes are noted.  No inguinal lymphadenopathy.  PELVIS: The urinary bladder and distal ureters are unremarkable.  There is no evidence of pelvic or inguinal lymphadenopathy.  There is no free fluid in the pelvis.  REPRODUCTIVE ORGANS: Uterus is not visualized.  Surgical clips project posterior to the vagina.  No adnexal abnormalities.  BONES: Degenerative changes are seen in the lumbar spine and bilateral femoral heads are unchanged in appearance.  Interval progression of L1 on L2 mild retrolisthesis with unchanged grade 1 anterolisthesis of L4 on L5.   No focal lytic or blastic lesions worrisome for malignancy.  SOFT TISSUES: The abdominal and pelvic wall is within normal limits besides a small fat containing umbilical hernia.'
);


