INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '20639685',
    '11833713-RR-11',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'LIVER OR GALLBLADDER US (SINGLE ORGAN)',
    'EXAMINATION: LIVER OR GALLBLADDER US (SINGLE ORGAN):  TECHNIQUE: Grey scale and color Doppler ultrasound images of the abdomen were obtained.  FINDINGS:   LIVER: The liver is diffusely echogenic.  The contour of the liver is smooth.  A simple appearing hepatic cyst is seen in the right hepatic lobe measuring 4.5 x 4 x 3.9 cm.  There is no focal liver mass. The main portal vein is patent with hepatopetal flow. There is no ascites.  BILE DUCTS: There is mild intrahepatic biliary dilation.  CBD: Two stones are seen in the proximal CBD, measuring 1.5 and 1 cm respectively, and the CBD itself appears dilated measuring up to 15 mm.  GALLBLADDER: The gallbladder is markedly abnormal.  The gallbladder wall is irregular, thickened and edematous and appears decompressed.  There is a focal defect in the anterior aspect of the wall which connects to a heterogeneous fluid collection medially along the undersurface of the liver.  This collection measures approximately 3.0 x 1.8 cm.  There is mild pericholecystic edema.  PANCREAS: The head and body of the pancreas are within normal limits. The tail of the pancreas is not visualized due to the presence of gas.  SPLEEN: Normal echogenicity.   Spleen length: 10.7 cm  KIDNEYS: Limited views of the kidneys show no hydronephrosis.   Right kidney: 11.1 cm  RETROPERITONEUM: The visualized portions of aorta and IVC are within normal limits.'
