INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '27377422',
    '11950373-RR-40',
    'MRCP',
    'Abdomen',
    'MRCP (MR ABD W&W/OC)',
    'EXAMINATION: MRCP:  TECHNIQUE: T1- and T2-weighted multiplanar images of the abdomen were acquired in a 1.5 T magnet. Intravenous contrast: 5 mL Gadavist. Oral contrast:  1 cc of Gadavist mixed with 50 cc of water was administered for oral contrast.  FINDINGS: Lower Thorax: Within the limitations of MRI, the lung bases are clear.  There are trace bilateral pleural effusions.  The base of the heart is normal in size.  There is no pericardial effusion.  Liver: The liver is normal in shape and contour.  There are no morphologic features of cirrhosis.  Evaluation for hepatic steatosis is limited on a 3T magnet.  The exam is also somewhat limited by motion.  Within the limitations, no focal liver lesion is identified.  The hepatic arterial anatomy is difficult to evaluate due to the motion artifact.  The portal and hepatic veins are patent.  Biliary:  In the distal common bile duct, there is a filling defect that measures 3 mm, and is compatible with a stone.  No other filling defects are identified.  The common bile duct measures 7 mm, which is at the upper limits of normal for a patient of this is age.  Mild dilation of the intrahepatic bile ducts noted.  There is no significant peribiliary enhancement to suggest cholangitis.  Heterogeneous enhancement of the liver on the arterial phase is nonspecific.  The gallbladder is distended.  The wall is intact.  There is moderate wall edema and pericholecystic fluid, as well as multiple gallstones in the neck of the gallbladder.  This is highly suggestive of ____.  In comparison the prior CT, the amount of edema around the gallbladder is slightly increased.  Pancreas: The pancreatic parenchyma is normal in signal and enhances homogeneously.  There is no duct dilation or mass.  Spleen: The spleen is normal in size, measuring 8.8 cm.  There are no focal lesions.  Adrenal Glands: The bilateral adrenal glands are normal.  Kidneys: The kidneys are normal in size.  Subcentimeter simple cysts are noted bilaterally.  There are no worrisome renal lesions, hydronephrosis, or perinephric abnormalities.  Mild bilateral symmetric perinephric edema is nonspecific.  Gastrointestinal Tract:  There is a tiny hiatal hernia.  The stomach and small bowel are otherwise normal in course and caliber.  There is no evidence of obstruction.  The imaged portions of the large bowel are normal.  There is trace perihepatic ascites.  Lymph Nodes: There is no periportal, retroperitoneal, or mesenteric lymphadenopathy.  Vasculature: The abdominal aorta is normal in caliber without evidence of an aneurysm.  There is moderate atherosclerotic plaque.  Osseous and Soft Tissue Structures: There are no concerning osseous lesions.  Moderate multilevel degenerative changes are noted throughout the spine.  The soft tissues are unremarkable.  NOTIFICATION: The findings were discussed with ___, M.D. by ___, M.D. on the telephone on ___ at 4 AM, 5 minutes after discovery of the findings.'
);


