VALUES (
    '24714062',
    '11984520-RR-8',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'EXAMINATION: CT of the abdomen and pelvis.  TECHNIQUE: Multidetector CT images of the abdomen and pelvis were obtained with oral and intravenous contrast.  Sagittal and coronal reformations were also performed.  DOSE: Acquisition sequence:    1) Spiral Acquisition 3.9 s, 51.2 cm; CTDIvol = 8.4 mGy (Body) DLP = 429.7 mGy-cm.    2) Stationary Acquisition 0.6 s, 0.5 cm; CTDIvol = 3.3 mGy (Body) DLP = 1.7 mGy-cm.    3) Stationary Acquisition 5.4 s, 0.5 cm; CTDIvol = 30.1 mGy (Body) DLP = 15.0 mGy-cm.  Total DLP (Body) = 446 mGy-cm.  FINDINGS: Small nodule in the left lower lobe measures up to 3 mm in diameter (2:4).  Small calcified granuloma present at the right lung base.  A small hypoattenuating lesion in the sixth segment of the liver measuring up to 15 mm corresponds to an echogenic focus on the recent ultrasound confirming the very high likelihood of a benign hemangioma.  No additional focal liver lesions are identified.  There is no intrahepatic biliary dilatation.  The common hepatic duct is again dilated up to 12 mm in diameter.  Mild dilatation extends to the ampulla.  The gall bladder is mildly distended, and shows mild irregular wall thickening which is not specific but these are findings which can be seen with ____.  The lumen is filled with stones.  No surrounding fat stranding is present.  A pancreatic ductal stent is in place.  Pancreatic duct is not dilated.  There is no inflammatory change about the pancreas.  The spleen is normal in size and appearance.  Adrenals appear normal.  There is no evidence for stones, solid masses, or hydro nephrosis involving either kidney.  Stomach and small bowel appear normal.  Large bowel is also unremarkable.  Uterus adnexa and bladder appear normal.  Trace free fluid is nonspecific but likely physiological.  There is no lymphadenopathy.  Major vascular structures appear widely patent.  There are no suspicious bone lesions.  Moderate degenerative changes affect lower lumbar facet joints.  L5-S1 interspace is mildly narrowed with small osteophytes.'
);


