INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '27850323',
    '10040056-AR-11',
    'MRCP',
    'Abdomen',
    'MRCP (MR ABD W&W/OC)',
    'FINDINGS: Included views of the lung bases demonstrates a trace left pleural effusion with bilateral mild atelectasis (series 4, image 3). The heart size is normal, and there is no pericardial effusion.  The hepatic parenchyma demonstrates marked signal drop-off on T1 weighted out of phase images in comparison to in phase sequences, denoting steatosis (series 7, image 28, 29). No concerning hepatic mass is detected. There is no intra or extrahepatic bile duct dilation.  There is mild prominence of the intrahepatic bile ducts, and the CBD measures up to 9 mm (series 3, image 19), however, the CBD tapers smoothly to the level of the ampulla without obstructing mass or stone.  The gallbladder is filled with sludge, without wall thickening, hyperenhancement, or pericholecystic fluid.  There is expansion of the pancreatic tail, which is mixed with nonenhancing phlegmon and fluid, demonstrating slightly decreased signal intensity relative to the normal parenchyma within the head and body on T1 weighted precontrast images (series 11, image 84), with heterogeneous mixed signal intensity on T2 weighted sequences (series 4, image 25), compatible with ____ with necrosis and underlying hemorrhage. No organized collection is detected. Mild ascites and edema extend throughout the bilateral anterior para renal space is (series 4, image 39, 34).  The spleen, adrenal glands, kidneys, stomach, and intra-abdominal loops of small and large bowel are normal. There is no mesenteric or retroperitoneal lymphadenopathy, and no ascites.  A replaced left hepatic artery arises from the left gastric (series 1301, image 56). The portal and hepatic veins are patent. The abdominal aorta, celiac trunk, SMA, and renal arteries are patent and normal in caliber. An accessory right renal artery is present (series 1301, image 118, 114). A circumaortic left renal vein is incidentally noted (series 1302 image 112, 142). No definite pseudoaneurysm is detected. A 6 mm focus of hyperenhancement anterior and inferior to the area of necrosis likely represents a confluence of adjacent vessels (series 1302, image 93).  There are no osseous lesions concerning for malignancy or infection.'
);


