    'EXAMINATION: LIVER OR GALLBLADDER US (SINGLE ORGAN):  TECHNIQUE: Grey scale and color Doppler ultrasound images of the abdomen were obtained.  FINDINGS:   LIVER: The hepatic parenchyma appears within normal limits. The contour of the liver is smooth. There there are hyperechoic lesions throughout the liver, one in segment 2 measuring 2.5 x 3.5 x 3.9 cm with central hypoechogenicity, unchanged from prior and characterized as a hemangioma by CT.  A hyperechoic lesion in segment 4 A measures 2.4 x 3.1 x 1.9 cm, it was not previously seen on the ultrasound but appears stable from the CT.  A third hyperechoic lesion in segment 8 measuring 1.6 x 1.7 x 1.6 cm is unchanged from the prior ultrasound and likely represents a hemangioma.  The main portal vein is patent with hepatopetal flow. There is no ascites.  BILE DUCTS: There is no intrahepatic biliary dilation. The CBD measures 10 mm, unchanged from prior with some sludge seen within it.  GALLBLADDER: Cholelithiasis without gallbladder wall thickening.  Sonographic ___ sign was negative  PANCREAS: The pancreas is enlarged and edematous appearing compatible with ____.  Small right pleura effusion.'
);


