);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '20738420',
    '10149959-RR-21',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABDOMEN W/CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: This is an outside hospital study acquired at ___.  The study date is ___ and study time 3:00 a.m.  The study is of diagnostic quality.  CT OF THE ABDOMEN WITH INTRAVENOUS CONTRAST: Minimal atelectasis is noted in the imaged lung lung base.  Imaged portion of the base of the heart is unremarkable.     The gallbladder is mildly distended with many stones.  The fundus is mildly thickened, but otherwise there is no evidence of wall thickening or of surrounding inflammatory change to generate a high suspicion for cholecystitis.  There is minimal intrahepatic biliary ductal dilation. There is a tiny high-attenuation focus in the distal CBD, best appreciated on the coronal sequences (___), and this measures 3.6 mm and is suspicious for choledocholithiasis.  The CBD is dilated measuring up to 1 cm.    There is marked peripancreatic fat stranding with mild pancreatic edema particularly in the region of the pancreatic head and body, consistent with ____.  The pancreatic duct is mildly prominent, measuring up to 2 mm on CT.  Overall, these findings are compatible with gallstone ____.  There are some focal cortical defects in the kidneys suggestive of remote scarring.  There are also multiple subcentimeter low-attenuation lesions among the kidneys, too small to characterize.  The left kidney demonstrates a cyst in the interpolar region measuring 1.9 x 2.7 cm with internal attenuation of 5.5, compatible with a simple cyst.  Bilateral adrenals are normal.  Bowel loops are unremarkable.  Trace free fluid is noted.  There is no mesenteric or retroperitoneal adenopathy.  There is no intraperitoneal free air.  CT OF THE PELVIS WITH INTRAVENOUS CONTRAST: Diverticulosis is noted without diverticulitis.  Large calcified fibroid is noted in the lower uterine segment.  Otherwise, the uterus and the adnexa are unremarkable.  Urinary bladder is within normal limits.  Evaluation of deep pelvis is limited due to significant streak artifact from hip hardware.  There are subcentimeter right inguinal nodes.  OSSEOUS STRUCTURES: Bilateral hip prosthesis is noted.  Minimal heterotopic ossification is noted around the bilateral hip joints.  Sclerotic focus in the right iliac crest appears benign and could be a bone island.  Extensive degenerative changes are noted in the lumbar spine with innumerable patchy sclerosis and lucency, patchy demineralization in the absence of malignancy.  These are not typical for diffuse metastases; however, if further concern, then an MRI may be considered.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
