INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '28540066',
    '10306702-RR-25',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABDOMEN W/CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: Multidetector helical scanning of the abdomen and pelvis was performed following the administration of oral and 30 cc of IV Optiray contrast.  Coronal and sagittal reformats were displayed.  CT OF THE ABDOMEN: There are tiny bilateral pleural effusions and new patchy opacities at the lung bases, which may represent pneumonia or aspiration.  Anteriorly and in a subpleural location within the lingula and right middle lobe are more fibrotic changes that are unchanged from the prior exam.  There are also calcified pleural plaques suggesting prior asbestos exposure.  Evaluation of the upper abdomen is limited due to motion.  The liver, spleen, and adrenal glands are normal.  There are gallstones within the neck of a nondistended gallbladder.    There is extensive inflammatory change associated with the pancreas.  The pancreas itself enhances homogeneously.  In fact the pancreas is overall intact with normal morphology.  There is less fluid and stranding within the pericolic gutters, however more extensive inflammatory change in mesenteric root and lesser sac.    A peripancreatic fluid collection inferior to the body of the pancreas is becoming more discrete and measures 4 x 2.6 cm.  Thickening of the splenic flexure and descending colon as well as the duodenum are likely reactive.  The SMA, SMV and splenic vein are grossly patent.  No pseudoaneurysms are identified.    The kidneys enhance and excrete contrast symmetrically, with a tiny 6-mm hypodensity noted in the lower pole of the right kidney which is too small to further characterize but likely a cyst.  No free air.  Mild-to-moderate atherosclerotic disease is seen within the aorta.  CT OF THE PELVIS: Foley catheter and air are seen within the bladder.  The prostate is enlarged measuring 6.4 x 4.9 cm in the axial plane.  There is a moderate amount of free fluid extending into the pelvis.  The sigmoid colon is decompressed, however unremarkable.  There is a fat-containing right inguinal hernia.  No pelvic lymphadenopathy.  The bones are osteopenic and there are multilevel degenerative changes, worse in the lower lumbar spine.  There are also mild compression deformities of the superior endplates at L1 and L2, unchanged from ___ and age indeterminate.  No retropulsed bony fragments within the spinal canal.'
);


