INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '28540066',
    '10306702-RR-38',
    'CT',
    'Chest',
    'CT CHEST W/CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT-acquired axial images were obtained through the chest, abdomen, and pelvis with intravenous and oral contrast.  Coronal and sagittal reformations were evaluated.  CT OF THE CHEST WITH INTRAVENOUS CONTRAST: Moderate atherosclerotic calcification is noted involving the aortic arch, with the heart and great vessels appearing otherwise unremarkable and no pathologically enlarged supraclavicular, or axillary nodes identified.  Scattered mediastinal nodes are present up to 12 mm in the lower right paratracheal chain.  Trace bilateral pleural effusions remain, and there is fairly extensive bilateral noncalcified and calcified pleural plaques in the setting of peripheral interstitial lung fibrosis as depicted by increased peripheral reticular markings extending to the pleural surface and mild subpleural honeycombing predominantly involving the right and left lower lobes with milder involvement of the lingula and right middle lobe.  Superimposed patchy parenchymal opacities within the lower lobes are again noted clearly progressed from the ___ outside CT examination and slightly progressed from the more recent ___ exam.  Mild right and left lower lobe atelectasis is also noted.  CT OF THE ABDOMEN WITH INTRAVENOUS AND ORAL CONTRAST: Moderate inflammatory changes surrounding the pancreas are again noted with the parenchyma displaying predominantly homogeneous enhancement with the exception of partial heterogeneous enhancement noted within the pancreatic body-tail junction (2:55).  The splenic artery and vein remain patent and no arterial pseudoaneurysms are identified with the splenic artery again noted to be markedly ectatic and tortuous.  The overall size of peripancreatic fluid collections is slightly diminished from the most recent exam with no well-defined rim-enhancing organized collection identified.  The largest fluid collection is again noted to extend from the tail of the pancreas towards the spleen, currently 21 x 32 mm (301B:59).  Reactive edema around the greater curvature and mesenteric root is also slightly improved with persistent scattered mesenteric and peripancreatic nodes identified.  No free air is identified with the remaining intra-abdominal organs including the kidneys and adrenal glands as well as the atherosclerotic disease of the intra-abdominal aorta appearing unchanged.  A feeding tube is noted to be terminating distal to the ligament of Treitz.  Oral contrast is present within the gallbladder likely related to prior ERCP, no clear fistula noted.  CT OF THE PELVIS WITH INTRAVENOUS AND ORAL CONTRAST: Amount of intrapelvic free fluid has diminished from the most recent examination and does not appear organized.  Air is noted within the urinary bladder likely related to recent Foley placement.  The prostate is also again noted to be enlarged.  Contrast has progressed into the rectum with the large bowel displaying some mild continued reactive edema about the splenic flexure and distal transverse colon, but otherwise unremarkable.  BONE WINDOWS: Multilevel degenerative changes are again seen with no aggressive-appearing osseous lesions identified.  Streak artifact from prior right shoulder arthroplasty is noted.'
);


