    'ABDOMEN U.S. (COMPLETE STUDY)',
    'STUDY: Abdominal ultrasound.  FINDINGS: The liver demonstrates a normal echotexture without focal lesion or intrahepatic biliary dilatation.  The portal vein is patent with hepatopetal flow.  The gallbladder is distended, but shows no stones, wall edema or pericholecystic fluid.  The common bile duct is 2 mm in caliber.  Pancreatic head and body appear normal and the tail is mildly obscured by overlying bowel gas.  The IVC appears unremarkable.  The spleen measures 7.4 cm in its long axis.  It is normal appearing.'
