INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '23248166',
    '10441330-RR-24',
    'MRCP',
    'Abdomen',
    'MRCP (MR ABD W&W/OC)',
    'MRCP:   TECHNIQUE: Multiplanar T1- and T2-weighted imaging were acquired on a 1.5 Tesla magnet including dynamic 3D imaging obtained prior to, during and after the uneventful intravenous administration of 15 mL of Magnevist.  In addition, 300 cc of Gastromark and 450 cc of Readi-Cat were administered orally.  FINDINGS: The imaged lung bases are clear.  Normal hepatic parenchymal signal intensity without focal liver lesion.  No intra- or extra-hepatic biliary dilatation.  The portal vein is patent.  No gallstones are evident within the gallbladder.  No evidence for choledocholithiasis.   Spleen and adrenal glands are unremarkable.  Note is made of pancreas divisum. There is slight irregularity of the duct noted within the tail of the pancreas (series 10A, image 4), likely sequelae from prior episode of ____; however, no pancreatic ductal dilatation.  Normal homogeneous signal intensity to the pancreas which enhances normally.  No pancreatic cystic lesion or mass is identified.  No peripancreatic fluid.  No evidence for ____ on today''s study.    There are no retroperitoneal masses or adenopathy.  No abnormally dilated small or large bowel loop in the visualized upper abdomen.  No free fluid.    Bone marrow signal is unremarkable and there are no osseous lesions.    Incidental note is made of an accessory renal artery on the right side.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '22712915',
    '10473631-RR-16',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABDOMEN W/CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: Multiple axial images of the abdomen and pelvis from lung bases through the pubic symphysis were obtained following the uneventful administration of oral and 130 cc Optiray IV contrast.  FINDINGS:   CT ABDOMEN: There is minor bibasilar atelectasis.  No pleural or pericardial effusion.  The liver, spleen and adrenal glands are normal in appearance.  There is a 7-mm low attenuation lesion in the upper pole of the right kidney which is too small to characterize, likely representing a small cyst.  There is no hydronephrosis.  The gallbladder is fluid filled.    There is ill defined fluid in the retroperitoneum centered about the pancreas. There is non-enhancement in the region of the distal body and tail of pancreas, less than 30% of the total gland worrisome for early necrosis. There are no well defined fluid collections. There is fluid tracking in the paracolic gutters and a small amount of hemorrhagic fluid layering in the pelvis.  The extent of ill-defined fluid has progressed, and non-enhancement of a portion of the distal pancreas is new.  The wall of the descending duodenum is also newly thickened.  There is sigmoid diverticulosis without evidence of diverticulitis.  Bowel loops are normal caliber without evidence of obstruction.  There is no retroperitoneal or abdominal adenopathy.  CT PELVIS: The bladder is decompressed with a Foley in place.  There is contrast opacifying the bladder.  There is no pelvic lymphadenopathy.  There are no lytic or sclerotic bone lesions.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '22712915',
    '10473631-RR-17',
    'MRCP',
    'Abdomen',
    'MRCP (MR ABD W&W/OC)',
    'PROTOCOL: MRCP.  TECHNIQUE: Multiplanar T1- and T2-weighted images were acquired on a 1.5 T magnet including dynamic 3D imaging obtained prior to, during, and after the uneventful intravenous administration of 0.1 mmol/kg of gadolinium-DTPA.  Multiplanar 2D and 3D reformats and subtraction images were generated on an independent workstation.  FINDINGS: The body and tail of the pancreas appear swollen with high-signal intensity within the pancreatic parenchyma on T2-weighted in keeping with ____.  An ill-defined fluid collection is noted anterior to the junction of the body and tail of the pancreas.  Free fluid and stranding is present within the peripancreatic fat and in the anterior pararenal space however no collection is present.  No significant duct dilatation is identified.  There is a focal area of nonenhancing pancreas at the junction of the body and tail of the pancreas measuring 4.7 cm.  This accounts for approximately 30% of total pancreatic parenchyma.  The adjacent mesenteric vessels enhance normally.  The portal vein, splenic vein, and SMV are patent.  No gallstones are present within the gallbladder.  The common duct is nondilated, measuring 4 mm maximally.  No intrahepatic bile duct dilatation.  The spleen, adrenal glands, and liver are normal.  Stranding is present in the mesenteric fat in keeping with ____.  Simple cortical and parapelvic cysts are identified in both kidneys.  Mildly dilated loops of jejunum are noted in keeping with an ileus.  There are small bilateral pleural effusions and a small amount of free fluid is present within the pelvis.  Marrow signal is unremarkable.  Degenerative changes are present within the spine.    Multiplanar 2D and 3D reformats provided multiple perspectives for the dynamic series 156.'
);


