INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '28031214',
    '10544163-RR-31',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABDOMEN W/CONTRAST',
    'CT SCAN OF THE ABDOMEN AND PELVIS PERFORMED ON ___.: Comparisons are made with prior chest radiographs dating back to ___.  TECHNIQUE: MDCT through the abdomen and pelvis was performed following IV contrast administration with coronal and sagittal reformations provided.  FINDINGS:   LUNG BASES: There is chronic-appearing elevation of the left hemidiaphragm and the heart is displaced into the right lower chest.  Bilateral lower lobe consolidations appear chronic.  There are also two loculated fluid colelctions tracking along the right oblique fissure measuring up to 3.5 x 3.2 cm. There is a hiatal hernia also noted.  Pacer leads extend into the right heart.  Aortic and mitral valvular calcifications are noted as are mild coronary artery calcifications.  No pleural effusions are seen.  Areas of calcification along the right basilar pleural surface are also noted.  ABDOMEN: The liver appears grossly unremarkable without focal lesions identified.  The spleen is normal.  Gallbladder contains hyperdense material posteriorly within the lumen likely representing small stones or sludge, though there are no additional findings to suggest acute cholecystitis.  The adrenal glands appear grossly unremarkable.  There is mild stranding adjacent to the pancreatic head which may be compatible with ____.  Correlate clinically.  There is no pancreatic ductal dilatation or evidence of biliary ductal dilation.  Kidneys enhance symmetrically and excrete contrast promptly.  The abdominal aorta is slightly tortuous but normal in caliber with scattered atherosclerotic calcifications noted.  Circumaortic left renal vein is incidentally noted.  There is no retroperitoneal lymphadenopathy.  The stomach appears grossly unremarkable.  PELVIS: Loops of small bowel demonstrate no evidence of ileus or obstruction. Colonic diverticulosis is noted with moderate fecal loading of the ascending colon.  Diverticulosis is noted without evidence of diverticulitis.  Urinary bladder is collapsed around a Foley catheter.  The prostate gland is mildly enlarged measuring approximately 6 cm in transverse dimension.  No pelvic free fluid is seen.  BONES: Bones are osteopenic.  Rib cage deformity is noted on the right side, likely chronic.  Degenerative disease is noted in the lumbar spine.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '28031214',
    '10544163-RR-32',
    'CT',
    'Chest',
    'CHEST (PA & LAT)',
    'CHEST RADIOGRAPH PERFORMED ON ___.: Comparison made with prior study from ___.  FINDINGS: AP upright and lateral views of the chest are obtained.  A pacer device projects over the left chest wall, with lead tips in the expected location of the right atrium and right ventricle, unchanged.  There is stable elevation of the left hemidiaphragm.  There is patient rotation and shift of the heart into the right chest, which likely results from the elevated left hemidiaphragm.  Comparison with multiple prior studies dating back to ___ demonstrates no change in this finding.  There is mild improvement in aeration at the right lower lung, though there is mild persistent opacity which may reflect chronic scarring or possibly small effusion.  There is marked widening of the AP diameter of the chest, which likely reflect the significant thoracic kyphosis in this patient with significant osteopenia.  There is no pneumothorax.  The aorta is unfolded and appears similar in contour to prior exam.'
);


