INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '29265811',
    '10653798-RR-20',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT-acquired 5 mm axial images of the abdomen and pelvis were obtained following the uneventful administration of intravenous contrast.  Coronal and sagittal reformations were performed at 5 mm slice thickness.  CT OF THE ABDOMEN WITH IV CONTRAST: Included views of the lung bases are clear.  There is no pericardial or pleural effusion.  The heart size is normal. There is mild gynecomastia.   Tiny subcentimeter hypodensities within the liver (2:38, 29) are statistically likely biliary hamartomas, but remain too small for further characterization.  There is no intra- or extra-hepatic bile duct dilation.  Minimal stranding about the pancreas is present (2:24). The gallbladder, spleen, adrenal glands, kidneys, stomach, and intra-abdominal loops of small and large bowel are normal.  There is no mesenteric or retroperitoneal lymphadenopathy, and no free air or free fluid.  CT OF THE PELVIS WITH IV CONTRAST: The rectum, sigmoid colon, urinary bladder, and prostate are normal.  The appendix is normal (2:57).  There is mild colonic diverticulosis, with no evidence of diverticulitis.  VASCULATURE: The abdominal aorta, celiac trunk, SMA, and ___ are patent and normal in caliber.  There is minimal atherosclerotic calcification of the infrarenal abdominal aorta and iliac branches.  OSSEOUS STRUCTURES: There is no acute fracture.  There are no bony lesions concerning for malignancy or infection. Mild multilevel degenerative changes are seen throughout the lumbar spine, including mild disc space narrowing, calcification of anterior longitudinal ligament across the lower thoracic spine (602B:40), and a large L1/2 right paramedial osteophyte (2:30).'
);


