    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT images were acquired from the lung bases through the pubic symphysis following administration of intravenous contrast, with multiplanar reformations.  CT ABDOMEN: With the exception of bilateral dependent atelectasis, the lung bases are clear.  There is no pleural effusion.  The heart is normal in size without pericardial effusion.  Trace pneumobilia is noted anteriorly along the liver, likely sequela of recent transhepatic cholecystostomy drainage.  The gallbladder demonstrates persistent wall thickening and hyperemia, but significantly decompressed since ___.  The gallbladder now contains hyperdense material.  There is no intrahepatic biliary dilatation.  The common duct is somewhat prominent, measuring 5 mm.  The spleen, a small splenule, and adrenal glands are unremarkable.  The nephrograms are symmetric without hydronephrosis or hydroureter.  The stomach, small and large bowel loops are normal in caliber.  Note is made of a few small foci of extraluminal air along the superior aspect of the greater gastric curvature (for example, 2, 23 and 2, 21), felt to be intravenous in distribution and trace in volume, etiology and clinical significance unclear.  There is marked inflammatory stranding centered around the pancreas and fluid associated with this inflammatory process, with thickening of bilateral Gerota''s fascia, consistent with ____.  Small amount of simple fluid also layers along the dependent portion of the right paracolic gutter.  Allowing for such, the pancreatic parenchyma enhances normally, without evidence of necrosis.  There is no pseudocyst.  Arterial and venous structures are patent.  No pseudoaneurysm or thrombosis is apparent.  There is significant inflammatory stranding and fluid around the duodenum, involving the second and third, possibly fourth segments, likely reactive.  There is no mesenteric or retroperitoneal adenopathy.  CT PELVIS: The bladder, distal ureters, prostate, and rectum appear within normal limits.  There is no inguinal or pelvic side wall adenopathy.  No free fluid in the pelvis.  BONE WINDOW: No focal concerning lesion.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '21849575',
    '10717708-RR-49',
    'MRI',
    'Abdomen',
    'MRI ABDOMEN W/O & W/CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: Multiplanar T1- and T2-weighted images were acquired on a 1.5 Tesla magnet including dynamic 3D imaging obtained prior to, during, and after the uneventful intravenous administration of 0.1 mmol/kg (19 mL) of gadolinium-DTPA.  FINDINGS: There are small bilateral pleural effusions with associated compressive atelectasis.  There is trace of ascites also seen.  Moderate loss of signal from the liver on out-of-phase compared to in-phase T1-weighted images is consistent with hepatic steatosis.  No concerning focal liver lesions are seen.  The portal vein and hepatic veins are patent.  There is a replaced right hepatic artery arising from the celiac trunk.  No intrahepatic duct dilatation. The gallbladder is not distended but is thick walled consistent with chronic inflammation.  This may be due to chronic cholecystitis or the sequelae of the recent cholecystostomy.  There is some T1 hyperintense material within the gallbladder lumen, compatible with hyperconcentrated bile. The pancreas is normal in contour and minimally increased in signal intensity on T2-weighted images consistent with the patient''s known ____.  There is induration of the peripancreatic fat with T1 hyperintense material in the small bowel mesentery extending laterally anterior to the left perirenal fascia (10:84) consistent with hemorrhagic or proteinaceous fluid.  No pseudocyst is seen at this time.  No pseudoaneurysm formation or venous thrombosis secondary to this inflammatory process.  There are small retroperitoneal lymph nodes along the left paraaortic region which do not meet the size criteria for pathologic enlargement (1202:122).  The spleen is not enlarged.  Both adrenal glands and both kidneys are unremarkable in appearance.  There is mild edema of the duodenal and jejunal walls consistent wtih secondary involvement.  The visualized osseous structures are unremarkable.'
);


