INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '21849575',
    '10717708-RR-53',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'STUDY: CT of the abdomen and pelvis with IV and oral contrast.  TECHNIQUE: MDCT images of the abdomen and pelvis was obtained from the level of the lung bases to the level of the proximal femur after the administration of IV and oral contrast.  Multiplanar reconstructions were performed and reviewed.  FINDINGS:   LUNG BASES: Small bilateral pleural effusions are seen, with adjacent atelectasis in the lower lobes bilaterally.  ABDOMEN AND PELVIS: The liver appears within normal limits.  There is no intra- or extra-hepatic biliary ductal dilatation.  The spleen appears normal. There is a cylindrical-shaped density in the anterior abdominal wall at the subcostal level on the right at the site of surgery, which measures approximately 42-45 ___ units and may represent a postoperative hematoma.  Also seen is high-density in the region of the gallbladder bed, likely representing a postoperative hematoma.  No fluid collections are seen in this region. Cutaneous surgical staples are seen in the right upper quadrant of the abdomen.  Again noted is marked inflammatory stranding centered around the pancreas in the anterior pararenal space, consistent with the previously documented ____.  The degree of inflammatory changes appears to have increased since previous study.  There is no evidence of pancreatic necrosis or hemorrhage.  There is no evidence of a pseudoaneurysm/ thrombosis.  The kidneys appear normal.  Nonspecific perinephric fat stranding is seen.  The stomach, duodenum and small bowel appear within normal limits.  The colon appears normal.  There is no evidence of retroperitoneal or mesenteric lymphadenopathy.  There is again noted inflammatory changes in the subcutaneous soft tissues of the anterior abdominal wall.  Bones are intact.'
);


