INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '21508628',
    '10778867-RR-85',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS W/O CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: Axial MDCT images were obtained through the abdomen and pelvis without intravenous contrast material and with oral contrast material.  Reformatted coronal and sagittal images were obtained.  DOSE: DLP:  365 mGy-cm. CTDIvol:  7 mGy.  FINDINGS:   THORAX: The visualized lung bases are clear with no pleural effusions, pneumothorax or focal opacities. The visualized heart and pericardium are normal.  Evaluation is limited without the use of intravenous contrast material.  LIVER: Diffuse hypoattenuation of the liver is compatible with steatosis. There are no focal hepatic lesions.  There is no intra or extrahepatic biliary duct dilatation.  GALLBLADDER: The gallbladder is unremarkable and contains no radiopaque gallstones.  SPLEEN: The spleen is normal in size and shape.  PANCREAS: Mild ___ stranding is seen about the head of the pancreas which is slightly ill-defined without focal fluid collection or main pancreatic duct dilatation.  ADRENALS: The adrenal glands are normal in size and shape.  KIDNEYS: The patient is status-post left nephrectomy.  The right kidney is normal in size and shape.    There is no hydronephrosis or perinephric stranding.  BOWEL: The stomach is mildly distended and unremarkable. The small bowel opacifies with oral contrast without obstruction or focal wall thickening.  The appendix is not visualized, but there are no secondary findings to suggest appendicitis. The large bowel contains feces without wall thickening or evidence of obstruction. There is no intraperitoneal free air or free fluid. The small bowel is not well distended with oral contrast material, but there is no evidence of acute bowel inflammation to suggest active Crohn disease.  LYMPH NODES: There is a 2.2 x 2.0 mesenteric nodal mass anterior to the duodenum is grossly unchanged from prior exam (2:41).  PELVIS: The bladder is relatively well distended without focal wall thickening. There is no pelvic free fluid. There are no pathologically enlarged pelvic sidewall or inguinal lymph nodes by CT size criteria. The rectum is unremarkable.  Small amount of fluid is seen within the right inguinal canal.  VESSELS & SOFT TISSUE:  There is no aneurysmal dilatation of the abdominal aorta.  There are no hernias.  BONES: The patient is status post left femoral fixation.  L3 and L5 sclerotic foci are compatible with bone islands (2:39).'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '27792983',
    '10786656-RR-20',
    'CT',
    'Chest',
    'CTA CHEST W&W/O C&RECONS, NON-CORONARY',
    'CT TORSO WITH INTRAVENOUS CONTRAST:   TECHNIQUE: MDCT axial images of the torso were obtained prior to and following administration of intravenous contrast per CTA torso and CT abdomen and pelvis protocol.  Coronal and sagittal reformatted images were obtained.  CTA CHEST: No filling defects in the pulmonary arteries to suggest presence of pulmonary embolism.  There is a small left pleural effusion.  There is trace pericardial fluid.  There is a dual-chamber pacemaker in place.  The aorta demonstrates a small amount of calcified and noncalcified plaque.  There is no evidence of aortic dissection.  The airways are patent to the segmental levels bilaterally.  There is no parenchymal consolidation.  There is no mediastinal, hilar, or axillary lymphadenopathy.  CT ABDOMEN WITH INTRAVENOUS CONTRAST: There are inflammatory stranding and organizing fluid surrounding the pancreas, consistent with subacute ____.  The pancreatic parenchyma enhances homogeneously, there is no evidence of necrosis.  The gallbladder wall is mildly thickened, there is no intra- or extra-hepatic biliary ductal dilatation.  The liver, spleen, adrenal glands are unremarkable.  Kidneys enhance equally and excrete contrast normally.  There is no free air in the abdomen.  Abdominal loops of large and small bowel are unremarkable.  Normal appendix is seen.  CT PELVIS WITH INTRAVENOUS CONTRAST: There is no evidence of urolithiasis. Urinary bladder, distal ureters, uterus, adnexa bilaterally, rectum, sigmoid colon are unremarkable.  There is no free pelvic fluid, and no pathologically enlarged pelvic or inguinal lymph nodes.  BONE WINDOWS: Demonstrate no concerning lytic or sclerotic lesions.'
);


