INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '25154998',
    '10835235-RR-36',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'CT ABDOMEN AND PELVIS WITH CONTRAST: ___:  TECHNIQUE: Contiguous axial images were obtained through the abdomen and pelvis after the administration of intravenous contrast.  Coronal and sagittal reformats were reviewed.  FINDINGS: Lung bases are clear.    The liver, spleen, kidneys, adrenal glands are unremarkable.  Patient is status post cholecystectomy.  The common bile duct measures up to 10 mm in diameter compatible with prior cholecystectomy.  There is slight enlargement of the pancreatic tail with loss of the normal interdigitating fat and surrounding inflammatory changes compatible with ____.  There is no focal collection.    There is a small hiatal hernia.  The stomach is decompressed and otherwise unremarkable.  Small bowel is normal in caliber.  Scattered diverticula was seen throughout the colon without evidence of active diverticulitis.  The appendix appears normal.  Uterus is notable for multiple subserosal fibroids, one seen adjacent to the left adnexa measuring up to 2.5 cm in diameter.  There is also focal low-attenuation in the region of the endometrial canal suggestive which may distort the endometrial canal.  It may also represent a large polyp or submucosal fibroid.  Fluid is seen within the upper vagina.  The adnexa are unremarkable.  No free fluid identified.  There is no intra-abdominal adenopathy.  Note is made of a left-sided IVC which drains into the left renal vein.  No suspicious osseous lesions detected.'
);


