    'MRCP:   TECHNIQUE: Multiplanar T1- and T2-weighted images were acquired on 1.5 Tesla magnet including dynamic 3D imaging obtained prior to, during, and after the uneventful intravenous administration of 0.1 mmol/kg (15 cc) of gadolinium-DTPA. Non-breathhold technique was performed as the patient was unable to follow breathhold instructions.  FINDINGS: The liver demonstrates normal signal intensity throughout without focal lesions.  There is no evidence of intrahepatic or extrahepatic biliary dilatation.  The CBD in its extrahepatic portion measures 7 mm.  There is no definite filling defects in the biliary tree.  The gallbladder contains small stones.  There is no evidence of gallbladder wall edema and mucosal or pericholecystic enhancement on the current study.   The pancreas demonstrates normal signal intensity throughout without evidence of focal lesions or pancreatic duct dilatation.  The spleen is of normal size and signal intensity throughout.  The adrenals are unremarkable bilaterally.  There is no evidence of retroperitoneal or mesenteric lymphadenopathy.  The kidneys are within normal limits.  Minimal amount of free fluid is seen in the right gutter (series 10, image 19).'
