    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABDOMEN W/CONTRAST',
    'CT ABDOMEN: Small right and trace left pleural effusion are noted.  Mild cardiomegaly is stable.  Segmental peripheral subcentimeter cystic lesions in the right liver periphery predominantly involve the subcapsular portion of segment VIII, with some extending to segment V peripherally. They are slightly more prominent since ___.  Fluid tracking along the falciform ligament is within the spectrum of postsurgical change and there is no evidence of rim enhancement or drainable fluid collection.  A right abdominal appraoch drainage catheter enters medial to the ___ costochondral junction and courses through the gallbladder fossa to terminate near the falciform ligament. A second right abdominal catheter enters below the right 10th rib anteriorly courses posterior to the liver and loops around the liver to terminate anterior to the left lobe adjacent to the falciform ligament. Stranding adjacent to the splenic flexure is within the spectrum of post- surgical change.  Scattered subcentimeter renal hypodensities likely represent cysts but are too small to characterize. The abdominal loops of large and small bowel are unremarkable. There is no pneumatosis, free air, or evidence of obstruction.  CT PELVIS: The rectum, sigmoid, prostate and seminal vesicles are unremarkable.  Air within the bladder is likely related to Foley catheterization. Small left greater than right fat-containing inguinal hernias are noted.  Bone windows demonstrate no lesion concerning for metastasis or infection.'
);


