    'EXAMINATION: LIVER OR GALLBLADDER US (SINGLE ORGAN); RENAL TRANSPLANT U.S.:  TECHNIQUE: Grey scale and color Doppler ultrasound images of the abdomen were obtained.  FINDINGS:   RENAL TRANSPLANT ULTRASOUND: Left lower quadrant renal transplant is unremarkable in its appearance. It measures 12.1 cm. There is no hydronephrosis.  No worrisome masses.  No perinephric collection. Doppler and spectral waveform analysis demonstrates patent main renal artery and main renal vein. Arterial waveforms demonstrates sharp upstrokes with resistive indices measuring 0.60, 0.64, 0.65 in the upper mid and lower poles respectively.  RIGHT UPPER QUADRANT ULTRASOUND: The liver is mildly heterogeneous in architecture. No focal liver lesions are identified. There is no ductal dilatation. Common bile duct measures 4 mm. Main portal vein is patent.  The gallbladder is distended with a wall noted to be edematous and there is a trace amount of pericholecystic fluid, however no stones are identified. The patient negative sonographic ___ sign.'
);


