)
VALUES (
    '24706695',
    '11241609-RR-111',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'LIVER OR GALLBLADDER US (SINGLE ORGAN)',
    'EXAMINATION: LIVER OR GALLBLADDER US (SINGLE ORGAN):  TECHNIQUE: Grey scale and color Doppler ultrasound images of the abdomen were obtained.  FINDINGS:   LIVER: The hepatic parenchyma appears coarsened. The contour of the liver is smooth. There is no focal liver mass. There is no ascites.  BILE DUCTS: There is no intrahepatic biliary dilation. The CBD measures 6 mm in diameter, borderline in diameter.  GALLBLADDER: Several stones are noted within the gallbladder lumen without evidence of cholecystitis. There is no gallbladder wall thickening.  PANCREAS: Imaged portion of the pancreas demonstrate decreased echogenicity suggestive of edema. No focal lesion is identified.  The pancreatic duct is top normal in size.  SPLEEN: Normal echogenicity, measuring 12 cm.  KIDNEYS: The right kidney measures 13.1 cm. The left kidney measures 13.7 cm.  Limited images demonstrates no hydronephrosis.  Patient is status post TIPS. Doppler evaluation demonstrates wall-to-wall flow. Velocities measure 89, 77, and 99 cm/sec in the proximal, mid, and distal portions respectively. When compared to prior study, these velocities have decreased. Flow within the left portal vein is towards the TIPS shunt. Flow within the right anterior a right posterior portal vein is towards the TIPS. The hepatic veins are patent. The main portal vein is patent with hepatopetal flow with velocity is 37 cm/sec.'
);


