    'RIGHT UPPER QUADRANT ULTRASOUND: Three echogenic hepatic lesions compatible with hemangiomas are unchanged from the prior ultrasound, the largest in the right hepatic lobe measuring 7.0 x 5.6 x 4.6 cm.  Two small additional echogenic lesions compatible with hemangiomas are identified, measuring 9 x 7 x 6 mm and 7 x 7 x 6 mm.  The gallbladder is distended, with small stones.  There is no gallbladder wall edema.  Sonographic ___ sign is negative.  The common duct is dilated, measuring 7 mm.  there is intrahepatic ductal dilation.  There is a small amount of pericholecystic fluid, and free fluid in ___''s pouch.  The right kidney is normal, without hydronephrosis.  The portal vein is patent, with anterograde flow.'
