INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '23511843',
    '11325145-RR-19',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'CT OF THE ABDOMEN AND PELVIS:   TECHNIQUE: Multidetector CT images of the abdomen and pelvis were obtained with oral and intravenous contrast.  Sagittal and coronal reformations were also performed.  FINDINGS:   CT ABDOMEN: Patchy opacities, dependent portions of the lower lungs are most consistent with atelectasis.  There is no pleural effusion.  The liver, gallbladder, spleen, and adrenal glands appear within normal limits.  There is mild fat stranding about the pancreas which demonstrated slight fullness.  A small hypodense focus in the interpolar region of the right kidney measuring 4 mm is too small to characterize but unchanged.    There is new mild left-sided hydronephrosis, and the left ureter is moderately dilated down to the pelvic inlet after which its course is difficult to follow.  There is a small calcification near the left ureterovesical junction, but already present before and probably a phlebolith lying near the area.  Fat stranding is present about the left kidney and the nephrogram is slightly delayed.  The left renal vein is mildly narrowed as it crosses beneath superior mesenteric artery, which arises from the aorta at a highly acute angle.   The patient is status post colectomy.  There is a rectal stump with persistent inflammatory mucosal enhancement, mild wall thickening, and surrounding fat stranding.  CT PELVIS: Intermingled with small bowel along the superior aspect of the bladder to the right of midline is a small rim well-circumscribed focus of gas and fluid which is suspected to represent a segment of small bowel within the pelvis, noting collapsed but poorly delineated small bowel in the area, but it is difficult to exclude a small fluid collection measuring up to perhaps 28 x 13 mm in axial ___ (2:64).  There are also small tubular fluid-containing structures along each pelvic sidewall, but quite small and more extensive on the left than right, which may represent a small postoperative fluid collections (2:63)  On the right, areas of slight fluid accumulation measure up to approximately 24 x 14 mm in axial ___.  On the right it is hard to distinguish post-operative change from small bowel.  The major mesenteric arteries and veins appear patent.  There is no ascites.  BONE WINDOWS: There are no suspicious lytic or blastic lesions.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
