VALUES (
    '23511843',
    '11325145-RR-20',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'ABDOMEN US (COMPLETE STUDY)',
    'TYPE OF THE EXAM: Abdominal ultrasound.  FINDINGS: The liver demonstrates normal echotexture without evidence of focal masses or intrahepatic biliary dilatation.  The gallbladder is well distended without evidence of cholelithiasis.  The gallbladder wall is normal in caliber.  There is no pericholecystic fluid.  The common bile duct is normal in caliber measuring 2 mm.  The right kidney measures 11.3 cm.  There is no hydronephrosis, nephrolithiasis, or suspicious renal masses.  The visualized aspect of the aorta and IVC are normal without aneurysmal dilatation.  The spleen is normal in size, measuring 8.8 cm.  The left kidney measures 11.6 cm. There is pelvicalyceal fullness, as seen on the prior CT. The pancreatic head, neck, and body are well visualized and demonstrate no evidence of focal masses.  Partially obscured pancreatic tail.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '29394743',
    '11341524-RR-92',
    'CT',
    'Chest',
    'CHEST PORT. LINE PLACEMENT',
    'TYPE OF EXAMINATION: Chest, AP portable single view.  FINDINGS: AP single view of the chest was obtained with patient in sitting upright position.  A right-sided PICC line can be identified.  It is, however, very difficult to identify its termination point in the right apical area as apparently the guide wire has been removed already.  A buckling curvature in the axillary area of the line suggests that there must be resistance.  Just above the right clavicle, one can identify a portion of the line again pointing upwards and suggestive that it was directed towards the internal jugular vein in retrograde fashion.  No pneumothorax has developed.  Lungs, as before, suggestive of rather advanced COPD, but no new infiltrates and no pneumothorax on either side.  Referring physician, ___, was informed and suggestion made that line placement will be performed under fluoroscopic control.  Preceding study of ___ demonstrated a right-sided PICC line terminating overlying the upper mediastinum, presumably located at the junction between jugular and subclavian veins.  As before, there exist multiple right-sided old rib fractures described before.'
);


