INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '29394743',
    '11341524-RR-95',
    'MRCP',
    'Abdomen',
    'MRCP (MR ABD W&W/OC)',
    'MR OF THE ABDOMEN, ___.:   TECHNIQUE: Multiplanar T1- and T2-weighted images were acquired on a 1.5 Tesla magnet including dynamic 3D imaging, obtained prior to, during and after the uneventful administration of 15 mL of Magnevist.  300 cc of GastroMARK and 450 cc of Redicat were also administered as bowel contrast.  Multiplanar 2D and 3D reformations and subtraction images were generated on an independent workstation.  FINDINGS: There is a moderate amount of free fluid in the left anterior pararenal space extending down the left paracolic gutter.  There is also small amount of perihepatic free fluid and moderate amount of free fluid in the right paracolic gutter, extending down to the right lower quadrant.  The pancreas has lost its normal texture.  The pancreatic duct is dilated up to 5.3 mm in the neck region and up to 5.6 mm in the area of pancreatic head with some irregularity distally. The distal pancreatic duct is seen to be tapering at the most distal portion, in the ampullary region.  There may be an ampullary stricture in this location. The findings are consistent with ____.  No organized fluid collection is seen.  There are two pancreatic cysts, one in the region of the tail measuring 8 mm and the other in the neck measuring 5 mm.  Both communicate with the central pancreatic duct.   The CBD is 8.5 mm in the porta hepatis, tapering down to 6.6 mm in the pancreatic head, with mild intrahepatic biliary dilatation.  There is no mass in pancreatic head, ampulla or CBD stone.  Other incidental findings include fundal focal adenomyomatosis of the gallbladder as well as round 3.8-cm fluid collection in the right cardiophrenic angle, most probably extension of the abdominal ascites through an anterior right Morgagni hernia.  There is an area of focal fatty change in segment IVb, adjacent to the fissure of the falciform ligament.  Multiplanar 2D and 3D reformations were essential in demonstrating the ductal anatomy.'
);


