)
VALUES (
    '29059416',
    '11461906-RR-34',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABDOMEN W/CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT axial images were obtained from the lung bases to the symphysis pubis after administration of IV contrast.  Coronal and sagittal reformations were obtained.  CT OF THE ABDOMEN WITH IV CONTRAST: Within the visualized lung bases, there is dependent atelectases bilaterally.  There is no pleural effusion. Visualized heart and pericardium are unremarkable, without pericardial effusion.  The liver, gallbladder, spleen, pancreas, and adrenal glands are unremarkable.  Few scattered rounded hypodensities within the left kidney are too small to characterize.  Nonspecific bilateral perinephric stranding is similar in appearance to prior study.  A stone within the lower pole of the left kidney is better assessed on non-contrast CT from the same day.  Both kidneys enhance and excrete contrast symmetrically, without evidence of obstruction.  Within the distal left ureter, there is area of low attenuation posteriorly, with suggestion of a contrast-fluid level.  This may reflect contrast and urine mixing artifact.  The stomach, small bowel, and colon are within normal limits.  There is no free fluid, free air or pathologic adenopathy.  CT OF THE PELVIS WITH IV CONTRAST: Prostate is mildly enlarged.  Rectum and urinary bladder appear unremarkable.  Small bilateral fat containing inguinal hernias are evident.  There is no pelvic free fluid or adenopathy.  OSSEOUS STRUCTURES: No suspicious lytic or sclerotic lesion is identified. There are degenerative changes of the hips bilaterally, and transitional anatomy at the lumbosacral junction.  Focal lucency in the right ilium, without any aggressive features are unchanged from as far back as ___.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
