    'TECHNIQUE: Ultrasonography of the abdomen.  FINDINGS: The liver echotexture is normal, and there is no focal intrahepatic lesion or intrahepatic bile duct dilation.  The main portal vein is patent, demonstrating proper hepatopetal flow.  The gallbladder is partially collapsed, containing numerous stones, at least two are located within the gallbladder neck, which are immobile.  The wall is not thickened and there gallbladder is relaxed.  There is no pericholecystic fluid or sonographic ___ sign.  The CBD measures up to 7 mm in diameter, unchanged since the CT examination.  The spleen is not enlarged, measuring 8.7 cm.  A 10 mm pancreatic tail cyst was also seen on the ___ CT examination.  The right and left kidneys measure 9.9 and 10.1 cm, respectively, without stone or hydronephrosis. No free fluid is present.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
