    '11585755-RR-34',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'ABDOMEN U.S. (COMPLETE STUDY) PORT',
    'PORTABLE ABDOMINAL ULTRASOUND: The liver appears normal in echotexture and architecture, with no focal liver lesion seen.  The main portal vein is patent, with normal hepatopetal direction of flow.  No intra or extra-hepatic biliary ductal dilatation is noted, with the common duct measuring 3-mm.  The gallbladder is nondistended and appears normal, without evidence of stones. The pancreas is well visualized and appears normal.  The kidneys measure 11.4- cm and 13.7-cm on the right, both are without definite evidence for mass, stone, or hydronephrosis.  The spleen is not enlarged measuring 9.9-cm.  No ascites is seen in the upper or lower quadrant.  The visualized abdominal aorta again demonstrates a normal caliber, with the aortic wall measuring 2-3 mm thick.'
);


