)
VALUES (
    '27929956',
    '11589051-RR-26',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABDOMEN W/O CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT axial images were obtained from the lung bases to the lower abdomen without IV or oral contrast.  Coronal and sagittal reformations were obtained.  CT OF THE ABDOMEN WITHOUT IV CONTRAST: Visualized lung bases are clear. There is no pleural effusion.  Visualized heart and pericardium are unremarkable.  Evaluation of the abdomen is markedly limited due to retained contrast from a small bowel follow-through performed on the same day at 10 a.m., creating dense streak artifact.  However, there is no evidence for free intraperitoneal air.  Limited views of the liver, gallbladder, and spleen appear unremarkable. Assessment of the posterior duodenal wall is limited due to the retained contrast.  OSSEOUS STRUCTURES: No suspicious lytic or sclerotic lesion is identified.'
);


