    '11689448-RR-36',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABDOMEN W/CONTRAST',
    'STUDY: CT of the abdomen and pelvis with contrast; MDCT images were generated through the abdomen and pelvis after administration of 130 cc of Optiray intravenous contrast.  Coronal and sagittal reformatted images were also generated.  FINDINGS:   ABDOMEN: The visualized portion of the heart, lungs, and the chest appears unremarkable.  The liver shows no focal lesion or intrahepatic biliary dilatation.  The gallbladder shows no stones or wall edema.  The spleen is normal in size and appearance.  The adrenal glands are normal appearing bilaterally.  The kidneys enhance with and excrete contrast symmetrically.  Multiple well-circumscribed fluid densities are seen in the left kidney, the largest of which measures 5.5 cm in diameter (2; 38).  The pancreas appears normal.  The small intestine demonstrates an unusual looping pattern without evidence of obstruction (301b;19); nonobstructive small bowel hernia is a consideration.  The large intestine shows no evidence of obstruction, although significant fecal burden is noted.  The aorta, IVC, portal vein, and the major branches all appear patent.  There is no lymphadenopathy, free air, or free fluid.  PELVIS: The bladder, prostate, and rectum appear unremarkable.  BONES: No aggressive-appearing lytic or sclerotic lesion is seen.'
);


