    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT axial imaging was obtained from lung bases to the pubic symphysis following the administration of intravenous contrast material.  Coronal and sagittal reformats were completed.  FINDINGS: CT ABDOMEN WITH CONTRAST:  The visualized lung bases are clear.  The heart and pericardium are unremarkable.  The liver enhances homogenously without any focal lesions or intra- or extra-hepatic biliary dilatation.  The main portal vein, splenic vein and SMV are patent.  The gallbladder is unremarkable without distention or pericholecystic fluid.  The spleen and left adrenal gland is unremarkable.  There is a 1.4 x 1.4 cm nodule within the right adrenal gland which is indeterminant on this single-phase CT scan.  The kidneys enhance and excrete contrast symmetrically without any focal lesions or hydronephrosis.  Patient is status post gastric bypass without evidence of obstruction or complication.  The stomach, small and intra-abdominal large bowel are unremarkable without evidence of obstruction.  There is significant peripancreatic stranding and edema of the head and uncinate process of the pancreas consistent with ____.  There is no pseudocyst or significant fluid surrounding the pancreas.  There is no evidence of a splenic artery aneurysm or abnormal enhancement to suggest necrosis.  There is no free fluid, free air or lymphadenopathy within the abdomen.  The aorta is of normal caliber without evidence of aneurysm.  CT PELVIS: The bladder, rectum and sigmoid colon are unremarkable.  Suture lines are noted at the rectosigmoid junction.  There is no free fluid or free air or lymphadenopathy in the pelvis.  OSSEOUS STRUCTURES: There are no concerning osseous lesions.'
);


