    '11828074-RR-13',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CTA ABD W&W/O C & RECONS',
    'TECHNIQUE: ___ MDCT images were obtained through the abdomen after the administration of 200 cc of IV contrast.  Multiplanar reformatted images in coronal and sagittal axes were generated and reviewed.  FINDINGS: The bases of the lungs demonstrate mild bibasilar atelectasis.  There is a right middle lobe demonstrates a 4-mm nodule (series 3, image 6).  The liver is unremarkable without evidence of focal lesions or intrahepatic biliary ductal dilatation.  The portal vein is patent.  The gallbladder is normal without evidence of stones or wall thickening.  The spleen is homogenous and normal in size.  The adrenal glands bilaterally are normal.  Left kidney demonstrates extrarenal pelvices as well as hypodensities within the parenchyma, too small to characterize by CT but likely secondary to renal cysts.    The pancreas demonstrates significant peripancreatic stranding with fluid extending to the inferior splenic pole. There appears to be diffuse involvement of the entire pancreas.  There is no evidence of pancreatic duct dilatation.  There is no evidence of an aneurysm or surrounding abscess.  The stomach, duodenum and small bowel are unremarkable without evidence of obstruction or wall thickening.  There is no retroperitoneal or mesenteric lymphadenopathy.  No intra-abdominal free air is identified.  OSSEOUS STRUCTURES: No lytic or blastic lesions concerning for malignancy are identified.'
);


