INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '23674046',
    '11945588-RR-14',
    'MRCP',
    'Abdomen',
    'MRCP (MR ABD W&W/OC)',
    'EXAMINATION: MRCP (MR ___:  TECHNIQUE: Multiplanar T1 and T2 weighted MR images of the abdomen were obtained on a 1.5 Tesla magnet including dynamic 3D imaging prior to, during, and after the administration of 8 mL Gadavist gadolinium based contrast.  1 mL Gadavist mixed with 50 mL water was also administered for oral contrast.  FINDINGS: Bowel: There is a 5.1 x 4.4 x 3.7 cm heterogeneous mass which appears to be centered over the second portion of the duodenum (2:26, 3:37), displacing the pancreatic head and duodenal lumen. The mass demonstrates peripheral enhancement, which may represent the adjacent duodenal mucosa. Multiple internal foci of T1 hyperintensity are noted which likely representing hemorrhage or, less likely, enteric contrast. No significant adjacent lymphadenopathy is identified. Colonic diverticulosis is noted.  Pancreas:  Within the tail of the pancreas, there is a 6 mm T2 hyperintense cystic structure likely representing a side branch IPMN. The remainder of the pancreas itself is normal in signal intensity without evidence of focal mass or ductal dilatation.  While the pancreatic head is displaced by the adjacent mass, no other definite parenchymal abnormality.  Liver: The liver is homogeneous and demonstrates diffuse signal dropout on out-of-phase imaging, compatible with fatty deposition.  There is a 7 mm T2 hyperintensity seen within segment ___ of the liver, likely representing a biliary hamartoma.  There is no significant intra or extrahepatic biliary ductal dilatation.  Gallbladder: The multiple tiny layering gallstones are noted. The gallbladder is otherwise unremarkable in appearance.  Spleen: The spleen is normal in appearance.  Kidneys and Adrenals: The adrenal glands and kidneys are normal bilaterally. A 7 mm T2 hyperintensity is seen within the interpolar region of the left kidney, likely a simple cyst.  Lymph Nodes:  There is no significant mesenteric or retroperitoneal lymphadenopathy.  Vessels: The abdominal vasculature is widely patent.  Bones: The osseous structures are unremarkable.'
);


