INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '25233319',
    '12004475-RR-5',
    'MRCP',
    'Abdomen',
    'MRCP (MR ABD W&W/OC)',
    'TECHNIQUE: Coronal HASTE, axial in- and opposed-phase, axial HASTE, and coronal thick slab MRCP, axial 3D LAVA, pre- and triphasic post-contrast images with subtraction were acquired through the biliary system.  9 mL of intravenous Gadavist and 1 cc of oral Gadavist were administered without complications.  FINDINGS: There is mild atelectasis at the right lung base.   The liver demonstrates minimal signal drop off on out-of-phase imaging when compared to in-phase T1-weighted imaging suggesting mild fatty deposition.  Note is made of a 6 mm enhancing lesion in the right hepatic lobe, which likely represents a nonspecific perfusional difference within the liver (1101:44).  Otherwise, no focal hepatic lesions are identified.    Stones and sludge are filling the gallbladder.  There is slight edema of the gallbladder wall at the edge that faces the liver.  There is no intra- or extra-hepatic biliary duct dilatation. There is no evidence of biliary stones.   There is very mild fat stranding seen anterior to the pancreas, compatible with known diagnosis of ____ (4:29).  The pancreatic duct is not dilated.  No stones are noted within the pancreatic duct.    The adrenal glands are unremarkable.  The spleen is within normal limits. The kidneys enhance and excrete contrast symmetrically without evidence of hydronephrosis or masses.   Visualized portions of stomach, small and large bowel are within normal limits.   The intra-abdominal aorta is unremarkable.  The celiac axis, SMA, bilateral renal arteries and ___ are patent.  There is normal hepatic arterial anatomy.  There is no free fluid or lymphadenopathy.  No concerning osseous lesions are identified.'
);


