INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '26561933',
    '12095158-RR-3',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'LIVER OR GALLBLADDER US (SINGLE ORGAN)',
    'RIGHT UPPER QUADRANT ULTRASOUND: The pancreas is not visualized due to overlying bowel gas.  The liver appears normal in echotexture and architecture.  No focal liver lesion seen.  The main portal vein is patent with normal hepatopetal direction of flow.  Where visualized, the common duct is not dilated, measuring between 5 and 6 mm.  The gallbladder is somewhat distended and contains multiple mobile stones. Mildly echogenic material within the gallbladder neck does not reposition on decubitus imaging, possibly representing tumefactive sludge.  There is gallbladder wall thickening, concerning for cholecystitis.  No pericholecystic fluid is noted.  ___ sign was not present.  Views of the right kidney show no hydronephrosis.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '26561933',
    '12095158-RR-4',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABDOMEN W/O CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: Images obtained during CT abdomen/pelvis performed at ___ ___ on ___, 1:35 a.m. is uploaded onto PACS from CD ROM for second opinion consultation read.  Apparently, MDCT axial imaging is performed through the abdomen and pelvis after administration of oral contrast only.  No IV contrast was administered.  Images are displayed as 5 mm thick axial and 2 mm thick coronal and sagittal reformations.  CT ABDOMEN WITHOUT IV CONTRAST: The study is degraded due to respiratory motion.  There may be trace right pleural effusion.  Dependent atelectasis is noted in the lung bases, more on the right.  No pericardial effusion is seen. Coronary artery calcifications involve the left main, left anterior descending, left circumflex and right coronary arteries.  Aortic valvular calcifications are also noted, of indeterminate hemodynamic significance. There is a small hiatal hernia.  Assessment of the abdominal viscera is limited due to lack of IV contrast administration.  The nonenhanced liver, spleen and right adrenal gland appear unremarkable.  There is nodular thickening of the left adrenal gland without discrete nodule.  Nonspecific perirenal stranding is noted bilaterally.  No stone or hydronephrosis is noted within the kidneys.  The gallbladder is distended with large calcified gallstones.  There is suggestion of gallbladder wall thickening or edema.  No definite biliary distention is seen, although assessment is limited due to noncontrast study. There is mild pericholecystic fat stranding.  Findings are concerning for acute cholecystitis.  A 17 x 21 mm cystic lesion is noted in the uncinate of the pancreas, the enhancement pattern of which cannot be assessed without IV contrast (3:40). Note is also made of a vague hypodense area at the junction of the body and head of the pancreas measuring 8 x 11 mm (3:32) which is also incompletely characterized.  No definite pancreatic ductal dilatation is noted.  Hazy appearance of the mesentery may well be due to respiratory motion.  No free air is noted within the abdomen.  The stomach, small bowel and colon appear unremarkable.  Atherosclerotic calcifications are noted along the abdominal aorta, the SMA and the origin of the celiac axis and right renal artery.  No aortic aneurysm is seen.  Aortocaval nodes measure up to 10 mm in short axis (3:40).  Portocaval nodes measure up to 8 mm in short axis.  CT PELVIS WITHOUT IV CONTRAST: The urinary bladder appears unremarkable.  The prostate, seminal vesicles, rectosigmoid colon and pelvic loops of bowel appear unremarkable.  No pelvic free air, free fluid or adenopathy is noted. Vascular calcifications are noted along the iliac arteries and femoral arteries.  There are bilateral fat-containing inguinal hernias with small amount of fluid noted within the right hernia sac.  OSSEOUS STRUCTURES: Mild sclerotic change along the lateral left seventh and tenth ribs could represent prior fractures.  There is S-shaped scoliosis of the thoracolumbar spine with multilevel degenerative change.  Degenerative changes are also noted along the left sacroiliac joint.'
);


