    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'LIVER OR GALLBLADDER US (SINGLE ORGAN)',
    'TECHNIQUE: Grayscale and limited Doppler ultrasound of the right upper quadrant was performed.  FINDINGS: Hepatic echogenicity is normal.  There are no liver lesions identified.  There is no intrahepatic biliary duct dilation.  The common bile duct measures up to 8 mm in its free segment.  The gallbladder is surgically absent.  The main portal vein is patent with normal hepatopetal flow.  Spleen is normal in appearance, measuring 9.4 cm.  The included portions of the head and body of the pancreas are unremarkable.  The tail of the pancreas is not included on the study.  There is no ascites.  Included portions of the abdominal aorta and IVC are unremarkable.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '24639523',
    '12109423-RR-37',
    'CT',
    'Chest',
    'CHEST (PA & LAT) PORT',
    'STUDY: PA and lateral chest radiograph ___.  FINDINGS: There are old pacemaker wires on the right side.  There is a left-sided pacemaker generator with dual leads.  There is cardiomegaly.  There is tortuosity of the thoracic aorta.  These are all unchanged.  There is no focal consolidation.  There is no pneumothoraces.  Postoperative changes with resection of the lateral clavicle on the right is seen.  There is loss of subacromial space, consistent with rotator cuff rupture.  Suture is seen within the humeral head, consistent with previous rotator cuff repair.  There are some wedging and compression deformities of a lower thoracic vertebral body, possibly T10.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '20695044',
    '10025862-RR-17',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'PORTABLE ABDOMEN',
    'TECHNIQUE: Portable supine and left lateral decubitus abdominal views were obtained.  FINDINGS: Mild stool burden, predominantly in the right colon.  Gas is seen within the small and large bowel.  There are no abnormally dilated loops of large or small bowel.  The diaphragms are not completely imaged on the left lateral decubitus view; within this limitation, there is no gross pneumoperitoneum.  In addition, no air-fluid levels are identified on the left lateral decubitus view.  A CBD stent is in place in appropriate position. Osseous structures are unremarkable. There are no unexplained soft tissue calcifications or radiopaque foreign bodies.  Note is made of mesenteric calcification within the left lower quadrant, better characterized on prior CT.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '20695044',
    '10025862-RR-18',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS W/O CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: Multidetector CT images of the abdomen and pelvis were acquired without intravenous contrast. Non-contrast scan has several limitations in detecting vascular and parenchymal organ abnormalities, including tumor detection. Oral contrast was not administered. Coronal and sagittal reformations were performed and reviewed on PACS.  DOSE: Total DLP (Body) = 1,527 mGy-cm.  FINDINGS:   LOWER CHEST: Visualized lung fields are within normal limits.  There is no evidence of pleural or pericardial effusion.  ABDOMEN:   HEPATOBILIARY: Steatohepatitis is noted.  There is no evidence of focal lesions within the limitations of an unenhanced scan.  Pneumobilia is consistent with recent ERCP and biliary stent placement.  The gallbladder is within normal limits.  PANCREAS: There is an area of fullness at the head of the pancreas which may represent region that was recently biopsied.  The pancreatic duct is dilated.  Significant peripancreatic stranding in the pancreaticoduodenal groove may be related to ____ or mass.  SPLEEN: The spleen shows normal size and attenuation throughout, without evidence of focal lesions.  ADRENALS: The right and left adrenal glands are normal in size and shape.  URINARY: The kidneys are of normal and symmetric size.  There is no evidence of focal renal lesions within the limitations of an unenhanced scan.  There is no hydronephrosis.  There is no nephrolithiasis.  There is no perinephric abnormality.  GASTROINTESTINAL: The stomach is unremarkable.  Small bowel loops demonstrate normal caliber and wall thickness throughout.  The colon and rectum are within normal limits.  The appendix is normal.  No evidence of free air or leakage of contrast in the abdomen.  PELVIS: The urinary bladder and distal ureters are unremarkable.  There is no free fluid in the pelvis.  REPRODUCTIVE ORGANS: Lobulated uterus consistent with uterine fibroids.  LYMPH NODES: There is no retroperitoneal or mesenteric lymphadenopathy.  There is no pelvic or inguinal lymphadenopathy.  VASCULAR: There is no abdominal aortic aneurysm.  Mild atherosclerotic disease is noted.  BONES: There is no evidence of worrisome osseous lesions or acute fracture.  SOFT TISSUES: The abdominal and pelvic wall is within normal limits.  NOTIFICATION: The findings were discussed by Dr. ___ with Dr. ___ on the telephoneon ___ at 5:00 ___, 5 minutes after discovery of the findings.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
