    'EXAMINATION: LIVER OR GALLBLADDER US (SINGLE ORGAN):  TECHNIQUE: Grey scale and color Doppler ultrasound images of the abdomen were obtained.  FINDINGS:   LIVER: The liver is diffusely echogenic. The contour of the liver is smooth. There is no focal liver mass. The main portal vein is patent with hepatopetal flow. There is no ascites.  BILE DUCTS: There is no intrahepatic biliary dilation. The CHD measures 4 mm.  GALLBLADDER: There is no evidence of stones or gallbladder wall thickening.  The gallbladder is not distended.  PANCREAS: The pancreas is not well visualized, largely obscured by overlying bowel gas.  SPLEEN: Normal echogenicity, measuring 16.3 cm.  KIDNEYS: Limited views of the right kidney show no hydronephrosis.  RETROPERITONEUM: The visualized portions of aorta and IVC are within normal limits.'
);


