    'TECHNIQUE: Single frontal supine portable view radiograph of the abdomen.  FINDINGS: A catheter projects over the left femoral region, presumed venous.  Large central drainage catheter projects over the mid abdomen.  In the left upper quadrant there are 2 linear densities with associated adjacent rectangular densities, likely representing two towels, reportedly known to be left within the abdominal cavity.  No other radiopaque foreign object is identified.  Mild gaseous distention of multiple loops of bowel likely represents postoperative ileus.  Evaluation for min pneumoperitoneum is limited on this single supine radiograph excludes the hemidiaphragms from the field of view.  NOTIFICATION: The findings were discussed with ___, M.D. by ___ ___, M.D. on the telephone on ___ at 1:27 AM, 2 minutes after discovery of the findings.'
);


