INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '22470405',
    '10448910-RR-11',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABDOMEN W/CONTRAST',
    'EXAMINATION: CT abdomen with contrast  TECHNIQUE: Multidetector CT images of the abdomen were acquired with intravenous contrast. No oral contrast was administered. Coronal and sagittal reformations were performed and reviewed on PACS.  DOSE: Acquisition sequence:    1) Stationary Acquisition 5.5 s, 0.5 cm; CTDIvol = 26.5 mGy (Body) DLP = 13.2 mGy-cm.    2) Spiral Acquisition 3.3 s, 35.5 cm; CTDIvol = 9.1 mGy (Body) DLP = 322.0 mGy-cm.  Total DLP (Body) = 335 mGy-cm.  FINDINGS:   LOWER CHEST: The visualized heart and pericardium are within normal limits.  There is mild bibasilar atelectasis, more marked on the left.  ABDOMEN:   HEPATOBILIARY: The liver is normal in size and attenuation.  There is no intra or extrahepatic biliary ductal dilatation.  There is a bilobed 2.2 x 1.8 cm hepatic cyst at the liver dome (02:11).  The gallbladder is within normal limits.  Subcentimeter hepatic hypodensities are too small to characterize on  CT.:   PANCREAS: The pancreas has normal attenuation throughout, without evidence of focal concerning lesions.  There is no pancreatic ductal dilatation.  There is no peripancreatic stranding.  SPLEEN: The spleen shows normal size and attenuation throughout, without evidence of focal lesions.  ADRENALS: The right and left adrenal glands are normal in size and shape.  URINARY: The kidneys are of normal and symmetric size. There is no hydronephrosis.    Subcentimeter hypodensities throughout both kidneys are too small to characterize on CT.  There is no perinephric abnormality.  GASTROINTESTINAL: The stomach is unremarkable.  Visualized small bowel loops demonstrate normal caliber and wall thickness.  The visualized colon is unremarkable.  LYMPH NODES: There is no evidence of retroperitoneal or mesenteric lymphadenopathy.  VASCULAR: There is no upper abdominal aortic aneurysm.  Mild atherosclerotic disease is noted.  BONES: There is no evidence of worrisome osseous lesions or acute fracture.  SOFT TISSUES: The abdominal and pelvic wall is within normal limits.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '22470405',
    '10448910-RR-12',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'LIVER OR GALLBLADDER US (SINGLE ORGAN)',
    'EXAMINATION: LIVER OR GALLBLADDER US (SINGLE ORGAN):  TECHNIQUE: Grey scale and color Doppler ultrasound images of the abdomen were obtained.  FINDINGS: There is a small right pleural effusion.  LIVER: The hepatic parenchyma appears within normal limits. The contour of the liver is smooth.  A 1.2 x 2.0 x 1.5 cm (transverse x AP x CC) cyst is visualized within the right lobe of the liver, unchanged compared to the prior CT.  The main portal vein is patent with hepatopetal flow. There is no ascites.  BILE DUCTS: There is no intrahepatic biliary dilation. The CBD is not dilated.  GALLBLADDER: The gallbladder is mildly distended.  There is irregular echogenic material within the gallbladder, that likely represents sludge balls/tumefactive sludge.  There is no evidence of gallbladder wall edema or pericholecystic fluid.  PANCREAS: Imaged portion of the pancreas appears within normal limits, without masses or pancreatic ductal dilation, with portions of the pancreatic tail obscured by overlying bowel gas.  SPLEEN: Normal echogenicity, measuring 8.9 cm.  KIDNEYS: The right kidney measures 11.0 cm. The left kidney measures 11.7 cm. Normal cortical echogenicity and corticomedullary differentiation is seen bilaterally. There is no evidence of masses, stones, or hydronephrosis in the kidneys.  RETROPERITONEUM: Visualized portions of aorta and IVC are within normal limits.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '22332642',
    '10648030-RR-7',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'LIVER OR GALLBLADDER US (SINGLE ORGAN)',
    'EXAMINATION: LIVER OR GALLBLADDER US (SINGLE ORGAN):  TECHNIQUE: Grey scale and color Doppler ultrasound images of the abdomen were obtained.  FINDINGS:   LIVER: The hepatic parenchyma appears within normal limits. The contour of the liver is smooth.  An 1-cm echogenic, round focus in the left hepatic lobe without demonstrable vascularity with color Doppler could be a hemangioma or focal fat (Series 1, image 57).  The main portal vein is patent with hepatopetal flow.  No ascites.  BILE DUCTS: There is mild intrahepatic biliary dilation. The CBD is dilated and measures 8 mm.  Several echogenic obstructing common bile duct stones are identified, the largest in the distal common bile duct in the area of the pancreatic head measuring up to 1.3 cm.  It is unclear if there is debris more centrally in the bile ducts.  GALLBLADDER: The gallbladder is markedly distended with numerous gallstones.  The gallbladder wall measures up to 3 mm common top-normal.  No sonographic ___ sign.  No pericholecystic fluid.  PANCREAS: Imaged portion of the pancreas appears within normal limits, without masses or pancreatic ductal dilation, with portions of the pancreatic tail obscured by overlying bowel gas.  The main pancreatic duct does not appear dilated.  SPLEEN: Normal echogenicity, measuring 9 cm.  KIDNEYS: The right kidney measures 9.5 cm. The left kidney measures 9.7 cm.  No evidence of hydronephrosis on limited images of the kidneys.  RETROPERITONEUM: Visualized portions of aorta and IVC are within normal limits.  NOTIFICATION: The findings and impression were discussed with ___, M.D. by ___, M.D. on the telephone on ___ at 9:08 ___, 1 minutes after discovery of the findings.'
);


