    'EXAMINATION: Portable chest radiograph  TECHNIQUE: Portable chest radiograph  FINDINGS: Lung volumes are low.  Bibasilar opacities may represent dependent atelectasis.  However, there are also air bronchograms at the medial right lung base which should be followed closely to exclude aspiration.  No pleural effusion or pneumothorax.  Cardiomediastinal silhouette is within normal limits.  No acute osseous abnormalities identified.  No subdiaphragmatic free air is detected.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '22726387',
    '10745469-RR-62',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'EXAMINATION: CT ABD AND PELVIS WITH CONTRAST:  TECHNIQUE: Single phase split bolus contrast: MDCT axial images were acquired through the abdomen and pelvis following intravenous contrast administration with split bolus technique. IV Contrast:  150 mL Omnipaque. Coronal and sagittal reformations were performed and reviewed on PACS. Oral contrast was not administered.  DOSE: Acquisition sequence:    1) CT Localizer Radiograph    2) CT Localizer Radiograph    3) Stationary Acquisition 0.5 s, 0.5 cm; CTDIvol = 2.4 mGy (Body) DLP = 1.2 mGy-cm.    4) Spiral Acquisition 5.1 s, 56.0 cm; CTDIvol = 16.9 mGy (Body) DLP = 945.9 mGy-cm.  Total DLP (Body) = 947 mGy-cm.  FINDINGS:   LOWER CHEST: There is bibasilar dependent atelectasis.  No pleural effusions.  Heart size is normal, and there is no pericardial effusion.  Coronary artery calcifications are noted.  ABDOMEN:   HEPATOBILIARY: The liver demonstrates homogenous attenuation throughout.  There is no evidence of focal lesions.  There is no evidence of intrahepatic or extrahepatic biliary dilatation.  There is gallbladder wall edema which is most likely due third spacing or reactive from adjacent inflammation, rather than from a primary acute cholecystitis.  Portal veins are patent, without evidence of thrombosis.  PANCREAS: There is diffuse peripancreatic fat stranding surrounding the entire pancreas, consistent with ____.  No organized fluid collection.  SPLEEN: The spleen shows normal size and attenuation throughout, without evidence of focal lesions.  ADRENALS: The right and left adrenal glands are normal in size and shape.  URINARY: The kidneys are of normal and symmetric size with normal nephrogram.  There is no evidence of focal renal lesions or hydronephrosis.  There is no perinephric abnormality.  GASTROINTESTINAL: There is a moderately-sized hiatal hernia.  Small bowel loops demonstrate normal caliber, wall thickness, and enhancement throughout.  There is extensive colonic diverticulosis, without evidence of acute diverticulitis.  The colon and rectum are otherwise unremarkable.  There is mesenteric edema predominantly in the epigastric region, but also trace nonhemorrhagic fluid in the lower abdomen (300b:36).  No pneumoperitoneum.  Normal appendix.  PELVIS: Evaluation of pelvic structures is limited by streak artifact from the left hip arthroplasty.  The urinary bladder is unremarkable in appearance. There is no free fluid in the pelvis.  REPRODUCTIVE ORGANS: The prostate and seminal vesicles are unremarkable.  LYMPH NODES: There is no retroperitoneal or mesenteric lymphadenopathy.  Bilateral external iliac nodes appear mildly prominent measuring up to 8 mm in short axis, although are not pathologically enlarged by CT size criteria.  There is no pelvic or inguinal lymphadenopathy.  VASCULAR: There is no abdominal aortic aneurysm.  Mild atherosclerotic disease is noted.  Incidental note is made of the replaced right hepatic artery.  BONES: There is no evidence of worrisome osseous lesions or acute fracture.  There is no evidence of periprosthetic lucency about the left hip arthroplasty.  Severe degenerative changes are noted in the lumbar spine.  There has been prior hemilaminectomy at L4 on the right.  SOFT TISSUES: The abdominal and pelvic wall is within normal limits.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '22726387',
    '10745469-RR-63',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'LIVER OR GALLBLADDER US (SINGLE ORGAN)',
    'EXAMINATION: LIVER OR GALLBLADDER US (SINGLE ORGAN):  TECHNIQUE: Grey scale and color Doppler ultrasound images of the abdomen were obtained.  FINDINGS:   LIVER: The liver is diffusely echogenic, suggestive of hepatic steatosis. The contour of the liver is smooth. There is no focal liver mass. The main portal vein is patent with hepatopetal flow. There is no ascites.  BILE DUCTS: There is no intrahepatic biliary dilation. The CBD measures 8 mm.  GALLBLADDER: The gallbladder is not abnormally distended.  There is gallbladder wall thickening, measuring up to 5 mm in addition to trace pericholecystic fluid.  These findings are most likely reactive secondary to adjacent inflammation rather than from primary acute cholecystitis.  No cholelithiasis.  PANCREAS: The pancreas is not well visualized on the current study.  Imaged portion of pancreas shows no ductal dilation and small amounts of peripancreatic fluid and echogenic inflammatory changes in adjacent fat.  However, extensive peripancreatic inflammation and fluid is better depicted on the CT performed on the same date.  KIDNEYS: Limited images of the right kidney demonstrates no evidence of hydronephrosis.'
);


