t adrenal glands are normal in size and shape.  URINARY: The kidneys are of normal and symmetric size with normal nephrogram.  There is no evidence of focal renal lesions or hydronephrosis.  There is no perinephric abnormality.  GASTROINTESTINAL: The stomach is unremarkable.  There is mild wall thickening of the duodenum, likely reactive in the setting of ____.  Inflammation around the hepatic flexure of the colon is also likely reactive.  There is diverticulosis of the sigmoid and descending colon without evidence of diverticulitis.  The appendix is not visualized.  PELVIS: The urinary bladder and distal ureters are unremarkable.  There is no free fluid in the pelvis.  REPRODUCTIVE ORGANS: The prostate and seminal vesicles are unremarkable.  LYMPH NODES: Scattered retroperitoneal and mesenteric lymphadenopathy is likely reactive in the setting of active inflammation.  There is no pelvic or inguinal lymphadenopathy.  VASCULAR: There is no abdominal aortic aneurysm.  Mild atherosclerotic disease is noted.  There is attenuation of all 3 vessels at the portal confluence however the main portal vein, splenic vein and SMV remain patent.  BONES: Degenerative changes are again seen in the lumbar spine.  The patient is status post left total hip arthroplasty with streak artifact from the hardware limiting evaluation the lower pelvis.  SOFT TISSUES: The abdominal and pelvic wall is within normal limits.  NOTIFICATION: The findings were discussed by Dr. ___ with Dr. ___ on the telephone on ___ at 3 ___, 5 minutes after discovery of the findings.'
