ond and third portion of the duodenum.  There is no small-bowel obstruction.  Other than colonic diverticulosis, the colon and rectum is unremarkable.  Appendix is normal in caliber.  There is no ascites.  There is a small amount of pneumoperitoneum, which is most likely postsurgical.  PELVIS: Evaluation of the pelvis is slightly limited by streak artifact from right hip arthroplasty.  Urinary bladder is unremarkable in appearance.  There is no free fluid in the pelvis.  REPRODUCTIVE ORGANS: Prostate gland and seminal vesicles are unremarkable.  LYMPH NODES: There is no retroperitoneal or mesenteric lymphadenopathy.  There is no pelvic or inguinal lymphadenopathy.  VASCULAR: There is no abdominal aortic aneurysm.  Mild atherosclerotic disease is noted.  The portal venous system is patent.  BONES: There is no evidence of worrisome osseous lesions or acute fracture.  SOFT TISSUES: Evaluation of the soft tissues is notable for soft tissue air throughout the right lateral soft tissues, and stranding at the umbilicus, compatible with changes from recent laparoscopic surgery.'
