INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '26133494',
    '11137177-RR-26',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: Single phase split bolus contrast: MDCT axial images were acquired through the abdomen and pelvis following intravenous contrast administration with split bolus technique. Oral contrast was administered. Coronal and sagittal reformations were performed and reviewed on PACS.  DOSE: Acquisition sequence:    1) CT Localizer Radiograph    2) CT Localizer Radiograph    3) Stationary Acquisition 6.0 s, 0.5 cm; CTDIvol = 28.9 mGy (Body) DLP = 14.4 mGy-cm.    4) Spiral Acquisition 5.4 s, 58.9 cm; CTDIvol = 16.7 mGy (Body) DLP = 982.8 mGy-cm.  Total DLP (Body) = 997 mGy-cm.  FINDINGS:   LOWER CHEST: There is a small right and trace left nonhemorrhagic pleural effusion with associated bibasilar atelectasis, increased from ___.  There is no pericardial effusion.  ABDOMEN:   HEPATOBILIARY: The liver is mildly hypo attenuating compatible with hepatic steatosis.  There is no evidence of focal lesions.  There is no evidence of intrahepatic or extrahepatic biliary dilatation.  The gallbladder demonstrates mucosal hyperemia and wall thickening , however is more decompressed than on the prior study  PANCREAS: The pancreas again appears edematous thick continues to enhance uniformly.  There is interval increase in the amount of fluid surrounding the pancreas some of which appears to be starting to organize.  There more loculated areas of fluid superior to the pancreatic tail abutting the lesser curvature of the stomach as well as anterior to the pancreatic head along the hepatic flexure of the colon.  The amount of ascites has decreased.  SPLEEN: The spleen shows normal size and attenuation throughout, without evidence of focal lesions.  ADRENALS: The right and left adrenal glands are normal in size and shape.  URINARY: The kidneys are of normal and symmetric size with normal nephrogram.  There is no evidence of focal renal lesions or hydronephrosis.  There is no perinephric abnormality.  GASTROINTESTINAL: There is mild wall thickening of the stomach particularly in the antrum likely reactive relating to adjacent ____.  The duodenum appears thickened also likely reactive.  Note is made of a small duodenum diverticulum.  The remainder of the small bowel is normal in caliber with no evidence of obstruction.  Diverticulosis of the sigmoid colon is noted, without evidence of wall thickening and fat stranding.  The appendix is surgically absent.  PELVIS: The bladder appears mildly thick walled which may be related to under distension.  There is trace free fluid in the pelvis.  REPRODUCTIVE ORGANS: The prostate and seminal vesicles are unremarkable.  LYMPH NODES: There is no retroperitoneal or mesenteric lymphadenopathy.  There is no pelvic or inguinal lymphadenopathy.  VASCULAR: There is no abdominal aortic aneurysm.  Mild atherosclerotic disease is noted.  The portal vein is patent.  There is attenuation at the portal confluence however the splenic and superior mesenteric veins remain patent.  There is no evidence of vascular pseudo aneurysm.  BONES: There is no evidence of worrisome osseous lesions or acute fracture.  SOFT TISSUES: A left inguinal hernia containing fat is noted.'
);


