    'CT',
    'Chest',
    'CHEST (PORTABLE AP)',
    'TECHNIQUE: Chest PA and lateral  FINDINGS: Single AP view of the abdomen demonstrates the tip of a Dobhoff tube at the level of the diaphragm in similar positioning left of midline when compared to CT dated ___ given the tube was within the stomach at that time, this likely suggests that the tube is now in the distal esophagus or proximal stomach.  Gentle advancement is recommended.  Tip of the right PICC appears at the level of the lower SVC and slightly crosses midline likely due to rotation.  Within the partially imaged lungs, layering bilateral pleural effusions with adjacent atelectasis appear similar.  The heart appears enlarged although this is likely accentuated by low lung volumes.  There are no abnormally dilated loops of bowel within the small or large intestines.  No intraperitoneal free air is seen.'
