VALUES (
    '29167571',
    '11432819-RR-19',
    'MRCP',
    'Abdomen',
    'MRCP (MR ABD W&W/OC)',
    'EXAMINATION: MRCP:  TECHNIQUE: T1- and T2-weighted multiplanar images of the abdomen were acquired in a 1.5 T magnet. Intravenous contrast: 9 mL Prohance. Oral contrast:  1 cc of Gadavist mixed with 50 cc of water was administered for oral contrast.  FINDINGS: Lower Thorax: Small bilateral pleural effusions, right greater than left, new. Abnormal signal within the right lung base may represent atelectasis.  Liver: The liver is normal in size.  There is no evidence of signal dropout on out of phase imaging to suggest diffuse hepatic steatosis.  No focal hepatic lesions are seen.  The portal vein, SMV, and splenic vein are patent.  The portal vein and splenic vein are dilated.  Biliary: The gallbladder is present. There is no intrahepatic or extrahepatic biliary ductal dilatation.  Pancreas: There is decreased intrinsic T1 hyperintense signal diffusely within the pancreatic parenchyma with surrounding fluid signal and stranding.  There is no evidence of pseudoaneurysm and the pancreatic parenchyma enhances uniformly.  The pancreatic duct is not dilated.  T2 hyperintense nonenhancing foci throughout the pancreatic parenchyma are unchanged in location and number compared to the prior MRCP, however some are slightly increased in size from the prior MRCP from ___.  These most likely represent pseudocysts.  The largest is in the head of the pancreas measuring 16 x 15 mm in the coronal plane (7:87), previously 15 x 11 mm.  A smaller lesion in the head/uncinate process measures 11 x 7 mm in the coronal plane on 07:56, previously 6 x 5 mm.  No focal peripancreatic fluid collections are seen.  Spleen: Splenomegaly measuring 14.6 cm, previously 15.5 cm.  The signal intensity is normal. There is no focal lesion seen.  Adrenal Glands: The adrenal glands are normal in shape and size.  Kidneys: The kidneys measure atrophic bilaterally compatible with the history of medical renal disease.T2 hyperintense nonenhancing foci are compatible with cysts.  No suspicious renal lesions are seen.  Gastrointestinal Tract:  The visualized large and small bowel demonstrate normal thickness and caliber.  Lymph Nodes:  There is no lymphadenopathy.  Diffuse mesenteric and retroperitoneal edema.  Vasculature: The abdominal aorta is normal in size.  Osseous and Soft Tissue Structures: No suspicious osseous lesions are seen. Diffuse anasarca.'
);


