troperitoneal or mesenteric lymphadenopathy.  There is no pelvic or inguinal lymphadenopathy.  VASCULAR: There is no abdominal aortic aneurysm.  No atherosclerotic disease is noted.  BONES: There is no evidence of worrisome osseous lesions or acute fracture.  There is transitional vertebral anatomy with sacralization of L5.  SOFT TISSUES: The abdominal and pelvic wall is within normal limits.'
