    'EXAMINATION: CT CHEST W/O CONTRAST:  TECHNIQUE: Contiguous axial MDCT images were obtained through the chest without intravenous contrast material.  DOSE: Total DLP (Body) = 416 mGy-cm. ** Note: This radiation dose report was copied from CLIP ___ (CT ABD AND PELVIS W/O CONTRAST):  FINDINGS:   NECK, THORACIC INLET, AXILLAE, CHEST WALL: The thyroid gland is enlarged with a 2.8 x 3.4 cm hypodense left thyroid nodule (series 2:image 6). The trachea is displaced to the right and mildly narrowed.  There is no axillary lymphadenopathy.  There is no pathologically enlarged supraclavicular lymph node.  UPPER ABDOMEN: Please see the separate report from the abdominal division for findings in the upper abdomen.  MEDIASTINUM: There are no pathologically enlarged mediastinal lymph nodes.  The esophagus is normal in course and caliber, and there is no hiatal hernia.  HILA: There is no hilar lymphadenopathy.  HEART and PERICARDIUM: The heart is normal in size, and there is no significant pericardial effusion.  There is no significant coronary artery calcifications.  The thoracic aorta is normal in course and caliber without aneurysmal dilation.  PLEURA: There is no pleural effusion or pneumothorax.  LUNG:   -PARENCHYMA: Anterior right upper and middle lobe subpleural changes may be due to prior radiation therapy.  The lungs are clear without focal consolidation.  There is mild centrilobular emphysema.  -AIRWAYS: The airways are patent to the subsegmental level.  -VESSELS: The main pulmonary artery is mildly enlarged measuring 3.4 cm in diameter (series 2:image 25).  CHEST CAGE: There is no concerning osseous lesion.'
