    'EXAMINATION: LIVER OR GALLBLADDER US (SINGLE ORGAN):  TECHNIQUE: Grey scale and color Doppler ultrasound images of the abdomen were obtained.  FINDINGS:   LIVER: The liver is diffusely echogenic. The contour of the liver is smooth. There is no focal liver mass.  The main portal vein is patent with hepatopetal flow. There is no ascites.  BILE DUCTS: There is mild intrahepatic biliary dilation in the right hepatic lobe.  CHD: CBD is dilated up to 6 mm.  No evidence of obstructive stones on ultrasound.  7 mm  GALLBLADDER: The patient is status post cholecystectomy.  PANCREAS: The head and body of the pancreas are within normal limits. The tail of the pancreas is not visualized due to the presence of gas.  KIDNEYS: Limited views of the right kidney shows no hydronephrosis.  RETROPERITONEUM: The visualized portions of aorta and IVC are within normal limits.  NOTIFICATION: The findings were discussed with ___. by ___ ___, M.D. on the telephone on ___ at 1:26 am, 1 minutes after discovery of the findings.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
