    'MRCP (MR ABD W&W/OC)',
    'EXAMINATION: MRCP:  TECHNIQUE: T1- and T2-weighted multiplanar images of the abdomen were acquired in a 1.5 T magnet. Intravenous contrast: 8 mL Gadavist. Oral contrast:  1 cc of Gadavist mixed with 50 cc of water was administered for oral contrast.  This examination is limited by use of non breath hold techniques.  FINDINGS: Lower Thorax: Tiny bilateral pleural effusions.  The lung bases are clear.  Heart size normal.  No pericardial effusion.  Liver: There is signal loss on the out of phase sequence as opposed to the in phase sequence, consistent with mild hepatic steatosis.  The liver is homogeneous in signal characteristics.  The liver contours are smooth.  No concerning solid or cystic lesions.  Biliary: No intra- or extra-hepatic duct dilatation.  The common bile duct is within normal limits.  The gallbladder is unremarkable.  No cholelithiasis or choledocholithiasis.  Pancreas:  The pancreas demonstrates fatty atrophy.  There is mild edematous change in the neck and proximal body with peripancreatic standing.  The remainder of the pancreatic parenchyma maintains normal intrinsic hyperintense T1 signal and enhancement pattern.  There are no pancreatic or peripancreatic fluid collections.  A 10 mm cystic lesion in the neck is most in keeping with a side-branch IPMN.  No ductal abnormality is seen.  Spleen: The spleen is normal in size and signal characteristics.  There are no focal lesions.  Adrenal Glands: Normal in size and signal characteristics.  No focal lesions.  Kidneys: The kidneys are normal in size and signal characteristics.  The corticomedullary differentiation is well-maintained with normal excretion of contrast on the delayed phase images.  There are no solid or cystic lesions.  No hydronephrosis or hydroureter.  Gastrointestinal Tract:  The GI tract is of normal caliber throughout.  Lymph Nodes: No significant mesenteric, retroperitoneal or porta hepatis lymphadenopathy by size criteria.  Vasculature:  No splenic vein thrombosis or splenic artery pseudoaneurysm.  The visualized abdominal aorta and proximal mesenteric vessels appear patent without any significant areas of narrowing or dilatation.  Osseous and Soft Tissue Structures: The bone marrow demonstrates normal signal characteristics.  No concerning osseous lesions.'
);


