ormality.  GASTROINTESTINAL: The stomach is unremarkable.  There is mild thickening of small bowel wall in the area anterior to the pancreas, likely a sequela of active ____.  The colon and rectum are within normal limits.  The appendix is normal.  PELVIS: The urinary bladder and distal ureters are unremarkable.  Small amount of free fluid is noted within the pelvis.  REPRODUCTIVE ORGANS: The uterus is lobular.  No adnexal abnormalities are seen.  LYMPH NODES: There is no retroperitoneal or mesenteric lymphadenopathy.  There is no pelvic or inguinal lymphadenopathy.  VASCULAR: There is no abdominal aortic aneurysm.  No atherosclerotic disease is noted.  BONES: There is no evidence of worrisome osseous lesions or acute fracture.  SOFT TISSUES: The abdominal and pelvic wall is within normal limits.'
