INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '26078032',
    '11982995-RR-20',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'EXAMINATION: CT ABDOMEN/PELVIS WITH CONTRAST:  TECHNIQUE: Single phase split bolus contrast: MDCT axial images were acquired through the abdomen and pelvis following intravenous contrast administration with split bolus technique. Oral contrast was administered. Coronal and sagittal reformations were performed and reviewed on PACS.  DOSE: Acquisition sequence:    1) Sequenced Acquisition 9.5 s, 7.6 cm; CTDIvol = 5.8 mGy (Body) DLP = 43.7 mGy-cm.    2) Sequenced Acquisition 0.5 s, 0.4 cm; CTDIvol = 5.7 mGy (Body) DLP = 2.3 mGy-cm.    3) Stationary Acquisition 20.4 s, 0.2 cm; CTDIvol = 347.5 mGy (Body) DLP = 69.5 mGy-cm.    4) Spiral Acquisition 8.0 s, 51.9 cm; CTDIvol = 12.2 mGy (Body) DLP = 623.1 mGy-cm.  Total DLP (Body) = 739 mGy-cm.  FINDINGS:   LOWER CHEST: Minimal atelectasis at the bases.  HEPATOBILIARY: There is a 2 cm indeterminate hypoenhancing lesion within segment 3 (05:10).  Remainder the liver is unremarkable with no biliary ductal dilatation.  Gallbladder is unremarkable.  PANCREAS: Pancreatic divisum present.  There is re-demonstration of a 1.4 cm hypoenhancing lesion with a probable cystic central component at the pancreatic neck with associated upstream mild dilatation of the pancreatic duct measuring up to 0.4 mm.  The radiologic appearance is in keeping with the histologic diagnosis of poorly differentiated adenosquamous carcinoma.  There has been interval development moderate amount peripancreatic fluid tracking along the stomach.  The pancreas itself does not demonstrate enlargement and remains enhancing.  Findings are consistent with acute interstitial ____.  There is an intramural loculated collection along the lesser curvature of the stomach measuring up to 3.3 cm.  SPLEEN: No splenomegaly.  ADRENALS: Unremarkable.  URINARY: Post right nephrectomy.  There is a left interpolar renal cortical hypodensity likely a cyst.  There is no hydronephrosis on the left.  GASTROINTESTINAL: Inflammatory changes extend along the greater and lesser curvatures of the stomach.  There is no bowel obstruction.  There are scattered colonic diverticulosis without diverticulitis.  PERITONEUM: There is small amount of free intraperitoneal air tracking from the pancreatic region.  LYMPH NODES: There is no adenopathy.  VASCULAR: Abdominal aorta is normal in caliber with patent intra-abdominal branches.  There are no acute vascular occlusions are pseudoaneurysms.  There is severe attenuation of the portal vein at its confluence with patent SMV, splenic vein and main portal vein.  PELVIS: Urinary bladder demonstrates a small bladder diverticulum along the posterolateral aspect on the right.  BONES: There are multilevel degenerative changes of the lower thoracic upper lumbar spine with no acute osseous abnormalities or suspicious osseous lesions.  SOFT TISSUES: Soft tissues are unremarkable.'
);


