INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '26078032',
    '11982995-RR-23',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS W/O CONTRAST',
    'EXAMINATION: CT abdomen/pelvis without contrast  STUDY AS PATIENT HAS ONLY ONE KIDNEY AND ___:   TECHNIQUE: Multidetector CT images of the abdomen and pelvis were acquired without intravenous contrast. Non-contrast scan has several limitations in detecting vascular and parenchymal organ abnormalities, including tumor detection. Oral contrast was not administered. Coronal and sagittal reformations were performed and reviewed on PACS.  DOSE: Acquisition sequence:    1) Spiral Acquisition 8.8 s, 57.4 cm; CTDIvol = 20.5 mGy (Body) DLP = 1,164.7 mGy-cm.  Total DLP (Body) = 1,165 mGy-cm.  FINDINGS:   LOWER CHEST: Visualized lung fields are notable for small bilateral non hemorrhagic pleural effusions with associated compressive atelectasis, increased since prior examination.  Heart is normal in size.  Small nonhemorrhagic pericardial effusion has minimally increased in size since prior examination.  Moderate coronary artery calcifications involving the left anterior descending and proximal left circumflex arteries are noted.  ABDOMEN:   HEPATOBILIARY: The liver demonstrates homogeneous attenuation throughout.  There is no evidence of focal lesions within the limitations of an unenhanced scan.  There is no evidence of intrahepatic or extrahepatic biliary dilatation.  The gallbladder is within normal limits.  PANCREAS: There is a focal calcification in the pancreatic tail which is unchanged since ___ can be seen in setting of chronic ____.  Mild pancreatic atrophy noted.  No large lesions within limitations of a nonenhanced scan.  No pancreatic duct dilatation.  Mild peripancreatic fat stranding is again noted and has slightly decreased in conspicuity since ___.  Along the lesser curvature of the gastric cardia there is enlarging 5.1 x 4.7 x 8.4 cm fluid density collection consistent with an acute peripancreatic collection (04:30).  Additional 4.8 x 3.3 cm and 4.7 x 4.3 cm fluid collections are within the left mid mesentery adjacent to and abutting the mesenteric aspect of the distal transverse colon, new since prior examination.  (04:37).  No locules of air within these collections.  SPLEEN: The spleen shows normal size and attenuation throughout, without evidence of focal lesions.  ADRENALS: The right and left adrenal glands are normal in size and shape.  URINARY: Status post right nephrectomy with associated postsurgical changes.The left kidney is of normal size.  A 2 x 1.6 cm cyst is noted along the interpolar region of the left kidney.  No evidence of worrisome renal lesions within the limitations of an unenhanced scan.  There is no hydronephrosis.  There is no nephrolithiasis.  There is no perinephric abnormality.  GASTROINTESTINAL: An enteric feeding tube courses midline with tip within the proximal jejunum.  Small bowel loops demonstrate normal caliber and wall thickness throughout.  Diverticulosis of the sigmoid colon is noted, without evidence of wall thickening and fat stranding.  There is mild fat stranding along the mid and distal transverse colon at the level of the described fluid collections consistent with associated edema within the bowel wall long the anti mesenteric surface (6: 16).  Colon is otherwise unremarkable.  The appendix is not visualized however no secondary signs acute appendicitis.  PELVIS: The urinary bladder and distal ureters are unremarkable.  A 2.8 x 2.2 cm bladder diverticulum is noted adjacent to the right UVJ (4:87).  Moderate nonhemorrhagic pelvic free fluid noted.  REPRODUCTIVE ORGANS: The prostate and seminal vesicles are normal.  LYMPH NODES: There is no retroperitoneal or mesenteric lymphadenopathy.  There is no pelvic or inguinal lymphadenopathy.  VASCULAR: There is no abdominal aortic aneurysm.  Mild atherosclerotic disease is noted.  BONES: There is no evidence of worrisome osseous lesions or acute fracture.  SOFT TISSUES: Few locules of gas within left anterior subcutaneous tissues with associated fat stranding is most consistent with injection granulomas.  Mild diffuse anasarca noted.  The abdominal and pelvic wall is otherwise within normal limits.  NOTIFICATION: The findings were discussed with ___, M.D. by ___ ___, M.D. on the telephone on ___ at 9:44 pm, 10 minutes after discovery of the findings.'
);


