    'Chest',
    'CHEST (PORTABLE AP)',
    'SUPINE PORTABLE CHEST RADIOGRAPH: Comparison is made to ___, and ___, exams.  Elevation of the left hemidiaphragm persists with regions of adjacent probable compression atelectasis.  No new consolidation, pneumothorax, pulmonary edema, or large effusions are identified.  Configuration of the cardiomediastinal silhouette is stable as are post surgical changes from prior median sternotomy and CABG.'
