    'TYPE OF EXAMINATION: Chest AP portable single view.  FINDINGS: Single view of the chest obtained with patient in upright position is analyzed in direct comparison with a preceding similar study of ___.  Previously described PICC line in unchanged position terminating in the mid SVC.  Heart size unchanged and within normal limits.  No pulmonary vascular congestion.  No signs of acute infiltrates.  Evidence of pneumoperitoneum persists.'
