);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '28627153',
    '10207476-RR-76',
    'CT',
    'Chest',
    'CT CHEST W/O CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT-acquired axial imaging of the chest was performed without IV contrast.  5-mm and 1-mm axial reconstructions in sagittal and coronal reformations were performed.  FINDINGS: The previously seen scattered ground-glass opacities, predominantly within the right lung have resolved.  However, new focal opacities, to a much lesser extent than previous, are seen within the right upper lobe in the azygoesophageal recess and along the medial anterior right lower lobe abutting the fissure and mediastinum (5:180).  There is diffuse acute dilatation of the airways with several areas of mucoid impaction as well as bronchial wall thickening bilaterally.  There are no discrete pulmonary nodules.  There are small bilateral pleural effusions, left greater than right, the left has slightly increased in size since ___.  There is no pericardial effusion or lymphadenopathy.  A new right main coronary artery stent has been placed.  This examination was not tailored for subdiaphragmatic evaluation.  Limited views of the upper abdomen demonstrate new ascites.  Layering gallstones are noted.  The remainder of the upper abdomen is unremarkable.  There is extensive worsened anasarca.  There are no osseous lesions suspicious for malignancy.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '28627153',
    '10207476-RR-78',
    'CT',
    'Chest',
    'CHEST (PORTABLE AP)',
    'FINDINGS: In comparison with the study of ___, there is increasing opacification at the left base silhouetting the hemidiaphragm.  Although this could be a technical artifact, in view of the clinical history, the possibility of developing left lower lobe pneumonia must be seriously considered.  If the condition of the patient permits, a lateral view would be most helpful.  Right lung remains clear.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '28627153',
    '10207476-RR-79',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABDOMEN W/O CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT-acquired axial images were obtained through the abdomen and pelvis with oral contrast only.  Intravenous contrast was withheld due to history of contrast allergy.  Coronal and sagittal reformations were evaluated.  CT OF THE ABDOMEN WITH ORAL CONTRAST: Included portions of the lung bases display interval development of a small simple left pleural effusion with adjacent compressive atelectasis and stable appearance to known coronary artery calcifications.  Unenhanced images of the liver, spleen, stomach, small bowel, pancreas, adrenal glands, and kidneys are unremarkable.  There is unchanged appearance to likely hyperdense biliary sludge and small gallstones noted within the gallbladder which is not significantly distended.  No intra-abdominal free fluid, free air, or pathologically enlarged lymph nodes are identified.  CT OF THE PELVIS WITH ORAL CONTRAST ONLY: In the interval, the patient has underwent a diverting colostomy which exists in a lower left paramidline location.  There is extensive colonic diverticulosis again noted, but no findings to suggest ____.  Contrast has not yet reached the large bowel and into the colostomy at the time of examination.  Oral contrast remains within the ___ pouch.  A large and likely multiloculated fluid collection is noted to extend from the midline lower pelvis, adjacent to chain sutures into the upper left abdomen.  Given its extension through the pelvis into the upper abdomen exact size measurements are difficult but it measures approximately 7 x 8 x 14 cm (300B:56 and 301B:17).  Additional smaller components of fluid are noted to track into the right anterior pelvic cavity as well.  Inflammation of the pericolonic fat and omentum is not unexpected given recent surgery.  Air is noted within the urinary bladder, likely related to recent instrumentation. No pathologically enlarged inguinal or pelvic sidewall lymph nodes are identified.  Mild anasarca is noted.  BONE WINDOWS: No malignant-appearing osseous lesions are identified. Multilevel degenerative changes within the spine are again noted.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '28627153',
    '10207476-RR-80',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT PERITINEAL DRAIN EXCLUDING APPENDICEAL',
    'CT-GUIDED PELVIC ABSCESS DRAINAGE:   PROCEDURE: Procedure and its complications were explained.  Informed consent obtained.  Laboratory values checked, INR was initially elevated, fresh frozen plasma was used to lower this to 1.5.  The patient is also on aspirin and Plavix, which could not be discontinued because of the cardiac considerations. It was decided to proceed with the CT-guided abscess drainage.  Timeout was performed.  Area of interest was localized under CT fluoroscopy.  The skin was prepped and draped in the usual manner.  1% lidocaine used for local anesthetic.  Conscious sedation was also used.  Under CT fluoroscopic guidance, a 10 ___ ___ catheter was placed in the left pericolic abscess.  Approximately 30 cc of thick pus were aspirated.  Specimen has been sent for microbiology and cell count.  Patient tolerated the procedure well.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '28627153',
    '10207476-RR-82',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABDOMEN W/O CONTRAST',
    'EXAMINATION: CT of the abdomen and pelvis.  TECHNIQUE: MDCT-acquired axial images from the lung bases to the pubic symphysis were obtained with the administration of oral contrast only. Coronal and sagittal reformations were obtained.  Intravenous contrast was withheld secondary to allergic reaction in the past to iodinated contrast.  FINDINGS: CT OF THE ABDOMEN WITH ORAL CONTRAST ONLY:  There is a stable appearance of a moderate left pleural effusion with associated atelectatic changes at the left base.  There is a minimal right pleural effusion.  No pulmonary nodules or opacities are seen.  The liver, spleen, pancreas, both adrenal glands, both kidneys, both ureters, visualized portions of small bowel are unremarkable.  The gallbladder demonstrates mild gallbladder wall edema with a dependent gallstone.  There is no intra- abdominal free air, free fluid, or mesenteric or retroperitoneal lymphadenopathy.  There is a small 2- x 1-cm fluid collection seen in the mesentery best seen on image (2:19) that is unchanged from prior examination from ___ and is not in a location amenable for drainage.  CT OF THE PELVIS WITHOUT INTRAVENOUS CONTRAST: There has been interval placement of a pigtail catheter with tip within a left paracolic fluid collection with interval decrease in size in the fluid collection which now measures approximately 16 x 64 mm.  In addition there is a secondary fluid collection which demonstrates an interval decrease in size superior to the larger left paracolic fluid collection.  There is a third fluid collection in the right paracolic gutter adjacent to right sided loops of small bowel that measures approximately 45 x 21 mm that appears to have been present on previous examinations from ___ dating back to ___. This collection has an area of high attenuation that likely represents entrapped contrast from prior known contrast extravasation secondary to sigmoid perforation. There is a general haziness of the mesentery that is related to either post-operative changes or proximity to above mentioned inflammatory collections.  Patient is status post diverting colostomy with a ___ pouch.  Again noted is extensive colonic diverticulosis without evidence of ____. The bladder, uterus are unremarkable.  There is no pelvic or inguinal lymphadenopathy.  BONE WINDOWS: There are no suspicious or sclerotic lesions identified.  Again noted are multilevel degenerative changes within the spine.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '28627153',
    '10207476-RR-84',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABDOMEN W/O CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: Axial MDCT images were obtained from the lung bases to the pubic symphysis without intravenous contrast.  Coronal and sagittal reformatted images are provided.  CONTRAST: Oral contrast only. This examination was performed ___ and is submitted for dictation on ___ as the original report was lost.  CT OF THE ABDOMEN WITHOUT INTRAVENOUS CONTRAST: At the imaged portion of the lung bases, coronary artery stents and calcifications are noted.  Low density bilateral pleural effusions, left greater than right, are noted and slightly increased on the left and new on the right since ___.  Adjacent atelectasis in the left lower lobe and to a lesser extent right lower lobe are noted.  There is minimal atelectasis in the lingula.  The liver is mildly hypodense suggesting fatty infiltration.  Hyperdensity within the gallbladder lumen likely represents a combination of stones and sludge.  The gallbladder is nondistended.  The spleen, pancreas, and adrenal glands appear unremarkable.  There is mild prominence of the common bile duct which measures 7 mm in the pancreatic head, probably slightly increased from previous when it measured approximately 5 mm although the duct is visualized to the level of the ampulla with no definite obstructing mass seen on this non-contrast CT. Compared with the most recent previous study of ___, minimal prominence of the renal collecting systems bilaterally and slight prominence of the proximal left ureter is unchanged.  Focal ectasia of the abdominal aorta up to 2.5 cm is unchanged.  The patient is status post diverting colostomy in the left lower quadrant with ___ pouch.  A collection in the left paracolic gutter is being drained by a percutaneous pigtail catheter which enters via the left flank.  The tip of the catheter is well positioned within the collection, which has decreased minimally in size (2.4 x 6.1 cm, previously 2.6 x 6.9 cm, 2: 63).  A small amount of air within the collection is consistent with the presence of the percutaneous catheter.  The inferior U-shaped extent of the collection which is located adjacent to the blind end of the ___ pouch, is approximately unchanged in size.  A small collection in the right paracolic gutter containing hyperdense material measures 3.5 x 2.2 cm, not significantly changed.  No new collections are identified.  Oral contrast passes throughout the entire bowel and is seen within the ostomy bag.  There is diverticulosis of the sigmoid colon to the level of the colostomy with mild wall thickening in the most distal segment.  Mesenteric stranding is unchanged.  CT OF THE PELVIS WITHOUT INTRAVENOUS CONTRAST: Contrast has been placed within the ___ pouch.  The pouch is well opacified without evidence of leak of contrast material into the fluid collection adjacent to its stump. Tiny foci of hyperdensity within this collection (2: 70) are unchanged in appearance from the previous study.  No new collections are identified in the pelvis.  Diffuse subcutaneous stranding is unchanged.  BONE WINDOWS: Degenerative changes are noted without lesions worrisome for osseous metastatic disease.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
