    'PELVIC ULTRASOUND: Transabdominal and transvaginal ultrasound were performed, the latter for better visualization of the ovaries/adnexa.  The uterus measures 9.0 x 3.8 x 5.5 cm, normal in size and shape for the patient''s age. The endometrium measures 2 mm and appears normal.  However, in the endometrial cavity to the right of midline, a 1.3 x 1.3 x 1.1 cm round slightly hyperechoic structure is seen without demonstrated vascularity.  There is no evidence of vascularized retained products of conception.  The right ovary measures 3.2 x 2.4 x 3.3 cm, and the left ovary measures 2.6 x 1.9 x 2.7 cm.  There is normal arterial and venous flow to both ovaries.  A small amount of pelvic free fluid is noted.'
