INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '22612249',
    '10335293-RR-76',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS W/O CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: Axial MDCT images were  obtained through the abdomen and pelvis without IV or oral contrast.  Sagittal and coronal reconstructions were generated.  FINDINGS: Lung bases are clear.  There is no pleural or pericardial effusion.  CT OF THE ABDOMEN: Evaluation of solid abdominal viscera is limited by lack of IV contrast. The liver is homogeneous and no focal liver lesions are seen. The gallbladder, spleen, pancreas and adrenal glands are unremarkable. No stones are seen in the kidneys or ureters.     Note is made of a small hiatal hernia.  The stomach, duodenum and small bowel are otherwise grossly unremarkable.  There is stranding and wall thickening of the mid to distal sigmoid colon, most compatible with ____.  Adjacent tiny locules of gas are concerning for microperforation.  There is no extraluminal fluid collection.  Increased fullness of the left renal pelvis is likely due to mass effect from the aforementioned inflammatory changes.  The appendix is not clearly visualized but there is no evidence of appendicitis.  The intra-abdominal aorta demonstrates significant atherosclerotic calcifications. The aorta is of normal diameter. Vessel patency cannot be evaluated in this examination.   There is no retroperitoneal or mesenteric lymph node enlargement by CT size criteria.  CT OF THE PELVIS: The urinary bladder and terminal ureters are normal.  No pelvic or inguinal lymph node enlargement is seen.  OSSESOUS STRUCTURES: No blastic or lytic lesion suspicious for malignancy is present. There is scoliosis of the lumbar spine. Severe degenerative changes are seen in the lumbar spine.  There is a new compression deformity of the superior endplate of the T12 vertebral body.'
);


