INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '28967154',
    '10414036-RR-58',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT axial images were acquired from the liver to pubic symphysis after the uneventful administration of 130 mL of Omnipaque.  Coronal sagittal reformations were provided and reviewed.  DLP: 474.83 mGy/cm.  FINDINGS: Bibasilar atelectasis is noted in the imaged lower lungs.  There is no pleural effusion or pneumothorax.   Abdomen:  There are at least 6 discrete liver lesions, new from prior. These appear centrally hypodense with internal septations, and there is mild peripheral enhancement. The larger of these measure: 3.4 x 3.2 cm in segment ___, 2.5 x 2.4 cm (2:13) at the dome of the liver and 2.1 x 2.1 cm (2:22) in segment 7. This finding is concerning for metastasis, though abscess is a less favored consideration. A linear hypodensity abutting one of these lesions is seen on series 2, images ___, could reflect a thrombosed hepatic vein branch. The portal vein, splenic vein, SMV and IMV are patent. There is no portal venous or IMV gas. The aorta is unremarkable.  The spleen, pancreas and left adrenal gland are normal.  A left adrenal lesion is unchanged from ___ but increased in size from ___, currently measuring 2.6 x 2.5 cm. Please note, based on prior CT from ___, this lesion has been characterized as an adrenal adenoma. There is a small hiatal hernia.  The stomach and small bowel are normal.   The patient is status post a partial left nephrectomy.  Multiple hypodensities within both kidneys have increased in size and number from ___.  The largest on the right measures 3.6 cm and the largest on the left measures 2.1 cm.  While the majority of these appear to be simple cysts, several are hyperdense centrally such as a left renal lesion seen on series 2, image 35 measuring 1.8 x 1.4 cm - new from ___ CT. There is no hydronephrosis.  Both kidneys enhance symmetrically and excrete contrast promptly.  Fat stranding seen around the right kidney has increased but is non-specific.  There is no free air.    Pelvis: A small hernia containing nonobstructed large bowel is seen along the left flank and is unchanged, likely an incisional hernia relating to prior left partial nephrectomy. There is no bowel obstruction. Extensive inflammatory fat stranding and bowel wall thickening is seen involving the sigmoid colon.  A rim enhancing fluid collection superior to the bladder and abutting the uterus measures 4.2 x 1 cm (S601b: 28).  Another extra-luminal collection superior and lateral to the sigmoid measures 3.6 x 2.5 cm (___) - this ocllection contains gas and appears to communicate through a small neck with the sigmoid lumen ((2:67). Findings are concerning for a contained perforation secondary to ____ though perforation in the setting of colonic neoplasm is also a consideration.  There is a 1 cm adjacent lymph node (2:62).  There is no free air.  The appendix is not visualized. The bladder is normal without evidence of colovesical fistula.     The rectum is normal.  There is trace free pelvic fluid.  There is no definite pelvic lymphadenopathy.  Bones:  There are no concerning lytic or blastic osseous lesions.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '28967154',
    '10414036-RR-60',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'US ABD LIMIT, SINGLE ORGAN',
    'TYPE OF THE EXAM: Ultrasound of the right upper quadrant with intent of finding a hepatic lesion for aspiration and potential biopsy.  TECHNIQUE: Multiple grayscale images through the right upper quadrant were obtained with a curvilinear transducer.  Multiple hypoechoic lesions through the liver were seen.  A superficial right hepatic lobe lesion was selected for biopsy.  An 18-gauge spinal needle was advanced into the right hepatic lobe lesion under ultrasound guidance via a right lateral intercostal approach and 4 cc of frank pus was aspirated.  Please see dedicated procedure note under CT fluoroscopy-guided placement of a drainage catheter performed on the same day.  The patient tolerated the procedure well with no immediate complication.  Estimated blood loss was less than 2 mL.  Dr. ___ attending radiologist, was present throughout the entire procedure.  Post-procedure instructions were written in the ___ medical record.'
);


