INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '23162159',
    '10456934-RR-13',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: Contiguous axial MDCT images were obtained through the abdomen and pelvis after the administration of IV contrast.  Sagittal and coronal reformatted images were obtained and reviewed.  FINDINGS:   LUNG BASES: The base of the lungs are clear without consolidations, nodules, or pleural effusions.  The base of the heart is unremarkable.  ABDOMEN: The liver is normal in shape and contour.  There are no focal hepatic masses.  The portal vein is patent.  There is no intra- or extra-hepatic biliary duct dilation.  The gallbladder is unremarkable without evidence of stones or sludge.  The spleen is normal.  The pancreas, adrenal glands, and kidneys are unremarkable.  There are no focal renal masses.  There is no evidence of hydronephrosis.  The kidneys enhance and excrete contrast appropriately.  There is no abdominal or mesenteric lymphadenopathy.  The abdominal vasculature is normal in course and caliber.  The small bowel is unremarkable without evidence of obstruction or inflammatory changes.  PELVIS: In the sigmoid colon, there is a region of wall thickening, stranding, and an inflamed diverticulum (2, 63), which is consistent with ____.  There is a 2.2 x 1.5 cm irregular locule of free air in the mesentery adjacent to this region of ____.  There is no drainable collection.  The remainder of the colon is notable for scattered diverticulosis without evidence of other regions of ____.  The patient is status post an appendectomy.  The bladder and prostate are unremarkable.  There is no pelvic or inguinal lymphadenopathy.  There is no free fluid or abscess in the pelvis.  Small fat umbilical hernia noted.  OSSEOUS STRUCTURES: There are no concerning lytic or sclerotic bone lesions.  Degenerative changes are noted at L5-S1 with disc space narrowing, endplate sclerosis, and a small disc bulge.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '20729231',
    '10548564-RR-27',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT axial imaging was obtained through the abdomen and pelvis following the administration of intravenous contrast material.  Coronal and sagittal reformats were completed.  CT ABDOMEN/PELVIS WITH CONTRAST:  The visualized heart and pericardium are unremarkable.  A small granuloma at the right lung base is stable from prior exam.  There is minimal atelectasis at the right lung base.  There is no pleural effusion.  There is a large hiatal hernia.  The liver enhances homogenously without any focal lesions. There is no intra or extra-hepatic biliary dilitation.  The portal vein is patent.  The gallbladder, pancreas, and spleen are unremarkable.  The kidneys enhance and excrete contrast symmetrically without evidence of hydronephrosis.  There are small hypodensities in the left kidney that are too small to characterize but stable from prior exam.  The adrenal glands are unremarkable. The stomach and small bowel are unremarkable except for a stable duodenal diverticulum. There is mild atherosclerotic disease of the abdominal aorta.  There is a large amount of pneumoperitoneum.  Evaluation of the colon demonstrates multiple sigmoid diverticula with stranding adjacent to a diverticulum in the proximal sigmoid colon consistent with acute ____. Image ___:31 shows what most likely represents the offending diverticulum.  There is no evidence of abscess, colovesicular fistula or thrombophlebitis.  The appendix is visualized and is normal.   There is no mesenteric or retroperitoneal lymphadenopathy.   The bladder is unremarkable without intravesicular air.  The visualized rectum, uterus, and right ovary are unremarkable.  The left ovary shows mild loss of fat plane between the ovary and the colon.  There is no free fluid within the abdomen or pelvis.  OSSEOUS STRUCTURES: There are no suspicious lytic or sclerotic lesions seen.  There are mild degenerative changes in the lumbar spine.'
);


