INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '20729231',
    '10548564-RR-34',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT PELVIS W/O CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT-acquired axial images were obtained through the pelvis without oral or IV contrast.  Coronal and sagittal reformations were prepared.  FINDINGS: Imaged small bowel is unremarkable.  Proximal large bowel is normal with thickening of the lower portion of the sigmoid colon as it passes over the left adnexa.  Residual contrast is seen within the distal colon. Though no active extravasation of intraluminal contrast is seen, there is a collection of air and fluid surrounding the uterus, both dependently between the uterus and bladder as well as wrapping around to the right and superior to the uterus.  The dependent collection measures 6.4 x 1.9 cm and the likely contiguous superior collection measures 4.7 x 2.0.  These collections do not appear at the current time to be matured abscesses but rather are simply the dependent pooling of expelled air and fluid from the sigmoid colon.  There is no pathologic adenopathy seen with normal-appearing bladder and uterus otherwise. The rectum is normal.  There is no inguinal adenopathy.  Soft tissues are unremarkable with the exception of air in the anterior abdominal wall soft tissues, likely from injection.  OSSEOUS STRUCTURES: There is no lytic or sclerotic bony lesion concerning for osseous malignant process.'
);


