    'PORTABLE UPRIGHT CHEST, ONE VIEW: Cardiomediastinal and hilar contours are normal.  Lungs are clear without focal consolidation or pulmonary edema. There is no pleural effusion.  Osseous structures are unremarkable.  There is no evidence of free intraperitoneal air.'
