INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '20918942',
    '10875567-RR-14',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABDOMEN W/CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT-acquired axial images were obtained through the abdomen and pelvis with intravenous and oral contrast.  Coronal and sagittal reformations were evaluated.  CT OF THE ABDOMEN WITH INTRAVENOUS AND ORAL CONTRAST: Limited evaluation of lung bases is unremarkable.  There is no pleural or pericardial effusion. Visualized breast parenchyma appears normal.  The liver, gallbladder, spleen, stomach, small bowel, adrenal glands, and kidneys appear unremarkable.  A 7mm hypoattenuating pancreatic body lesion is noted.  No pathologically enlarged lymph nodes or free air is noted within the abdominal cavity.  CT OF THE PELVIS WITH INTRAVENOUS AND ORAL CONTRAST: There is marked wall thickening involving the entire descending colon but predominantly just distal to the splenic flexure with associated stranding of the adjacent fat and thickening of the adjacent fascial planes.  Small amount of free fluid is also noted within the left paracolic gutter and there appears to be a small contained microperforation (2:26 and 301B:55).  No focal fluid collection or drainable abscess is identified and there is no evidence of bowel obstruction. The remaining large bowel including the appendix appears unremarkable.  Uterus is slightly enlarged but likely within normal limits given recent pregnancy and a small 17 x 26 mm hypoattenuating lesion within the uterine fundus is likely post-surgical in nature.  The adnexa appear unremarkable.  No free fluid is noted within the cul-de-sac.  No pathologically enlarged inguinal or pelvic sidewall lymph nodes are identified.  BONE WINDOWS: No malignant-appearing osseous lesions are identified.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '26399211',
    '10892159-RR-54',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT axial images were obtained from the dome of the liver to the pubic symphysis after the administration of IV contrast.  Coronal and sagittal reformations were provided and reviewed.  DLP: 449.47 mGy-cm.  ABDOMEN: The visualized bases of the lungs are clear.  There is no pleural effusion or pneumothorax.  The imaged portion of the heart is normal.  There is no pericardial effusion.  The liver enhances homogeneously without focal lesions.  The gallbladder is normal and there is no intrahepatic biliary ductal dilatation.  The spleen and pancreas are unremarkable.  There is slight fullness to the right adrenal gland, unchanged from prior exam.  The kidneys enhance symmetrically and excrete contrast without hydronephrosis.  There is no retroperitoneal or mesenteric lymphadenopathy.  No free air or free fluid is seen.  The abdominal aorta and its major branches are unremarkable.  Incidental note is made of a low lying, retroaortic left renal vein.  Multiple diverticula are seen scattered throughout the colon with fat stranding seen near the ascending colon.  There is no extraluminal air or fluid collection.  PELVIS: The bladder and rectum are normal.  At least one fibroid, measuring 4 cm is seen within the uterus.  The appendix is not visualized.  There is no inguinal or pelvic lymphadenopathy.  BONES: There are no suspicious osseous lesions.  Minor degenerative changes of the lower lumbar spine are marked by anterior osteophytosis, particularly at L5.  Small posterior disc bulges are seen at L3-L4 through L5-S1.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '26779520',
    '10895299-RR-49',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABDOMEN W/CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT-acquired axial images were obtained from the lung bases to the pubic symphysis after the administration of 130 mL of Optiray intravenous contrast and oral contrast.  Coronal and sagittal reformatted images were also displayed.  FINDINGS: The lungs bases demonstrate a 4 mm pulmonary nodule at the right lung base. The heart size is within normal limits. There is a small hypodensity in the right lobe of the liver (2:13), which measures 9 x 7 mm and is too small to characterize but unchanged since the prior study. There is mild intrahepatic biliary dilatation which was not seen on the previous study. The patient is status post cholecystectomy.  The common bile duct is dilated and measures up to 13 mm and is more dilated than on the previous study. The pancreas, adrenal glands, kidneys, spleen, stomach, and abdominal loops of bowel are within normal limits. Retroperitoneal and mesenteric lymph nodes are seen, none meeting CT criteria for pathologic enlargement.  There is no free air or free fluid.  CT OF THE PELVIS WITH IV AND ORAL CONTRAST: The rectum and bladder are within normal limits.  The uterus is absent.  The patient is status post ileocecal resection with surgical suture material seen at the prior resection site.  The distal ileum demonstrates minimal wall thickening which was apparent on the previous study of ___.  There are no significant associated inflammatory changes around this site. There is no pelvic or inguinal lymphadenopathy.  BONE WINDOWS: No suspicious osseous lesions are identified.'
);


