INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '27371462',
    '11182240-RR-16',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABDOMEN W/CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT images from the abdomen and pelvis were obtained after administration of IV contrast.  Coronal and sagittal reconstructions were generated.  CT OF THE ABDOMEN WITH IV CONTRAST: Partially visualized lungs are clear, without consolidation, mass or pleural effusion.  Partially visualized heart and pericardium appear unremarkable.  The liver enhances homogeneously, with small hypodensities at the left lobe (2:12) measuring 5 mm and 12 mm (2:13), too small to fully characterize. There is mild left sided intrahepatic biliary dilatation, with a biliary stent seen within the left hepatic duct extending into the common bile duct and duodenum. The CBD measures up to 10 mm, which is dilated.  Intra-abdominal vasculature is normal.  Spleen, pancreas, stomach, gallbladder and small bowel appear unremarkable.  There is a 10-mm right adrenal lesion(2:13), not fully characterized on this study. The left adrenal gland is normal.  Descending aorta with diffuse atherosclerotic disease.  The kidneys enhance and excrete contrast symmetrically, without evidence of hydronephrosis or mass.  There is no lymphadenopathy.  Tiny sub-cm hypodensity in left kidney is too small to fully characterize. There is no free air or free fluid.  A duplicated IVC is incidentally noted.  CT OF THE PELVIS WITH IV CONTRAST: The bladder, distal ureters, right adnexa, appendix are unremarkable.  There is a calcifed fibroid in the uterus. Left adnexal mass has been previously evaluated on MR from ___. Focal segment of sigmoid colon demonstrates mild circumferential wall thickening, mucosal enhancement, and pericolonic fat stranding (2:60), with multiple small inflamed diverticula noted in this region. No abscess or perforation present, and no bowel obstruction seen.  OSSEOUS STRUCTURES: Degenerative changes are seen throughout the thoracolumbar spine. L1 vertebral compression deformity (301:35) is unchanged when compared to study of ___ plain radiograph.'
);


