)
VALUES (
    '24649986',
    '11215260-RR-17',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABDOMEN W/CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT axial images were acquired from the lung bases through the pubic symphysis following administration of 130 mL of Optiray IV contrast.  Multiplanar reformatted images were generated.  CT ABDOMEN WITH IV CONTRAST: There is minimal atelectasis at the lung bases.  The lung bases are otherwise clear.  Free intraperitoneal air is present throughout the abdomen, with the largest amount anterior to the liver.  There are no focal hepatic lesions.  The gallbladder appears normal.  The spleen is normal in size.  The pancreas enhances homogeneously.  The kidneys enhance and excrete contrast normally.  The adrenals are unremarkable. The abdominal aorta is normal in caliber.  The proximal celiac, superior mesenteric, renal and inferior mesenteric arteries are patent.  Multiple enlarged mesenteric lymph nodes measure up to 11 mm in greatest transverse dimension, with surrounding mestenteric stranding.  Multiple retroperitoneal lymph nodes are seen, not meeting size criteria for pathologic enlargement.  The small bowel measures up to 3 cm in diameter and is fluid-filled throughout.  There is no free fluid in the abdomen.  There is no discrete transition point of the small bowel.  The appendix is at the upper limts of normal to slightly enlarged in size (7mm in diameter).    There are multiple colonic diverticula.  Focal wall thickening and pericolonic stranding is seen along the proximal sigmoid colon consistent with acute ____.  There are small locules of free air adjacent to area of inflamed sigmoid.  CT PELVIS WITH CONTRAST: There is excreted contrast in the urinary bladder.  The prostate, seminal vesicles and rectum are unremarkable.  There are no drainable collections within the abdomen or pelvis.  There are no osseous lesions concerning for malignancy.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
