)
VALUES (
    '23782753',
    '11488639-RR-15',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABDOMEN W/CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: Post-contrast axial images were obtained through the abdomen and pelvis.  Multiplanar reformatted images were generated.  CT ABDOMEN WITH IV CONTRAST: Lung bases are clear without consolidation or pleural effusion.  There is no pericardial effusion.  In the abdomen, the liver, gallbladder, pancreas, spleen, adrenal glands, stomach and duodenum are unremarkable.  The kidneys enhance and excrete contrast symmetrically without hydronephrosis, stones or renal masses.  The abdominal aorta and its major branches are normal.  There is no free air or free fluid in the abdomen.  CT PELVIS WITH IV CONTRAST: A 6-cm segment of descending colon at the splenic flexure demonstrates asymmetric wall thickening and edema and pronounced pericolonic inflammatory changes extending posteriorly.  There are scattered diverticula in this region, although an inflamed diverticulum at the ___ the inflammatory change is not definitively seen.  There is no extraluminal air or evidence of abscess.  The remainder of the large and small bowel is normal in appearance, without wall thickening, surrounding inflammatory changes or mesenteric hyperemia.  The appendix is normal.  Small bowel is normal in caliber.  A small amount of fluid tracks within the mesentery, particularly along the left abdomen and pelvis.  The urinary bladder, distal ureters, uterus and adnexa are unremarkable.  There is a small amount of intermediate density fluid layering dependently in the pelvis is seen.  There is no pelvic or inguinal lymphadenopathy by size criteria.  OSSEOUS STRUCTURES: There is no fracture or worrisome bony lesion.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '25841363',
    '11559338-RR-21',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABDOMEN W/CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT-acquired axial images were obtained through the abdomen and pelvis after administration of 130 ml IV Optiray contrast.  Coronal and sagittal reformats were displayed.  CT ABDOMEN WITH IV CONTRAST: There is dependent subsegmental atelectasis, but the lung bases are otherwise clear.  Soft tissue density and coarse calcifications are noted in the right breast which is incompletely imaged.  Visualized portion of the heart is unremarkable.  the liver, gallbladder, pancreas, spleen and bilateral adrenal glands are normal.  The kidneys enhance and excrete contrast symmetrically without evidence of hydronephrosis or hydroureter.  The nonopacified stomach and intra-abdominal loops of small bowel are normal.  There is mild focal wall thickening of the cecum with minimal associated fat stranding, but the remainder of the colon is unremarkable.  There is are scatter diverticula of the cecum. The appendix is normal.  There is no free air or fluid in the abdomen.  No mesenteric or retroperitoneal lymphadenopathy meeting CT criteria for pathologic enlargement is noted.  There is atherosclerotic calcification of the aorta which is of normal caliber throughout.  CT PELVIS WITH IV CONTRAST: The urinary bladder, distal ureters, uterus, sigmoid colon and rectum are normal.  There is a 4.6 x 3.0 cm hypodense cystic structure in the right adnexa.  The left adnexa demonstrates a 1.7 x 1.5 cm cystic structure.  There is no free fluid in the pelvis.  No pelvic or inguinal lymphadenopathy is noted.  BONE WINDOWS: No suspicious lytic or sclerotic osseous lesions identified.  There is multilevel degenerative change of the thoracolumbar spine.'
);


