INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '29866181',
    '11574089-RR-16',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABDOMEN W/CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT-acquired axial images were obtained through the abdomen and pelvis after administration of 130 cc IV Optiray contrast.  Coronal and sagittal reformats were displayed and essential in delineating the anatomy and pathology.  CT ABDOMEN / PELVIS WITH IV CONTRAST:  The lung bases are clear without focal opacity, mass, or pleural effusion.  There is a significant amount of free intraperitoneal air with the largest pocket in the anterior abdomen.  Small locules of gas are noted in the deep pelvis where and in the sigmoid mesentery (2:63). There are two small fluid collections measuring approximately 2.7 cm and 1.7 cm. There is some mild mesenteric stranding and thickening of the sigmoid wall.  In the setting of multiple sigmoid diverticula, these findings are most suggestive of acute perforated ____.  The liver demonstrates homogenous enhancement.  There is no intrahepatic biliary ductal dilatation.  The common bile duct is dilated up to 1 cm which is not significantly changed from ERCP of ___.  The gallbladder is not seen. The pancreas, spleen, and bilateral adrenal glands are unremarkable. The kidneys enhance and excrete contrast symmetrically without evidence of hydronephrosis or hydroureter.  There is a low-density 1.9-cm lesion that appears to be arising from the interpolar region of the right kidney, likely simple exophytic cyst.  There are extensive atherosclerotic calcifications of the abdominal aorta which is of normal caliber throughout. Non-opacified stomach and intra-abdominal loops of small bowel are unremarkable.  The urinary bladder, distal ureters, uterus, adnexa, and rectum are unremarkable.  There is no pelvic or inguinal lymphadenopathy meeting criteria for pathologic enlargement.  Multiple calcified granulomas are noted in the bilateral buttocks.  BONE WINDOWS: No suspicious lytic or sclerotic osseous lesion is identified. Mild multilevel degenerative change of thoracolumbar spine is seen.  There has been prior right total hip replacement which is incompletely evaluated but unremarkable.'
);


