INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '20534897',
    '11644013-RR-51',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS W & W/O CONTRAST, ADDL SECTIONS',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT axial images were obtained through the abdomen and pelvis with and without the administration of IV contrast.  Multiplanar reformats were generated and reviewed.  FINDINGS:   CT OF THE ABDOMEN: The visualized lung bases show mild opacification of the left lung base which may represent atelectasis versus infection in the correct clinical setting.  The liver, spleen, pancreas, bilateral adrenal glands appear unremarkable.  Gallstones are noted; however, gallbladder wall appears unremarkable.  Subcentimeter hypodensities in bilateral kidneys are too small to characterize but likely represent renal cysts.  Intra-abdominal loops of small bowel are within normal limits.  CT OF THE PELVIS: The bladder, distal ureters, rectum and sigmoid colon are unremarkable.  There is evidence of sigmoid diverticulosis with surrounding fat stranding.  Adjacent locule of gas and small 12mm focal fluid collection (604b, 36 and 4,82) likely represents small nondrainable abscess or contained perforation.   There is no free fluid within the abdomen.  Retroperitoneal and mesenteric lymph nodes do not meet CT size criteria for pathologic enlargement.  Extensive atherosclerotic changes are noted within the abdominal aorta and its branches.  No lytic or sclerotic osseous lesions are identified.  Multilevel degenerative changes are noted.'
);


