INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '20534897',
    '11644013-RR-54',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABD & PELVIS WITH CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT helical images were acquired through the abdomen and pelvis after administration of oral and 130 cc of Optiray intravenous contrast.  Sagittal and coronal reformats were generated and reviewed.  FINDINGS: A small-moderate amount of new intra-abdominal free air is seen, consistent with perforated sigmoid ____.  Again seen is diffuse fat stranding and mild wall thickening of a short segment of sigmoid colon, with no significant interval change since the prior study.  Previously seen pelvic 12-mm fluid collection has resolved and no drainable fluid collections are seen in the current study.  Small amount of fluid tracks along the left paracolic gutter.    The liver, spleen, adrenal glands, and pancreas are normal.  The gallbladder contains two calcified gallstones, without evidence of acute cholecystitis.  Few subcentimeter hypodensities in the lower pole of the left kidney, are too small to characterize. No hydronephrosis or concerning renal masses are seen. The stomach and small bowel are normal in appearance, without evidence of bowel wall thickening or obstruction.  Moderate atherosclerotic calcification is seen in the abdominal aorta, without aneurysmal dilation.  CT OF THE PELVIS WITH INTRAVENOUS CONTRAST: The urinary bladder and distal ureters are normal.  There is no pelvic lymphadenopathy. Small amount of air within the vagina, raises concern for colovaginal fistula.  BONES AND SOFT TISSUES: Mild compression deformity of T9 vertebral body, unchanged since the prior study.  No bone lesions suspicious for infection or malignancy are detected.'
);


