INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '20534897',
    '11644013-RR-57',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT PELVIS W/O CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: MDCT axial images were obtained from the iliac crest to the pelvic outlet.  Rectal contrast was administered.  Coronal and sagittal reformations were performed.  FINDINGS: Redemonstration of sigmoid diverticulosis with persistent though significantly improved wall edema with trace residual surrounding fat stranding.  The previous region of maximal bowel wall inflammation and associated fluid collection and likely perforation has resolved; however, adjacent to a more superior portion of the descending colon, there is a new 2.4 x 4.2 cm fluid collection containing foci of air, likey representing a new contained perforation (2:17).  Of note, the overlying soft tissues are inflammed though no fistula with the sub/cutaneous tissues are noted at this time. Trace inflammatory changes are also noted extending along the left paracolic gutter.  The rectum, distal bladder are unremarkable.  There is no pelvic sidewall or inguinal lymphadenopathy.  The uterus and adnexa are unremarkable.  There is no suspicious lytic or blastic lesions identified.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '20180280',
    '11662214-RR-10',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABDOMEN W/CONTRAST',
    'TECHNIQUE: Axial images from the lung bases to the symphysis pubis were obtained after oral and intravenous contrast.  Comparison is made to previous CT dated ___.  FINDINGS:   LUNG BASES: Small bilateral pleural effusions are seen.  Minimal right lower lobe atelectasis is present.  No pulmonary nodules or masses are seen.  ABDOMEN: Within the liver in segment VII, there is a poorly defined low-density lesion, that measures 10 x 17 mm in diameter.  It is somewhat less well seen on the previous CT(non-contrast), however, it was present then.  There are no new liver lesions.  Cholecystectomy clips are seen.  The right kidney is malrotated, however, no focal abnormality is seen in the right kidney.  The left kidney is normal.  The spleen, pancreas, and both adrenal glands are normal with no focal abnormality.  Again free air is seen throughout the peritoneal cavity however there is less free air today.  No free fluid is seen within the abdomen.  There is aneurysmal dilatation of the abdominal aorta, which is very focal, with maximum transverse diameter of 30 x 32 mm in diameter.  There is calcification of the abdominal aorta.No fat stranding is seen in the region of the duodenum to suggest a perforated duodenal ulcer.  CT PELVIS: Again there is significant artifact from the left total hip replacement, obscuring fine detail.    An air-filled collection is seen to lie in the left hemipelvis, lateral to the sigmoid colon.  This measures 25 x 50 mm in diameter, when it previously measured 16 x 55 mm in diameter.  This is almost completely filled with air with only a trace of fluid within the dependent portion of this collection.  The second collection, which lies anterior to the rectum also contains mainly air with the fluid component also. It previously measured 36 x 56 mm in diameter, and now measures 55 x 75 mm in diameter.  A third pelvic collecion lying above the sigmoid colon measures73 x 21 mm in diamter and is nes since the previous CT.  Three new smaller more anterior fluid collections are seen to lie anterior to the uterus and above the urinary bladder.  These measure 22 x 23 mm in diameter, 25 x 72 mm in diameter and 28 x 25 mm in diameter respectively.  The sigmoid colon is markedly thickened with evidence of diverticular disease.  The dilated loops of small bowel have resolved.  Again, an abdominal wall hernia seen in the suprapubic region containing small bowel which is not obstructing.  Urinary bladder contains a urinary catheter within it and is decompressed.  No large pelvic adenopathy, however, evaluation for adenopathy is limited due to artifact from the hip prosthesis.  BONES: There is extensive degenerative disease of the spine.  A wedge compression fracture of L3 and L1 as well as T12, T10 and T9 are unchanged.  No new concerning focal bony lesions.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '20180280',
    '11662214-RR-12',
    'CT',
    'Abdomen',
    'CT ABDOMEN W/O CONTRAST',
    'ABDOMEN AND PELVIC CT.:   TECHNIQUE: MDCT axial images were acquired from the lung bases to the symphysis pubis, without administration of intravenous contrast.    Long preparation with oral contrast was performed. Coronal and sagittal reformations were also performed.  FINDINGS: There is no evidence of pleural or pericardial effusion.  Coronary artery calcifications are noted.  Minimal ground-glass opacities are demonstrated in the lung bases.  Small hiatal hernia is seen.  Non-contrast view of the liver demonstrates a single hypodense lesion in segment VII (series 2, image 22), which could not be characterized on current study.  Non-contrast view of the spleen, adrenals and left kidney are unremarkable.  Right kidney is malrotated without evidence. Visualized bowel loops are unremarkable.  Pancreas is of normal attenuation and size.  There is no evidence of retroperitoneal or mesenteric lymphadenopathy.  There is a stable abdominal aortic aneurysm measuring up to 3 cm.  PELVIC CT: Urinary bladder is very distended.  Sigmoid colon shows diffuse thickening, correlating to the area of previously seen perforation.  A drainage catheter is seen in the right lower pelvis with no residual fluid collection surrounding it.  There is residual fluid collection in the left lower pelvis, currently measuring approximately 2.3 x 3.7 cm, previously measuring 2.5 x 7.2 cm.  Also seen ventral hernia (series 2, image 66) in the midline pelvis, containing small bowel loops.  There is no evidence of obstruction or incarceration.  There is no evidence of free fluid in the pelvis.  Extensive artifacts are seen from the metallic hardware in the hips.  OSSEOUS STRUCTURES: Diffuse osteopenia is noted with numerous compression fractures along thoracic and lumbar spine, unchanged from prior studies. Total hip replacement in the left hip and internal nailing in the right femur.'
);


INSERT INTO radiologyreport (
    clinicalcaseid, noteid, modality,
    region, examname, text
)
VALUES (
    '20180280',
    '11662214-RR-13',
    'CT',
    'Venous',
    'UNILAT UP EXT VEINS US RIGHT',
    'TECHNIQUE: Ultrasonography of the right upper arm.  FINDINGS: Grayscale and color Doppler ultrasonography reveals normal flow and compressibility of the right subclavian, IJ and basilic veins.  A PICC line is present extending to one branch of the brachial vein.  No clot is seen within the region of the PICC.  However, distally, there is loss of flow on color Doppler ultrasound and loss of compressibility.  There is mild echogenicity within the vein at this level, within the antecubital fossa, which may represent a thrombus.  The second branch of the right brachial vein is widely patent.  The cephalic vein was not well visualized due to overlying edema.  No focal fluid collections were detected.'
);


