    'EXAMINATION: CT ABD AND PELVIS WITH CONTRAST:  TECHNIQUE: Single phase contrast: MDCT axial images were acquired through the abdomen and pelvis following intravenous contrast administration. Oral contrast was administered. Coronal and sagittal reformations were performed and reviewed on PACS.  DOSE: Acquisition sequence:    1) Spiral Acquisition 3.6 s, 48.2 cm; CTDIvol = 14.0 mGy (Body) DLP = 671.6 mGy-cm.    2) Stationary Acquisition 0.6 s, 0.5 cm; CTDIvol = 3.4 mGy (Body) DLP = 1.7 mGy-cm.    3) Stationary Acquisition 2.4 s, 0.5 cm; CTDIvol = 13.4 mGy (Body) DLP = 6.7 mGy-cm.  Total DLP (Body) = 680 mGy-cm.  FINDINGS:   LOWER CHEST: Severe emphysema is noted in bilateral lung bases.  A 4.3 x 1.8 cm opacity in the posterior right lung base is new.  ABDOMEN:   HEPATOBILIARY: Nodular contour of the liver is consistent with cirrhosis.  There is no evidence of focal lesions. Dilated common bile duct measures 1.3 cm in diameter, likely secondary to post cholecystectomy status.  PANCREAS: 1.3 x 0.8 cm hypodense lesion is identified in the pancreatic head (601:28).  Pancreatic duct is prominent but not dilated.  There is no peripancreatic stranding.  SPLEEN: The spleen shows normal size and attenuation throughout, without evidence of focal lesions.  ADRENALS: The right and left adrenal glands are normal in size and shape.  URINARY: The kidneys are of normal and symmetric size with normal nephrogram.  Millimetric hypodensities in bilateral kidneys are too small to be fully characterized but statistically likely renal cysts.  There is no hydronephrosis.  There is no perinephric abnormality.  GASTROINTESTINAL: The stomach is unremarkable.  Small bowel loops demonstrate normal caliber, wall thickness, and enhancement throughout. Left lower quadrant colostomy is noted.  ___ pouch is unremarkable.  There is no evidence bowel obstruction.  The appendix is normal.  No drainable collections. Right pelvic drain terminates in left pelvis.  PELVIS: Bladder is distended.  there is no free fluid in the pelvis.  REPRODUCTIVE ORGANS: Uterus is unremarkable.  LYMPH NODES: There is no retroperitoneal or mesenteric lymphadenopathy.  There is no pelvic or inguinal lymphadenopathy.  VASCULAR: Fusiform ectasia of the abdominal aorta measures 2.6 cm in maximum diameter.  Severe atherosclerotic disease is noted.  BONES: There is no evidence of worrisome osseous lesions or acute fracture.  SOFT TISSUES: Postsurgical changes are noted in the anterior abdomen.'
);


