granuloma in the lingula (302:145).  There is generalized thickening of the septa, suitable to pulmonary edema or atypical pneumonia.  The airways are patent to the level of the segmental bronchi bilaterally.  BASE OF NECK: Visualized portions of the base of the neck show no abnormality.  ABDOMEN: Included portion of the upper abdomen is unremarkable.  BONES: No suspicious osseous abnormality is seen.? There is no acute fracture.  NOTIFICATION: The findings were discussed with  ___. by ___ ___, M.D. on the telephone on ___ at 1:24 pm, 10 minutes after discovery of the findings.'
